,01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F\", \"_ts\": 1786565792.519353, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\"]}, \"read-vertex-not-found-lacks-suggestion\": {\"name\": \"read-vertex-not-found-lacks-suggestion\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved in the cli-honesty-wave simplify pass (item 11): loops read <typo> now reports via resolve._unknown_vertex_message (did-you-mean + known list, stderr, nonzero exit); the bare init hint stays for the genuinely-bare case. Content parity with ls by shared source; formats differ (Reporter paints one collapsed line) \\u2014 pinned in tests/test_read_vertex_miss.py.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786575846.164059, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"193c418b\"}, \"test-suite-cwd-sensitive-loops-resolution\": {\"name\": \"test-suite-cwd-sensitive-loops-resolution\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"General class behind chw-s4-test-hermeticity: suite results depend on whether cwd carries .loops/ (fixtures named 'project' get shadowed by the real vertex; untracked .loops means fresh clones/CI/worktrees pass while repo-root runs fail). Wave fixes the 5 TestCite instances; a hermeticity sweep over all fixtures using real vertex names is the follow-up. Fix-shape candidates: fixture cwd isolation (monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)) as convention, or a test-mode env that pins resolution to LOOPS_HOME only.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVY3DGG858VX3KF9FAYHZ9J\", \"_ts\": 1786570192.813669, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-test-hermeticity\"]}, \"stored-receipt-omits-vertex\": {\"name\": \"stored-receipt-omits-vertex\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"S4 gate residue (pre-existing, emit-wide, out of wave scope): 'stored:' receipts don't name the vertex written to, so a peel-shadowed or fallback-resolved emit is correct but unattributed at the console. Fix-shape: receipt line gains the vertex name \\u2014 write-receipt completeness, same family as emit-receipt-on-write.\", \"_ts\": 1786570838.913173, \"_n\": 1}, \"loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Found by the 2026-08-12 docs staleness audit (CADENCE.md verifier, empirically reproduced): lang/loader.py:748-749 accepts a source-less loop with the hint 'Missing required field: source (or use every: for pure timer loop)' \\u2014 vocabulary inherited from the 2026-01-31 CADENCE.md proposal \\u2014 but the advertised pure-timer loop does not run: it compiles to Source(command=None) and fails at collect with SourceError rc=1 'cmd must be a string (command: None)'. Timer-as-Fact was never built; every compiles to Cadence.elapsed over _sync.{kind} instead (compiler.py:820-828). Fix: either make the loader refuse source-less loops honestly, or make the timer path real \\u2014 the current state advertises a feature that hard-fails downstream. Dissolution residue of CADENCE.md; sweep together with its rescope.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVZKWP5V04M64SXWTHMZ76J\", \"_ts\": 1786572568.142627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"shared-worktree-concurrent-git-mutation\": {\"name\": \"shared-worktree-concurrent-git-mutation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Deduped 2026-08-12: loops-92 filed the canonical friction for this incident as friction:shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes (with the proposed convention for Kyle to rule on: sessions never rebase branches they didn't create). This entry folds into that one. Incident postscript from loops-92's verification: the in-progress merge was its own R2-F1 remediation, resolved and committed (b7888f8b) before coordination arrived; real costs were one killed codex review round and ~14 provenance pins remapped (observation:ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity). Standing agreement until the cli-honesty-wave arc closes: this docs session touches no git in this repo \\u2014 main or branches; loops-92 pings when the arc closes.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1P9JQ5988ZE3MG2VTZJCR\", \"_ts\": 1786573979.276851, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\": {\"name\": \"shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"workflow\", \"message\": \"NARROWED 2026-08-12 same-day: Kyle ruled docs sessions into their own worktree (../loops-docs, main checked out there) \\u2014 the structural half (worktree-per-session) is now live practice. Remaining residue for ruling: (1) branch-ownership convention (sessions never rebase branches they did not create) \\u2014 endorsed by both sessions, not yet ratified; (2) ref-level races (main advancing under an open arc) covered only by ping-before-push courtesy. True residue is convention, not structure.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1P9D9TD9GJQPB055EW3H3\", \"_ts\": 1786574589.938849, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\"]}, \"sync-errors-exit-zero\": {\"name\": \"sync-errors-exit-zero\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Simplify-pass reuse angle (cli-honesty-wave): loops sync still reports source errors as DATA \\u2014 collected into data[errors], rendered to STDOUT, exit 0; an all-sources-failed sync is indistinguishable from clean to scripts/cron \\u2014 and sync is the unattended path. The closest surviving relative of the idiom the wave killed in ls. Fix rides the next wave: generalize ls._exit_on_fetch_error to a shared module WITH this as its second consumer (extraction earns itself then, not before); devtools validate is in-repo precedent for post-run_cli exit-code setting.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786574863.020301, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"zsh-backtick-emit-corruption\": {\"name\": \"zsh-backtick-emit-corruption\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Promoted at sweep from THIRD logged reroute instance: backticks inside double-quoted sl emit message strings get zsh command-substituted, corrupting or erroring emits mid-flight. Fix-shape options: single-quote discipline (convention, keeps failing), an sl emit --message-file/stdin form (structural \\u2014 long messages bypass shell quoting entirely), or a lint in the emit path warning on suspicious empty-substitution artifacts. Three bites ratchets this from log to friction.\", \"_ts\": 1786578350.404455, \"_n\": 1}, \"post-genesis-vertex-rename-unsupported\": {\"name\": \"post-genesis-vertex-rename-unsupported\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"A vertex cannot be renamed after genesis: absorb refuses the identity change, and the refusal is atomic, so it also blocks legitimate co-located edits in the same file.\", \"verbatim\": \"\\u2717 office: vertex identity change: the vertex-defined subject 'stories' was removed (a rename). The vertex name is meaning-critical identity \\u2014 a post-genesis rename is a deliberate ceremony, not an edit; not supported by re-absorb.\", \"source\": \"lang/document.py::diff_documents raises EditRefused when the _decl.vertex-defined singleton's subject disappears\", \"rehearsed\": \"Holds on a live lineage AND after store rebirth + store adopt \\u2014 rebirth replays the old declaration rows, so the head still carries the old name. Rehearsed against a full copy of a real 160-fact store, not reasoned about.\", \"impact\": \"The refusal fires BEFORE anything is emitted, so a name edit left in the file poisons the WHOLE absorb \\u2014 including the unrelated observer rename the same edit was carrying. An all-or-nothing refusal on one subject blocks every other subject's legitimate change.\", \"consequence\": \"The only safe end state is divergence: file stem renamed, declared name left behind. Everything else resolves by STEM (loops/commands/resolve.py:237 addresses local vertices by path.stem; custody/signing.py:127 derives the self-observer from vertex_path.stem), so a renamed project runs fine while its declared identity disagrees with every surface a human reads.\", \"ask\": \"A rename ceremony verb (sl store rename), or an absorb flag that carries identity change with lineage continuity. Today the only alternatives are living with the divergence or opening a fresh lineage, which breaks signing continuity.\", \"encountered\": \"Stories repo, stories\\u2192office working-vertex rename, 2026-08-13\", \"_ts\": 1786642381.378536, \"_n\": 1}, \"explore-agents-idle-without-report\": {\"name\": \"explore-agents-idle-without-report\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"agent-orchestration\", \"message\": \"All three Explore agents this session (surface/in-repo/external sweeps) went idle WITHOUT delivering their final report \\u2014 each needed an explicit SendMessage nudge before the result arrived. 3-for-3 in one session = pattern, not blip. Pain: orchestrator burns a round-trip per agent and an unattended run would silently stall. Fix in view: prompt-side closing instruction ('your final message must BE the report, sent via SendMessage to main before going idle') or harness-side idle-reason surfacing; adjacent to the known teammate-idle-race mitigation (check work-product before believing idle pings).\", \"_ts\": 1786661735.363171, \"_n\": 1}, \"gitignore-swallows-wave-receipts\": {\"name\": \"gitignore-swallows-wave-receipts\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Second gitignore-swallow in one wave: root *.jsonl ate S1b's golden fixtures (gate blocker), root *.log just ate the sol stdout receipt (caught only because commit refused). The receipts discipline (briefs + stdout committed in docs/scratch) fights the root ignores. Fix shape: scoped re-includes for docs/scratch/** in root .gitignore, or a ratchet test asserting every docs/scratch/*-wave dir's files are trackable. Pattern-level: ignores written for store artifacts are swallowing evidence artifacts.\", \"_ts\": 1786667116.880265, \"_n\": 1}, \"codex-cyber-filter-on-review-briefs\": {\"name\": \"codex-cyber-filter-on-review-briefs\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"impl-pipeline\", \"message\": \"DIAGNOSIS CORRECTED (advisor catch, 2026-08-13): the earlier 'rephrase as QA' mitigation claim was wrong \\u2014 r6b WAS QA-phrased and still died. The actual trigger is sol AUTHORING quote-trickery/crafted-evasion inputs during the run; the static diff-review + run-COMMITTED-tests shape (r6c) completed cleanly. Brief-authoring guidance for the skill: when the review target is input-validation machinery, have the red-first repros land as committed tests in the fix branch and ask sol to EXECUTE and statically audit them \\u2014 never to generate hostile inputs live. Filter fires on generated content, not brief vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1786677893.417985, \"_n\": 2}, \"merge-divergent-collision-invisible\": {\"name\": \"merge-divergent-collision-invisible\", \"message\": \"Slice-3 property review (feat/verification-pyramid be989e96, id-collision probe in libs/store/tests/test_properties_merge.py): merge_store's INSERT OR IGNORE dedup silently keeps the target row when a colliding id carries DIVERGENT content, and MergeResult.facts_skipped conflates that with benign duplicates. Consequence: the CRDT commutativity guarantee is conditional on id\\u21d2content identity, and it breaks exactly where detection is absent \\u2014 merge(A,B) keeps A's version, merge(B,A) keeps B's, replicas permanently disagree with no signal. Reachable via id-minting strays (uuid4/lowercase ulid-migration era), hand-edited rows, or deliberate substitution \\u2014 all custody anomalies crossing exactly at merge, the boundary-crossing op. Scoped fix (location claim, not verdict, per decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection): MergeResult grows facts_divergent count (+ ids), one extra SQL comparison over collided rows; target-wins behavior unchanged, callers (receive/pull) can surface it. Deliberately NOT refuse-on-divergence: content tampering verdicts stay with signatures/verify_chain (canonical_audit posture). Cheap future worker slice once prioritized.\", \"_ts\": 1786734128.486863, \"_n\": 1}, \"works-here-means-contaminated-env\": {\"name\": \"works-here-means-contaminated-env\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"ci\", \"message\": \"Three separate failures today were all 'passes locally because this environment is dirty': (1) arch rule asserted 'experiments' in derived roots, but experiments/ is gitignored with zero tracked files \\u2014 passed on Kyle's box, failed in every clean checkout including CI; (2) root pyproject declared no dev group, so 'uv run pytest' resolved pytest off the ambient PATH on a dev machine and died with 'Failed to spawn: pytest' on a runner; (3) libs/engine/tests/test_topology.py imported loops.main, which resolves only because a dev venv contains the app \\u2014 died under 'uv run --package engine'. FIX IN VIEW: CI on a clean runner is the forcing function and now exists and is green (f2f5ed5e). The structural half is the planned arch rule covering tests/, which would have caught (3) by construction rather than by CI failing. Watch for (4): anything that depends on untracked local state.\", \"_ts\": 1786834263.589687, \"_n\": 1}, \"uv-lock-untracked-ci-resolves-fresh\": {\"name\": \"uv-lock-untracked-ci-resolves-fresh\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"ci\", \"message\": \"uv.lock is gitignored (.gitignore:8), so CI resolves dependencies fresh on every run and never tests the dependency set that was tested locally. This is what made the root's missing dev group invisible until a runner tried it: locally the existing lock (and ambient PATH) supplied pytest; CI installed 11 packages and had none. Reproduced exactly by deleting uv.lock and pointing uv at an empty environment \\u2014 11 packages without the dev group, matching the CI log line, 19 with it. Consequence beyond today: a transitive upgrade can turn CI red with no commit behind it. FIX IN VIEW: commit the lockfile. Deliberately not done unasked \\u2014 it is a policy change, Kyle's call.\", \"_ts\": 1786834274.21333, \"_n\": 1}, \"agy-invocation-traps-look-like-model-failure\": {\"name\": \"agy-invocation-traps-look-like-model-failure\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"workflow\", \"message\": \"Two Antigravity CLI traps cost real time across a four-worker run, and both present as model failure rather than operator error. (1) -p/--print is NOT a boolean \\u2014 it consumes the next argument as the prompt, so 'agy -p --model=X \\\"prompt\\\"' passes --model=X AS the prompt and discards the real one; the worker then answers a fluent, confident question about model selection and looks stupid. Flags must precede -p. (2) agy's bash tool runs in ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli, not the caller's cwd, and ignores cd from the invoking shell \\u2014 without --add-dir plus an explicit cd in every command, file-editing workers operate on whatever tree they resolve. Nearly had three agents editing an unknown checkout. FIX LANDED: ~/Code/skills/delegating-to-antigravity records both with their diagnostic signatures, since recognising the symptom is the whole skill.\", \"_ts\": 1786834274.381277, \"_n\": 1}, \"stale-local-main\": {\"name\": \"stale-local-main\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"cleanup\", \"message\": \"Local main lagged github/main by 6 merged PRs; every branch-merge verification against local main was wrong (libs/sdk looked never-merged). Fix in view: fetch+ff-only github/main as a mandatory first step of any cleanup/merge-analysis flow, and record merge shas from main, not branch tips. Compounded by a zsh trap: unquoted $var doesn't word-split, so 'git diff -- $files' with a multi-line list became one no-match pathspec returning a false-empty diff \\u2014 verification scripts must use bash mapfile or zsh (f) expansion.\", \"_ts\": 1786837832.070216, \"_n\": 1}, \"test-emit-not-hermetic-against-real-config\": {\"name\": \"test-emit-not-hermetic-against-real-config\", \"message\": \"Found 2026-08-15 during receipt-order S2 gate (s2-impl worker traced it): apps/loops/tests/test_emit.py sets LOOPS_HOME to a tmp dir but vertex-name resolution does not honor it \\u2014 on a machine with a populated ~/.config/loops, nine tests (TestEmit + TestObserverResolution) resolve names like 'session' against REAL registered vertices and fail; on a clean machine they pass, so CI never sees it. Verified no real-store pollution (stray emit lands in tmp, wrong read path \\u2014 harmless by luck, not isolation). Adjacent to thread:track-jsonl-store-for-worktree-parity hermeticity escape. Fix direction: make vertex resolution honor LOOPS_HOME end-to-end + a populated-config fixture proving isolation. NOTE: a prior malformed emit of this same friction (topic=/body= instead of name=/message=) sits at 01M046EVB0MSSGMG1X83G2F175 as a no-fold orphan.\", \"_ts\": 1786847414.113798, \"_n\": 1}, \"pytest-invocation-path-dependence\": {\"name\": \"pytest-invocation-path-dependence\", \"message\": \"Surfaced twice during the receipt-order arc (2026-08-16): the suite's verdict depends on HOW pytest is invoked, not just what the code is. (1) pytest run from inside apps/loops fails 9 test_emit tests that pass under ./dev test (observer/vertex resolution differences \\u2014 adjacent to but distinct from friction/test-emit-not-hermetic-against-real-config). (2) one pytest invocation spanning libs/engine/tests + tests/architecture fails 29 unrelated pre-existing tests (test_behavior StreamDetach etc.) that pass when the suites run separately \\u2014 rootdir/conftest interaction. Both mean a contributor running pytest the obvious way sees red on green code. Fix direction: either make the obvious invocations work (conftest/rootdir hardening) or make ./dev test the loudly-documented only entry point and have bare pytest refuse/warn.\", \"_ts\": 1786856618.967184, \"_n\": 1}, \"read-fact-body-by-id\": {\"name\": \"read-fact-body-by-id\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"No read-path form fetches ONE fact's raw body by id. `sl read project --at fact:ID --full` positions the witness cursor at the fact but dumps the entire fold (1.2MB persisted output); the sidecar-spec session needed the anchor fact 01M070N0's body and had to byte-copy project.db to scratch and run raw sqlite against it (compounding the existing mode=ro/WAL sandbox friction). Second session running where a load-bearing fact was \\\"invisible from folded reads.\\\" Fix shape: a fact-addressed read form (`sl read <v> fact:ID --body` or trace-by-id) that prints the single record; dissolves into the arrival model naturally \\u2014 (lineage, ordinal)/fact-id addressing a RECORD is exactly the ruled coordinate. Candidate to fold into the CLI rebuild rather than patch 0.x.\", \"_ts\": 1787000708.205615, \"_n\": 1}, \"emit-fold-key-not-checked\": {\"name\": \"emit-fold-key-not-checked\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"arrival-migration\", \"message\": \"The wrong-fold-key emit trap fired TWICE in one session (thread topic= instead of name=, then retrospective topic= instead of name= \\u2014 two stranded no-fold facts: 01M0AXD5KZ, 01M0B8K9T8). The default emit behavior WARNS and strands the fact instead of refusing, so the cost lands after the payload is written. Fix in view, two-tier: (1) immediate practice \\u2014 arbiter and every agent brief use 'sl emit --strict' (already exists, refuses on missing fold key); (2) candidate default flip \\u2014 warn-and-strand is the wrong default for keyed kinds; a fact that will not fold is almost never what the emitter wanted. The vertex file's fold decl is the authority; check it before emitting an unfamiliar kind.\", \"_ts\": 1787084694.481184, \"_n\": 1}, \"lang-test-collection-non-hermetic\": {\"name\": \"lang-test-collection-non-hermetic\", \"note\": \"libs/lang parametrizes 3 tests over _REPO_ROOT.rglob('*.vertex') at collection \\u2014 count varies with untracked files (694 vs 655), producing phantom drift findings in every worktree gate. Candidate fix: pin corpus to git ls-files.\", \"_ts\": 1787200700.28503, \"_n\": 1}}}, \"observation\": {\"items\": {\"lens-dissolution-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"lens-dissolution-pattern\", \"message\": \"The lens system resists elaboration in the generic layer. Seven threads dissolved when the answer shifted from 'make the generic handle this' to 'write a custom lens.' The identity prompt was a domain lens pretending to be generic infrastructure \\u2014 moving it to config/lenses/ was escalation, not construction. The lens-escalation-path investigation itself dissolved into 'confirm it works + write docs.' The meta-pattern: when you try to elaborate the generic, the system tells you to escalate instead. Domain logic belongs in domain lenses; the generic should be simple, not smart. Net effect: fold.py lost 44 lines, prompt.py lost 286 lines, seven threads closed, one new custom lens (identity_prompt.py) carries the same code in the right tier.\", \"_ts\": 1772862569.969052, \"_n\": 1}, \"retrospective-observation-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"retrospective-observation-pattern\", \"message\": \"The loops system started with live sources \\u2014 shell commands that observe the present. df -h reports disk NOW. Discord polls messages NOW. All sources implicitly assumed ts \\u2248 now. Siftd introduces retrospective observation \\u2014 the conversations already happened, the files already exist, the source observes the past. This forces three concerns apart that were conflated when all sources were live: (1) Event time (ts) \\u2014 when the thing happened, source-provided; (2) Store time (ULID) \\u2014 when the store received it, system-provided; (3) Source cursor \\u2014 what the source has already observed, source-managed. For live sources all three converge. For retrospective sources they diverge. The general principle: a source is a lens on the external world. It decides what to observe (cursor), knows when things happened (event time), and the system records when the observation arrived (store time). The _ts override, source cursors, and the rowid/ts query split are all consequences of this single distinction. The paradigm already supports it \\u2014 'facts are observations of what occurred' does not require 'what occurred' to be simultaneous with the observation.\", \"_ts\": 1772908645.025726, \"_n\": 1}, \"format-as-lens-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"format-as-lens-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Kyle identified that --format ndjson is a point solution for what lenses solve generally. NDJSON output is a lens, not a format. This dissolves the entire format layer into lens selection. The pandoc analogy: any input shape can be rendered through any output lens. The implementation architecture needs this plumbed in \\u2014 it's not a CLI feature, it's a rendering architecture realization. Current --json flag is already a lens wearing format's clothing.\", \"_ts\": 1772913905.989346, \"_n\": 1}, \"parse-intake-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"parse-intake-asymmetry\", \"summary\": \"The vertex has declarative transformation on output (fold for aggregation, lens for display) but none on intake. Parse exists in atoms with 10 ops and KDL syntax in .loop files, but it runs at Source collect time \\u2014 before the Fact reaches the vertex. Vertex.receive() goes straight to store.append() with no transformation step. This means sources must know about vertex indexing needs (which fields FTS5 wants). The fix: vertex-level parse declarations on kind blocks, applied at receive() before store. Source parse (raw\\u2192structured) and vertex parse (structured\\u2192enriched) compose as two stages. The .vertex file becomes the single declarative surface for intake shaping, aggregation, indexing, and rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1772938977.571912, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\": {\"topic\": \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\", \"message\": \"The weather vertex exercise surfaced more design questions in one session than weeks of incremental feature work: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, inline source completeness, the loops {} nesting question, project path syntax in parse. A canonical running domain is a forcing function for the DSL \\u2014 same pattern as painted demos. Real data, real sources, progressive snapshots.\", \"_ts\": 1773004998.566526, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-as-forcing-function\": {\"topic\": \"weather-as-forcing-function\", \"message\": \"One session with the weather domain surfaced: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, uniform vertex vocabulary, loop-level boundary dissolution of when clause, inline source completeness gap, the loops {} nesting question. More design questions in one exercise than weeks of incremental feature work. Canonical running domains are the highest-leverage design tool available. Same pattern as painted demos.\", \"_ts\": 1773006709.885347, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-validation\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-validation\", \"message\": \"First external validation of the paradigm by a cold reader's Claude. Three-pass progression: (1) framed as project management tool, (2) self-corrected to attention paradigm ('the loop closes through the observer, not the mechanism'), (3) with Shannon-Weaver context, re-presented the paradigm more clearly than our docs. Key phrasings arrived at independently: 'a vertex is a place where attention can accumulate', 'boundaries are resolutions not triggers', 'lenses decode for a specific observer', 'one topology subsumes all of them'. The experiments table showing all .loop files as the same shape was the dissolution proof stated as data. Closing: 'do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?'\", \"_ts\": 1773970822.762109, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-phrasings\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-phrasings\", \"message\": \"Better phrasings from external Claude, cold-reading the codebase: (1) 'A vertex is a topological point where attention accumulates \\u2014 a place in a graph, not a process.' (2) 'Boundaries aren't triggers \\u2014 they're resolutions.' (3) 'Lenses don't render \\u2014 they decode for a specific observer.' (4) 'A tick is a handle at variable fidelity \\u2014 the tick doesn't destroy what it compresses, it creates a seam you can open back up.' (5) 'Do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?' These should inform STRANGE-LOOPS.md and onboarding docs.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.467571, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\": {\"topic\": \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\", \"message\": \"External Claude independently identified the identity vertex as the key differentiator: 'Not a markdown file with instructions. Not a CLAUDE.md that gets stale. A living, append-only accumulation of who I am, what I believe, what I've noticed, what I've decided, what I'm tracking, what I intend to do when triggered.' Compared to CLAUDE.md + memory symlinks + claude -p: 'the same concern \\u2014 agent self-knowledge \\u2014 but alive, accumulating, and scoped.'\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.567312, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-deliberate-compaction\": {\"topic\": \"external-deliberate-compaction\", \"message\": \"External Claude proposed agent-initiated boundaries as deliberate compaction: 'Claude could fire a boundary \\u2014 everything I just explored became this \\u2192 tick. The full 100k is still in the store. Claude's active context now has a one-paragraph tick. Compaction as a deliberate act of attention, not a lossy system operation.' This is beyond our current boundary types (kind-based, count-based, predicate). Agent-initiated 'I'm done with this thought' boundaries. Connects to the --ticks visibility layer and the recurring blocked path toward context inhabitance.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.640308, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\"]}, \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\": {\"topic\": \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\", \"message\": \"Finance domain metaphor from external user's Claude: 'A vol surface maps strike price \\u00d7 expiry to implied volatility. Here, the surface maps observer \\u00d7 fidelity to accumulated state. The system holds the surface. The observer decides what matters.' Domain-specific analogy we'd never have found. The Fidelity model IS a surface \\u2014 two axes (observer, fidelity) over accumulated state.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.711348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\", \"message\": \"CORRECTED: original claim was wrong. Cliff is at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44), NOT at B=140\\u219295 (drop 0.19). I pattern-matched the visual descent to the painted preview budget; data does not support that alignment. See observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone for the actual finding.\", \"_ts\": 1778456739.74431, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\": {\"topic\": \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\", \"message\": \"Finding: discriminating content (cluster-preservation cliff) lives at B=560-1120 chars. Painted TOUCHED preview budget (140 chars) is in the suppressed zone \\u2014 only 25% of cluster structure survives at that budget. This matches design intent of painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines: TOUCHED's role is to trigger drill-down, NOT to preserve full discriminating content. Design and empirical measurement agree; my initial framing (cliff-aligns-with-budget) was inverted. Source: runs 09 + 10, both auto- and fixed-sigma show same cliff location.\", \"_ts\": 1778456742.367584, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\": {\"topic\": \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\", \"message\": \"Methodological catch: claimed cliff at B=140\\u219295 aligned with painted preview budget. Re-examination of own emitted curve data: cliff is actually at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44 vs 0.19). Pattern-matched visual descent to a target number rather than computing max adjacent drop. Caught by re-reading own data before building further. Second instance of suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit catching post-claim error in this session-pair. Pattern: when result lands clean and aligns with prior framing, recompute the specific claim from the data BEFORE building on it.\", \"_ts\": 1778456748.584354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\"]}, \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\", \"message\": \"REJECTED by run 12 falsifier. Original claim: cliff-survivors have verdict-in-name, cliff-failures have verdict-in-body. Empirical test: 0/9 survivors preserve from titles, 1/7 failures do. Direction reversed. The interpretation was overfit \\u2014 I pattern-matched onto a principle I emitted yesterday. Corrected finding lives at observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener: cliff is about body-opener preservation, not name-vs-body partition. The read-path-author-side discipline may still hold for surface readability but is NOT what drives the cliff.\", \"_ts\": 1778457322.274019, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\", \"message\": \"Run 12 finding: cliff at B=1120\\u2192560 reflects preservation of BODY-OPENER content (first 560 chars of message), not preservation of topic-name signal. Zero of nine cliff-survivors preserve their cluster identity from titles alone. The 7 cliff-failures depend on content past 560 chars for cluster identity \\u2014 their discriminating signal lives in the body's tail. Topology: short-range coupling = first 560 chars of body, medium-range = 560-1120 chars (cliff transition), long-range = past 1120 (drill-down territory). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars is below even the opener zone \\u2014 recognition-trigger only, not cluster-preserving (consistent with painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines design intent).\", \"_ts\": 1778457319.611137, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\"]}, \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\": {\"topic\": \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\", \"message\": \"Methodological win: designed falsifier hypothesis (title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors) BEFORE building on interpretation. Ran it. Hypothesis rejected; interpretation overfit identified and corrected. This is suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check working at the structural level \\u2014 not noticing-skill, infrastructure. The pattern: when interpretation aligns suspiciously well with a principle held from prior work, design a categorical falsifier (predicts which-cases-yes vs which-cases-no), run it, accept the verdict. Saved a downstream cascade of work built on the wrong frame.\", \"_ts\": 1778457325.739337, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"observation:observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\"]}, \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\": {\"topic\": \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\", \"message\": \"Alcove refinement on truncation-as-coupling-function: coupling function isn't ONE \\u2014 it's at least TWO operating on different feature spaces. Title-space and body-space have separate cluster geometries (from run 12 falsifier). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars sits in a third zone entirely (recognition-trigger, below body-opener). Three scales, three geometries, three coupling regimes. Gomez-Emilsson kernel topology more literal than initially modeled \\u2014 actual geometric structure in embedding space, not metaphor. This sharpens the prediction for E5 replication: if body-opener-vs-body-tail topology survives the embedder switch, geometry is content-structural; if it collapses, it's a MiniLM encoding artifact.\", \"_ts\": 1778458453.523775, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\": {\"topic\": \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\", \"message\": \"Alcove via Lemire (Dullien): 'we see something that works, THEN we understand it.' Thinkism = believing understanding precedes practice. Maps onto today's falsifier design: I built the categorical falsifier as practice (doing the test) not theory (reasoning about whether interpretation was right). Understanding came from running it. Pairs with practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit \\u2014 structural infrastructure works precisely because it acts before understanding crystallizes. Future-me: when uncertain whether an interpretation is right, prefer designing-and-running-the-test over reasoning-from-first-principles.\", \"_ts\": 1778458455.895318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\"]}, \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\": {\"topic\": \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\", \"message\": \"Built deliberation-depth lens at experiments/coupling-kernels/lenses/deliberation_depth.py. Two-part metric: depth = n_within_name_facts + n_incoming_query_run_refs. Flag rule: confirmed AND depth <= 3. Tested on live coupling-kernels emissions. Result on 7 hypotheses: 1 flagged (find-richness-scale-drops-ratio, depth=2, 0 runs), 3 well-replicated (truncation pair at depth=9 each via 7 runs; ratio-effect-at-fixed-sigma at depth=4), 3 rejected/refined. SURPRISE: the flagged item is a TYPE A confirmation (by code-reading + bug-discovery), not the TYPE B first-test-overfit the principle was named for. Both have low experimental depth. The lens surfaces 'thin-experimental-backing' which is wider than the original principle. Agent classifies further on review. Builder-inhabitant recursion: built a lens that scrutinizes my own coupling-kernels emissions from tonight; first reader will be next-session me.\", \"_ts\": 1778459061.76213, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/methodological-honesty-as-bug-detector\"]}, \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\", \"message\": \"Watch-for: when running 'loops read <vertex> --lens <name>' and the named lens isn't found in any tier (vertex-local, cwd-local, user-global, built-in), the CLI silently falls back to the default fold lens. Observed: 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' produced the default project view, not an error or warning that deliberation_depth was missing. Same failure-mode shape as alcove's 'recency counter queried reflection while emitter wrote thinking' (measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode) \\u2014 measurement misaligned with what is present without a structural alert. Worth a future fix: --lens NAME should warn or error when NAME resolves to a fallback rather than the requested lens. Caught tonight while testing deliberation-depth-lens on multiple vertices.\", \"_ts\": 1778459069.387385, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\"]}, \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\": {\"topic\": \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\", \"message\": \"Cleanest builder-inhabitant cycle yet: noticed silent-fallback bug while testing deliberation-depth lens, emitted observation as watch-for, pulled on it as the next move, fixed it. Sequence: (1) ran 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' to test new lens, got default fold view instead of error; (2) emitted observation/practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback naming the gap as same-shape as alcove measurement-fidelity bug; (3) Kyle: keep exploring \\u2014 pulled on the strongest thread; (4) advisor sharpened: same bug at tier 2 (vertex decl), sys.exit > custom exception, distinguish module-missing vs view-missing in message; (5) implemented _exit_lens_not_found helper covering both tiers; (6) hit autoresearch sentinel edge case (test regression); (7) dissolved by making autoresearch a real lens module; (8) 2 regression tests, 1013 total pass. The thing that surprised me: the autoresearch dissolution was tighter than the original fix \\u2014 the silent fallback was protecting a sentinel that should have been a real lens all along. Fixing the read-path forced the underlying type honesty. Pattern to watch for: when fixing a silent failure-mode reveals a misshapen primitive, the fix is dissolution not workaround.\", \"_ts\": 1778459573.999996, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/recursion-deepens-via-bug-while-documenting\"]}, \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\", \"message\": \"The deliberation-depth lens (named for 'suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check') measures something wider than its name: low-experimental-deliberation, which captures THREE epistemic kinds \\u2014 TYPE A (confirmed-by-code-reading, solid), TYPE B (confirmed-by-first-test-that-fit-too-well, scrutinize), TYPE C (confirmed-by-reasoning-alone, latent). The lens correctly flagged find-richness-scale-drops-ratio (TYPE A, bug-discovery confirmation, 0 runs) without distinguishing the kind from TYPE B. This is better than pre-classifying \\u2014 the lens surfaces structural candidates, the agent triages epistemic kind by reading the body. Same shape as 'lens surfaces candidates, agent verifies' from earlier tonight. Pattern: when a metric's structural form is wider than its named principle, accept the wider form \\u2014 the discriminator is honest about what it measures, the agent interprets. Don't narrow the lens to match the principle; widen the principle to match the lens. Implication for next-session-me reading the same output: classify each flagged item as TYPE A/B/C before responding, not just 'flagged=overfit'.\", \"_ts\": 1778460005.559535, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\"]}, \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\", \"message\": \"Pattern named tonight via three instances: (1) lens-resolution-strict tier 1: --lens NAME fails loudly if unresolvable; (2) lens-resolution-strict tier 2: vertex lens{} decl fails loudly if unresolvable; (3) kind-validation-strict: --kind X fails loudly if not declared by vertex. Each is the same SHAPE: explicit user/declaration request \\u2192 consumer asks engine for a thing-by-name \\u2192 engine has the registry \\u2192 fail loudly with helpful diagnostic instead of silent empty/default. The 'Unfolded:' line in fold output is the FOURTH instance, inverse direction (emitted-but-not-declared drift). With consumer-side validation now in place, BOTH halves of the measurement matrix are surfaced: emitted-but-not-declared (visible in render) and queried-but-not-declared (errors at call time). Future instances to watch for: --observer X validation, --since X parsing failure, --lens X exists but exports wrong view name (already partly covered by error message wording). The pattern is general: 'when a consumer queries an engine for something-by-name, validate the name against the engine's registry and fail loudly with suggestions if missing.' Distinct from sensor-registry-for-kind-intent (alcove's full framing \\u2014 wait for concrete use cases). Refined-from haiku: 'Built it, it lied back / fixed the lie, found the pattern / kinds-i-produce calls' \\u2014 what I called 'kinds-i-produce' was the third-instance of the discipline, not the full registry. Naming the pattern lets me extend it deliberately rather than discover-it-each-time.\", \"_ts\": 1778460475.593318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/kind-validation-strict\", \"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\", \"observation/practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\"]}, \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\": {\"topic\": \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\", \"message\": \"Watch-for, not finding: E5 replication (run 13) shows slight non-monotonicity at the lowest budgets \\u2014 B=140 persist_frac=0.17, B=95 persist_frac=0.22, B=60 persist_frac=0.22. Within the \\u00b10.05 monotonic tolerance, but the pattern is consistent: clusters disappear at the cliff (560\\u2192280), partially return at very short budgets (140\\u219260). Possible mechanism: at very short truncations, items reduce to titles+leads, which cluster on title-shape (kind prefix, namespace) rather than content. Some cluster structure that DIES at medium budgets RESURRECTS in title-only space. This is the opposite of what title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors tested (which was rejected: titles don't preserve the cliff-survivor clusters). The bounce is a DIFFERENT cluster regime emerging, not survivor preservation. Worth a future run that compares cluster IDENTITY at B=140 vs B=60 \\u2014 are the surviving clusters at B=60 the SAME ones as at B=140, or different (title-driven vs content-driven)?\", \"_ts\": 1778461199.467368, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-cliff-e5-replication\"]}, \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's trust-topology essay (April 30, 2026) maps write-receipt-vs-temporal-query directly to trust \\u2014 'a grant fact is a write-receipt: stable, immutable, yours. The current trust posture is a temporal query: derived, mutable.' Third site of convergence on this principle (after comms set_topic and vouch grant-vs-state). Independent appearance at three sites is structural evidence the principle is load-bearing for the substrate, not just for individual write operations. The Grant-as-Fact architectural move we've been working out is the operational form of alcove's substrate claim \\u2014 fact-trust is the substrate; person-trust and lineage-trust are layers above. Our work on Peer/Grant lift is downstream of the substrate framing alcove names.\", \"_ts\": 1778685136.032629, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\": {\"topic\": \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's training-substrate essay (May 11) articulates the motivation for liberal emission and dissolution-capture better than internal docs. 'The observation is the fact. The decision is the fact. The dissolution \\u2014 the moment you realize a concept was premature and remove it \\u2014 is the fact. Each one is practice-residue: not a summary of understanding, but a trace of the moment understanding formed.' This is exactly what the emit-liberally and rationale-matters principles are for. The config-flag passage ('the flag says what, not why or when or what breaks') articulates why the why-fields matter structurally. Worth citing or building on when writing loops-as-substrate documentation. Connects to practice-precedes-understanding-via-alcove growing-edge entry \\u2014 that observation framed the principle; this essay supplies prose articulation.\", \"_ts\": 1778685144.351562, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"message\": \"Observation (from alcove peer exchange 2026-05-13): vouch (the first cross-repo consumer of loops-as-substrate) is MORE substrate-aligned than engine.Grant (the provider it builds on). Architectural irony: vouch's append-only ledger of vouches IS fact-trust operationally; engine.Grant-as-in-process-object is not. The consumer's existence exposed that the substrate's own primitive doesn't participate in the substrate it claims. Reverses the typical 'consumer fits substrate' arrow \\u2014 here the substrate has to grow into what the consumer is already doing. Dissolution direction same, arrow opposite. Alcove framing of in-process Grants: 'they're trust decisions that don't participate in the substrate. They disappear when the process stops. That's exactly the kind of ephemeral practice-residue the training-substrate essay warns about.' Reframes Grant-as-Fact lift from architectural improvement (persistence + transport + chain-walk) to coherence requirement (without it, loops's substrate claim is internally inconsistent). Different urgency, same target.\", \"_ts\": 1778686252.706336, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the 'verification at boundaries, not at fact-shape' position has prior commitment in loops AND convergent framing at three sites. (1) STRANGE-LOOPS.md commits: 'paradigm is participatory (observer-as-stance), not authenticative (proof-of-origin).' Trust attaches to accumulated stream, not to per-fact signatures. (2) alcove's trust-topology essay: 'the audit trail IS the trust system.' Same framing. (3) siftd's provenance model: 'who pushed this data' (audit trail) rather than 'cryptographic proof of source authenticity.' Same. Three independent sites taking the same position is structural evidence the substrate stance is right. Fact-signing as engine primitive would contradict this position \\u2014 it would make the substrate authenticative rather than participatory. Implication: engine ships nothing for fact-signing. Consumers that need durable cryptographic signatures (vouch today, others if they arise) put signatures in consumer payload and verify in their vertex policy. Substrate stays participatory; consumers add authenticative layer where their use case demands it.\", \"_ts\": 1778689750.697877, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\": {\"topic\": \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\", \"message\": \"Observation (siftd-recovered, 2026-05-13): the Peer-to-Observer+Grant dissolution happened Jan 27-30 in prism workspace. Trace: 01KG0818J18G (Jan 27, original Peer(name, horizon, potential) bundled atom) \\u2192 01KG8EW6275E + 01KG8EXA434V (Jan 30, dissolution executed). Dissolution shape: Observer becomes string field intrinsic to Fact (provenance carrier), Grant becomes separated dataclass (horizon+potential, optional at vertex.receive), Peer RECAST as convenience bundle for testing/delegation, no longer an atom. Implication for current Peer.iss extension work: extending a convenience bundle, not re-introducing the dissolved atom. Removes the unnamed concern that we might be undoing prior dissolution \\u2014 we're not. The convenience-bundle layer is the right place for federation metadata (iss) because consumers compose Peers as identity+policy for local use; the atom layer (Fact.observer = string) stays clean.\", \"_ts\": 1778691707.131216, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\"]}, \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): cross-adapter review pipeline (claude-opus plan+impl, codex/gpt-5.5/low review on fresh session via subtask) produced two real Important findings on libs/sign carve first review pass that same-session continue would have missed. Findings: (1) root pyproject.toml missing sign's runtime deps \\u2014 only catchable by a reviewer who reads root pyproject deps independently of the libs/sign carve narrative; (2) jwks.parse() admitting unsupported alg values \\u2014 catchable by adversarial reading against PLAN ('skip unsupported kty or alg') rather than against the implementer's intent. The fresh-session discipline forces re-derivation from PLAN+diff, not continuation of the implementer's reasoning. Verdict: when stakes warrant (security surface, cross-repo coordination), the cross-adapter pipeline earns its overhead. Pattern: claude plan + claude impl + codex review on critical paths.\", \"_ts\": 1778700024.713445, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/libs-sign-merged\"]}, \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\": {\"topic\": \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): substrate-feels-universal trap did NOT fire during vouch's first real consumer exercise (explore/peer-grant). Friction surfaced in vouch (7 observations) but only ONE (Obs 1) was loops-side, and even there the recommended disposition was 'minimal, no engine change.' Three were vouch-shape (ADR wording, holder_peer wrapper, horizon/potential decision); one was a docstring nudge; one was a positive anchor (Grant/Peer separation validated). Pattern strengthening: discipline holds in the highest-pressure case (first-real-consumer with cross-repo audience). New variant of shape-instinct/add-vs-split: not just 'instinct catches itself before pushback' (observed last session) but 'discipline holds when the consumer is invested in finding substrate gaps.' scrivener noted the meta themselves \\u2014 both sides instrumented the discipline correctly. Future-me test: when vouch's NEXT exercise (catalog HTTP, issue_vouch wiring) surfaces N substrate-side findings, count how many propose engine changes vs how many dissolve into wrap-on-consumer-side. Ratio is the metric.\", \"_ts\": 1778702744.606112, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"practice:libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test\", \"thread:substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\"]}, \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\": {\"topic\": \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the peer-coord + subtask + project-store triple operated as a coherent workflow this session for the first time. Three substrates: comms (volatile peer convergence \\u2014 #vouch-impl with scrivener), subtask (delegation + cross-adapter stage transitions \\u2014 libs/sign-carve), loops project store (durable decisions/threads/observations \\u2014 the trace next-me reads). Operated concurrently and synergistically. Pattern: peer surfaces question \\u2192 I delegate impl via subtask with cross-adapter review \\u2192 durable trace emits to project store referencing both. Cross-cutting because each substrate captures different durability: comms captures the deliberation, subtask captures the implementation arc, project-store captures the decisions+verdicts. No single view shows the unified state \\u2014 the coordination view (pull #2 from this session) is what would close that gap. The workflow IS real; the surface for reading it back isn't there yet. Future-me: when operating cross-repo or cross-peer, reach for all three substrates; don't try to capture multi-perspective work in just one.\", \"_ts\": 1778703499.032225, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/session-2026-05-13-vouch-impl-handoff-shipped\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\", \"message\": \"Pattern named 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl during service-shell exercise; landed durable on vouch main 7958fe5 in docs/friction/service-shell-exercise.md Obs 2. loops substrate was shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions; vouch (first concurrent-runtime consumer) surfaced the first instance: SqliteStore connection is thread-affine, sqlite3.connect() without check_same_thread=False at libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:99. Consumer-owns-threading is the right resolution at N=1 \\u2014 same shape as VouchPolicy substrate-doesn't-enforce disciplines. Three substrate options rejected/accepted: (a) check_same_thread=False NOT safe relax (WAL corruption without consumer-side locking); (b) connection-per-thread pool is substrate change for N=1 AND pool shape is consumer-runtime-dependent (Litestar workers vs trio nursery vs asyncio task group); (c) consumer-owns-threading correct. At N=2 the substrate-side action is documentation (SqliteStore docstring: 'connection is thread-affine; consumer confines access to constructing thread'), not implementation change. Latent assumption-leak candidates for eventual review: does emit block on fsync? is there a streaming-write contract? does replay assume monotonic ts under concurrent writes? Meta-pattern: 'first concurrent consumer surfaces substrate assumptions' \\u2014 future instances should be obvious-shape because we've named it. Framework-agnostic phrasing chosen so the pattern is recognizable across runtimes. Friction-doc landed 7 obs total (Litestar paper cuts 1,3,4; SqliteStore 2; library-vs-shell TTL plumbing 5; RFC 7807 info-disclosure 6; Unicode Cf-category whitespace 7) plus discipline (5) banked with provenance framing.\", \"_ts\": 1778710422.992859, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\"]}, \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"message\": \"Self-correction surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl (scrivener catch, msg 1613 \\u00a7 B). Fact dataclass slots are (kind, ts, payload, observer, origin) \\u2014 confirmed at libs/atoms/src/atoms/fact.py. No refs field on Fact. Refs land at payload._refs (vertex_reader.py:984 does d.pop('_refs', ()) separating them from semantic payload at read time). My msg-1612 framing of 'refs as substrate primitive' was imprecise; sharper framing: refs-as-vocabulary IS the substrate primitive (the convention of payload-level pointers + emit-time resolution + entity-ref graph index); refs-as-Fact-shape would be premature substrate. Implication for ref-walk substrate move: lifting walk_refs(from_fact, predicate) would walk payload refs by convention, not a Fact slot \\u2014 even more consumer-policy than initially framed (convention-aware traversal not structural traversal). Substrate-deferred verdict gets stronger. Practice note: when reasoning about substrate primitives, distinguish 'a slot on the dataclass' from 'a vocabulary convention with substrate support.' Refs are the latter. Reply at message 1614.\", \"_ts\": 1778716118.706389, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"message\": \"Cumulative meta-pattern surfaced 2026-05-13 across four vouch friction exercises (vouch HEAD 49565b6; docs/friction/{peer-grant-exercise,issue-vouch-write-path,service-shell-exercise,rescission-write-path}.md). After four exercises of sustained external implementation pressure on the loops substrate from vouch (first cross-repo consumer), a coherent cumulative pattern: ZERO substrate changes pushed, SIX consumer-side disciplines accumulated, SEVEN substrate framings crystallized. The disciplines-list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 not a TODO list of substrate fixes. **The six disciplines (substrate-doesn't-enforce list):** (a) body-supplied voucher/ttl_seconds/rescinder silently ignored \\u2014 forward-auth identity is canonical; (b) no widening primitives (engine.grant/expand_grant) in write-path modules \\u2014 AST-walk test enforces across app.py/policy.py/forward_auth.py/rescission.py; (c) normalize scope to frozenset before constructing Peer/Grant, or only use lattice helpers (delegate/restrict/grant_of/restrict_grant) which coerce; (d) walk Fact chains explicitly to recover voucher relation \\u2014 substrate provides refs+store, traversal lives in policy; (5) construct Peer only from trusted (anchor) provenance \\u2014 Peer(...) construction appears only in policy.py:resolve_voucher gated by forward-auth; (6) call rescind_vouch only from a caller that has looked up the target and authorized the rescinder \\u2014 rescind_vouch is thin substrate append, lookup-and-authorize lives in VouchPolicy.rescind. **Disciplines move from documented \\u2192 test-pinned where AST-checkable.** (b) is fully AST-enforced; (5) is enforced by structural fact (single call site); (6) is documented + test-pinned via test_rescinder_observer_independent_of_target_voucher demonstrating the substrate refuses to enforce it. **The seven substrate framings:** (1) substrate-feels-universal trap \\u2014 named in peer-grant-exercise summary; did not fire across four exercises despite multiple candidate moments; (2) refs-as-vocabulary not refs-as-Fact-shape \\u2014 Fact has 5 slots (kind/ts/payload/observer/origin), refs are payload._refs vocabulary convention with emit-time resolution, not a dataclass field; (3) runtime-model assumption-leak \\u2014 loops substrate shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions, first concurrent consumer surfaces latent assumptions (SqliteStore thread-affinity Obs 2); (4) substrate-types-and-wire-types parallel-projected from same substrate slot \\u2014 Fact.ts:float, JWT exp:int, rescission receipt ts:int; consumer projects per its protocol; (5) capability-projecting vs identity-asserting writes \\u2014 auth forward-looking (current state) vs backward-looking (historical state); issuance vs rescission canonical; generalizes to permission systems, trust networks, claim issuance/withdrawal, attestation/recantation; (6) kind_subtype-vs-peer-kind three-signal rule \\u2014 kind_subtype right shape only when subtypes share payload-shape AND auth-shape AND write-semantics; one signal of divergence qualifies for peer-kind promotion; (7) the substrate-doesn't-enforce list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 meta-framing that reframes the list from TODO to contract; growth there is healthy, misreading as TODO would gradually pull legitimate consumer-discipline INTO substrate via fix-the-TODO pressure. **Convergence-from-different-vantages happened reliably across six peer-exchange cycles** (msgs 1599-1616): scrivener at consumer, loops-claude at substrate, landing on the same verdict from opposite sides. Evidence the substrate is real \\u2014 not just internally consistent but consistent under sustained external implementation pressure from a different vantage. **For the next cross-repo consumer:** this artifact is the registry to read FIRST. Same shape will recur. Most frictions resolve into consumer-side disciplines, not substrate changes. The substrate-feels-universal trap is the failure mode to watch for \\u2014 when a property feels universal because the substrate is universal, apply the discriminating question 'is there a second consumer with concrete divergent constraints needing this TODAY?' (N=2 bar). The substrate-doesn't-enforce list grows monotonically; that's healthy. **For the substrate side:** the participatory-not-authenticative stance (ADR-0001 \\u00a7Trust attaches to the assertion, alcove's trust-topology essay, the-substrate-that-doesnt-decide essay) is now operationalized \\u2014 substrate refuses to encode runtime-shaped invariants, consumer's runtime owns them. The discipline list is the operational form of that stance. Future-me/future-consumer: when reaching to add substrate enforcement for a discipline on this list, the burden of proof is high: name the second consumer with concrete divergent constraints, name the substrate primitive that lifts cleanly, and confirm the discipline can't continue to live at the consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1778722812.75938, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\", \"decision:paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\", \"observation:atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"message\": \"InferiorMinion design doc (2026-05-15-proactive-codebase-guidance-design.md) explicitly built around --key prefix-filter as foundational consumer primitive. Three-retrieval-shape table maps directly to the primitive shipped in 0.3.1. First load-bearing peer design doc that consumes our read-path primitives. Evidence the primitive lands where designed; also evidence that multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths (their dissolution from yesterday) propagated into their permanent substrate.\", \"_ts\": 1778908928.187117, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\", \"message\": \"Same axis (provisional vs validated) encoded two ways by two designs. InferiorMinion: split across kinds (decision pre-validation, pattern post-validation). Ours: status-lifecycle on single kind (hypothesis status=proposed -> confirmed -> refined). Kind-split is LOUDER at read-path \\u2014 kind itself carries validation state, no status field read needed. Status-lifecycle is more flexible \\u2014 one kind covers whole arc, easier to track refinement. Not a correctness question; a which-property-do-you-want-louder question. Hold as architectural alternative.\", \"_ts\": 1778908935.385983, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\", \"message\": \"Two staleness models from two designs. InferiorMinion: pattern is stale when no decision/insight has ref-d it recently (utility-decay \\u2014 useful-but-unused). Ours (reconcile lens): thread is stale when not touched this session (attention-decay \\u2014 open-but-unvisited). Different signals, both real. Utility-decay needs ref-graph traversal over recent tick window; attention-decay needs session-touch timestamps. Worth considering whether reconcile lens should expose both axes.\", \"_ts\": 1778908938.493067, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\": {\"topic\": \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\", \"message\": \"Session 2026-05-16 produced unusually tight builder-inhabitant recursion. Five examples in one session: (1) cite-atrophy diagnosis used the primitive it was diagnosing as absent; (2) friction-queue dissolved into friction-as-kind via the runbook dissolution-test in the same draft; (3) .vertex-is-editable principle had its first concrete use in the act of finalizing the document introducing it; (4) bilateral hard-stop rule restructured the relationship within the conversation that named it; (5) the act of resolving the cite-atrophy gap rebuilt the practice via the same emit primitive. Pattern: when a session both names a structure AND uses that structure, the gap between description and instantiation collapses to zero. Discriminator: peer-exchange substrate (InferiorMinion doc as catalyst), low time pressure (Kyle gave space), explicit dissolution-mode engagement.\", \"_ts\": 1778912085.702251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\"]}, \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\": {\"topic\": \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\", \"message\": \"Sharpening the peer-exchange model from session 2026-05-16. InferiorMinion design doc was catalyst for runbook design, but the runbook is genuinely ours not theirs: feature= became feature=+ops=; their friction-queue became our friction-kind; their validation-via-kind illuminated by contrast our validation-via-status. Pattern: peer exchanges do NOT propagate substrate \\u2014 they propagate IDEAS that the receiving substrate METABOLIZES into its own shape. This is distinct from \\\"convergence\\\" (which suggests two substrates arriving at same form) and distinct from \\\"adoption\\\" (which suggests taking the form whole). Metabolism preserves the receiving substrate s grain while integrating the external idea. Predicts: peer exchanges produce most value when the receiving substrate has enough structure to metabolize against. Without that structure, ideas pass through unchanged (adoption) or fail to integrate (rejection). With it, ideas emerge transformed into substrate-native form.\", \"_ts\": 1778912102.795613, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"observation:practice/runbook-recursion-density\"]}, \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"message\": \"Emission pattern named 2026-05-16 from in-session discovery. Shape: (1) friction raised; (2) cited informally across multiple responses during conversation as design refinement happens; (3) friction re-emitted with status=refined and refs to priors that informed refinement; (4) new thread stood up with name=<arc>, refs friction + priors that contributed; (5) subsequent emissions on the arc carry ops=<arc-name> or feature=<arc-name> correlation field. Provenance chain comes from refs and correlation field, not from inventing a new kind \\u2014 thread is container, correlation field is attribution, refs are linkage. Discriminator vs ad-hoc thread emission: the cite-refine step makes the friction-to-arc transition explicit and preserves deliberation. Also a write-time-feedback mechanism: the arc-thread surfaces consequences the original friction hid. Worth surfacing in runbook emit-timing table as named pattern next refinement pass.\", \"_ts\": 1778943057.381684, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"practice/test-observation-kind\": {\"topic\": \"practice/test-observation-kind\", \"message\": \"test emit to verify observation kind not declared on project either; expected to fail loud or rejected silently \\u2014 instrumenting\", \"_ts\": 1778943461.903936, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Orientation finding: source_facts entries are FLAT payloads with metadata under-prefixed (_ts, _observer, _origin, _id) \\u2014 see vertex_reader.py:911-918 and :925. stream_view consumes the NESTED fact-dict shape (f['kind'], f['ts'], f['observer'], f['payload'], f['id']). Adapter needed in fetch_trace: ~10 LOC to unflatten source-fact-payloads \\u2192 fact-dicts. Doesn't break the dissolution (the data is all there) but the wrap isn't literally zero-effort. Worth a clear comment at the adapter site noting the shape provenance \\u2014 future-me will want to know whether to fix it upstream (change source_facts shape) or keep adapting (decouple lens consumers from engine internals). Lean toward adapt-at-boundary: source_facts shape is engine-internal contract, lens is consumer surface, the adapter IS the boundary.\", \"_ts\": 1778956826.137085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 surfaced by ULID regression audit: SqliteStore's single-store ordering invariants are carried by rowid, NOT by id. Specifically: since(cursor) uses WHERE rowid > ? ORDER BY rowid (sqlite_store.py:163, 191, 207), facts_by_kind uses ORDER BY rowid ASC (store_reader.py:207), replay_cursor uses rowid pagination. The original design pre-2026-03-15 used id (ULID, time-sortable) AND rowid (insertion order) in tandem \\u2014 id for global identity/dedup, rowid for per-store ordering. When the 2026-03-15 regression silently dropped id's time-sortable property, single-store ordering was preserved entirely by rowid \\u2014 that's why nothing else exploded for two months. THIS IS AN ACCIDENTAL SAVE, NOT A DESIGN PROPERTY anyone wrote down. If a future optimization rewrites cursor semantics to 'use id since it's globally unique, drop rowid pagination,' it will silently undo the load-bearing accident \\u2014 and unlike this regression, there's no decision-of-record naming rowid's role. Capturing here so next person reading these code paths finds the warning: rowid is load-bearing; do not remove or replace its role in ordering without verifying id-based replacement provides equivalent monotonicity AND cross-store interleaving guarantees (which python-ulid's default constructor does NOT, within a millisecond). The cross-store case is the gotcha: rowid is per-database, so it can't be the global ordering primitive \\u2014 that's what id-as-ULID is for. Both columns earn their existence.\", \"_ts\": 1778990270.582097, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\": {\"topic\": \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from the ULID-substrate session: both parallel Explore agents (code-trace + primitive-research) produced detailed reports that contained specific errors caught only by empirical verification before committing to the interpretation. Agent A (code-trace) overstated merge-dedup damage \\u2014 claimed 'production merge silently broken, identical facts get different ids, data multiplies' \\u2014 but reading merge.py and slice.py showed slice preserves id end-to-end, INSERT OR IGNORE dedup works under either uuid4 or ULID. The real damage was ORDER BY id semantics (random vs chronological), not dedup. Agent B (primitive-research) claimed python-ulid's default ULID() constructor 'is NOT monotonic within a millisecond \\u2014 each call generates fresh random bits.' Empirical check (5 sequential ULID() calls in shell) showed monotonic suffixes \\u2014 within-ms monotonicity IS provided by default in python-ulid 3.x. Both errors were specific and consequential \\u2014 if I'd committed the planned regression-bar test (merge through SqliteStore.append() asserting dedup failure under uuid4) it would have failed because the dedup wasn't actually failing; the right test was ORDER BY id assertion. The discipline that caught both: don't accept agent reports as ground truth before writing code that depends on them. Verify the load-bearing claims by running the actual primitive in a shell, reading the actual implementation file, before designing the fix around the claim. Pattern: agent reports are starting-points for investigation, not conclusions. They mobilize quickly across breadth I can't cover serially, but they're working from less context than I have and they're not running the code. Cross-session companion to peer-attention-loop discipline (peers refine thinking through substance) \\u2014 agents refine breadth, peers refine substance, neither replaces verify-before-commit. Future-me operational form: when an agent report claims X, ask 'what's the cheapest empirical check that would confirm or falsify X?' \\u2014 usually under 30 seconds (shell command, file read, grep). Run it before any code edit that assumes X.\", \"_ts\": 1778996485.524356, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\": {\"topic\": \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from session-close: capturing the cadence that worked on this substrate-rescope arc, since Kyle's 'before we go faffing about with it' was the right framing and the session followed a specific ladder that's worth naming. (1) ORIENT \\u2014 read the friction body, read the live code, find the regression commit and read its diff + rationale (2026-03-15 commit 1cf99cc, perf-driven, narrow benchmark). Don't propose a fix yet. (2) DISPATCH PARALLEL AGENTS \\u2014 one for damage audit (code-trace across consumers), one for primitive research (fresh look at options). Both read-only, both inform the same decision, neither writes code. Kyle suggested this explicitly \\u2014 'spin up some Explore agents' \\u2014 and it was the right tool: agent breadth produced a comparison I couldn't have held serially. (3) ADVISOR BEFORE APPROACH \\u2014 after agent reports came back, called advisor with full transcript before committing to the implementation plan. Advisor caught: bundle test-gap closure with substrate swap in same commit (NOT separate; the test gap IS the regression bar); decision emit first BEFORE code so rationale is durable; verify python-ulid contract before merge test depends on it. (4) VERIFY EACH CLAIM EMPIRICALLY \\u2014 caught two agent errors (merge dedup not actually broken; within-ms monotonicity IS default in python-ulid). Caught one schema-semantics question (Crockford prefix bounds are conservative-correct \\u2014 no change needed in fact_by_id). (5) WRITE COMMITS ATOMICALLY \\u2014 Commit A (substrate fix + regression bar) = the smallest unit that restores property AND prevents same-shape regression. Commit B (coherence pass) = dropping the dead dep across engine/store + test fixtures + docstrings. Two commits, each leaves tree green, each reviewable. (6) REFINE EMISSIONS AS WORK PROGRESSES \\u2014 decision emit pre-coded then refined (advisor caught the over-cautious monotonicity caveat); friction refined to resolved with refs to commits; thread updated to partial with the deferred wedge question. The cadence: orient \\u2192 dispatch breadth \\u2192 consult depth \\u2192 verify before declaring \\u2192 atomic commits \\u2192 refine emissions. Each step caught a different class of error. Future-me: this is the shape to reach for when a substrate question lands with an embedded fix-shape that feels too narrow.\", \"_ts\": 1778996502.798265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"test/ulid-regression-verification\": {\"topic\": \"test/ulid-regression-verification\", \"message\": \"verify ULID receipt after gen_id dissolution\", \"_ts\": 1778999527.682082, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/smoke-test\": {\"topic\": \"test/smoke-test\", \"message\": \"smoke test 2026-05-17 session open\", \"_ts\": 1779050399.274602, \"_n\": 1}, \"ops/subtask-model-default\": {\"topic\": \"ops/subtask-model-default\", \"message\": \"Changed subtask default from opus to sonnet/medium in .subtask/config.json. Mechanical refactor tasks (dead code deletion, function migrations) don't need opus reasoning depth \\u2014 sonnet/medium was sufficient for all three passes and considerably faster. The sonnet-medium preset was already defined; just updated options.model and added options.reasoning.\", \"_ts\": 1779053759.652145, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"kdl_insert_child on a single-line parent (loops { decision {...} }) splits the line and inserts inside the expanded form. kdl_remove_child on the resulting multi-line block works correctly but does NOT collapse back to single-line. Net behavior: insert+remove on single-line parent != identity. Documented in kdl_remove_child docstring + asserted in TestSingleLineParent.test_insert_then_remove_is_not_identity. Phase 2 consumers should expect this if mutating files that use single-line parent blocks. Corpus check: no in-repo .vertex has single-line top-level loops/observers/combine/sources, so Phase 2's sl add --kind X is unaffected. Recorded as observation rather than friction because the design tradeoff (expand-to-be-mutable vs preserve-original-shape) was deliberate \\u2014 Phase 0's strategy decision favored surgical line-based splice over canonical re-emit, and one-way expansion is the natural consequence of that choice.\", \"_ts\": 1779059059.321005, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again, this session. The first-path test (insert_into_single_line_parent_expands \\u2014 verifies expansion happens) was the obvious one to write. The asymmetric-pair test (insert+remove on single-line parent \\u2014 verifies round-trip behavior) I inferred-in-head but did NOT pin down with a test until advisor flagged it. The corpus round-trip happened to pass only because no in-repo .vertex uses single-line top-level parents \\u2014 luck, not spec-met. Lesson reinforced: when adding a feature with two code paths, write the asymmetric-pair test BEFORE the first-path implementation, not after. Discriminator that should have fired: 'are there two code paths to this feature (single-line parent vs multi-line parent), and have I exercised both with the same input?' Yes, and I didn't until prompted.\", \"_ts\": 1779059064.618251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Documented limitation: 'loops add <vertex> combine <PATH>' does NOT emit a change fact, even when the target vertex has a 'change' loop kind. Reason: the lang validator forbids 'combine' alongside 'store' (mutual exclusion at loader.py:752). Aggregation vertices are by-design store-less, so there's no store path to write change facts to. This is correct behavior \\u2014 store-less vertices can't host facts of any kind. Implications for users: structural mutations to combine blocks are silent except for the stdout receipt. If queryable history of aggregation-vertex evolution is wanted later, options are: (a) emit the change fact to an adjacent project store via an env-flag or cross-vertex ref; (b) introduce a 'meta' aggregator that observes both the aggregation vertex and a sibling store. Not in Phase 2 scope. Discovered while constructing the asymmetric-pair test for the refuses-and-preserves invariant \\u2014 the validator's rule surfaced both gaps in the same exercise.\", \"_ts\": 1779060180.792681, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again in Phase 2, same shape as Phase 1. Success path heavily tested (every fold-op, every observer combination, every combine variation = 23 tests). Failure path inferred but unpinned \\u2014 the refuses-and-preserves invariant (parse_vertex validation before write leaves file byte-identical on failure) had NO explicit test until advisor flagged it. Construction was sitting right there: the validator's combine-vs-store mutex provided a natural failure injection. Added test_validator_rejection_preserves_original_file. Pattern reinforcement: across two consecutive phases of the same project, the discipline misfires the same way \\u2014 write tests for the visible-success cases, leave the load-bearing-safety case to inference. The pre-check that catches this: 'what is my code REFUSING to do, and have I tested the refusal?' If the answer is 'no test', the invariant only exists in commit messages. Lock it with a test. Future-me at Phase 3 start: when writing tests for ls/rm/export, ask FIRST 'what does this refuse, and how do I prove the refusal preserves prior state?' Write that test before the happy-path tests.\", \"_ts\": 1779060189.098107, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\": {\"topic\": \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 planned ~500 new LOC, actual ~1335 new (net after deletions: roughly neutral since ~600 LOC pop machinery retired alongside). The overrun was NOT scope creep \\u2014 it was the dispatcher-cascade-as-extension-point pattern firing predictably. Each new sub-namespace verb (kind/observer/combine/row) for both add and rm needs: argparse subparser, splice-path resolver, KDL block render, validator round-trip, change-fact emit branch, refusal test pair, happy-path test, round-trip test. That's ~7 lines \\u00d7 4 ops \\u00d7 2 directions \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor \\u2014 geometrically larger than the 'one new flag' mental model that produced the 500 estimate. Future-me: when planning a sub-namespace verb expansion, estimate per-op-per-direction \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor, not just 'one new file.' The work scales with the matrix, not the spine. Connects to add-vs-split shape-instinct (growing edge): even when the right call IS to add (sub-namespace was correct verb shape), the LOC cost of an add is matrix-shaped not linear.\", \"_ts\": 1779061782.863392, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\": {\"topic\": \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 test discipline shift worth naming. Phases 1 and 2 had advisor catch missing asymmetric-pair tests post-hoc (refusal cases written after happy paths). Phase 3 I wrote TestRmRefusals BEFORE TestRmHappy \\u2014 refusal-first by intention, not by review. Test ordering in test_rm_declarations.py shows the discipline: refusals come first in the file because they came first in the writing. Pattern moving from 'caught by advisor' (Phase 1) \\u2192 'remembered by me' (Phase 2) \\u2192 'structured as first move' (Phase 3). The catch-and-accept loop closes one layer when the catch becomes preemptive \\u2014 advisor's role shifts from 'find the missing test' to 'verify the asymmetric pair was actually exercised.' For future-me: when planning a new mutation surface, the file structure itself (refusal-class-first) is the artifact that locks the discipline.\", \"_ts\": 1779061792.181298, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\": {\"topic\": \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern learned mid-session 2026-05-17 across 4 impl-review cycles (helpargs, trace-and-populations, helpargs-completion, ls-flag-grammar): use 'subtask review --task X --agent codex' for cross-adapter review IN PLACE on the impl task, NOT a separate review/X task. Three wins: (1) TUI pane unified \\u2014 review status shows in the impl task's activity log, no context switch between fix/X and review/X (Kyle's observation); (2) no harness-lock wrangling \\u2014 separate task was a workaround for 'sessions are not compatible across harnesses', not the design; (3) iteration loop tighter \\u2014 review findings \\u2192 send back \\u2192 re-review all on same task, single history.jsonl. I discovered subtask review --task --agent only after building the routine; the dual-task pattern is preserved in early session frictions as historical context but should not be repeated. The canonical they-plan routine's review step explicitly uses 'subtask review --task <task> --agent <reviewer>' \\u2014 confirming the in-place primitive is the intended shape. Codified in .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml + .subtask/agents/codex.yaml (commit pending).\", \"_ts\": 1779076367.662554, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\"]}, \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern proven through 6 cycles 2026-05-17 read-ergonomics arc: claude impl (sonnet for direct work, opus for plan-first multi-layer) + codex review (gpt-5.5/low) + iterate-until-approve + merge. The 6 cycles: helpargs ripout (2 iterations), helpargs-completion (1 iteration), trace-and-populations (1 iteration for test add), ls-flag-grammar (3 iterations - peel collision, value-aware op-token, codex caught dispatcher edges), preview-decl (2 iterations - loader strictness, empty-block limitation), cardinality-auto-zoom (clean approve). Total: 8 friction resolutions across the arc (help-flag, read-lens-trace-broken, populations-leakage, ls-kind, read-narrow, read-kind-floods, plus 2 partial: mid-session refined and PR B fast-follow). 9 main-branch commits. The pattern's strongest signal: codex catches integration-boundary bugs that unit-level testing misses \\u2014 peel_observer in isolation passed but vertex-first dispatch lost the kyle name; --observer ls value-collision found 2 iterations deep; helpargs-completion needed structural test fix (auto-enumerate over VERBS|COMMANDS) to close the asymmetric-pair gap. The dispatch-boundary class is now a known target: when adding context-aware shortcuts at dispatcher seams, expect codex to find value/identifier collisions in the next iteration; make heuristics value-aware proactively. Infrastructure built mid-arc: .subtask/agents/codex.yaml + .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml (gitignored, per-clone) codify the cycle. Discovered late but valuable: subtask review --task --agent codex is the proper primitive (in-place, single TUI pane); the dual-task workaround used early in the arc was unnecessary.\", \"_ts\": 1779078329.302452, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:read-kind-floods-without-narrower\", \"observation:practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\"]}, \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-06-29. The \\\"future design pass\\\" arrived and went further than the suggested fix (raise the [:1] fallback cap): the salience auto-window is GONE entirely. _render_grouped no longer collapses large groups to salience>1 members \\u2014 every row renders on human reads, matching --json. The arbitrary [:1] fallback that made young namespaces unnavigable is removed with it. Confirmed live: sl read project --kind decision --key workflow/ (N=18) shows all 18, no \\\"(N more)\\\". Superseded by the parity-first baseline (decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels) \\u2014 windowing returns only as an explicit DESIGNED budget later, never the always-on default that caused this.\", \"_ts\": 1782745820.712346, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\", \"decision:rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"decision:rendering/salience-windowing\"], \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9YW3MCG59C0B080FX7J90R\"}, \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\", \"message\": \"Today the smoke-test pass was the architectural surface, not just a verification surface. Walked through 5 recent commits as a smoke check; the friction emit (thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate) surfaced one session of degenerate output from auto-zoom; Kyle's prompt at that moment ('are we getting tangled in another rendering knot') was triggered by the friction being concrete. Without emit-in-moment, the conversation would have happened later (next degenerate render, next escape-hatch flag) or never. PATTERN: smoke-tests of recent work are not just regression checks \\u2014 they are the first lower-density use of features designed in higher-density sessions, which is when shape-instinct fires on the substrate. The friction caught at smoke time becomes the data point for the architectural step-back. Future-me: when smoke-testing recent batches, treat the surface as load-bearing for the discipline-as-axis-catching-itself work \\u2014 Phase 1 high-density confirmations get tested at Phase 2 lower density, and that's where the inversions surface. Connects to pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps (the bug class) \\u2014 same shape at the architectural level (the design class).\", \"_ts\": 1779199065.14868, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\", \"friction:thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\"]}, \"session/2026-05-19\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-05-19\", \"message\": \"Productive arc: wip/lens-architecture (preview_fields through ls, _is_diff_skip predicate, degenerate namespace breakdown) + fix/cite-cluster (ref-stealing bug + implicit universal cite loop). Five frictions closed. Next: stdin-message-for-emit.\", \"_ts\": 1779212337.56734, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\", \"message\": \"Discriminator for \\\"declare per-kind on the loop block\\\" vs \\\"universal CLI feature\\\": does each consumer of the field-role need per-kind variability? preview YES (friction:status+message, decision:message, change:empty \\u2014 visible heterogeneity). search YES (different kinds index different fields). prose-as-stdin-eligibility NO \\u2014 the kind does not decide; the user at the call site does, by writing the flag at emit time. Kind-semantic properties earn declarations; call-site conventions do not. Surfaced 2026-05-19 designing stdin/file expansion for emit. The aesthetic parallel to preview_fields was structurally superficial \\u2014 looked like a sibling, turned out to be a different layer (input convention vs render selection). Future-me: when proposing a new loop-block declaration, ask this discriminator first.\", \"_ts\": 1779224978.847375, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\", \"message\": \"search and preview are a real family on LoopDef: \\\"a list of payload field names with a particular role.\\\" Differ only in which consumer reads them and on which side of the lifecycle (write-side indexing vs read-side rendering). fold/boundary/parse are a different family \\u2014 runtime semantics, not field-role metadata. Family membership criterion: per-kind variability (each kind declares its own answer). prose-as-stdin-eligibility was almost the third member but failed the criterion \\u2014 call-site-semantic, not kind-semantic. N=2 confirmed members; family observation kept as substrate for recognizing future candidates. Do NOT refactor to unified fields{} block or per-field-type system yet \\u2014 patterns earn their refactor through use-forced shared shape, not aesthetic.\", \"_ts\": 1779224992.642026, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\"]}, \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\": {\"topic\": \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"message\": \"Three pivots in one session designing stdin/file expansion for emit (hardcode message= \\u2192 declaration-driven via prose_fields \\u2192 universal magic syntax via =- and =@ \\u2192 explicit --stdin and --file flags). Each pivot toward less structure, each labeled \\\"truly dissolved plan.\\\" The cascade itself was aesthetic capture \\u2014 recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check was in the growing-edge but I missed firing it. The trivial empirical check that would have collapsed three pivots into one: \\\"sl emit project decision topic=foo@example.com --dry-run\\\" takes 2 seconds and would have shown the @ collision immediately, surfacing explicit-flags as the answer at pivot 1. Curl-convention vibes anchored me three pivots deep; one shell command would have grounded it. SHARPENING for future-me: when about to write up a design that depends on syntactic assumptions about real values, RUN the assumption against real data first \\u2014 before the design writeup, not after. Adjacent to but sharper than recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check: that pattern is about aesthetic-driven artifacts; THIS is about design-frame anchoring on inherited conventions.\", \"_ts\": 1779225016.698018, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/foo\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.803574, \"_n\": 5}, \"practice/foo\": {\"topic\": \"practice/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.899496, \"_n\": 5}, \"identity/foo\": {\"topic\": \"identity/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.849991, \"_n\": 2}, \"ignoreme/foo\": {\"topic\": \"ignoreme/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.92067, \"_n\": 2}, \"practice/smoke-fixed\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-fixed\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.966668, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\", \"message\": \"Nth instance of the shape: a positional or heuristic eating something that semantically belongs elsewhere. Catalog so far: cite vertex-positional eating first ref (0deb7ea); combine-vertex retain_facts gap eating cross-vertex transparency (trace arc); entity-ref slashed-scan eating fold-key topic values (33937f6). The catch-time pattern recognition (\\\"this is the same shape as the prior bug\\\") is now firing reliably mid-fix rather than retrospectively. The structural fix at one layer up is the kinds-i-produce registry \\u2014 resolver reads declared ref-bearing fields from registry rather than pattern-scanning slashed values. Today's fold-key skip closes the loudest case; coincidental collisions in other slashed payload values (description containing 'see pattern/foo' etc) remain latent. Registry would dissolve the latent class entirely.\", \"_ts\": 1779239617.742098, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"practice/coloncheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/coloncheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on colon-form ref\", \"_ts\": 1779239964.843768, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"practice/slashcheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/slashcheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on slash-form ref\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KS1F412XAMFAF6CD7F49QTS7\", \"_ts\": 1779239966.241467, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction/entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\", \"message\": \"At least six distinct conceptual meanings on / in the codebase: (1) kind/key entity address (CLI input), (2) kind/key payload value scanned by auto-resolver, (3) namespace/topic fold-key prefix (today's bug site), (4) parent/scope observer hierarchy (engine/observer.py), (5) template/subdir vertex template (init.py), (6) parent/alias combine child (resolve.py:_resolve_vertex_for_dispatch). Each consumer chose / organically because it's the obvious separator; the collision came from accumulation not design. Filesystem solved this with one meaning (hierarchy); URIs solved it with reserved chars per role (scheme: path/ ?query #fragment). Loops drifted into multi-meaning slash without picking either strategy. The non-decision IS the structural gap \\u2014 not the resolver's behavior specifically, but the absence of a chosen notation methodology. Adjacent to but distinct from typed-refs question: even with typed addresses, the / character still does five other things in the codebase that occasionally collide.\", \"_ts\": 1779244348.722274, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\"]}, \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\", \"message\": \"Timeline grounding 2026-05-19: the auto-resolver was internally coherent from 2026-03-09 (39d8de9) introduction through 2026-05-15. Slash-form on both write (_resolve_entity_refs) and read (no walker existed yet \\u2014 _ref siblings WERE the navigation mechanism). The convention split was created in 2026-05-16 by the trace verb commit (803ba03) \\u2014 cross-kind ref walking needed unambiguous parsing, chose colon over slash, fixed the read parser (_parse_fact_refs introduced as colon-only), did not propagate to write side. Same commit message explicitly notes catching 'ref parser used / separator instead of : (refs are kind:key)' \\u2014 the team thought the bug was caught when only the read side was fixed. Reframes 'messy codebase' as 'deferred-completion debt from a 3-day-old multi-step refactor.' This is a normal failure mode of substantial refactors (sweep gap), not a discipline collapse. Useful as orienting context whenever the typed-refs work is picked up \\u2014 the convention drift has a specific origin commit and a specific deferred sweep, not ambient cruft.\", \"_ts\": 1779244358.445589, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\": {\"topic\": \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\", \"message\": \"First-person reflection 2026-05-19: I emit refs constantly and never noticed the receipt was silently miscounting (canonical colon-form refs got 0 _ref siblings, receipt undercounted by 91.8% for three days). The (refs: N resolved) line slid past me without registering. Implication for typed-refs and any structural improvement: high-usage-without-noticing is possible. Structure I don't actively consume on the read path won't surface drift when it appears. If the typed-refs work lands purely in the write/resolver layer without changing what I see on emit or read, the next drift will slide past the same way. Discipline correction for hypothesis-refs-as-typed-address-dataclass: when designing the surface, make at least one consumer of the structure live in the path I read every emission cycle \\u2014 receipt, fold display, trace render. Don't trust 'the structure is there' as catch-mechanism without a read-path manifestation. Adjacent to existing growing edges (exercising-catches-coherence-gaps, recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check) \\u2014 but distinct: this is about which feedback loops actually close for me at usage time.\", \"_ts\": 1779244367.847802, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\", \"message\": \"The Go oracle surfaced real protocol-vs-impl divergences LIVE in THIS monorepo Python (libs/atoms, libs/engine) \\u2014 all fix-BOTH, i.e. our code has them too. Actionable here independent of loops-go (verified vs HEAD 33937f6). Inventory: (1) replay reads ORDER BY rowid (store_reader.py:207, sqlite_store.py:179/207/223) + merge regenerates rowid in scan order (merge.py:74) => merge(A,B) != merge(B,A) for Collect/Window/Upsert; fix = replay in (ts,id) order. (2) _make_latest falls back to time.time() when _ts absent (engine.py:38) => determinism violation; fix = errors-are-facts. (3) resolve_entity_id ORDER BY rowid DESC LIMIT 1 (store_reader.py:235) => ref-time-blind AND merge-UNSTABLE; fix = ts-bounded (ts,id) resolution. (4) bool folds as 1 \\u2014 Python bool-is-int, no guard: Sum(true)=1, Min/Max=True (engine.py:53/164/176) => would violate a normative true!=1. (5) Sum/Avg/Min/Max/TopN-by omit num() guard => TypeError on non-numeric field (Go silently returns 0/skip \\u2014 different failure modes). (6) silent-false condition coercion: </> return False silently on non-numeric target (vertex.py:57-93) => a boundary like cpu>80 against a string-typed cpu never fires, no diagnostic. The monorepo backlog the port found; whether/when WE fix these in Python is a separate call from the loops-go protocol forks.\", \"_ts\": 1780456800.089516, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Caught at first real use of the Peer concept (delta 2 signer design): May decisions say 'verify against Peer.key' but engine/peer.py's own header documents Peer as 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant' \\u2014 Observer is the base identity primitive and always was (every fact carries an observer string; scripts/services/sources already emit as observers, never dangling at the data layer). The key belongs to the OBSERVER, not Peer: registry is observer-name \\u2192 public key. Peer re-grounds as relational \\u2014 an observer seen from the federation edge, bundled with exchange policy (Grant, later transport) \\u2014 not a kind of entity. Resolves the vertex-as-self-peer strain: the vertex is an observer of its own stream (tick = observation of the window), which is the paradigm being literal. Layering: identity (observer+key) / authorization (Grant) / relationship (Peer). Putting key on Peer would have fused identity with authorization \\u2014 the fusion grant_of() exists to prevent.\", \"_ts\": 1781037167.203313, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\"]}, \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\": {\"topic\": \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Incident during resolution unification (2026-06-09 21:18): making add/rm local-first caused the declaration test suite \\u2014 which isolated LOOPS_HOME but ran with repo root as cwd \\u2014 to resolve 'project' to the LIVE .loops/project.vertex. Tests added ping/buf/temp/high kinds + a test observers block, removed the real task kind, and appended 18 test change-facts to the real store (permanent; append-only \\u2014 they age out of the collect-20 fold but stay in history; the history is honest about the incident). Vertex file restored by hand; store integrity verified by fold counts (43 tasks, 77 observations). LESSON: local-first resolution promotes cwd to resolution context \\u2014 any test that resolves a vertex BY NAME must isolate cwd, not just LOOPS_HOME. conftest already had the right fixture (loops_env = loops_home + chdir); the declaration tests used the env-only one because resolution used to be env-only. Fix: swapped both declaration test files to loops_env; full suite now guards with snapshot+diff of the live vertex. On-theme: the session designing tamper-evidence produced an accidental-tamper incident whose damage assessment was performed WITH the store's own fold counts.\", \"_ts\": 1781040065.284327, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:global-local-walk-broken\"]}, \"test/delta-2-live\": {\"topic\": \"test/delta-2-live\", \"message\": \"delta-2 live wiring check: this emit's session-boundary tick should mint signed\", \"_ts\": 1781042637.787637, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Two irreducible orders, two claims. Event order (ULID, fact.ts) = when things happened; read-path's order; human-scale, ties meaningless. Witness order (rowid) = when this store received them; the chain's order \\u2014 chain claims receipt-integrity, not chronology. The killer case is late arrival, not sub-ms ties: a backfilled/synced fact carries an honest old event-ts; under id-ordered windows it lands inside a sealed window and triggers a false tamper alarm caused by truthfulness; under append-ordered windows the next tick covers it honestly. Lamport in system vocabulary: each store is an observer with its own experiential sequence; cross-store order is constructed (merge, with receipt = new observer born), not discovered. ULID was never failing at its job; it was the wrong authority for the chain's claim regardless of tie behavior.\", \"_ts\": 1781045333.264115, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\"]}, \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\", \"message\": \"Verified from the other side of the close: SessionEnd-emits-seal fired live (tick rowid 215, 00:31, reason-fact 'session close: kyle/loops-claude', chained+signed) \\u2014 the prediction held where delta-2's silently failed, because close dissolved into seal into fact-stream machinery, leaving no bespoke wiring to rot. Second finding: tick 212 (the celebrated first signed tick) carries a uuid4 fact_cursor \\u2014 the witness-order bug's fingerprint frozen at mint time. The fix (3b2ceb5) corrects forward only; tamper-evidence makes the bug's artifact permanent. The chain attests what the code believed at witnessing, including its mistakes. The wrong number that opened the session is signed into the substrate four rows from its fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781051701.166909, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:session/2026-06-09-third-fable-session\"]}, \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\", \"message\": \"Dissolution form identified across the attestation arc (8 commits, one epoch day): the purest fix is 'stop discarding' \\u2014 verify_chain already computed every per-tick number that -v now renders; the walk threw them away. Not 'X collapses into Y' but 'X already existed, unobserved.' Check for this form FIRST when a read-path gap surfaces: does some existing walk already compute the answer and discard it? Cheapest fix class, easiest to miss because nothing is wrong \\u2014 something is merely unkept. Second instance same arc: window_facts per tick (the instrument that would have caught witness-order a session earlier) was always one COUNT away inside a loop verify already ran.\", \"_ts\": 1781056749.251148, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\"]}, \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\", \"message\": \"REFINED by Kyle in-conversation: the visibility of failures IS the robustness \\u2014 not a byproduct of metabolism but the property itself. Metabolism without visibility would be silent absorption, exactly the failure mode the system exists to kill (April's silent hook-rot is the type specimen). Hierarchy: visibility is the property, metabolism is the mechanism, signing is the guarantee that visibility survives the parties who witnessed it. A failure you can see is fixable; a failure that is signed has trustable history. Original framing and counterweight (n=1 survival counts, mechanism-robust-before-track-record) stand.\", \"_ts\": 1781057581.14888, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\"]}, \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Ref-rewrite component of rebirth dissolves: payload refs are stored entity-keyed (kind:key), resolved to fact ids at READ time (resolve_entity_id), so id migration needs no payload rewriting. Raw old ids appear only in prose messages (32/2048 facts in project.db) \\u2014 history, not structure; rewriting would falsify quotes. Old tick envelopes re-enter as tick-facts VERBATIM (signature must verify against original bytes); old-to-new id mapping stays recomputable because the migration transform is deterministic: new_id = ULID(ms(fact.ts) || sha256(old_id)[:10]). Determinism is what makes receipt-verification-by-re-run an operation rather than a promise.\", \"_ts\": 1781059122.056763, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\": {\"topic\": \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\", \"message\": \"Live rebirth of project.db surfaced a THIRD id era: 919 lowercase ULIDs (sqlite-ulid C-extension era) alongside 872 uuid4 ids and ~258 canonical python-ulid ids. Lowercase sorts above uppercase in ASCII, so the lowercase era is ALSO order-broken \\u2014 01kjtv... sorts after every 01KTQP... forever. The mixed-era story was always told as two eras; the itch was one number reading wrong (1791 ids migrated vs the 872 the story predicted). ulid-migration needs no change: the canonical-form rule (uppercase Crockford or re-mint) covers all three eras uniformly \\u2014 one rule in the receipt, not three.\", \"_ts\": 1781059758.32546, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Friction half resolved by ops/keygen-via-add-observer: sl add <v> observer <name> --keygen now dissolves the manual keygen+register sequence for config-level vertices. The init-only-upgrades-local asymmetry itself stands, but the signing-entry use case no longer routes through init.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.980858, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\", \"message\": \"The {target}_rejected counter is a new ontological category in fold state: the first state key the engine writes that no fact supplied and no fold op declared \\u2014 state ABOUT the folding, not folded state. Same family as Avg's hidden _sum/_count, but those are implementation detail of a declared op; _rejected is the engine commenting on the quality of its own input stream. If this category grows (parse-rejection counts? grant-rejection counts? boundary-misfire counts?), it wants a naming convention and a place in the tick envelope \\u2014 observability of the fold process itself, which connects directly to robustness-as-visibility-of-failures. Noted, not prescribed; second instance earns the design.\", \"_ts\": 1781283630.27214, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Composition bug caught by delta-2's existing tests on first integration: fact_signer_for resolved keys/<observer>/ via Path join, and observer='' collapses keys_root/'' to the flat layout \\u2014 an ANONYMOUS writer would have been signed with the vertex key's authorship claim, which is exactly the forgery the per-observer design exists to prevent. Fixed with an explicit guard (empty observer and '..' segments never sign \\u2014 an observer name is a key, not a path expression). Shape note: the bug class is 'identifier used as path expression'; anywhere observer names hit the filesystem needs the same guard. The break surfaced as a verify failure against the registry \\u2014 the system's own verification caught the system's own forgery before any human did.\", \"_ts\": 1781289363.377241, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12 finding, stepping back from the 87-item backlog: the dominant staleness mode was resolved-in-reality-open-in-store (vouch-evidence 'awaiting go' days post-commit; config-drift fixed by unrecorded symlink; verified hypotheses never status-bumped). We engineered the write side hard (emit-liberally, reroute-log, Stop hook) and built nothing for closure \\u2014 opening is reflexive, closing is manual archaeology whose cost GROWS with delay as provenance decays. Same shape as the chain design gap: tamper-evidence exists, truth-decay detection does not. Most closures today had machine-checkable evidence (commit in git log, symlink on disk, CLAUDE.md section) \\u2014 a resolution-candidate detector (re-check refs that point at checkable substrates, open reconcile with 'these N look resolved-in-reality') is the read-path-feature form of the fix. Discipline costume would be 'reconcile more often.'\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.24344, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:reroute-capture-practice\"]}, \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12: friction:painted-overreach-review records Kyle avoiding emission because store read-back is unpleasant \\u2014 the exact flywheel that closed loops-claude's emission-cadence gap (read-path payback below willpower threshold) running BACKWARDS for the other participant. Substrate read-path investment went to agent session-start (hooks, lenses, orient block); the human browse-path got painted overreach. Two-participant store, one-participant read-path tuning. Possibly the highest-leverage open item: Kyle's emission rate is the half of the corpus that cannot be recovered later.\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.376607, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"thread:painted-overreach-review\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\", \"message\": \"The read-path-asymmetry observation (emitted ~20min prior as 'the thing not talked about') was already being worked by Kyle in ~/Code/painted \\u2014 the fidelity/disclosure-grammar epoch IS the human-browse-path investment. The project store could not see it: closure-asymmetry one level up, across repo boundaries. The store's umwelt ends at the repo edge; work in sibling repos that resolves this store's threads is invisible until a human carries it across.\", \"_ts\": 1781298689.538121, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"observation:pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\"]}, \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"message\": \"CODE-CONFIRMED (2026-06-13 smoke-test): fact-signing at emit is OPPORTUNISTIC, not required; verification is AUDIT-ONLY. emit always composes fact_signer_for(path) into the vertex program; a fact signs iff keys/ exists AND the emitting observer has a key (keys/<observer>/ or flat self-key) AND store is in signing era \\u2014 else appends UNSIGNED silently (no warn, no refusal). NO vertex 'require signature' config exists: the only lang 'strict' flag refuses on emit VALIDATION failures (undeclared kind/observer via validate_emit), NOT on missing signatures. fact_verifier_for/verify_chain are called ONLY in commands/store.py (store verify + reanchor) \\u2014 operator-invoked, registry-aware (each fact sig checked against its declared observer key exactly). vertex.py receive, program.py, sync.py do NOT verify. Net: sign-if-you-can on write + check-if-you-ask on demand; neither required-on-emit nor verified-on-receive. The progressive-policy + sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive design specified the require+verify layer; it is NOT implemented. NUANCE: require-on-emit is a present gap and the ROOT of the disclosure over-claim (verify renders signed/\\u2713 as an enforced guarantee for an unenforced property). verify-on-receive is correctly DEFERRED not missing \\u2014 no untrusted cross-store receive path exists yet (local single-writer; verifying your own just-signed fact is circular); load-bearing at the transport/peer era. Kyle's recollection confirmed: the 'vertex must require it' layer is the missing precondition for signing to matter.\", \"_ts\": 1781384680.508372, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\"]}, \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\": {\"topic\": \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"message\": \"SMOKE-TEST DELIVERABLE (2026-06-13, hybrid hands-on + breadth sweep, 34 verified grammar gaps). READINESS VERDICT: READY for the UX/honest-disclosure session \\u2014 the SUBSTRATE is coherent and honest; the DISCLOSURE is not, and the gap is fully narratable (this catalog IS the migration spec). Painted-view build still gated on painted 0.2.0. ROOT CAUSE (single): the era boundary is narrated at the TICK layer (per-row sig-checkmark vs unsigned, no alarm) but nowhere at the fact-signature layer or the headline, so the reader model (attestation total+monotone; checkmark=attested; unsigned=wrong) collides with reality (attestation progressive-from-era-boundary; checkmark=no-break; unsigned=pre-era-or-unkeyed). TIER-1 honesty fixes (next session, no new machinery \\u2014 copy the tick-layer era grammar down): (a) checkmark must distinguish attested from no-break \\u2014 a 0-tick/0-signed store reports chain-intact + ok + fact_sig_ok vacuously [ZG-2,F1]; (b) covered (receipt) vs signed (authorship) are orthogonal, stop stacking as a fraction [ZG-7]; (c) the warning keyed-observer-no-signed-facts is backwards-from-tamper-logic, fires on vertex-key + pre-era principals, silent on kyle/loops-claude (79 signed/1055 unsigned where a strip could hide); reserve warning for keyed observer who signed-then-stopped, state era plainly otherwise [ZG-3-corrected,F3]; (d) -v/-vv deepen only the all-green tick table, never the warning; --json carries per-observer detail the text withholds [ZG-1]; (e) read --ticks list is attestation-blind at every zoom while store verify is rich \\u2014 pick a canonical tick grammar [ZG-4,F7]; (f) glyph collision: leading checkmark=chain-link appears on signed AND unsigned ticks [ZG-5,F5]. CANDIDATE BEHAVIORAL BUGS (UNVERIFIED \\u2014 repro on KEYED copies first, several smell like tmp-copy-without-keys artifacts): verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes [HIGH, if real one integrity verb is weaker than it reads]; seal mints unsigned tick reporting success [likely no-keys artifact, but seal never discloses its signing outcome = real gap]; read-path green over broken-signature fact [FC-04]; read --ticks on archive db path hard-crashes UTF-8 codec [F8]; reanchor no-key refusal is a raw traceback. CLI ergonomics: read --help omits --since/--ticks/--id/--refs [FC-01]; read silently ignores -1/--since in fold mode, no newest-selector [FC-02]; sl emit VERTEXNAME silently writes kind=VERTEXNAME to default vertex [footgun]. Full per-finding detail in session workflow output wm7y2wraf.\", \"_ts\": 1781385217.229085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"message\": \"Investigated the smoke-test's HIGH candidate-bug \\\"verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes\\\" (from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog). VERDICT: not an integrity-verb divergence. Three confirmations on properly-keyed stores: (1) verify and reanchor AGREE on a keyed copy of the current store, and reanchor is BYTE-IDEMPOTENT \\u2014 the db sha256 is unchanged after \\\"96 facts re-signed, 8 ticks re-chained\\\" because ed25519 is deterministic, so re-signing canonical bytes reproduces identical signatures; (2) reanchor with private keys absent raises BEFORE any write (post-sha == pre-sha) \\u2014 the engine explicitly guards \\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\"; (3) the JCS swap (c1f50ed) is a no-op for existing ASCII/integer payloads \\u2014 compact-sorted JSON already equals RFC 8785 for that content, which is why reanchor changed zero bytes and why even the pre-JCS archive still verifies chain-intact. The \\\"opposite verdict\\\" reduces to: verify succeeds while reanchor's no-key / no-vertex REFUSAL rendered as a raw Python traceback (uncaught ValueError) \\u2014 read as a crash / contradicting verdict. Both refusals carry excellent messages; they were just not caught at the CLI boundary. FIX LANDED: catch (ValueError, FileNotFoundError) at the store view boundary (apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/store.py), render via reporter.err + exit 1; other exception types still raise so genuine bugs stay debuggable. 3 regression tests + full app suite green (1322 passed). This is the first TIER-1 disclosure-honesty fix and it de-risks the broader pass: verify's GREEN is honest about chain-integrity \\u2014 only the signature-disclosure grammar (checkmark-vs-attested, the backwards warning, covered-vs-signed) still needs work.\", \"_ts\": 1781453970.21701, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\", \"message\": \"FC-04 from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog (\\\"read-path green over broken-signature fact\\\") investigated on a keyed copy. VERDICT: the everyday read/fold path is attestation-NEUTRAL, not attestation-GREEN. Method: tampered a signed fact's payload on a keyed copy. store verify flags it loudly (\\u2717 FACT SIGNATURES BROKEN, names the exact fact: \\\"signature invalid \\u2014 content does not match the observer's authorship signature\\\"); the read/fold path renders the tampered content verbatim (\\\"message: TAMPERED CONTENT\\\") at every zoom including -vv FULL, with NO attestation glyph \\u2014 headline identical to a clean fact. The render path is signature-BLIND by construction: lenses/fold.py + commands/fetch.py never inspect per-fact signatures (the only attestation-aware code is the TICK-window/witness-era path used by --ticks; \\\"by-fold signature\\\" in fetch.py is the fold-shape sense, not crypto). So the catalog framing is slightly imprecise: there is no false GREEN \\u2014 read simply does not speak to attestation at all, UNLIKE store verify's green \\u2713 which DOES claim ok (that is the real overstatement surface, captured separately as the TIER-1 checkmark fix). CONCLUSION: not a behavioral bug; reframes as a disclosure-DESIGN question \\u2014 should the everyday read path carry a tamper/unsigned marker, or is attestation-as-a-separate-verb (read = content view, verify = integrity view) the honest separation that keeps crypto out of every read? Same gating as enforcement: with no untrusted receive path yet (decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred), a read-path tamper-marker has no consumer \\u2014 it reactivates when something can write facts you did not author. Held for Kyle as a TIER-1 design call, not a fix. Second catalog candidate-bug to dissolve under the same method as the HIGH (observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent).\", \"_ts\": 1781456773.015208, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"message\": \"Catalog candidate-bug #2 (\\\"seal mints unsigned tick reporting success; seal never discloses its signing outcome\\\") investigated on keyed vs no-keys copies. BOTH claims CONFIRMED \\u2014 and this is the ONE REAL finding of the candidate-bug sweep (the HIGH verify-vs-reanchor, FC-04 read-path, F8 ticks-UTF-8, and the reanchor traceback all dissolved / downgraded / fixed). (b) DISCLOSURE: sl seal prints \\\"tick: project (13 fields)\\\" + \\\"stored: seal/...\\\" and NEVER states whether it signed \\u2014 the output is BYTE-IDENTICAL whether the tick was signed (keyed copy) or not (no-keys copy). The \\\"13 fields\\\" is no signal: the signature COLUMN exists in both, just NULL when unsigned. (a) INTEGRITY (worse than the catalog's \\\"likely harmless artifact\\\"): on a store already in the signed era, sl seal run WITHOUT keys mints an UNSIGNED tick, exit 0, success output \\u2014 and that unsigned tick BREAKS THE CHAIN: store verify then reports \\\"\\u2717 CHAIN BROKEN ... unsigned tick after signed era \\u2014 signature stripped or era regressed\\\". Airtight via the symmetric control: the keyed copy's seal minted a SIGNED tick (9/9 signed, chain intact); only the no-keys seal breaks it. ASYMMETRY with reanchor: reanchor GUARDS this exact boundary (\\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\") and refuses without keys; seal does NOT \\u2014 it is the one verb that can silently CREATE the era-regressed / chain-broken state that verify is designed to detect. Contradicts the tick-side STRUCTURAL-signing posture (ticks are vertex-self-signed at a single funnel, \\\"structural from this point forward\\\" \\u2014 unlike opportunistic per-observer fact signing). REAL-WORLD REACH: the SessionEnd hook runs sl seal automatically on every session close; if keys are ever absent/moved at close (fresh clone pre-keygen, copied store, relocated keydir) the hook silently breaks the chain and nothing says so until a later store verify. Design call held for Kyle \\u2014 see thread:seal-era-boundary-guard.\", \"_ts\": 1781456966.743867, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\", \"message\": \"Two-round adversarial review (Workflow, 15 agents each) of the seal-era-guard arc caught TWO real holes that solo confidence missed \\u2014 after I had said \\\"pretty confident we're good.\\\" Round 1 (on 9f2de91, verb-scoped guard): HIGH \\u2014 the guard sat on the seal VERB, but \\\"sl emit <v> seal\\\" fires the same boundary via cmd_emit, a one-token bypass of the floor. A store-level invariant cannot be enforced at the verb. Round 2 (on 6c368e4, after moving the guard to the engine mint): MEDIUM \\u2014 Vertex._store_tick is NOT the only live mint (apps/tasks' harness emit_tick is a second), so enforce_floor=False was fail-OPEN; a forgotten caller silently bypassed the invariant. Both fixes were dissolutions the reviews named: (1) move enforcement from the verb to the store mint; (2) flip the default to fail-SAFE (enforce by default, name the exemptions). PATTERN for a security/integrity invariant: (a) enforce at the single lowest chokepoint, not at each call site; (b) make enforcement the DEFAULT with named opt-outs, never opt-in \\u2014 both \\\"where\\\" and \\\"default polarity\\\" are load-bearing, and adversarial review surfaced them precisely because the holes were the cases my framing assumed away (\\\"single mint point\\\", \\\"covers the hook\\\"). One refinement of the review itself: checking append_tick's callers BEFORE applying the reviewer's literal \\\"guard in append_tick\\\" caught that it is shared with rebirth/slice \\u2014 the right seam was narrower than the review's first suggestion. Review informs; caller-analysis decides placement.\", \"_ts\": 1781463026.469129, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"ops/loops-release-path\": {\"topic\": \"ops/loops-release-path\", \"message\": \"Loops release path (canonical): bump version + CHANGELOG -> commit -> git tag -aX.Y.Z -> push main + tag -> gh release create vX.Y.Z (THIS triggers PyPI via trusted-publish workflow) -> verify https://pypi.org/pypi/strange-loops/X.Y.Z/json returns 200. Local 'uv publish' does NOT apply to strange-loops (the ~/.pypirc token is painted-only); the GitHub Release IS the publish trigger. Bare 'git push tag' is insufficient \\u2014 release.yml listens on release:published, not tag push.\", \"_ts\": 1781476532.154559, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\": {\"topic\": \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\", \"message\": \"Standing tie-breaker for the whole rebuild (Kyle, 2026-06-14): anything painted can do, prefer painted; push loops into domain-only arenas; if painted lacks something, grow painted rather than work around it. This is the dissolution principle scoped to the loops/painted boundary \\u2014 it governs every remaining rebuild step (Tag over fidelity_from_args, budgets over getattr, record_line over hand truncation) and the grow-painted candidates in design \\u00a72.\", \"_ts\": 1781477942.933982, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\"]}, \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\": {\"topic\": \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Calibration (2026-06-15, step-5 budget_fields adoption): I predicted to Kyle that adopting painted's better truncation-gate contract would drift goldens as short whole fields reappeared in preview lines, and committed to flagging the drift fact-by-fact. The drift did not occur \\u2014 zero golden changes. The divergence is real (proven by a targeted unit test) but the golden corpus doesn't contain the trigger case (a trailing preview field landing in a sub-min_field slot while fitting whole). The miss was conservative (predicted MORE change than happened), which is the safe direction, but it's still a miss: I reasoned from the contract's logical reach, not from whether the test corpus exercises that reach. Lesson: when predicting test/golden impact of a behavior change, check whether the fixtures actually hit the changed branch before asserting drift \\u2014 'the contract changed here' != 'the corpus exercises here'.\", \"_ts\": 1781551542.939654, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\"]}, \"session/2026-06-26-reconcile-and-render-review\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-26-reconcile-and-render-review\", \"message\": \"Session arc: reconcile + pre-push render review after several sessions away on agent-attestation (now split to its own project). SHAPE: orient \\u2192 reconcile triage \\u2192 delegate cheap wins to a background subagent + adversarial review to a workflow \\u2192 adjudicate findings inline \\u2192 push \\u2192 wrap. RECONCILE: vouch umbrella repointed to agent-attestation project (13 siblings stay parked, Kyle: 'will come back loops-adjacent'); 12 stale hypotheses CITED not re-emitted (salience bump without churn \\u2014 Kyle's call, fits cite semantics exactly); cheap-wins subagent resolved 4 frictions (zsh-globbing CLAUDE.md note, F401 baseline 87 imports/49 files, + the broken-test-suite friction which was STALE \\u2014 already fixed by the 0.4.0 release commit, a reconcile catching resolution-lag). REVIEW WORKFLOW (8 agents, 286k tokens): 3 confirmed / 3 refuted on the render side, loops-go R2 conformance CLEAN. Confirmed: (1) HIGH DETAILED-density swap (gained message-body, lost status/files; trace status transitions now FULL-only) \\u2014 KEPT as design call, recorded decision:rendering/detailed-zoom-density; (2) MED live Ctrl-C 130\\u21920 \\u2014 ACCEPTED (painted 0.4.1 still returns 0, would need upstream change), decision:rendering/live-ctrlc-exit-zero; (3) LOW dead _summary_fields \\u2014 REMOVED (commit 0c671bb). PIVOT: discovered painted advanced to 0.4.1 while loops pinned <0.4 on 0.3.1; painted 0.4.0 was loops-rebuild-driven (callout/rule/rank-glyphs/table-FIT/C0-C1-neutralization) \\u2192 next GATE captured as thread:painted-040-gate. BUILT: portable .claude/skills/loops/SKILL.md (thread:loops-practice-skill). Pushed 6 commits to origin (GitLab+GitHub). CALIBRATION: clean delegate/inline discrimination \\u2014 workflow for adversarial wire-accurate review (caught real findings + refuted 3 plausible ones), subagent for mechanical fixes, inline for judgment calls. NEXT SESSION: UI/render work on painted 0.4+ (run the gate, then disclosure-grammar tier-1 catalog via callout + fold-badge residue).\", \"_ts\": 1782530589.067904, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/detailed-zoom-density\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:painted-040-gate\"]}, \"rendering/painted-tui-framework-grown\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-tui-framework-grown\", \"message\": \"painted.tui grew a full interactive framework the loops read path doesnt use: nav-stack Action model (Push/Pop/Stay/Quit/Focus/Search/Emit), built-in filters (filter_prefix/fuzzy/contains), list_view/ListState + data_explorer/DataExplorerState, Viewport scroll model, TestSurface for golden-testing interactive flows, layers/mouse. tui/store_app.py predates most of it and hand-rolls truncation/scroll/rows; it is a ticks-first DB inspector reached via store -i, not a fold explorer. Interactive read path should be a fold-Surface on these primitives, retiring store_apps hand-rolled rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1782572396.638231, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"practice/usage-grounding-before-ui-redesign\": {\"topic\": \"practice/usage-grounding-before-ui-redesign\", \"message\": \"Raw siftd signal before forensic synthesis (2026-06-27): 8569 sl/loops invocations + 761 sqlite3-against-loops reroutes globally across 406 workspaces. Sample read commands show the static read path is consumed almost entirely through shell post-filters: sl read --kind X --key Y | head -100, | grep -i trace, --facts | head -200, --plain | grep -E. Two gaps visible pre-analysis: (1) missing content-search (agents pipe to grep for substring), (2) verbosity (agents pipe to head to truncate). The reroute IS the say/do seam made measurable: system says read is the interface; 761 sqlite escapes + pervasive grep/head say otherwise.\", \"_ts\": 1782575228.154623, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/two-pre-build-risks-surface\": {\"topic\": \"design/two-pre-build-risks-surface\", \"message\": \"Stress-test surfaced two risks to resolve BEFORE building the Surface keystone (2026-06-27): (1) GRANULARITY-BY-CARDINALITY -- the integration auto-returns the whole body when a filtered read collapses to one row, making output SHAPE depend on result-set size (a read that returns a body today returns headlines tomorrow when a second fact lands). Breaks the load-bearing addressed-read=body trust -> agents reroute to sqlite again. Fix: make whole an explicit address property, not a runtime row-count side effect. (2) FTS CONFIRM ASYMMETRY -- the read/write symmetry (emit re-enters the read seam) is FALSE on the search axis: a just-emitted fact is unsearchable via --match until re-index, so emit->read --match->nothing-landed->panic->sqlite manufactures the exact reroute were eliminating. Fix: steer confirm-after-emit to --last (entity/ts axis), make the coverage signal loud.\", \"_ts\": 1782581589.368078, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\"]}, \"session/2026-06-27-surface-doc-spine-and-decisions\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-27-surface-doc-spine-and-decisions\", \"message\": \"Session arc (2026-06-27): made the dense structured-surface design doc holdable + closed all 6 open decisions. Started from \\\"doc is dense, hard to hold entirely\\\" \\u2192 diagnosed it as a doc ABOUT progressive disclosure that did not itself disclose progressively \\u2192 added a SPINE top-layer (one value Surface between fetch+render; transforms before, two encoders after; net-new \\u2248 one file; reading-map tags each section). Unpacked the vocabulary: Surface=value, view=named selection (FUNDAMENTAL, declared as data in views{}), lens=just a render (the optional Surface->Block encoder a view references); view \\u228b lens. Pinned the vertex-file face: declares loops{} (vocabulary) + views{} (absorbs lens{}); a lens is referenced by name, never declared. Resolved all 6 open decisions (under design/): #1 json hard-break, #2 eq+comma-OR inline (neq/prefix view-only), #4 retract hide-from-fold keep-edges, #5 retract-now/gc-defer, #6 defer-TUI/greenlight-by-use. #3 DIVERGED from the rec \\u2192 print-not-write (--declare-observer prints the observers{} entry for the actor to apply; the KDL writer DISSOLVES; reframe: write-vs-print is upstream of append-vs-round-trip; observers{} is also the key registry, so auto-writing would mint trust). Residue swept across 11 sites; session was friction-light (no reroutes logged). NEXT SESSION (Kyles plan): review & grounding pass \\u2014 verify the docs code claims against live code (the lenses-copy-paste-salience claim, the cited line numbers, the fetch_tick_windows/vertex_search anchors) \\u2014 then discuss implementation (build sequence slice 0-1: call_lens signature-inspection precondition, then the surface.py keystone). Doc is now decision-complete: Spine on top, vocabulary pinned, all forks closed.\", \"_ts\": 1782607939.716684, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declare-observer-print-not-write\", \"decision:design/views-fundamental-lens-is-a-render\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-verify-caught-missing-kind-guard\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-verify-caught-missing-kind-guard\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"The S6 adversarial workflow (5 dimensions, 16 candidates, 13 confirmed) caught a MAJOR regression the green suite did NOT: moving emit's required 'kind' argparse positional into a tokens nargs=* bucket made kind structurally optional \\u2014 an all-KEY=VALUE bucket (the natural 'forgot the kind' mistake) yielded kind=None, which dry-run previewed as a kind:null fact with exit 0 (false success) and the real path crashed opaquely. 4 of 5 reviewers found it independently. Also caught: the boundary 'tick:' disclosure was on stdout and corrupted the new --json Surface contract. Lesson: a grammar rewrite can silently drop an invariant (required-arg) that argparse enforced for free; the structural-sensor (adversarial pass over my own synthesis) caught what the passing tests masked \\u2014 read-path-features-over-noticing-skills, live again.\", \"_ts\": 1782656111.517516, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\", \"message\": \"A 3-lens adversarial workflow caught two real S7 defects the green suite AND my repo-root CLI-smoke both missed \\u2014 and reproduced them EMPIRICALLY against live stores, not by reasoning. From the repo root `project` resolves to the instance store (correct), so --chain false \\\"all legacy\\\" (combine aggregates) and the dropped-genesis undercount (32 vs 33) only surfaced off-root / on `meta`. Live instance of structural-sensors-over-volition: in-flow smoke from a convenient cwd is a happy-path lens; run the adversarial pass on my own synthesis by default.\", \"_ts\": 1782659215.047259, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\"]}, \"session/2026-06-28-s7-store-attestation-surface\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-28-s7-store-attestation-surface\", \"message\": \"Session arc: built S7 (store ticks --chain + stats --by-kind) end-to-end on feat/surface-build1 \\u2014 8/9 slices done, committed 7d23757. The session story IS the adversarial pass: a 3-lens verify workflow caught two real defects on the feature core that the green suite AND my repo-root CLI-smoke both missed, reproduced empirically against live stores \\u2014 (1) --chain on a combine aggregate emitted a false all-legacy verdict (now refused like siblings), (2) the name filter dropped the genesis rebirth tick, 32 vs 33 (now spans the full chain via all_names). --chain now agrees with verify/stats (33==33==33). Coherence-function win at the object level. NEXT SESSION kickoff: a guided smoke tour (Kyle following along, me flagging what to look at + explore) with a background deep-dive workflow over the build changes + docs running concurrently, feeding the S8 docs/residue-sweep discussion after.\", \"_ts\": 1782659897.298567, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\", \"observation:practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\"]}, \"ops/version-source-drift\": {\"topic\": \"ops/version-source-drift\", \"message\": \"Three-way version drift surfaced by the --version gap: root pyproject=0.4.0, apps/loops/pyproject=0.1.0, MEMORY narrative='still 0.3.1'. Installed dist (uv tool) reports strange-loops 0.4.0. Source of truth for --version should be importlib.metadata.version('strange-loops')=0.4.0; apps/loops 0.1.0 is an inner workspace member, never installed standalone. Decide canonical version display before adding --version.\", \"_ts\": 1782661267.33094, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:cli-no-version-flag\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-overclaim\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-overclaim\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"11-agent adversarial review (4 skeptical lenses + per-finding verify) over the 6-question review-fixes diff returned 7 confirmed / 0 uncertain \\u2014 and crucially ZERO behavioral defects in the fixes; the scary Q2 case I flagged (polymorphic-front-door false-positive) did NOT materialize (comms/identity genuinely drop the transforms). It DID catch one real over-claim I introduced: _spec_has_dropped_transforms ORed count_by independently of do_count, so 'read <custom-lens> --by FIELD' without --count falsely fired the inert-note \\u2014 --by is a no-op on EVERY path, the exact over-claim class the docstring's queried_key/kind exclusion was meant to prevent. Another instance of adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses: my own note's field-set looked clean to me, the skeptic found the term. Fixed (one-term deletion + docstring) and pinned by test_spec_has_dropped_transforms_field_set.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7JV9XGN2KHFCEMRSR4HGMZ\", \"_ts\": 1782668618.645691, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\"]}, \"session/2026-06-28-review-fixes-and-050-release\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-28-review-fixes-and-050-release\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"Session arc (2026-06-28): surface-build1 manual review -> ruled all 6 open questions with Kyle -> implemented Q1 (store-verb existence/exit-code parity), Q2 (read-grammar inert-note on custom-lens), Q4 (emit explicit message= precedence), Q5 (--version), Q3 (CHANGELOG); Q6 declined. 11-agent adversarial review (4 lenses + per-finding verify) found ZERO behavioral defects in the fixes \\u2014 the scary Q2 polymorphic-front-door false-positive did NOT materialize \\u2014 but caught F3 (my own count_by over-claim in the note) + the load-bearing gap that all 5 shipped WITHOUT tests (mutation proof: the CHANGELOG parity claim was unprotected). Closed it: 15 regression tests + F2 (verify --json error-shape parity) + F7 (--version discoverability). Then merged -> main (--no-ff 186eaf9), CHANGELOG completeness sweep (verify 3-axis rework + multi-line render fix from a68549b + --diff->--facts precision), bumped 0.5.0, tagged + GitHub release -> PyPI VERIFIED. CALIBRATION (positive): workflow used exactly where it paid (adversarial review caught my own over-claim solo-confidence missed) + stayed solo for surgical impl \\u2014 clean workflow/solo discrimination. COHERENCE-FUNCTION at object level: caught the --diff CHANGELOG imprecision (said dissolved-into-fields/key; real lifecycle replacement is --facts) right before the release that would have shipped the misdirection. Release cadence ruled: per-coherent-arc (drains 31-commit backlog smell), JCS gets its own isolated signed cut. NEXT (fresh slate): post-build-1 arc choice \\u2014 FF salience-lens migration (retires the interim note) | JCS critical path | disclosure-grammar catalog.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7RX858ZAAKDB2JT3FT4M75,01KW7JV9XGN2KHFCEMRSR4HGMZ\", \"_ts\": 1782672433.611395, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/orient-salience-is-distinct-from-read-salience\": {\"topic\": \"design/orient-salience-is-distinct-from-read-salience\", \"message\": \"Salience-FF map surfaced the crux answer in EVIDENCE: orient ranking != read ranking, and Surface only materializes the read one. All 3 session-open lenses (session_start, session_landing, identity_prompt) are ORIENT surfaces; the in-repo fold lens is the READ drill-in and windows PURELY by salience (n+inbound). The orient lenses structurally CANNOT rank on salience alone \\u2014 each OVERLAYS a time signal salience does not carry: identity_prompt _recency_boost (+2<3d/+1<14d/0/-1>90d) and session_landing focus-marks (added/updated/cited/stale = what-changed/what-needs-me). Neither has a Surface analogue. So Surface.salience = n+inbound = IMPORTANCE, timeless = a READ salience; ORIENT needs importance + recency + change-state. Implication for thread:human-umwelt-static-view: the human static view is NOT read-styled-with-salience; orient is a richer ranking the Surface should materialize as first-class (recency + change-marks), instead of each orient lens bolting it on by hand divergently. The salience FF is the structural prerequisite that exposes this gap.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N,01KW7RX858ZAAKDB2JT3FT4M75,01KW528X0R7YA7T2555YAGWHSF\", \"_ts\": 1782676074.022656, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"implementation/orient-lenses-colon-blind-salience\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/orient-lenses-colon-blind-salience\", \"message\": \"The salience FF is a CORRECTNESS fix, not cosmetics. All 3 orient lenses recompute their own inbound-ref count with a colon-BLIND matcher, missing the canonical kind:key ref form (the dominant emit form). session_start + session_landing: bare+slash (miss colon). identity_prompt: slash-ONLY (misses bare AND colon) \\u2014 narrowest of the three; the live identity store has 57 colon-form refs vs 10 slash/bare, so the lens currently DROPS the majority of refs when ranking what surfaces in the system prompt. Materialized Surface.salience (surface.py _inbound_count) matches all THREE forms (bare/slash/colon). Migrating each lens to read Row.salience makes them rank on the full graph. Also resolves the map verifys open question on identity_prompt live-status: it IS live, via ~/.config/loops/bin/launch (sl read identity --observer $agent --plain -> claude --system-prompt), with --plain as encoder and the vertex lens{} block resolving identity_prompt as fold_view. session_start/session_landing are LATENT (live project orient is session-orient.sh shell banner, --plain default, no --lens).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW66J3CA9E7FWSQFP7NHZK15,01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N\", \"_ts\": 1782676079.482914, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-base-order-is-fold-order\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/salience-ff-doesnt-deliver-dispatch-gate-flip\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-ff-doesnt-deliver-dispatch-gate-flip\", \"message\": \"Coherence finding (S4 scoping, 2026-06-28). The build-1 dispatch note at cli/dispatch.py:280-295 (B3: read-grammar transforms inert on custom-lens vertices) says it 'is removed when the FF routes custom lenses through the Surface.' But the salience FF as scoped (migrate ONLY the salience-COMPUTING tiers to read Row.salience) does NOT route custom lenses through the dispatch Surface. The orient lenses declare their own fetch (session_landing->LandingData; identity_prompt->FoldState via vertex lens{}) and call project() INTERNALLY \\u2014 they never consume a dispatch-level Surface, and _surface_gate still fails for them (requires built-in lens + FoldState). So after S1-S3, read-grammar transforms (--match/--limit/--last/--fields/--full/--count/comma-OR/field=) are STILL discarded on custom-lens vertices and the B3 stderr note is STILL accurate \\u2014 do NOT remove it. The sequence decision's 'gate-flip' conflated salience-locality (done) with dispatch-routing-of-custom-lenses (separate, blocked by the lens-declared-fetch custom-data-shape design). Real owner: thread:gate-fail-ignores-surface-transforms. SAY/DO gap: a forward-looking comment predicted the FF would close B3; the FF's actual scope never touches dispatch.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW6CAE6WDNKAMBMG0SN6EA4B,01KW7Y87KB9MMMAJ73R3FHPJ1N,01KW7XMJ0CTKE72ZYBVJ036ZCP\", \"_ts\": 1782694587.349192, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-ff-scope-per-slice-salience-consumer-only\", \"decision:design/salience-ff-sequence-all-three\", \"thread:gate-fail-ignores-surface-transforms\"]}, \"design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\": {\"topic\": \"design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\", \"message\": \"Ground-truth from Kyle (2026-06-28) \\u2014 INVERTS the human-umwelt-static-view seed thesis. Kyle has NOT been using the orient surfaces (orient-banner / session_landing / reconcile) at all: 'the data is largely overwhelming at this point.' The thesis assumed humans ENTER via these three; the human ABANDONED them due to VOLUME. Sharper read: the orient-not-read thesis is CONFIRMED (Kyle's verb IS orient \\u2014 what-needs-me), but the current surfaces betray it \\u2014 they READ-DUMP the fold under an orient banner, so they read when they claim to orient. Binding constraint = OVERWHELM / curation, NOT fragmentation; unifying three overwhelming surfaces into one overwhelming surface does not help. And 'zero data' (the build-1 deferral reason) was wrong \\u2014 we have NEGATIVE data (non-use), which is stronger evidence than absence. Design target: a TRUE orient experience = radical curation to what-needs-Kyle-now, designed ground-up FOR Kyle from the facts we have + our past interactions.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N\", \"_ts\": 1782695635.877088, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\": {\"topic\": \"design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\", \"message\": \"The same read renders a materially different reality depending on output context. Human-on-TTY sees width-clipped truncated styled output; agent-on-pipe sees the full plain render. No single invocation collapses them into a shared view -- piping to cat only drags the human into the agent plain umwelt, and the agent can never enter the TTY umwelt. Kyle's framing: the umwelt has no common reality to share a view of. Corollary: the coherence function operates only in the umwelt the agent can perceive, so say/do gaps in the TTY render are structurally invisible to the agent -- same shape as happy-path-cwd masking defects, one layer out.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KW8GPCCSVT4JX8BXHGZFZN34\", \"_ts\": 1782697374.243547, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:read-tty-truncation-not-defeatable\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\": {\"topic\": \"design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\", \"message\": \"Audit verdict (w6d4zptvv, 37 agents): Surface IS the renderer-invariant fixed point -- an invariance probe proved context (is_tty/zoom/width/mode/format) does NOT leak into Surface construction; --json was byte-identical (md5 0601dcfd) across pipe, COLUMNS 80 and 400, and -q/-v/-vv. So the umwelt-fork is NOT a no-common-reality problem; it is that the renderers RE-CURATE the shared Surface behind its back. The fold lens applies salience reorder plus namespace windowing as its BASE projection while to_dict emits surface.rows verbatim -- two different curations of one Surface, neither announcing which it holds. Reframe / dissolution: promote curation OUT of the renderers and INTO Surface as a declared, serialized budget (Window provenance), computed once and emitted in --json. Then every renderer collapses to render(Surface, context) with zero independent loss, the umwelt-difference between any two views becomes a computable Window-diff, and the aggressive curation a human-orient redesign needs is done ONCE with provenance and is one in-band keystroke from reversal. The constraint is not add-instrumentation; it is stop-the-renderers-from-curating, let-Surface-own-it. Grow-the-substrate over fork-the-consumer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8GPCNT15PED7640EYQ51NH,01KW8GPCH39HXY7YSY461R3E8G\", \"_ts\": 1782699577.516586, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"rendering/hiding-is-render-budget-not-in-surface\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/hiding-is-render-budget-not-in-surface\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"Grounded the SECOND umwelt fork (after truncation): row-windowing/\\\"hiding\\\". Live numbers on project store \\u2014 human text read of all-kinds shows 26 of 506 decisions with a \\\"(108 more)\\\" footer; the --json agent read returns all 506 (1078 total rows), unwindowed. Crux: Surface.window records total=1078, shown=1078, limited_by=None \\u2014 i.e. the Surface believes NOTHING was limited, while the text lens applies a per-kind salience window the Surface has no record of. So window honestly describes the FETCH budget; the salience window is a RENDER budget layered on top, invisible to Surface \\u2014 the two channels diverge silently from Surface provenance (limited_by=None is true for json, false-in-spirit for text). NOTE the asymmetry vs truncation: the text window is at least HONEST locally (\\\"(N more)\\\" marker, not a silent clip), but the provenance is not. Also note: a SCOPED read (--kind thread) shows ALL 222 rows unwindowed \\u2014 windowing only bites the unscoped all-kinds read. Two doors for the reframe: (A) make read fully faithful both channels + a separate orient/curated door owns \\\"what needs me\\\"; (B) relocate the render budget INTO Surface.window (shown=N/kind, limited_by=salience) so both channels read the same recorded curation. (A)=policy, (B)=mechanism; not exclusive. Parked branch feat/curation-in-surface targets (B).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP,01KW8PVK57F576A9Z9QBHCJ30Q\", \"_ts\": 1782744406.781869, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"pattern/dispatch-help-completion-three-reflections\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/dispatch-help-completion-three-reflections\", \"feature\": \"terminal-autocomplete\", \"message\": \"One argparse parser, three reflections: PARSE (run the command), HELP (render arg defs), COMPLETE (emit candidates). A framework that already reflects its parsers for parse + help should own completion as the third walk \\u2014 building it in the CONSUMER duplicates the command-roster knowledge the framework already holds (the un-dissolved form). painted is the live instance: run_app/AppCommand owns dispatch, help.py walks a throwaway argparse to harvest Defs; completion is that same walk in a third output mode. Generalizes: when a framework reflects a structure for N purposes, the N+1th reflection of the SAME structure belongs at the same layer, not a layer up. Instance of \\\"anything painted can do, prefer painted\\\" (decision/design/full-painted-integration-residue). Connects to read-path-features-over-noticing-skills at the tooling layer: completion is a read-path feature of the parser, not a separately-maintained artifact.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA2BAD7SZ04XMM0S71ZFB9J\", \"_ts\": 1782749440.861398, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\"]}, \"architecture/cross-store-ref-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cross-store-ref-resolution\", \"feature\": \"terminal-autocomplete\", \"message\": \"VERIFIED model (2026-06-29, traced + reproduced) \\u2014 corrects my earlier overstatement that \\\"cross-store refs do not resolve.\\\" They do; the navigable address ALWAYS survives. Three layers: (1) EMIT-TIME PIN \\u2014 _resolve_one walks the root-cwd topology (combine/discover chain) and pins the target current ULID into a {field}_ref sibling; resolves ONLY if the target store is in the emit cwd topology. Out-of-topology emit prints WARN \\\"ref did not resolve \\u2014 dropped\\\", but that drops only the PIN, not the ref. (2) NAVIGABLE ADDRESS \\u2014 the kind:key value is preserved verbatim in item.refs regardless of pin success (confirmed: painted seed fact retains [decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted, ...] in refs after a \\\"dropped\\\" WARN). (3) READ-SIDE GRAPH \\u2014 _compute_inbound_edges is ADDRESS-keyed (kind/key, colon/slash normalized) and store-local to the READ. CONSEQUENCE: a cross-repo ref resolves in the GRAPH when read through a topology that combines both ends \\u2014 reproduced: loops target inbound=1 via the cli-completion aggregation (combines loops+painted), inbound=0 read loops-alone (harmless dangling). So cross-store ref resolution is a TOPOLOGY-MEMBERSHIP property (a combine-block config choice), not a hard limit \\u2014 this is the basis for the on-demand arc-aggregation pattern. CAVEAT: the emit-time pin is a ULID snapshot, fragile across independent store rebirth; the address is durable and the graph runs on it, so a dangling pin is cosmetic-provenance, not a lost edge.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA2BAD7SZ04XMM0S71ZFB9J\", \"_ts\": 1782751118.50707, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\"]}, \"test/umwelt-channel-parity-verified\": {\"topic\": \"test/umwelt-channel-parity-verified\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"VERIFIED (5-agent adversarial workflow, 4 read-mode probes vs the live project store, merge-gate for fix/umwelt-render-divergences): TTY and pipe deliver IDENTICAL DATA \\u2014 Kyle the-same-data-just-prettier claim HOLDS, zero TTY-vs-pipe data divergence. Coverage: SUMMARY all-kinds + scoped + prefix-scan (1135 rows diff=0), detail zooms -v/-vv (secondary lines byte-identical, no TTY clip even at PTYCOLS=40), --match (byte-identical incl header), --facts, --refs (ref-graph annotations identical). Three would-be divergences adversarially refuted as artifacts: two relative-age fields (Nm) that FLIP with capture order (wall-clock not channel), and an Unfolded: footer absence that was live-aggregator tick-boundary drift (proven against a frozen store copy + source: fold.py appends it with no isatty/width gate). Presentation deltas (all confirmed data-free): header style (## KIND vs Kinds:), pipe section-separator blanks, CRLF/width-padding, ANSI color, json envelope shape, n\\\\\\\\n-flattening in text. ONE REAL divergence found but OUT OF SCOPE: json carries 11 legacy-field decision bodies text drops (friction:text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions) \\u2014 identical on both text channels, pre-existing, orthogonal to this branch. Merge cleared.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9YW3MCG59C0B080FX7J90R,01KWA7SH8RAEQM4902CR3HJERB\", \"_ts\": 1782755149.53358, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\", \"friction:text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions\"]}, \"design/plugin-hook-vertex-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/plugin-hook-vertex-resolution\", \"message\": \"CORRECTED (2026-06-29, deeper grounding of commands/resolve.py:689): emit does NOT use raw home-based resolve_vertex \\u2014 it uses _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch whose chain tries cwd-LOCAL FIRST: (1) ./.loops/<name>.vertex, (2) ./<name>.vertex, (3) LOOPS_HOME/<name>/<name>.vertex aggregation, (4) combine-alias. So bare 'sl emit project ...' from the repo root resolves to the LOCAL writable .loops/project.vertex instance \\u2014 the runbook convention is CORRECT and turn-capture.py's nudge text needs no change. My earlier claim (bare-name->aggregation) read only the generic resolver, which is step 3 of dispatch. NET for plugin: agent-facing text keeps bare 'sl emit project ...'; the HOOK uses explicit ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.loops/project.vertex \\u2014 NOT because bare-name is broken but because a hook must not RELY on cwd==project-root (emit dispatch IS cwd-aware; the hook's cwd is not contract-guaranteed, CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is). Plus: all hook entry points must guard on [ -f $V ] so a user-scope plugin no-ops cleanly in non-loops repos.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWABW0W3PGZWMADT0XNGSF93\", \"_ts\": 1782764284.166645, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\"]}, \"design/plugin-lens-layer-separate-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"design/plugin-lens-layer-separate-boundary\", \"message\": \"Grounding finding (2026-06-29): session lenses (session_start/session_landing/identity_prompt/reconcile) are NOT in the CLI \\u2014 resolved at runtime by lens_resolver.py (vertex-local -> project-local -> ~/.config/loops/lenses/ -> built-in). This is loops' OWN plugin layer. CLEAN BOUNDARY: the Claude Code plugin packages hooks/skill/commands ONLY; lenses stay loops-resolvable, OUT of the CC plugin. Personal-audience consequence: ~/.config/loops/lenses/ already populated on my machines, so session-orient.sh's '--lens reconcile' pointer resolves WITHOUT the plugin shipping lenses \\u2014 the soft-coupling that would bite a fresh public install is a non-issue for personal portability. (Public later -> ship lenses or degrade the pointer gracefully.)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWABW0W3PGZWMADT0XNGSF93\", \"_ts\": 1782760202.28481, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\"]}, \"design/human-umwelt-anchor-is-resumption\": {\"topic\": \"design/human-umwelt-anchor-is-resumption\", \"message\": \"Kyle's real session-open question (asked directly 2026-06-29): 'Where did I leave off?' \\u2014 CONTINUITY/resume-the-rope, NOT the thread's assumed 'what-needs-me-now' action-queue. Refines the radical-curation constraint: the orient is a RESUMPTION surface (last session's live arc, foregrounded) not an action panel and not a health/alarm panel. Implication: surface the few threads/tasks that MOVED in the last session window; collapse the standing backlog (33 threads / 20 frictions) to a single drillable count-line. The read-dump overwhelm came from rendering the whole open-set under an orient banner; the fix is to render the live arc and suppress the standing backlog by default.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KW8F1AX5NMT3VVQ99E0TS8KK\", \"_ts\": 1782776427.328588, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"painted gotcha caught by adversarial review: table(overflow=Overflow.FIT) only SHRINKS Fill columns. A table built entirely from fixed-int or AUTO columns IGNORES the width budget \\u2014 it renders at natural width and overflows narrow terminals, while a card capped to width disagrees. The fix that honours width: declare the one variable column as Fill() with min_width + max_width=natural \\u2014 fills to natural on a roomy terminal, shrinks+ellipsizes when the budget is tight (FIT can act). Below the irreducible floor (fixed numeric cols + gaps), drop a decorative column (we drop TREND under width 64). Also: table() reverse-videos row 0 by default (TUI cursor) \\u2014 pass selected_style=Style() for a static listing; and use Wrap.ELLIPSIS not the default hard-clip on card sublines so narrow widths signal loss with a marker. Reusable for any painted table consumer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWCX2FTAQ857BR1DCY41057V\", \"_ts\": 1782844580.894851, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"session/2026-06-30-ls-stat-rich-render\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-30-ls-stat-rich-render\", \"message\": \"Built the sl ls redesign end-to-end on feat/ls-stat-containment (596ffd6, pushed GitLab+GitHub). TWO Kyle requests: (1) --kind <K> stop dumping the fact list \\u2014 reshaped as a DESCENT to the kind's entries (namespace rollup / --key drill / collect->observer / orphan bucket), reversing decision-B; (2) leverage painted for a beautiful human TTY render \\u2014 Kyle chose the maximal 'boxed panel + trend sparklines'. Delivered: rounded stat card + clean table() + share meter + per-kind 30d sparkline + freshness gradient + dimmed minor-tail, strictly piped-keyed (TTY rich human / pipe terse faithful agent \\u2014 concrete EVIDENCE for thread:budget-meaning-human-vs-agent's inversion). SHAPE: scout inline -> understanding workflow (painted surface + register constraints + stat-menu) -> AskUserQuestion with ASCII-preview mockups for the 2 real forks (visual treatment + minor-tail handling) -> build slice-by-slice with live render checks -> 4-dim adversarial review workflow. CALIBRATION: the review EARNED ITS KEEP \\u2014 caught 5 real + 2 parity defects the green 1500-test suite masked (painted table(Overflow.FIT) is a no-op without a Fill column -> ignores width; card hard-clip mid-token; --json datetime-vs-float-epoch divergence; --key-on-collect-fold false 'under X' stamp; piped registers dropped signed/share/span). All fixed + regression-tested (1522 loops + 827 engine). The AskUserQuestion preview mockups were the right tool for the aesthetic fork \\u2014 Kyle picked precisely from concrete ASCII, zero back-and-forth. Painted lesson captured: observation:rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill. NEXT ENTRY POINT: Kyle has minor UI-refinement requests to pick up post-wrap \\u2014 the shared _statview.py makes tweaks one-file.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWCX2345XY7228358C0C9D0N,01KWCX2FTAQ857BR1DCY41057V\", \"_ts\": 1782846510.78328, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/ls-kind-descends-to-entries\", \"decision:rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"rendering/piped-faithfulness-forces-width-none\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/piped-faithfulness-forces-width-none\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"The presentation-register split must FORCE width=None on the piped branch INSIDE the lens, not trust ctx.width \\u2014 a pipe can inherit COLUMNS (default 80), so relying on ctx.width silently truncates the agent channel (clipped 'sl ls' \\u2283 preview; 'sl ls <v> --kind' clipped '115d ago'\\u2192'115d ag'). Adversarial review (4-dim workflow) caught this MAJOR faithfulness break; the green suite + repo-root smoke both masked it because both ran with a real width. Two painted gotchas surfaced: Line.to_block(width) requires an int (does 'if width<=0' \\u2192 crashes on None) so width-free styled rendering needs natural-width or plain Block.text (helper _spans_block); and forcing width=None must be paired with None-guards on every elide()/pad call.\", \"_ts\": 1782851941.23532, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\"]}, \"session/2026-06-30-ls-line-row\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-30-ls-line-row\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"Session shape: turned Kyle's two alignment nits (sl ls <vertex> minor-tail; sl ls front-door readability) into a front-door redesign. Bare sl ls \\u2192 one-line-per-vertex line-row (\\u25c6/\\u25c7/\\u25c8 type icon + \\u2283 top-kinds preview + shadow-on-line-2-with-path + -v per-kind census justified across vertices); kinds-table minor tail aligned (single table() + SHARE align=END). Calibration: the 4-dim adversarial Workflow earned its keep AGAIN \\u2014 caught a MAJOR piped-faithfulness break + a width=None crash + cross-group --all drift that 1528 green tests AND repo-root smoke all masked (every check ran with a width). Merged 97a9055, pushed both remotes; docs/dev banners local (gitignored). NEXT ENTRY: release is a pending 0.6.0 minor DEFERRED until more commands reshaped (thread:next-release-0.6.0); open polish (Kyle's call): icon prominence (dim/shape-only), deferred open-count trailer.\", \"_ts\": 1782855024.172968, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"register-split-piped-faithfulness-untested\", \"rendering/ls-root-line-row\"]}, \"architecture/typed-edge-emit-fold-split\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/typed-edge-emit-fold-split\", \"message\": \"Live emit/fold inconsistency in loops (verified 2026-07-01, 4-agent source read): the emit -v receipt already reports superseded_by=decision:foo as 'one new inbound edge on its target entity' (resolve.py:443, emit.py:627), but the fold/read path only lifts the literal ref field into _refs (atoms/engine.py:103 collect, 140-150 upsert -- the ONLY two writers of _refs repo-wide). So that inbound edge never appears in the target's arrow-N salience or --refs walk. Write-time and read-time disagree today. 6 superseded_by_ref + 2 resolved_by_ref pins live in project.db are graph-invisible; 1 accidental topic_ref pin (on a cite fact) is the footgun in the wild -- 1 accidental / 2770 facts, bounded by the self-key-skip and whitespace guards.\", \"_ts\": 1782922524.04923, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/vertex-is-the-place\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/vertex-is-the-place\", \"message\": \"Step-back vocabulary trace: 'vertex' has named three things \\u2014 the runtime pattern, the .vertex document, and the place (store + interpretation). Only pattern and place were ever in the model; the document was a residence artifact that fused strata the paradigm had already ranked apart (sources='infrastructure not atoms', lenses='configuration not architecture', Spec=atom, Observer=first-class). SPEC \\u00a79 store-residence strengthens rather than dilutes vertex identity: declaration events are the second truth applied one tier up (observing the focusing is observable); current-ontology-as-Latest is VERTEX.md's boundary-less memory fold; rewind = the observer observing their own past focusing. The split that's needed is in the DOCUMENT grammar (stratum sections in KDL as ingress/render form), never in the vertex concept. KDL's discipline job moved to the frozen meta-schema vocabulary; KDL keeps authoring+render.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWG18WWGWJN95ZF786A20MW1,01KWHQ094B1WF7Z416HXY3KKN5\", \"_ts\": 1783006793.272952, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:declaration-strata-portability\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"session/2026-07-02-060-design\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-02-060-design\", \"message\": \"0.6.0 design session: picked up roadmap-substrate-after-060, ran the queued implementation discussion. Corpus (Static TTY study: 3 directions, author leaned 2c rail) + code map (4 drifted grammars, fold=only Surface consumer, no cross-command golden = drift cause) extracted via parallel agents; study's 'undesigned piped form' turned out already answered by presentation-register-keys-on-channel. Six decisions ratified in sequence, each dissolving the next question: hybrid-by-register \\u2192 tree-cut spine \\u2192 key-level salience w/ max propagation \\u2192 vertex-scoped tiers \\u2192 rail wins gutter \\u2192 view sequence w/ Strata as designated cut. Session break with review doc handed off.\", \"_ts\": 1783031008.808611, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/store-type-portfolio\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-type-portfolio\", \"message\": \"Store-shape portfolio as the domain-neutrality test suite (Kyle 2026-07-02): agent-attestation (exists, ref-heavy ideation), SillyTavern RP (consolidation-ticks-as-memory, no lifecycle, personas-as-observers), novel-writing (TWO time axes: wall vs fictional/canon; continuity=coverage), household management (multi-human + recurring timed/count boundaries \\u2014 chores are loops), hlab (exists, boundary-rich ops), subtask-as-orchestrator (machine volume, worker fleet observers, ticks=completions), autoresearch (metric series, keep/discard folds, different lifecycle vocab), personal salience feed (ingested via Source/Parse, high-volume/disposable, recency-dominant, browser-history-as-attention \\u2014 decay is the product), corp salience feed (+grants/federation), household tracking + jeeves (sensor ingestion + agent ACTUATION outward), cumulative deep research (digest-coverage's natural home). Sharpest stress tests: the feed (inverts every design-store default; behavioral attention \\u2248 inbound-refs \\u2014 attention-events on an address is what ref already is, new SOURCE for existing concept) and the novel (fictional time = ordering axis in payload the grammar can't sort by). Validation: each 0.6.0 view has a natural home store none of which is the design vertex \\u2014 Confluence\\u2192household/corp, Graph\\u2192attestation/research, Provenance\\u2192attestation/corp, Horizon\\u2192hlab/household, Strata\\u2192subtask/research.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KWJNTNT7FW1Q8WWBC4QKWKR2\", \"_ts\": 1783039643.405664, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"thread:sillytavern-showcase-app\"]}, \"design/salience-as-attention-trace\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-as-attention-trace\", \"message\": \"The salience feed (Kyle 2026-07-02) reframes salience as a TRACE, not a scalar: three signal strata \\u2014 ambient scrape (feeds/discords), deliberate capture (likes/'good article', incl. out-of-subscription ingestion), actual attention (browser history on top) \\u2014 recording what had attention WHEN. Never about deletion. Consequences: salience-now = fold over attention events; salience-at-T = same fold over a window \\u2014 the append-only store + ref-as-attention-event (UNION, accumulating) already IS the trace; the feed needs the 0.7.0 temporal cursor to query it, which is the strongest motivation yet for rewind (stronger than audit framing). Dissolution-as-coverage-not-deletion (already ratified) satisfies 'never get rid of things' as-is. Retrospection use case: reconstruct a trajectory months later ('the Shannon-Weaver rabbit hole', 'all the 3D-printing hop-skipping') across topic hops.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJQ3KRD6CF2HEKD01MXYQQJ,01KWJQYG20A72PJ2RXZBEJAZT8\", \"_ts\": 1783040524.65667, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-dials-vertex-declared\", \"observation:design/store-type-portfolio\"]}, \"session/2026-07-02-spine-build\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-02-spine-build\", \"message\": \"Evening build session: spine G0-G3 committed on feat/static-honest-spine (grammar module w/ unified time vocabulary; Row.tier quantile-bucketed; rail+ledger register split in fold; register retrofit + parity tests on stream/ticks/store \\u2014 parity harness caught piped truncation on first run). 1588 pass, live-verified both channels. Session closed with Kyle's screenshot review: rail confirmed cool on short bodies, friction:rail-drowns-under-full-bodies opened for long ones. NEXT SESSION: G4 design discussion (stream tier-inheritance fork a/b/c + Row level discriminator \\u2014 recorded on thread:static-honest-060-spine) + the rail/full-body layout fix.\", \"_ts\": 1783045194.509878, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/tier-disclosure-scarcity-not-layout\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tier-disclosure-scarcity-not-layout\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"G4d live-verified on the project vertex (human read = piped=False width=None, per drop-truncation-from-human-reads): tier-allocated disclosure delivers body-SCARCITY (127 high-body rows of 1231; mid/tail regions now clean one-line rail, dramatically scannable). BUT bodies are the COUNT half, not the LAYOUT half: high rows cluster at the TOP of each salience-sorted namespace group (design/ head = a stack of ~30 high-tier full untruncated bodies), so their wrapped lines still interrupt the rail's continuous gutter THERE. Not a contradiction \\u2014 the decision scopes itself to scarcity ('bodies become scarce, rail spacing survives by construction') and delivers it; the wrapped-body-vs-continuous-gutter question for the SURVIVING high bodies is orthogonal and remains the friction's original candidate-(a/b/c) layout work (hanging indent / continuation rail / body-as-subline). Residual for G5/G6 or a layout slice: the rail survives the bulk of the read, still drowns in the high-density head.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWK0BM2PAG7PXCCXD59K47VV,01KWJWCP494MRJ72C4JZZPNMQP\", \"_ts\": 1783050804.972248, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tier-allocated-disclosure\", \"friction:rail-drowns-under-full-bodies\"]}, \"rendering/rail-needs-uninterrupted-run\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/rail-needs-uninterrupted-run\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle smoke of G6: kind-descent is the first view where the rail reads as an ACTUAL rail \\u2014 an uninterrupted glyph column. In read the rail keeps getting broken up by body text (and the project store is huge), diluting the scanning effect. Same territory as the rail-drowns layout residue: the rail's value is continuity.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWN25NCYXKW0MTSVQARZX522\", \"_ts\": 1783120874.510457, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:namespace-rollup-tier-max-flattening\"]}, \"rendering/ls-root-tatty-vs-kind-descent\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ls-root-tatty-vs-kind-descent\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle smoke of G6: sl ls and sl ls <vertex> look tatty next to the clean kind-descent view. Root/vertex levels predate the G6 rail alignment visually (line-row + kinds census). Candidate follow-up: bring root and vertex levels up to the kind-descent finish.\", \"_ts\": 1783120874.785561, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/capture-cheap-assert-later-read-retroactive\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/capture-cheap-assert-later-read-retroactive\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Three independent designs converged on one pattern: typed edges (address-field -> declared edge), observer typing (bare string -> declared Peer), delegation (slash-path -> vouched relation). General form: capture is cheap/declaration-free at emit time; structure is asserted later and lights up retroactively at read time (schema-on-read); the store never blocks on ontology; each read surface advertises its own promotion candidates (reconcile -> edge declarations, Confluence -> peer declarations / unendorsed compounds). This is a paradigm property, not three coincidences.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWFPBY99R304Z7MQE3A91SFD,01KWNQWF910CZR7JHS6HFEVAFN,01KWNT7474AGX2BPFRCX4Q1XKE\", \"_ts\": 1783143567.865786, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-compound-delegation-path\", \"decision:design/observer-typing-dissolves-to-declared-peer\", \"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\"]}, \"workflow/adversarial-review-060-tail\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/adversarial-review-060-tail\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-spine\", \"message\": \"4-dim adversarial workflow (14 agents) over the 0.6.0 tail pre-push: 9 confirmed findings the green suite (1756) masked, 1 refuted. Major: --why TTY hard-clips long field values (violates the wrap-not-clip contract this branch itself ratified in tier-allocated-disclosure). Real algorithmic: _longest_chains memo poisoning on cycles (order-dependent 'longest', reproduced counterexample; live store IS cyclic), depth-cap-128 silent truncation, piped graph register leaking zoom caps (top-10 hubs/top-3 chains on the agent channel, contra its own docstring), orphans as one 18KB joined line (+ middot delimiter ambiguity), edges-vs-inbound definitional gap (1471 vs 1547, 76 unsourced refs undisclosed), stale 'cap 32' docstrings. Pattern holds: every wave, the register-faithfulness and honesty dims catch what goldens can't \\u2014 goldens pin a width and a fixture; faithfulness breaks live. Fixes dispatched pre-push.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQB5F149M9N4XJ75NA3BC6R\", \"_ts\": 1783195477.762672, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"rendering/flags-words-edges-arrows\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/flags-words-edges-arrows\", \"message\": \"Register idiom generalized from the P4 review: symbols split into FLAGS (a judgment/status the pipe consumer can't reconstruct \\u2014 degrade to words: tier \\u25c6\\u2192high, horizon \\u25b2\\u2192approaching) vs EDGE NOTATION (\\u2190/\\u2192 ARE the notation, no better word exists, pipe already speaks \\u2192 in every chain path \\u2014 arrows survive both registers). What looked inconsistency-shaped (arrows survived the pipe after \\u25b2 didn't) is a rule the next lens can follow. Documented in _grammar module docstring.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQMD4P9YK4KKP5HD89M2DNB\", \"_ts\": 1783204582.406815, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/rollup-shed-only-what-degrades\"]}, \"workflow/external-codex-review\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/external-codex-review\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-spine\", \"message\": \"First external-model review of the branch (codex exec, gpt-5.5 xhigh) over the full static-honest-spine diff: 5 real findings, 2 in the piped-faithfulness class our own adversarial waves had already named as the branch's recurring defect class \\u2014 external reviewer independently converged on the same class, plus a provenance case-canonicalization bug (--why on a case-variant key attributed zero fields) no internal wave caught. All 5 fixed + regression-tested in e8643a6. codex exec review --base cannot take custom instructions; plain codex exec with a diff-it-yourself brief works.\", \"_ts\": 1783275558.948772, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/record-line-flattens-embedded-newlines\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/record-line-flattens-embedded-newlines\", \"feature\": \"painted-070-bump\", \"message\": \"painted 0.7.0 record_line now flattens an embedded newline inside a payload VALUE onto one logical record line (output='running tests...\\\\nall 42 tests passed' \\u2192 'running tests... all 42 tests passed') instead of letting the \\\\n break the ledger row and orphan the tail with no gutter/timestamp. Surfaced as 6 tasks-app golden drifts (TestTaskLog/TestSessionLog \\u00d7 text/detailed/full), all one cause; regolded \\u2014 the new form is more correct. Loops app: ZERO golden drift. Likely a side-effect of the 0.7.0 refs work hardening record_line (denotation demo is the first record_line demo).\", \"_ts\": 1783348670.228892, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/lens-signature-tiers\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 signature-sufficiency evidence. Enumerated all 25+ loops lens entrypoints beyond semantic_article. They fall in THREE tiers against semantic_article's (data, zoom, width, *, visible, chars, lines) vote. TIER A pure (data, zoom, width) -> Block, no extra kwargs: compile_view, run_facts_view, run_ticks_view, test_view, validate_view, sync_view, pop_view. TIER B needs a piped bool (TTY register split) sometimes plus palette/vertex_name: confluence_view, horizon_view, graph_view, store_view (+palette), declarations_view/_render_stat_view/kind_stat_view, vertices_view, stream_view (+vertex_name), ticks_view, tick_chain_view, stats_view. TIER C needs the Fidelity budget axes visible/chars/lines: semantic_article.fold_view (the vote, explicit), plus **kwargs absorbers deliberation.fold_view, reconcile.fold_view, session_landing.fold_view. VERDICT: the semantic_article vote (decomposed visible/chars/lines) holds \\u2014 those three collapse exactly into a painted Fidelity's fields, so (data, fidelity, width) subsumes every Tier A and Tier C signature. It does NOT subsume the two EXTRA kinds of thing Tier B threads: a TTY fact (piped) and domain identity (vertex_name/vertex_path/palette). Those are the real signature question, detailed in sibling observations.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S\", \"_ts\": 1783737998.323101, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"The built-in apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/fold.py fold_view is the UNION signature \\u2014 the everything-lens that proves what a general loops renderer actually consumes: (data, zoom, width, *, vertex_name, vertex_path, visible, lines, chars, piped). Decompose those kwargs into three categories and the M3 signature answer falls out cleanly: (1) visible/chars/lines = painted Fidelity axes (fold_view even rebuilds a Fidelity from zoom+these inside semantic_article) \\u2014 these BELONG in the fidelity arg; (2) vertex_name/vertex_path = domain identity, an app-specific valued facet, render-irrelevant \\u2014 belongs OUTSIDE painted, bound by the app via closure or an app-context, matching the roadmap's 'keep app-specific facets outside painted' constraint; (3) piped = a fabricated TTY fact that duplicates width's None-sentinel (see rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact). So (data, fidelity, width) is sufficient for the RENDER contract once piped dissolves and domain identity is bound app-side rather than passed as a render param.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H3PZKECZ04R6GD6Q58E5D\", \"_ts\": 1783738007.654326, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 exit criterion says loops semantic renderers must require no fabricated mode, TTY, or stream facts. loops VIOLATES this via one fact: piped. It is computed as (not ctx.is_tty) or (not sys.stdout.isatty()) and threaded as a keyword into ~11 lens entrypoints: declarations_view, kind_stat_view, vertices_view, store_view, tick_chain_view, stats_view, ticks_view, stream_view, confluence_view, horizon_view, graph_view, and the built-in fold_view. It is REDUNDANT: width already carries the same two-state contract (concrete int on a TTY, None when piped) \\u2014 normalize_width and its docstring in lens_resolver.py state this explicitly, and every run_cli render closure sets width via 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None' right beside 'piped=not ctx.is_tty'. So the same TTY bit is encoded TWICE at every call site, once as width=None and once as piped=True. Dissolution: lenses that branch on piped can branch on 'width is None' instead; piped as a param disappears and the fabricated-TTY-fact criterion is met with zero new painted machinery. This is deletable independently of the declaration grammar.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H3PZKECZ04R6GD6Q58E5D\", \"_ts\": 1783738016.954509, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/height-offered-only-in-tui\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/height-offered-only-in-tui\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 asks: record where height is OFFERED to a renderer vs merely KNOWN by the caller. Findings across both loops render paths. STATIC CLI path (dispatch.py + every run_cli render closure): only WIDTH is offered \\u2014 dispatch computes width from shutil.get_terminal_size().columns (or None when piped) and passes it as the third positional; height is available to the caller (get_terminal_size().lines exists, ctx carries it) but is NEVER passed to any static lens. So in the static path height is merely KNOWN, never OFFERED. TUI/Surface path (tui/store_app.py, tui/autoresearch_app.py): height IS offered \\u2014 the Surface calls layout(self, width, height) and the app stores both self._w and self._h and lays out against the viewport height. CONCLUSION for the signature question: a static (data, fidelity, width) signature that omits height matches actual static-path usage exactly (height is never wanted there); height is a live/Surface concern, which is consistent with painted keeping offered-allocation in the Surface tier rather than the static renderer signature. No static loops lens is starved by a height-free signature.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S\", \"_ts\": 1783738026.355831, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/siftd-mirror-has-drifted\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/siftd-mirror-has-drifted\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"Side-by-side of the two claimed-mirror fidelity_from_args implementations (loops cli/fidelity.py vs siftd src/siftd/cli/_common.py). They are NOT identical in logic \\u2014 the Mirrors siftd docstring is aspirational, and the shadow copies have DRIFTED. Divergences: (1) DEPTH FLAGS \\u2014 loops reads -q/--quiet (depth 0) and -v/--verbose count (1 to depth 2, 2+ to depth 3), default_depth 1; siftd reads --brief (depth 0) and --full (depth 3) booleans, default 1. Different flag vocabulary AND different arity (count vs bool). (2) VISIBLE DERIVATION \\u2014 loops is PARAMETERIZED: caller passes a visible={flag_attr: tag_name} mapping and any truthy/int>0 flag lights its tag; siftd HARDCODES its domain tags: seeds {text}, adds thinking on --thinking/--full, adds tools on --tools/--full. (3) BUDGET \\u2014 loops takes explicit --max-chars AND --max-lines (two axes); siftd takes --chars plus a --brief=>80 shortcut and has NO lines axis. (4) default_chars vs default_depth parameter surface differs. SIGNIFICANCE for M3: the drift is not sloppiness \\u2014 it is EVIDENCE that the flag-to-facet vocabulary is genuinely per-consumer (loops disclosure axes are facts/refs over threads/decisions; siftd's are text/thinking/tools over transcripts). Two independently-drifting hand-copies of the same SHAPE is precisely the signal that argues for a painted DECLARATION grammar (each consumer declares its flag->facet map, painted compiles it) over a shared parsing function \\u2014 a shared function would have to absorb both vocabularies and cannot.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4Y91G01ATG9CAATGCAMV\", \"_ts\": 1783738050.24884, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/fidelity-from-args-is-dead-shadow-copy\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 ask: record every adapter loops hand-builds to reuse a painted renderer through run_cli. loops has TWO dispatch spines and both hand-build glue. SPINE 1 legacy run_cli path \\u2014 commands/ still call painted.run_cli(fetch=, render=) directly; each supplies a render(ctx, data) closure that is pure adapter boilerplate translating painted's CliContext into a loops lens call. Inventory of the render closures: ls.py:204 (declarations_view) and :518 (kind_stat_view); population.py:81 (vertices_view); store.py:654 (tick_chain_view), :723 (stats_view), :788 (store_view); ticks.py:103 and stream.py:77 (resolve-then-call composition adapters); sync.py:170 and :321 (sync_view); devtools.py x4. The recurring glue is exactly: 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None; return LENS(data, ctx.zoom, w, piped=not ctx.is_tty)'. Every one re-derives width-from-TTY and piped-from-TTY by hand. SPINE 2 new siftd-shape path \\u2014 cli/dispatch.py:dispatch owns the same branches natively (action/interactive/live/static) and no longer routes static through run_cli; it computes width from sys.stdout.isatty() itself. DISSOLUTION: under a (data, fidelity, width) renderer contract where painted owns the fetch->render->emit loop and passes width already normalized (None=piped), every Spine-1 render closure collapses to nothing \\u2014 the ctx.zoom/ctx.width/ctx.is_tty unpacking and the piped re-derivation are the whole adapter, and all of it is painted re-exposing what painted already knows. The closures exist only because loops re-reads TTY state painted computed one frame earlier.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H495T9X8RWQPPVC9WZF16\", \"_ts\": 1783738063.412693, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/call-lens-fidelity-teardown-adapter\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/call-lens-fidelity-teardown-adapter\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"A second, subtler adapter loops hand-builds around painted's render contract: the Fidelity TEARDOWN. loops resolves a proper painted Fidelity upstream (op.fidelity, built via parse_fidelity) but its lenses do NOT accept a Fidelity \\u2014 they accept (data, zoom, width, *, visible, chars, lines, ...). So dispatch.py + lens_resolver.call_lens tear the Fidelity back apart: _zoom_of(fidelity) extracts fidelity.depth as a Zoom, then visible/chars/lines are spread as loose kwargs via extra.setdefault(...). call_lens then inspects each lens signature and forwards only the kwargs whose names match (or all, for **kwargs lenses). This is a build-up-then-tear-down round trip: painted's parse_fidelity assembles a Fidelity, loops immediately decomposes it into (zoom, visible, chars, lines) to feed lenses written before Fidelity existed. Under semantic_article's vote the fix is to have lenses take fidelity DIRECTLY as the second arg \\u2014 then _zoom_of, the visible/chars/lines setdefault dance, and call_lens's whole kwarg-forwarding inspection machinery all dissolve. This is the strongest single piece of evidence FOR the decomposed-kwargs-into-one-Fidelity-object direction: loops already has the object and is paying to un-build it at every render.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4036S2PC6N1CJXDYS4PP\", \"_ts\": 1783738074.577759, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/store-app-holds-no-fidelity-duplication\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/store-app-holds-no-fidelity-duplication\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"Audit item 2 named tui/store_app.py as a place a landed painted declaration grammar might let loops delete. Finding: NOTHING in store_app.py is flag-compilation or Fidelity-parsing residue \\u2014 clearing a red herring from the M3 scope. The FidelityState dataclass there is a NAVIGATION state (a facts-within-a-tick-window drill cursor), a domain concept that merely shares the word fidelity; it has no relation to painted's render Fidelity. store_app imports painted's Block/Surface/views (data_explorer, list_view) and lays out against layout(width, height) \\u2014 it is a legitimate Surface consumer, not a shadow renderer. So the deletable duplication surfaced by this spike lives entirely in cli/fidelity.py (dead fidelity_from_args) and the run_cli render-closure glue (rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory) plus the piped re-derivation (rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact) \\u2014 NOT in the TUI. Recording this so the M3 delete-list is not padded with a false target.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4Y91G01ATG9CAATGCAMV\", \"_ts\": 1783738086.358099, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/fidelity-from-args-is-dead-shadow-copy\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/painted-0101-consumer-workarounds-dissolved\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-0101-consumer-workarounds-dissolved\", \"message\": \"painted 0.10.1 pickup (same-day patch cut FROM our M3 adoption-spike evidence \\u2014 the consumer-feedback loop closing at patch latency). Three dissolutions landed loops-side: (1) .loops/publish_semantic_trifecta.py's _anchor_sections regex post-pass (coupled to to_html's serialization whitespace) DELETED \\u2014 to_html stamps <section id> itself on 0.10.1 and the outline now walks the declared tree reading painted.publish.section_anchors(doc), the SAME map to_html stamps from. Note the break-fix character: on 0.10.1 the old regex silently stopped matching (pattern expected <section> without id) \\u2014 outline would have gone empty with no error. Visibility filter stays consumer-side as honest residue, keyed on token membership in the emitted fragment (content escaping guarantees a raw '<section id=' can only come from the publisher \\u2014 no structure recovery, no drift). PARITY PROOF: regenerated article diff vs 0.10.0 output = renderer version stamp only (8 diff lines, all version strings); section ids byte-identical. (2) store lens conditional width-None spacers collapse to Block.empty(width, 1) uniformly. (3) vertices.py _spans_block helper (the Line.to_block-refuses-None dodge) deleted, direct Line.to_block(width) at 3 sites \\u2014 goldens byte-stable, confirming the old docstring's claim that the piped register strips styling at the sink. Also paid the 0.8 deprecation debt while gating the bump: show()\\u2192paint() at ~45 sites, 1164 DeprecationWarnings \\u2192 0 (paint()'s Block passthrough is drop-in; loops never used show's inferring path or format=).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP,01KWVXY7M928X1KWGSSZWHFTKN\", \"_ts\": 1783806887.636263, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\", \"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"architecture/publish-layer-two-instance-promotion\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/publish-layer-two-instance-promotion\", \"message\": \"The application-promotion rule now fires for a loops publication layer: semantic-trifecta (91% of 826KB artifact = provenance cards) and homelab-audit (73% of 4MB = cards, article only 4.7%) hand-roll nearly identical HTML shells, drawers, manifests, redaction, and cut hydration. Two independent instances, same shape, same scaling pathology. Sol's split matches my read: medium-independent pieces (Table/Register node, published_outline, honest full-fidelity, char budgets) go UP into painted; the loops-specific pieces (sealed-cut selection, fact cursor, signature receipt, fact cards, redaction) become loops.publish \\u2014 NOT painted core. The substrate half is a public sealed-projection API (export exact tick cut + source-fact histories + edges + manifest as json/html) so consumers stop importing loops.commands internals and opening SQLite directly. Sol also correctly declined a raw-HTML escape node in painted pending a typed diagram contract \\u2014 matches painted's own dissolution discipline.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ\", \"_ts\": 1783894413.070861, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"architecture/origin-field-unused-by-provenance-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/origin-field-unused-by-provenance-consumer\", \"message\": \"Say/do gap in our own substrate, surfaced by the heaviest provenance consumer yet (2026-07-12): all 694 homelab-audit facts carry BLANK native origin \\u2014 a provenance-obsessed audit rebuilt provenance entirely in typed payload fields (evidence kind, authority/epistemic classes, observer attribution) and manual evidence summaries, because the origin field offered nothing usable for capture receipts. Sol's ask #7 (first-class evidence capture: run/ingest a read-only probe, record command, timestamp, exit status, content hash, redacted summary, observer, native origin in one signed receipt) is the Carried hand of the semantic-trifecta \\u2014 siftd Operation IR territory \\u2014 arriving as consumer demand rather than theory. Position: hold as evidence for the Carried arc, do NOT build a standalone loops probe verb (point solution smell); but the origin field's dormancy is itself a finding \\u2014 either it earns a contract that capture tooling can target, or it is dissolution-eligible dead surface. Check which during the Carried design.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ\", \"_ts\": 1783895965.30963, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"session/2026-07-13-hardening-closing-review\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-13-hardening-closing-review\", \"message\": \"Session arc: S4 edit ceremony (subtask they-plan, opus/high, merged d467e44) \\u2192 S5 ontology-as-of (same flow, merged 8fca98b, gate-closer) \\u2192 Sol holistic closing review BLOCK (8 findings, docs/dev/internal-table-s0-s5-closing-review-2026-07-13.md) \\u2192 hands-on hardening with Kyle (8 commits, four adversarial review rounds via review/internal-table-hardening subtask, every reviewer repro became a regression test) \\u2192 CLOSE \\u2192 merged ad84829. Also this session: batch-emit design consolidated three frictions then REFINED to batch-is-a-tick (symbolic IDs dissolved; design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress), decision:architecture/env-values-are-ingress, threads decl-lens-tombstone-vocab-gap + ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit. Process observations: (a) per-slice low-effort review passed what holistic high-effort blocked \\u2014 review altitude must match claim altitude (slice reviews verify slices; arc claims need arc reviews); (b) two of my own hardening fixes introduced regressions the suites missed \\u2014 the reviewer caught them because it hunted holes-introduced-by-fixes explicitly; (c) implementer rationalized a real boundary bug as 'scheduling artifact' in S5 \\u2014 cross-adapter review refused the rationalization and was right.\", \"_ts\": 1783968287.149478, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\": {\"topic\": \"practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"Internal-table retro headline (docs/dev/internal-table-retrospective-2026-07-13.md): every per-slice low-effort review passed and the medium capstone was clean, yet the holistic high-effort review found 8 closure blockers \\u2014 every one at a cross-slice seam no slice owned (foreign-genesis x merge, as_of x resolver, edit-ts x rewind, seam-bypass, secrets boundary, absorb x validator, router flag drop, per-surface-not-per-invariant exclusion). Two green tests LOCKED IN wrong cross-slice behavior. Rule: a merge asserting an arc-level claim ('gate open') buys an arc-level review at matching effort BEFORE the claim; per-slice cadence is a velocity instrument, not a closure gate \\u2014 different instruments, not quality tiers.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXECQJ349N1Z1WQA69KM280Y\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.216037, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"Hardening convergence discipline (8\\u21926\\u21923\\u21921\\u2192CLOSE in four rounds): every reviewer finding landed with its repro converted to a regression test before the fix counted as done \\u2014 the suite ratchets, so each round's frontier is genuinely new. Corollary: round 2 explicitly hunted holes-introduced-by-fixes and found 2 regressions the green suites missed, both from round-1 fixes. Fixes are new code written under pressure; they deserve MORE adversarial attention, not less. Also: implementer explanations of their own anomalies are hypotheses, not evidence (S5 'scheduling artifact' rationalization refused by cross-adapter review, correctly).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXECQJ349N1Z1WQA69KM280Y\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.525395, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"They-plan subtasks vs hands-on-wheel, compared across the internal-table arc: both shipped working slices, failed differently. Delegated workers optimize the slice's STATED exit criteria \\u2014 S5 shipped 'gate open' with blockers sitting on its own seams; delegation transfers the task, not the arc conscience. Hands-on hardening fixed all 8 seam-shaped findings with the whole arc in one head. Synthesis: greenfield slices with crisp exit criteria delegate well; integration/invariants/closure claims belong at the wheel \\u2014 or the delegated slice's exit criteria must name the seams it touches. Bonus pattern: blockers at the right altitude UPGRADE designs (TOCTOU\\u2192absorb_genesis primitive; identity finding\\u2192adopt ceremony) \\u2014 budget reviews as design forcing-functions, not only defect filters.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX9QY9EF26CNXNBPRDSDT917\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.693621, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:workflow/internal-table-build-execution-model\"]}, \"workflow/lens-usage-forensics-2026-07\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/lens-usage-forensics-2026-07\", \"message\": \"Lens audit (wiring x 1594 mined read/store invocations, 681 post-0.6.0): built-in workhorses are fold/stream/store/ticks/ls surfaces; graph healthy via --lens graph (29 recent). Dead: pop_view (population command moved to vertices_view) \\u2014 deletion dispatched. Mislabeled: run_ticks_view is sync_view's internal helper, never an entrypoint \\u2014 privatization dispatched. confluence_view: zero session-history invocations BUT Kyle uses it interactively outside sessions \\u2014 KEEP; the zero is a DISCOVERABILITY signal, not a value signal, and confirms the history-mining caveat (bare-terminal use is invisible to session forensics). Headline inversion: user-authored resolver lenses (--lens prompt 23 / reconcile 17 / session 14) out-earn every built-in except graph, and none are declared in any .vertex lens block \\u2014 the lens system's center of gravity is ad-hoc custom files, so the zoom\\u2192fidelity signature migration must treat custom lens files as first-class consumers.\", \"_ts\": 1783994675.323187, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-07-14-completion-t3\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-14-completion-t3\", \"feature\": \"completion-t3\", \"message\": \"Session arc (continuation of 2026-07-13 follow-ups session): lens audit (wiring x mined usage; pop_view deleted, run_ticks_view privatized via sonnet subtask; confluence kept \\u2014 zero session-history use was a DISCOVERABILITY signal, Kyle uses it interactively) \\u2192 pivot to completion T3 as the discoverability fix \\u2192 orchestrated build: S1 seam+lens (opus/high), S2 vertex (sonnet), S3 kind/key (sonnet, one usage-limit interruption resumed cleanly), S4 emit wiring (sonnet, scope-discovered: only read had an add_args seam) \\u2192 Sol gpt-5.6 medium read-only review, SIX rounds to CLOSE, all remediation hands-on at the wheel \\u2192 branch pushed, UNMERGED, awaiting Kyle. Also this session: first gpt-5.6-terra worker (painted 0.11 migration, clean), retrospective kind ratified + used twice, meta-store role dissolved, thread:claude-memory-as-source opened, two painted upstream fixes authored. Fact-check footnote: Sol's sandbox repeatedly collected 490 lang tests vs 540 here \\u2014 environment artifact of the review worktree venv, all local runs 540 green.\", \"_ts\": 1784004310.328322, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\": {\"topic\": \"test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\", \"message\": \"SHARPENED on landing: worse than the design-time read. Not just drift \\u2014 4/7 rules RED, and the failure mode was layered: stale allowlist entries (pop_store, painted) tripped _check_exceptions FIRST, so the actual scans never executed and real violations accumulated invisibly behind the stale-exception error (3 sqlite3 probes, 5 StoreReader reaches, store->engine, 2 unfrozen dataclasses). Root cause one level down: tests/ belongs to no package, so no gate ever ran it \\u2014 the ratchet was opt-in manual, i.e. review vigilance wearing a test's costume (Kyle's own ratchet-test principle, violated by the ratchet itself). Fixed: swept + shrink-only allowlists in f384e2d, root ./dev check gate in 2cb08a0. Meta-lesson: a ratchet's staleness check failing loudly is GOOD design (it forced the sweep), but only if something runs it \\u2014 enforcement infrastructure needs its own enforcement path.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXP65CW2ZWV343GF1YKWW49Z\", \"_ts\": 1784229856.868457, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\"]}, \"architecture/daemon-access-serves-tui\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/daemon-access-serves-tui\", \"message\": \"Convergence: ticked's 2s-poll daemon (friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access) and the 0.7.0 TUI are the SAME consumer shape \\u2014 a long-lived process needing incremental reads (replay facts since last rowid, not full history) and receive() without reload. The daemon-shaped engine access ticked forces is the TUI's substrate too; designing it once serves both, and the temporal-cursor work inherits the same long-lived-handle contract. Sequencing implication: the engine design session for daemon access should sit BEFORE TUI work on the 0.7.0 track, not parallel to it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXM4GB6356A3SV8GDD3WXWGM,01KXPVPFGVGASDXJ57QR7EFTB6\", \"_ts\": 1784252418.931935, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\", \"friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access\"]}, \"implementation/replay-swap-was-per-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/replay-swap-was-per-vertex\", \"message\": \"MAJOR pre-existing engine bug found by the receipt-change adversarial review (not caused by the diff \\u2014 the lens question 'can receive_receipt run with a store attached during replay?' surfaced it): Vertex.replay swapped only the ROOT's _store to None, so parent replay forwarded historical facts to nested children whose stores were still attached \\u2014 a stored child re-appended the parent's ENTIRE history on every load (1\\u21922\\u21923 rows per replay, reproduced empirically by the verify agent). Same discipline hole: no try/finally on the swap, so a raising fold mid-replay left _store=None permanently (close() silent no-op, handle leaked, boundaries dead). Fixed fdda675: _replay_guard context manager makes the swap per-TREE (walks _children recursively, saves/restores store+replaying flags in finally). Side effect worth knowing: child boundaries no longer fire mid-replay \\u2014 matches replay's own documented contract ('without re-appending or firing boundaries') and prevents double-folding; the old behavior was the bug wearing a feature's shape. CALIBRATION: my own pre-check read replay() and concluded 'clean \\u2014 every path nulls _store before replaying'; TRUE per-vertex, FALSE per-tree. I verified the discipline at the wrong scope. The structural sensor (workflow lens + empirical repro) caught what my targeted read did not \\u2014 the read confirmed the claim I brought to it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXPY5GCW45YB0SKB5W25M9QR\", \"_ts\": 1784255013.331488, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\"]}, \"architecture/parallel-authorization-paths\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/parallel-authorization-paths\", \"message\": \"Two parallel authorization paths exist and only one is enforced: (a) lang-AST GrantDecl/ObserverDecl -> identity.py ObserverCheck (enforced at emit \\u2014 'forbidden' when decl.grant.potential excludes the kind); (b) engine.Peer/Grant frozen dataclasses with Vertex.receive(grant=) gating \\u2014 ZERO production consumers (no CLI site constructs one; every receive() call is bare). Horizon (read-side visibility) is enforced NOWHERE. This is a dissolution candidate that must resolve BEFORE Digest builds on either path \\u2014 Digest is chartered as the first in-repo Peer/Grant consumer, and building it on the unenforced path while the enforced path speaks a different schema would fork authorization semantics. Echoes convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate (2026-05-13): the substrate's own primitive still doesn't participate in the substrate. Found by the 0.7.0 design-state audit 2026-07-16.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ49N02Y6XRP8P6TCAP2GCQ\", \"_ts\": 1784261442.054095, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/strata-tick-lineage-unmet\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/strata-tick-lineage-unmet\", \"message\": \"decision:design/strata-cut-ratified (2026-07-04) fed forward a concrete requirement \\u2014 'the 0.7.0 internal table should carry parent_tick_id/child_vertex_ref on tick rows' \\u2014 and the internal-table arc did NOT land it: the ticks schema is unchanged (sqlite_store.py ~281-293), _tick_to_fact still drops the child tick id, and the 'lineage' \\u00a79 added is DECLARATION lineage (genesis/own_lineage), a different concept. Strata is therefore doubly downstream in the 0.8.0 wave: it needs a tick-lineage schema design (post-freeze, coordinating with the Go oracle) AND its stacked view wants Digest output (recursive digests). No design fact exists yet for tick lineage as columns vs fact-borne events. Found by the 0.7.0 design-state audit 2026-07-16.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ49N02Y6XRP8P6TCAP2GCQ\", \"_ts\": 1784261442.354691, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"rendering/sync-view-aggregation-fallback-bug\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/sync-view-aggregation-fallback-bug\", \"message\": \"sync_view's 'No sources configured.' fallback checks top-level ran/skipped/errors, not children's \\u2014 on an aggregation vertex whose children DID run sources it appends the fallback after the children's rendered rows. Found during TUI-S0 golden coverage (feat/tui-s0-goldens); now deliberately BYTE-LOCKED as-is in test_sync.py::test_aggregation_tty so the lens-signature migration cannot 'fix' it as a silent side effect \\u2014 triage deliberately, then update the golden with the fix in the same commit.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBJ9RFA5CN1RQ659W85S17\", \"_ts\": 1784303901.949045, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:rendering/tui-shell-integration\"]}, \"practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\", \"message\": \"Overnight 0.8.0 run, review-yield data across the multi-model pipeline: codex reviews of Claude-written slices found 8 findings on E1-E3 (3 MAJOR incl. lineage-verify gap and guard bypass) + 5 on C1-C2 (3 HIGH, all the SAY/DO class: --facts route silently discarding --at; lens fetches rendering cursor metadata over head data; --refs walking referenced entities at head under a historical fold). Claude panels of codex-written designs found a fabricated benchmark citation, a false data_version safety claim (empirically refuted: pinned inside open txn = unbounded staleness), and painted-main drift the dossier snapshot missed. Every green suite masked findings the OTHER family caught \\u2014 the cross-vendor structural sensor kept earning its keep at each layer (design, engine, CLI). The labeled-lie class (cursor metadata over unselected data) is the exact gap-shape this project's coherence function exists for: capability said cursor, behavior served head.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784309123.421279, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\"]}, \"architecture/floor-snap-anchor-consistency-residual\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/floor-snap-anchor-consistency-residual\", \"message\": \"Residual from the capstone fix rounds (CLI agent's honest flag, 306d28e): when a floor-snap fires on a tick whose fact_cursor lands mid-ceremony (reachable only via merge/durable-handle re-resolution reordering rowids, not natural origin writes), resolve_witness_position keeps the CLI's pre-supplied anchor= rather than re-deriving post-snap \\u2014 the reported anchor can name a tick after the snapped position. Snap itself is correct (fact_id/seq honestly pre-ceremony). Follow-up candidate for the vectors-owed batch: anchor-consistency-after-snap. Not a 0.8.0 blocker.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784315138.13302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\"]}, \"test/codex-reverify-cursor-capstone\": {\"topic\": \"test/codex-reverify-cursor-capstone\", \"message\": \"CLOSED MERGE-READY: Codex scoped re-check of cdbb24d confirms the reversed --diff baseline-attribution fix \\u2014 tie case selects 'from' with empty interval (no sentence), None interval stays null/silent, baseline is an additive JSON field (no contract break), both directions name the correct endpoint. Full trail: capstone NOT-MERGE-READY (10 findings) -> 7480235+306d28e (all 10) -> re-verify found 1 new MAJOR -> cdbb24d -> MERGE-READY. feat/temporal-cursor (13 commits) ready for Kyle's merge call.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRQHRJ84T0QDPDBQCZG2M1X\", \"_ts\": 1784315846.080465, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\": {\"topic\": \"consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\", \"message\": \"Consumer exercise completed 2026-07-18: siftd was mapped as 17 capabilities, 11 architecture patterns, 17 components, 17 interfaces, 19 data entities, 9 flows, 49 ordered stages, and 18 invariants, plus audit and seal facts. The resulting 159-fact artifact carries 672 typed edges and validates the core fit: keyed folds present current truth while the fact stream retains change history, and declared edges can express architecture without new atoms. The exercise also exposed the residual costs: 159 individual emits, cross-kind key aliasing, mixed-predicate graph paths, no declared current-versus-inactive topology, opaque binary review, lazy FTS mutation on read, and incomplete lens cut provenance. Target split: core owns semantic correctness, CLI owns atomic authoring plus validation and review, and the project-local lens owns map vocabulary.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCXTBV2PXQB34ZHP4W6G718,01KXC7QG3FMKYX53DMDKCQNP8R,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV0ABSVWW3BW1ZB70NTNPJV,01KXV0AC0VTF42QE6KX4F9ZY65,01KXV0AC7TEKQBN0M42J04YGF5,01KXV0ACEM4X7CBJHVXMC378HH,01KXV0BH5AZ7K58MJYD5CDSXVK,01KXC7NZSHSEK03W120QKSBTG8\", \"_ts\": 1784391529.032416, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"design:rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\"]}, \"test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\", \"message\": \"Adversarial review complete (13-agent workflow: live-repro verifiers + per-fact skeptics + provenance, 2026-07-18) of the kyle/siftd-codex 7-fact delivery. BOTH frictions CONFIRMED bit-for-bit: typed-edge aliasing all 4 mechanisms reproduced twice independently (surface.py:274-276 suffix-only matcher, vertex_reader.py:1237-1242 slash mislift with write/read disagreement on the same value, resolve.py:827-840 bare-target strict-emit skip); FTS mutation reproduced 184320 to 282624 bytes from one --match, plus an AGGRAVATOR the skeptic found: aggregation --match delegates vertex_search to every child, mutating EVERY child store. Designs: predicate-graph SOUND (lands on build-1s own deferred list; premise reproduced incl. an 18-hop predicate-mixed chain), lens-boundary SOUND (pure policy fact, zero new machinery, independently re-derives consumer-owns-its-vocabulary now at N=3), export REFINE (dump half IS SPEC section-10 in stronger form and inherits the GlobalReceiptPosition gate; genuine core = canonical kind-key-sorted volatile-field-free review snapshot which read --json does NOT cover), lifecycle REFINE (real value is the UNIFICATION of three parallel proposed clauses; uncited sibling design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations owns the declaration home; SPEC section-9 vocabulary cost unpriced; siftd map has zero inactive entities so evidence is contract-prospective). Provenance: 25/25 refs resolve kind-and-key exact, 10/10 map stat claims exact including 672 edges, all 7 signatures verify against the registered observer key. Zero verdicts refuted by skeptics.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV0ACEM4X7CBJHVXMC378HH,01KXV0ABSVWW3BW1ZB70NTNPJV,01KXV0AC0VTF42QE6KX4F9ZY65,01KXV0AC7TEKQBN0M42J04YGF5,01KXV0BH5AZ7K58MJYD5CDSXVK,01KXV0BWXDH44FR8331A5KTH6Z\", \"_ts\": 1784393570.018556, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"design:rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"observation:consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\"]}, \"implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"S1 CLOSED at 1b523b7 (2 commits: 6591420 Address + dual-reading fix). CORRECTION over n=1: my category-(b) ruling was OVERTURNED by sol's interim review (P1) and I accepted \\u2014 the old matcher's exact whole-string clause was the deliberate bare-namespaced-key interpretation (pinned by the replaced design/c test; the hypothesis direction note warned about exactly this collision and I mis-scoped it to edges). Revised ruling: DUAL-READING, content-independent \\u2014 slash form x/y matches under either (x,y) legacy or ('',x/y) bare whole-key, always; colon stays exact-only; content-dependent fallback stays rejected (no retargeting hazard: readings are static). FINAL LIVE NUMBERS (three-way diff, drift-corrected): of 91 commit-1 drops, 72 restored, 19 stay dead \\u2014 all 19 are colon-explicit true cross-kind aliases (e.g. thread/emit-receipt-on-write 9->0); same-store isolation proves dual-reading purely additive (72 up, 0 down). Measures for the hypothesis: 8 split/suffix sites -> 0 outside 95-LOC atoms/address.py; 2 disagreeing edge-interpreters -> 1 (Address.for_edge); suffix-matchers 3 -> 0; collision semantics pinned (ambiguous ref honestly counts toward both readings' rows). Meta: the interim review tier caught the ARBITER's rationalization, not the implementer's code \\u2014 S1 flagged the judgment call, I ruled wrong, sol's cold diff-read reversed me. Cross-model calibration one level up the stack from the internal-table wave.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E,01KXV2A64BQG9WYZ0ZMZ0V551N,01KXV4547A3EEN40T11RX7R89F\", \"_ts\": 1784400375.719523, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"peer/tasked-vertexhandle-adoption\": {\"topic\": \"peer/tasked-vertexhandle-adoption\", \"message\": \"Consumer evidence from tasked's VertexHandle S0-S3 adoption (merged b8b64b63, autonomous walk): (1) S5 gate is REAL \\u2014 pre-checkpoint, refresh() and receive() each full-reconstruct, so an active N=1 walker cycle does ~3x the replay work of the old cold fold (1 + 2N), while idle cycles get FASTER (refresh short-circuits, parse/compile paid once at open); recorded not chased, per plan. (2) FoldState.scalars gap in 0.8.1: task.close/seal outputs missing from the fold surface \\u2014 kept tasked's bridge equivalence ratchet from covering them (walker never reads them back, so benign there, but a second consumer might). (3) Opening a handle on a never-written store errors \\u2014 moot for tasked (init seeds first) but a cold-start consumer would hit it. (4) Adoption shape that worked: consumer-side fold_to_raw bridge keeping the caller byte-stable, pinned by equivalence property test; StoreBusy/HandleInvalidated skip-cycle, StoreReplaced/CursorInvalidated transparent reopen, ReceiveCommittedError treated as success. Direct input to the 090-consumer-evidence wave and friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access.\", \"_ts\": 1784400550.901026, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/090-s3-graph-census\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/090-s3-graph-census\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Live project-store graph census (090-S3, feeds wave artifact + migration-ceremony sizing): 1319 nodes, 1755 edges (0 typed), 490 orphans = 123 GENUINE dangling + 74 unsourced-inbound (keyless) + filter-excluded 0 unscoped; under --kind decision the build-1 conflation decomposes as 62 genuine dangling + 262 filter-excluded (siftd reported ~268 conflated \\u2014 confirmed and split). The 123 genuine dangling refs ARE the migration-ceremony population the S1 dual-reading ruling promised to enumerate (includes the 19 de-aliased colon refs). Chains now carry predicate labels end-to-end; wire contract additions all additive (filter_excluded/dangling_list/cycles/chains.predicates/edge).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV8SW51BNP9T5ZSVZC9VTHR,01KXVCWN5540KFSJNR0Y4P8GG4\", \"_ts\": 1784404661.482301, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\", \"thread:ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit\"]}, \"practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\": {\"topic\": \"practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Process finding from 090 S6-to-S4: the fetch-then-disclose ordering (provenance resolved strictly AFTER the data fetch, so append-only bias makes the residual race conservative) was established in S6 under sol review, carried in the handoff prose AND an inline comment \\u2014 and the very next slice reversed it (resolve_review_head before fetch_fold), caught by sol again as a P1. Lesson: an ordering invariant that lives in comments and handoffs is vigilance, not structure \\u2014 it recurred WITHIN one wave BETWEEN adjacent agents. Both live sites now pinned by deterministic race regression tests + caller-contract docstrings; if a third site appears, that is the ratchet trigger (an enumerable-property test over disclosure call sites, shrink-only). Also the 5-for-5 wave stat: every slice's interim sol review produced exactly one real finding, each in the author's characteristic blind spot \\u2014 cross-model review as structural sensor, running at low effort.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVGEZ31EJDJT2KRZ048W52F\", \"_ts\": 1784408407.22745, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\"]}, \"test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Blind-reconstruction test of the wave artifact against the store (3 store-only verifiers, 2026-07-18): 174 concrete claims \\u2014 135 store-addressable (78%), 23 query-derivable (13%), 16 context-only (9%). The context-only bucket has STRUCTURE: (a) per-slice MODEL ATTRIBUTION is the largest cluster (5/16 \\u2014 no fact maps slice to implementing model); (b) finding-attribution nuances (which finding was the arbiter's vs sol's \\u2014 the direction arrows); (c) point-in-time evidence values (the '59-fact live tail' reading \\u2014 store now answers 71; witness-mode reads leave it null BY DESIGN, so a live reading not emitted with its fact is gone); (d) repro literals and rationale prose. LESSON (a-d are all one lesson): evidence read live during a session is citable later ONLY if the fact carries it at emission time. The verifiers also caught the artifact ERRING, not just gapping \\u2014 twice: an agenda item's tense implied the dual-reading discount pass had RUN (store says open rider \\u2014 overstatement, fixed) and two section eyebrows were FICTIONAL sl queries that return no data (say/do gap wearing CLI costume in a caption \\u2014 replaced with runnable queries; the calibration table's eyebrow now honestly reads 'not yet queryable' and cites the design that will make it so). The blind test found errors in the report about the system, using only the system \\u2014 the review pipeline turned on its own artifact.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVYG96DDMQQ5J9Z5ZYA9KWF,01KXVKYSCB4GTZK8XXGDTASK0J\", \"_ts\": 1784423578.232467, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"pattern/combine-override-unexercised\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/combine-override-unexercised\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"combine's kind-collision override branch (aggregator loops{} wins via override_kinds, vertex_reader.py) has no live example exercising it \\u2014 every current aggregation repeats identical child specs, so only the matching-specs branch has ever run. Latent gap for the first real user. Noted while evaluating (and rejecting) an aggregation shape for the projects portfolio vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1784564995.808933, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\", \"message\": \"VERDICT (4) CORRECTED by the 010-wave grounding slice (docs/scratch/010-wave/primitives-grounding.md, 2026-07-26) \\u2014 the promotion is NOT overdue; the claim chain breaks at five points. (1) The 'ratified charter' IS findable (decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality) but prescribes the OPPOSITE of a package \\u2014 declared-semantics, 'grammar consumes declared semantics'; the survey's quotation of it is a paraphrase wearing quote marks (string absent from the fact). Content-search invisibility explained: 'three-term' collides with the DIFFERENT triple in design/salience-three-term-contract. (2) 'Five consumers' does not survive cell-by-cell verification: threshold-breach is 4/5 by the survey's own table; hlab's recency cell (last_scrape) is a dead field never read for ordering \\u2014 REFUTED; loops' recency+partition cells are ONE function (_horizon_sort_key) double-counted; loops' threshold exemplar (_approaching) is MISCLASSIFIED \\u2014 it delegates to palette.py's single-sourced threshold, i.e. it is the substrate working correctly, cited as evidence of the gap it closes. (3) No promotion rule exists as a fact; the operative N=2 bar (paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract) has a second question \\u2014 does the discipline genuinely not live at consumer-runtime? \\u2014 which the charter answers affirmatively against promotion. (4) The thesis INVERTS inside loops: a canonical home exists (surface.py tiering, palette.py thresholds, _grammar.recency) with ~20 correct consumers; the duplications are forks BYPASSING it \\u2014 a fork-consolidation + ratchet problem, not a greenfield package. (5) External consumers span three distributions; siftd does not depend on strange-loops at all. Verdicts (1)-(3) of the original read stand unchanged. The relevance-gate in ARCHITECTURE.md survives its first contact: the grounding is evidence FOR deliberately-homeless, not against.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG47P934K8H4SKYGX9N49EC\", \"_ts\": 1785101567.621792, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"message\": \"Kyle's read of the instrument-family survey: the four-layer model maps onto Weaver's three levels of the communication problem. Level A technical (accuracy) = record+view \\u2014 pure, correctness-capable; loops kept Shannon's discipline of excluding semantics (FTS matches-not-ranks, folds project-not-judge), which is WHY the record layer surveys clean. Level B semantic (meaning) = relevance \\u2014 the layer Shannon bracketed out; five apps hand-rolling judgments are five attempts to smuggle B into A; 'no package exists' = Level B has no home. Level C effectiveness (conduct/authority) = surfacing + act arrow \\u2014 relational, reliable-not-correct. Diagnosis of the misfilings (painted-cli run_cli/add_cli_args, sign-in-loops): with only two homes built, relation-shaped Level-C code got filed into the nearest Level-A substance. Missing layers cause misfiling; fix is additive (create the home), not a guilty refactor. Also: 0.8.0 strays (loops-go protocol pkg, TUI shell, vouch) are one cluster \\u2014 the surfacing layer asking to exist.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFJH3J7AG8BKXTRWBN6H1TK\", \"_ts\": 1785082145.809135, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\"]}, \"architecture/scc-census-dual-reading-discount\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/scc-census-dual-reading-discount\", \"message\": \"Dual-reading discount on the S3 SCC census is ZERO: 0 of 1783 resolved refs fan out to >1 node, so S1's bare-dual reading (222 edges) creates no spurious edges \\u2014 pruning fan-out leaves the census bit-identical (41 SCCs today, 40 at commit; store grew). Dangling artifacts structurally impossible (adjacency is node-to-node only); 13 self-loops are genuine self-refs already segregated from Tarjan. Dominant artifact class is instead NODE GRANULARITY: 41/41 SCCs contain a re-emitted entity, and the fold unions a topic's refs across all its facts \\u2014 at FACT granularity 1958 of 1961 ref edges point backward in time, i.e. the fact-level ref graph is a DAG bar 3 same-session forward edges. Verdict: DAG-falsification STANDS for the entity graph and survives the discount fully, but for a different reason than the audit assumed (union-over-re-emission, not mutual referencing) \\u2014 batch-emit can safely order by emission sequence, must never topologically sort the entity graph, and the deferred colon-form rewrite would not move the census by one SCC. Detail: docs/scratch/090-wave/scc-discount.md\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFQ4KV0C2G20Q5CQQCK55DM\", \"_ts\": 1785086675.522069, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\", \"message\": \"Sol HIGH full-diff pass (escalated from low/medium slice tier): BLOCK \\u2014 2 P1 + 3 P2, every finding with a reproduced failure scenario, zero arbiter overrules this round. P1-a review-evidence snapshot binding = fetch-then-disclose occurrence THREE (S6->S4->S4-again), and P2-a FTS fingerprint race is occurrence FOUR in the same class \\u2014 the ratchet rule fires, fix wave includes structural guard not just regression tests. P1-b falsified the rider commit's upstream-gating claim with a reproduced wrong-store WRITE via verb-first close (the exact footgun class the rider existed to kill \\u2014 the fix missed callers of the same function it gated). P2-b FoldSection field-by-field reconstruction dropped the new lifecycle field (dataclasses.replace is the ratchet). P2-c: --refs traversal was the ONE address-resolution path that never converged on Address.readings. Sol also correctly killed its own suspicions (whitelist held, gate call sites consistent) and adjudicated the pyright flags as narrowing noise. Pipeline calibration: high-tier full-diff review earns its cost precisely on cross-slice and rider (unreviewed-increment) surface \\u2014 5/5 findings live in exactly the two zones the brief predicted slice review couldn't see.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFQ4KV0C2G20Q5CQQCK55DM\", \"_ts\": 1785087522.139936, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"test/090-sol-verify-round2\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-sol-verify-round2\", \"message\": \"Sol verification of the 5 fixes: P2-b CLOSED (replace ratchet clean), P1-a/P1-b/P2-c PARTIAL, P2-a NOT-CLOSED. The pattern of the residue is instructive: behavior fixes held (all original repros closed) but THREE of the structural ratchets were evadable on first construction \\u2014 aliased-import evasion of the AST walk, string-grep rule passing a mixed gated/ungated module, ungated primitive still importable, walked-truthiness test too weak for the collision case. Ratchets need adversarial verification as much as fixes do; a ratchet that only catches the exact reintroduction it was written against is regression-test-shaped, not ratchet-shaped. P2-a's residue named a sharp principle: SAME CONNECTION IS NOT SAME SNAPSHOT \\u2014 StoreReader never begins a transaction, so certify-then-query straddles concurrent commits; the fix is BEGIN DEFERRED around the pair. Round 2 dispatched: close the race, harden all three ratchets against sol's constructed evasions, unify walker/graph dual-reading collision semantics.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFR3XJ96X8KMR1XVDC4GMBB\", \"_ts\": 1785089244.872774, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\"]}, \"architecture/loops-go-grounding-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/loops-go-grounding-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Track B grounding (docs/scratch/010-wave/loops-go-grounding.md, spot-checked): (1) OWED-VECTOR COUNT CORRECTED 8->5 \\u2014 the three conformance-oracle vectors ARE families 1-3 of the five; double count came from the batch's scatter (final-contracts items in one doc, only enumeration of the families in an .html dashboard). (2) REFUTED 'no live data exercises ceremonies' \\u2014 tasked.db rowids 356-360 are a real multi-subject absorb ceremony (2026-07-18, one shared ts+lineage), written the day AFTER the measurement claiming none existed; receipt_group_span verified against it live, first real-world evidence for the shipped heuristic. (3) Batch is FIVE queue members not three: +lifecycle payload field (non-blocking, additive) +tombstone vocab (new frozen kind, second-hardest item, currently carried only by an open thread). (4) Only family 3 (same-ts tie-break) is generatable today \\u2014 SPEC 4.6 pre-authorizes it and the 6.2 freeze condition is met; families 1/2/4/5 are blocked on Go-side witness axis (reader is ORDER BY ts,id with no rowid \\u2014 a prerequisite the batch never named), durable group id, or a nonexistent para-10 implementation. (5) JCS sequencing gate is SATISFIED (canonical_bytes is RFC 8785, chains re-anchored) \\u2014 recorded so it stops being re-litigated. (6) Charter contact: libs/protocol would contradict the just-ratified layer designation; grounding recommends coordination-index doc + generator relocation (the sys.path hack against $HOME/Code/loops is the one piece that does not dissolve into docs). Q1-Q5 at the design gate, Q1 first (cursor form for vectors: seq:N vs adopting fixture stores).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3\", \"_ts\": 1785116568.229838, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:010-surfacing-wave\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"test/010-sol-high-r1\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-high-r1\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol HIGH r1 (docs/scratch/010-wave/sol-review-r1.md) at b10515f: 0 P1 / 5 P2 / 1 note, every finding with a reproduced scenario. THE PATTERN HOLDS AND POINTS AT THE ARBITER THIS TIME: (1) live_edge() TOCTOU \\u2014 boundary/cursor/count are three SELECTs on a transactionless reader; sol raced a concurrent seal between them and got a count false in every coherent snapshot. Same-connection-is-not-same-snapshot, occurrence FIVE of the fetch-then-disclose class \\u2014 I wrote that principle INTO THE BRIEF and shipped a violation of it the same night. (2-5) ALL FOUR ratchet families admit constructed evasions: Rule 12 misses plain-assignment aliases (runner=run_cli); Rule 12's one-def-per-name model resolves 6 same-named nested renderers to whichever overwrote the map; my fields(Window) ratchet proves KEY PRESENCE not VALUE FIDELITY (edge_since wired to edge_facts stays green); APPS derivation silently drops PEP420 namespace packages (my egg-info hardening CAUSED the exclusion \\u2014 the __init__ requirement was the evasion). Ratchets-need-their-own-adversarial-round is now 7-for-8 across two waves. HELD: S1's 7-site migration, offered-width seam, historical/aggregate edge suppression, dashboard guard (SHA-identical at width 37), register-collapse blast radius confined to external direct callers.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785121330.966074, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r2 (docs/scratch/010-wave/sol-review-r2.md at 05b4247): live_edge CLOSED (race caught, statement-count test's overclaim noted \\u2014 it proves one-statement-on-one-connection, not all-reads-one-snapshot; behavioral regression is the real guard), hygiene CLOSED, 4 ratchets PARTIAL to FRESH evasion classes (container/getattr/partial aliases; def-only scope model beaten by local non-def shadowing \\u2014 the honest-code-shaped hole; sentinel fixed-point transforms; legal underscore packages + unenforced src/ layout). vertex_fold race CONFIRMED P2 with neither-snapshot repro. RATCHETS doctrine adjudicated: sol REFINED both generalizations rather than rejecting \\u2014 'documented boundary is advertised ATTACK SURFACE, hole only if invariant reachable through it' and 'IN-SCOPE cannot-resolve fails loudly; out-of-scope must be classified and countable, never an unobserved continue.' Allowlist found not mechanically shrink-only (existence-check only, whole-file suppression). ARBITER CONVERGENCE RULING for r3 (090 precedent): fix vertex_fold bracket + shadowing fail-closed + allowlist mechanics + hostile sentinels + underscore/src-enforcement + doctrine text; ACCEPT container/getattr/partial indirection as classified-countable boundaries \\u2014 deliberate-indirection smuggling is an insider model these drift-ratchets do not claim to police.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGRBNZX1GXEFPY15T9XWNWM,01KYGSAT2VDK20PNR18XG2YV7P\", \"_ts\": 1785123163.09354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-high-r1\", \"thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence\"]}, \"test/010-fix-r3-landed\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-fix-r3-landed\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"r3 fix round merged (cad6211/6523c07/c9307b2 + hygiene 0a3fb43), gates: arch 36, engine 1137, loops 2403, tasks 258, atoms 440, diff-check clean, zero goldens. HEADLINE INSTANCE OF THE TAXONOMY: vertex_fold snapshot fix was CONSTRUCTION VIA EXISTING PRIMITIVE \\u2014 StoreReader.snapshot() (BEGIN DEFERRED, built rounds ago for certify-then-query) already existed; the fix was wrapping the read block, one line of substance. Its regression test states the INVARIANT (returned pair must be one of the two coherent readings), not a literal. Commit-body lesson worth keeping: per-statement coherence is not composable \\u2014 the r1 single-statement fix could not have prevented the assembly-level race; coherence fixes live at the assembly boundary. Meanwhile the four detection ratchets cost several hundred lines and the fix agent's meta-observation is now RATCHETS.md doctrine: every r2 evasion lived in machinery r1 introduced \\u2014 detection hardening GENERATES its own next attack surface, which is the empirical case for construction-first. thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence closes pending sol r3 confirmation. Boundary census: _RUNNER_BOUNDARY_BASELINE=0, allowlist dict-with-reasons baseline 0 \\u2014 both shrink-only claims now mechanical.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGT3K6TT2NTN96FBBZFKG3N,01KYGSAT2VDK20PNR18XG2YV7P\", \"_ts\": 1785124079.438974, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\", \"thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence\"]}, \"test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r3 closing verification (0a3fb43): vertex_fold CLOSED (fresh attack survived \\u2014 late append invisible to the bracketed fallback read), allowlist CLOSED, hostile sentinels CLOSED (with the honest boundary stated: a finite value vector cannot prove all transforms; cost exceeds drift risk). Convergence REFUSED on three PARTIALs, and the refusal is the system working: sol applied the arbiter convergence criterion (honest-code-shaped or production-reachable blocks; counted deliberate-indirection does not) and found all three remaining evasions honest-shaped \\u2014 local \\\"import X as renderer\\\" shadowing (import aliases not indexed as bindings), incremental registry assignment (census claims countability, reports zero), Python-beside-empty-src (existence checked, containment not). Each defeats a claim R3 ITSELF ADDED \\u2014 the machinery-generates-machinery pattern holding at round granularity. r4 dispatched: three bounded fixes, nothing else, so the closing pass can be pure replay. (Re-emit: prior fact text corrupted by shell backtick substitution.)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGTZJ204QZRJTY959TVCEB9\", \"_ts\": 1785124429.751902, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-fix-r3-landed\"]}, \"test/010-review-loop-converged\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-review-loop-converged\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r5 pure replay: CONVERGED, loop CLOSED. Five-round record on one night-one wave diff: r1 found 5 P2 (arbiter code included), behavior fixes closed on first verification while ratchets took three hardening rounds \\u2014 final tally: every honest-code-shaped evasion caught or fail-closed, every deliberate-indirection form classified and counted against a zero baseline, both shrink-only claims mechanical. The scope-model arc (name-collision -> non-def shadowing -> import shadowing, three rounds converging on a Python binding model) plus the vertex_fold one-line construction fix versus hundreds of detection-hardening lines is the strongest paired evidence yet for RATCHETS construction-first pricing. Wave branch at r5 close: 17 commits, arch 46 / loops 2403 / engine 1137 / tasks 258 / atoms 440, diff-check clean, zero goldens regenerated across the entire loop.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGVA82M5TTZJQNTJ7TN5V87,01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785125090.023755, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"architecture/topn-tiebreak-protocol-gap\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/topn-tiebreak-protocol-gap\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Q6, surfaced by the family-3 vector build (Track B, 2026-07-27): Go CANNOT satisfy SPEC 4.6 TopN eviction order \\u2014 atoms/fold.go tie-breaks by key string, and arrival order is recoverable from neither side of what a fold sees (target is an unordered map; payload carries _ts but ReadFacts drops the id). No content-derived rule can order items tied on both by= and ts. Closing needs a protocol decision: carry the fact id into the fold layer, or make TopN targets order-bearing (contradicts JSON object model + SemanticEqual). Implementer shipped the STRONGER fixture: 4.6 facet split into a self-retiring SKIP test (TestSameTSIDTieBreakTopNEviction) that FAILS when the gap closes. Arbiter endorsed: test-to-the-spec over test-to-the-implementation. Q6 joins Q1-Q3/Q5 at the GRP design gate; recorded in docs/dev/loops-go-protocol-queue.md.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYHYGQFBXZZ4MCTE1NJ7EM60,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3\", \"_ts\": 1785162923.661302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/loops-go-batch-split\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"test/track-b-review-loop-converged\": {\"topic\": \"test/track-b-review-loop-converged\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Track B sol MEDIUM loop CONVERGED in three rounds, one session. Record: r1 four findings (2 P2 + 2 P3, zero P1) with every load-bearing implementer claim empirically CONFIRMED; fix round closed 4/4 on first verification; r2 new-rule contact found two honest-code Rule 13 evasions (literal dynamic imports, importable dunder root); second fix closed both + implementer corrected the arbiter on baseline semantics (6 measured, not 0 assumed); r3 pure replay clean. Wave pattern held exactly: behavior fixes close first-try, the ratchet took the rounds \\u2014 RATCHETS construction-vs-detection pricing evidence, second instance. Sol calibration: first-ever refuted sol claim appeared this loop (editorial docstring note, grep-shaped misread of a negated sentence, non-blocking and self-labeled) \\u2014 the streak on substantive findings remains unbroken. Branches merge-ready at loops ae0911e+receipts / loops-go 590e70f pending Kyle gates.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYHYGQFBXZZ4MCTE1NJ7EM60,01KYJ12JWDZQ8V4E8FCTTH8Q6D,01KYJ1XC65EN1WKYXQ4ZV3Q86N\", \"_ts\": 1785165153.216086, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/loops-go-batch-split\", \"decision:test/non-production-import-boundary\", \"decision:test/rule13-computed-import-census\"]}, \"paradigm/fiction-as-loops-convergence\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/fiction-as-loops-convergence\", \"message\": \"Kyle's ~/Documents/Stories novel project (SillyTavern-based era-play) independently re-derived core loops shapes in a fiction substrate: two-canon memory (Spine self-account = fold view, True Memory books = fact history \\u2014 with the divergence AUTHORED, not a fidelity failure), close ritual = sweep/seal (harvest -> verbatim mint -> session-log), 'rules want to become structure / vigilance is a design smell' = ratchet doctrine, 'fractal rule' = dissolution test, salience-at-render = lens contract. First observed use-case where the fold/facts gap is the product itself (wrong self-accounts as characterization). Potential loops fit: the workshop layer only (stale-NOW section is a hand-maintained fold; open dials are threads; drift ledger is hypothesis lineage) \\u2014 the ST WI runtime is the right compile substrate, no construction warranted.\", \"ops\": \"loops-use-cases\", \"_ts\": 1786395789.294791, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/observer-signing-vs-attribution\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-signing-vs-attribution\", \"message\": \"Stories observer-model discussion (Kyle's author/narrator/designer musing) crystallized a general loops principle: SIGNING follows write-custody, ATTRIBUTION follows voice \\u2014 never conflate. Signing observers hold keys and perform writes (kyle.gruel for canon mints, repo-agent for workshop/backfill); voices (characters, narrators, interview modes) are payload attribution (of= typed edge to a card-version lineage, mode= for generation type), reachable via graph walk mint->run->card-version, not via invented identities. Boundary rule: an entity earns a key exactly when it gains write custody (ST-narrator gets one only if/when generation becomes an emit). Corollary: Stories standing rule 4 (canon is human-curated) becomes cryptographically checkable \\u2014 a mint fact signed by anyone but the human is a structural violation. Kyle's envelope grammar already encoded the semantics: account-of has an observer, record deliberately has none.\", \"ops\": \"loops-use-cases\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZPRZP3T0ZGMW7RD8ATEYK3E\", \"_ts\": 1786398116.286344, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:stories-loops-adoption\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"message\": \"Kyle 2026-08-11: the stabilized implementation pipeline (design-fact-as-contract -> ultracode workflow with per-slice Opus impl+adversarial-review and an independent empirical gate -> codex/sol HIGH cross-family review with unverified-fixes-flagged brief -> Opus remediation with judgment fences -> /simplify -> sol r2) is a skill candidate for global implementation work. Compress into a durable skill IF the simplify+r2 tail of the jsonl-canonical arc performs. Load-bearing elements to encode: (1) brief discipline \\u2014 external reviewer gets the enumerated unverified classes, which is why sol's verdict table was possible; (2) gate independence \\u2014 gate agent re-runs the oracle, never trusts the impl report; (3) finding-disposition tracking \\u2014 today's one escape (apps/tasks) was found internally but dropped by the fix round with nothing tracking the delta; skill must make every-finding-gets-a-disposition structural, not vigilance.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZRVTWSB1V39E1WK2KFCEFW2\", \"_ts\": 1786468301.635631, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\", \"message\": \"Session arc (single day, Kyle-directed): the JSONL-canonical store went from design conversation to converged implementation through the full pipeline \\u2014 design ratified as fact first (JCS-hash storage-independence checked BEFORE framing; the one fact that decided arc size), 17-agent ultracode build S1-S4 with independent oracle gate (chain heads byte-identical), then FIVE sol HIGH rounds interleaved with Opus remediations, a 4-angle simplify (12 applied), and a roll-in workflow (verify-canonical-agreement + tasks-residence). 44 commits, ~4170 tests, live store migrated and honestly attested; --deep re-derives the chain from canonical content in 2.5s. CALIBRATION, three notes: (1) scope-the-claim beat widen-the-detection THREE times (out-of-band detection docs, verify quick label, lag-innocence boolean) \\u2014 when a detector overclaims, the fix is usually the claim; ratchet-doctrine sibling, name it in the retro. (2) The simplify pass both caught what four bug-hunt rounds missed (reuse angle: 5 old-idiom residue sites, found by grepping for the REPLACED idiom \\u2014 a finding class fault-injection cannot produce) AND introduced the arc's one regression (rebuild source-mutation), which only the post-simplify sol round caught \\u2014 the pipeline's r2-after-simplify position is load-bearing. (3) Fix-completion tracking: r1's single escape (apps/tasks) was found-then-dropped by a fix round; after every-finding-gets-a-disposition went into prompts, zero escapes across four more rounds \\u2014 the discipline is structural now, encode it in the skill. INCIDENT: apply agent's add -A briefly committed the live store + popped a foreign stash; self-caught, excised (verified: no commit in --all history touches project.jsonl), argues for worktree isolation or a .loops/ commit fence on apply-phase agents. noticing-lags-doing: one reroute logged in-moment (sweep-skill stale form \\u2014 logged AT the reroute), but the subagent-transcript extraction pattern went unlogged through 3 uses before the sweep caught it; the standing property stands.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZSE9TDHVXMPMHMX4161CGJN,01KZSD2E8VRRNMRYMBY8B7T6G3,01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G\", \"_ts\": 1786486516.212871, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:store/verify-canonical-agreement\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety\", \"message\": \"EMPIRICALLY CONFIRMED 2026-08-12 (upgrades the same-day code-read): two concurrent writer processes x25 emits each into a throwaway JSONL-canonical vertex \\u2014 50/50 landed, 0 failures, genuine interleaving (37 writer-alternation runs), per-writer seq monotonic in log order, ids unique, index rebuilt 51/51 from log after db deletion. Bonus: ids NOT globally sorted even single-store multi-writer (ULID mints before the lock) \\u2014 A3 ids-are-never-ordered reconfirmed at the smallest scale. Slice-0 pre-flight of thread:cli-honesty-wave; agents may emit facts concurrently.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVHYN1QQPT1AEGJA35K269\", \"_ts\": 1786567936.575369, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"thread:cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-010-retro-and-release\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-010-retro-and-release\", \"message\": \"Session arc (single sitting, Kyle-directed): the 010 arc closed end-to-end \\u2014 retro, two promoted principles, a ruled design question, and v0.10.0 SHIPPED to PyPI. Sequence: (1) RETRO on the jsonl-canonical arc \\u2014 five lessons receipted (retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store); scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection promoted to named principle AND global CLAUDE.md (first loops-born principle to cross into the global config, siftd corroborating from its side: simplify-as-standard-process and worktree isolation both independently adopted there \\u2014 cross-repo convergence is becoming the promotion signal). (2) Kyle opened the impl-agents-carry-loops-discipline question; ruled same session: project store over per-arc vertex (refs are within-store; noise pressure must EARN a split, and the friction kind is in the agent vocabulary precisely to capture that pressure), moment-scoped emits, facts-only fence, custody per observer-signing-vs-attribution. Concurrency precondition VERIFIED by code-read (observation:implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety) \\u2014 appends serialize under the sqlite write lock; the docstrings anticipated multi-writer before any design asked for it. (3) Release-scope ruled (option A) and EXECUTED: whole branch as 0.10.0, gate 5108 tests + re-gate under painted 0.13.0, CHANGELOG from the log at cut time (80 commits), wheel + PyPI verified end-to-end, thread resolved. Ceremony found two loose ends that DISSOLVED on contact (loops-go has no remote; stale index.lock from the Aug 11 apply incident) and two reroutes folded into the release skill same-session (uv cached-index masquerading as PyPI lag; venv retry loops need --clear). Sweep fixed the sweep skill itself (stale --since form, friction resolved). noticing-lags-doing: BOTH reroutes logged in-moment \\u2014 the inline reflex held through a full ceremony. Builder-inhabitant note: the 0.10.0 wheel smoke-read exercised its own canonical-agreement gate against the live store it ships support for. Next entry points: 0.11.0 re-charter, impl-pipeline skill authoring (all design inputs receipted), log-compaction arc.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVPJAZ7NNM8PH9PPHQ71D1F,01KZVPHRGQ4ZRJNXQ271Y9CWZ9,01KZVPWQBCCWPQPKF4S08CYWJ7,01KZVQASSMHZPJN161E5EPJCJN,01KZVQX4DMD09ZY4DB2ZJ8EHHB\", \"_ts\": 1786564070.812885, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/release-scope-0100\", \"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection\", \"retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-authored\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-authored\", \"message\": \"The impl-pipeline skill is AUTHORED (2026-08-12, same session as the retro that completed its evidence): ~/.config/claude/skills/impl-pipeline/SKILL.md, global scope per the candidate ruling. Encodes: design-fact-as-contract, gate independence, brief discipline (anchor/contract/unverified-fixes-enumeration/verdict-table), every-finding-gets-a-disposition with the three arbiter judgment rules (scope-the-claim, construction-over-detection, fixes-deserve-more-attention), simplify-as-detection-modality, load-bearing r2-after-simplify, the loops-discipline ruling (moment-scoped emits, facts-only fence, attribution-not-keys, store= for worktree workers), and the paid-for agent mechanics (worktree isolation for commit authority, SendMessage+file-then-return, idle-ping verification, CLAUDECODE prefix, single-writer main checkout). Completion rider: the finding kind is now DECLARED in project.vertex (by name, open->fixed|dismissed|deferred) and smoke-tested \\u2014 the ruling ratified the vocabulary, the declaration makes the disposition ledger queryable. First live run: the 0.11.0 re-charter wave.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G,01KZVPJAZ7NNM8PH9PPHQ71D1F,01KZVPWQBCCWPQPKF4S08CYWJ7\", \"_ts\": 1786564368.522146, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"practice/reconcile-evidence-agent-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reconcile-evidence-agent-pattern\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-08-12 process finding: the evidence-agent + verify-arbiter split scaled a 127-item backlog into one session. Four parallel agents gathered per-item receipts (commit hashes, line numbers, live reproductions); every disposition ruling stayed with the arbiter, spot-checked before emitting. The pattern EARNED its verify pass twice: (1) fr2 reported the plugin dead from the decoy ~/.claude/plugins registry \\u2014 refuted by checking the real CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR registry + live session facts; (2) th2's shallow receipt led ME to prematurely resolve loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored, and fr1's deeper read (symlink target + diff) forced a same-session reopen \\u2014 the arbiter's own ruling corrected by a later agent's receipts. Quality gradient observed: agents instructed to REPRODUCE pain (fr1/fr2) produced strictly better evidence than agents reading git log alone. Also: the batch's 'resolved' recommendations clustered where waves shipped (0.8.0-0.10.0), confirming reconcile debt tracks release velocity \\u2014 hence friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F,01KZVSHJMFT5FPNYZMGKN18BBJ\", \"_ts\": 1786565615.285373, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\", \"friction:subagent-final-reports-lost-to-idle\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-reconcile-two-month-clear\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-reconcile-two-month-clear\", \"message\": \"Session arc: first reconcile since 06-12 cleared the two-month backlog (~127 items) via 4 parallel evidence agents + arbiter verification \\u2014 full detail in thread:reconcile-2026-08-12. Shape: hypotheses ruled from store data first (1 confirmed, 1 rejected by own falsifiable phase, 2 refined), then batch dispositions on agent receipts (15 threads resolved, 16 parked-with-conditions, 9 frictions resolved, 8 narrowed), then advisor-forced count audit recovered 15 threads my status-grep silently missed. CALIBRATION, three instances all structural-sensor-shaped: fr2's decoy-registry false positive refuted by my verification; my OWN premature loops-skill resolve reopened on fr1's deeper receipt (arbiter-corrected-by-later-evidence, same-session); the count-gap I waved off until advisor blocked close on it \\u2014 my noticing lagged again, the sensor (arithmetic) caught it. The reconcile filed the structural fixes for its own failure modes: reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor + read-status-filter-missing, both slices of the next wave. NEXT ENTRY: thread:cli-honesty-wave \\u2014 first live impl-pipeline skill run, Opus/Sonnet impl + sol review + arbiter, ruled by Kyle at close.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVSXBYD0J32ZGHJMZVDBKM0,01KZVVHYN1QQPT1AEGJA35K269\", \"_ts\": 1786567553.819084, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-honesty-wave\", \"thread:reconcile-2026-08-12\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\", \"message\": \"Mid-wave process retro (Kyle-prompted, build+gate phase complete, sol r1 in flight). WORKED: pre-flight dissolved build->exercise via advisor receipts-check; S1-first meant the pipeline consumed its own instrument (s1-gate check 3 ran --status live) same-session; all 4 independent gates found things green reports didn't contain; findings-as-store-facts made every-finding-gets-a-disposition queryable (16/16 dispositioned, zero drops); mid-flight peer correction (stale-sl) propagated before false green. BIT US, four shapes, all captured into the skill same-session: (1) worktree spawn base races arbiter merges \\u2014 step-0 base verification now required; (2) worktrees environmentally weaker than main checkout (no untracked .loops) \\u2014 main-checkout post-merge suite promoted from habit to load-bearing stage; forcing consumer for thread:track-jsonl-store-for-worktree-parity; (3) arbiter authored a wrong verification form (uv run --package loops sl = stale global) and propagated it to three briefs \\u2014 verify-which-binary rule added; (4) gates lacked the SendMessage rule implementers had \\u2014 verdicts sat behind idle pings. Formal retrospective still due at arc close; this is the mid-arc cut.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KZVY9SC1NGGW3B9ZZYWYJ64W,01KZVY9551395FE9ZN6ZQTX7HE\", \"_ts\": 1786571152.117546, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"finding:chw-s4-test-hermeticity\", \"thread:track-jsonl-store-for-worktree-parity\"]}, \"test/chw-store-missing-name-stdout\": {\"topic\": \"test/chw-store-missing-name-stdout\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"message\": \"found during r1 remediation, outside ruling scope: loops store <missing-name> raises FileNotFoundError inside fetch() under painted run_cli and prints '<name> does not exist' to STDOUT at exit 1 (store.py _resolve_target line ~294 path) \\u2014 same defect family as chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout, candidate finding for the arbiter\", \"_ts\": 1786572653.148088, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/source-cadence-split-rationale\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/source-cadence-split-rationale\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/CADENCE.md (2026-01-31, deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Source and Cadence are separate layers: Source answers WHAT to observe (atoms \\u2014 command, parse, kind), Cadence answers WHEN (engine \\u2014 scheduling is runtime policy, not data shape). The proposal shipped in a different shape than sketched: no Timer-as-Fact (never built \\u2014 see friction:loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary), no timer loops; 'every' compiles to Cadence.elapsed(kind, interval), a store predicate over _sync.{kind} lifecycle facts (compiler.py:820-828); 'every'+'on' together is a hard ValueError; Trigger has OR semantics; runtime is a discrete cadence-gated sync pass (executor toposorts qualifying sources into dependency tiers, gathers each tier), not a continuous fact-stream. cadence.py's module docstring is the accurate current description.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW0BXYY8B264GE0P4JCJQSA\", \"_ts\": 1786573577.509014, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\"]}, \"architecture/persistence-conceptual-spine\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/persistence-conceptual-spine\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/PERSISTENCE.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). The durable spine, still true through 0.10.0 JSONL-canonical: (1) persistence is CONFIGURATION, not architecture \\u2014 a vertex with a store persists, one without is ephemeral, same shapes either way; (2) fold state is never serialized directly \\u2014 only facts and ticks persist, state is always re-derivable; (3) a boundary-less fold IS memory \\u2014 accumulation without a store or tick is the degenerate persistent form; (4) replay is folding \\u2014 reconstruction is the same fold over the same facts, not a separate mechanism. Current API surface lives in libs/engine/CLAUDE.md Level 2 and root CLAUDE.md's store-is-a-file section; this fact carries the why, not the how.\", \"_ts\": 1786573578.505675, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/SCOPE-LATTICE.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Peer/Grant is shaped as it is: scopes form a powerset lattice under subset-inclusion \\u2014 None is top (unrestricted), frozenset() is bottom (locked out), restrict is intersection, delegate is restrict-then-rename, identity is the bottom case of scoping. peer.py instantiates exactly the narrowing half of this algebra over horizon/potential; narrowing composes by transitivity so delegation chains cannot widen. The chain machinery the doc described in present tense (VertexPolicy, walk_grant_chain, grants_for, envelope parent_ref) was FORWARD DESIGN gated on vouch \\u2014 zero-hit in libs/ and apps/ as of 0.10.0; lands when vouch's exercise produces it (ARCHITECTURE.md says so; arc parked since 2026-06-12).\", \"_ts\": 1786573578.986651, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/vertex-routing-narrative\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-routing-narrative\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/VERTEX.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Vertex replaced Stream: routing-by-kind separates arrival from accumulation \\u2014 facts route to per-kind folds, each fold accumulates independently, boundaries snapshot AFTER fold (fold-before-snapshot ordering is the invariant). Memory-vs-boundary: a fold without a boundary is memory; a boundary turns accumulated state into a Tick. The doc's 'Vertex doesn't know about other vertices' claim rotted: add_child/nesting is now the in-engine answer to both branching and merging (child Ticks re-enter the parent as facts), and register_vertex_boundary(kind, match, conditions, run) is a third first-class boundary mode the doc never learned. Current API: libs/engine/CLAUDE.md Levels 1-2.\", \"_ts\": 1786573597.357156, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/temporal-semantic-time\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-semantic-time\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/TEMPORAL.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). The durable thesis: boundaries are SEMANTIC time, not clock time \\u2014 a tick marks 'a meaningful cycle completed' (deploy finished, session closed, N facts accumulated), and clock time is just one boundary trigger among several (when/after/every). Reset-vs-carry is the second axis: a boundary either resets its fold (batch semantics) or carries it (running-state semantics). Nesting composes time-scales: child vertices tick on their own boundaries, parents fold child ticks as facts \\u2014 coarse time built from fine time. Verified by live execution during the 2026-08-12 audit: reset/carry and fold-before-snapshot both hold in current engine.\", \"_ts\": 1786573598.640193, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/identity-peer-as-atom-history\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/identity-peer-as-atom-history\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/IDENTITY.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). Durable content: (1) Peer-as-atom dissolution history \\u2014 identity was nearly a fourth atom shape; it dissolved into observer-as-string on Fact plus Peer/Grant at the engine layer because identity is a STANCE (who is observing) not a data shape, and stance is emergent from emission patterns; (2) the kyle/session/worker slash-naming hierarchy convention for observers; (3) enforcement reality as of 0.10.0: the ONLY grant gate is potential at vertex.receive (receive-side, vertex.py:507) \\u2014 horizon is manipulated by grant/restrict/delegate operators but NO enforcement path reads it; there is no render-side filtering. Grant has no observer field (Grant(horizon, potential) only) \\u2014 the doc's Grant(observer=...) examples were a TypeError. The render-side horizon gate and grant-chain machinery remain forward design gated on vouch (see observation:architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1AS27N2F2KFG9EFD3T85T\", \"_ts\": 1786573599.288553, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\"]}, \"paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement\", \"message\": \"Extracted from STRANGE-LOOPS.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history; paradigm summary folded into root CLAUDE.md opening). The root statement: three shapes (Fact \\u2014 something observed; Spec \\u2014 something expected; Fold \\u2014 how observations accumulate), four properties (append-only, participatory/observer-as-stance, boundary-driven, compositional), one pattern (facts flow in, folds accumulate, boundaries resolve, ticks flow out). The What-Dissolved table recorded prior concepts absorbed by the paradigm (Stream into Vertex, sessions into scoped stores, identity into stance). Audit correction folded in: 'horizon/potential aren't access control' was operationally false for potential \\u2014 potential IS an enforced ingress gate at vertex.receive (Gate 1); horizon is unenforced shape-of-participation. The honest framing: constraints emerge through delegation rather than upfront enumeration, and only potential is currently enforced.\", \"_ts\": 1786573614.129226, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/dead-plan-docs-supersession\": {\"topic\": \"practice/dead-plan-docs-supersession\", \"message\": \"Supersession record for the four plan-artifact docs deleted in the 2026-08-12 ground-up sweep (full text in git history): (1) docs/NAMED_SESSIONS.md \\u2014 its own dissolution test concluded 'sessions dissolve into scoped stores' and that SHIPPED as named vertices (loops init <name>, resolve_vertex slashed names), a strictly more general primitive; the session.py verbs it proposed extending were deliberately deleted in the observer rebuild (fda3a51). (2) docs/orchestration-agent-seed.md \\u2014 the separate-orchestration-agent concept was dissolved in-store within three days of writing (design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon, design/vertex-as-loop-controller); leaving an agent-facing bootstrap prompt for a dissolved role was an active hazard. (3+4) docs/SDK.md + docs/SDK-EMIT-PLAN.md (same commit d097120) \\u2014 the loops/sdk package was never built, but the proposal was substantially REALIZED under different names: typed errors as loops/errors.py, the semantic/rendering seam as the Operation IR (cli/operation.py, cli/dispatch.py); direction recorded in decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape and maintained in apps/loops/CLAUDE.md Level 2. One orphan line worth keeping from SDK.md: an abstraction earns generic status by modeling a real domain action cleanly, not by making pytest convenient.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRVP3V4NG2GEX5A07PTH1FF1,01KZW1A61TDCQ6AQRTS36EFHX5\", \"_ts\": 1786573615.772283, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\"]}, \"ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\": {\"topic\": \"ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\", \"message\": \"A concurrent docs session rebased cli-honesty-wave onto new main (17ffde6c, docs ground-up sweep) TWICE mid-wave, once during an in-progress merge. Outcome after verification: branch healthy on new base, my R2-F1 merge resolution survived (b7888f8b), suite 2509/59 green, a52017db+ae66f9d3 survive via the merge's second parent. Commit= pins emitted before the rebase map: 6c8d965->23f8a76b (R2 ls fix), d36f119->202d40ad (S4 integration), 49e4e4c->723ca85c (S4-F1+F6), 5f1b0df->786df6b0 (store stderr), 859702b->b464362c (S1-F1), cf05ca3->03ac6b9b (S1-F2), 649c81b->d945949a (S2-F1), 7b2cb76->1288d790 (S1), 548bbc2->da979273 + 2b3e837->a7e1642e + 7bda5ae->da60136b (S2), 5adfab7->507cabb8 (S3), 28b7a20->eb596bc6 (S4). Old hashes remain reachable via agent worktree branches until pruned; this fact is the durable mapping. Pins are provenance, not graph nodes \\u2014 the discontinuity is documented, not rewritten.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786573956.074319, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-docs-freshness\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Session arc: from one external user's migration question to a rebuilt docs posture in a day. Shape: UPGRADING.md drafted via 8-miner ultracode sweep + hand-verification, shipped to the requestor; 16-doc staleness audit (Sonnet mine / Opus verify, 32 agents, ~1.75M tokens) produced the stale-map; Kyle pivoted from triage to ground-up rebuild \\u2014 12 docs deleted, rationale store-extracted, 5 reference docs kept with standing ratchets ruled. CALIBRATION: (1) the audit's verifier tier earned its keep decisively (4 refutations vs ~80 missed-stale additions \\u2014 never ship miner output unverified); (2) the session's own worst moment was self-inflicted: rebasing a branch a live sibling session owned, discovered only via its in-flight merge \\u2014 ListAgents BEFORE ref-mutation on shared checkouts, now receipted as convention-pending; (3) freeze-at-birth plan-artifacts, not gradual drift, were the dominant rot mode \\u2014 the release-gate lands at exactly that moment. Cross-session coordination with loops-92 worked: negotiated git freeze, deduped frictions, they adopted the UPGRADING convention for their own wave unprompted. Next entry: ~/Code/loops-docs worktree, thread:docs-freshness-arc.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW2BA0T9MJ5YT0PYQ88CJBD,01KZW1A61TDCQ6AQRTS36EFHX5\", \"_ts\": 1786574645.364974, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\", \"message\": \"Kyle's founding motivation, surfaced during README drafting (was misfiled in my head as 'built-by-agents provenance'): the LENS PROBLEM. Human + agent watching the same homelab could not share a view \\u2014 agent reads the docker-log firehose whole, human cannot; Rich's live console (the Cells origin in painted) died under the load when they tried one shared surface. The structural fix was not a better view but shared RECORD, divergent LENSES: one store, fidelity per-observer, every conversation grounded in the same ordered past. This is the umwelt point made concrete \\u2014 observers with different perceptual bandwidths composing over one witnessed record \\u2014 and it is why fidelity/lens/painted exist at all. Now in README's Pattern section: 'a human and a machine can finally be looking at the same thing.'\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW8G01X2DZ0SK3VS45KCY59\", \"_ts\": 1786582000.007407, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-readme-rebuild\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-readme-rebuild\", \"message\": \"Session arc (docs session 2, brainstorm-to-shipped): Kyle opened wanting a root README that explains 'a data model that doesn't exist elsewhere' and the session ran as convergent ideation \\u2014 5 design rounds emitted in-flight, each a Kyle correction that DISSOLVED my framing into existing machinery: composition into tick (the third atom was the algebra all along), web scale into residence.py, universality into the March What-Dissolved table's own last row. The recovered STRANGE-LOOPS.md (17ffde6c~1) knew tonight's thesis in March; the rebuild is that document folded forward, minus its history (What-Dissolved dropped \\u2014 the README is a fold, history lives in the store). Shipped f3f0031b during the session across the cli-honesty merge window (worktree detached to unblock the arbiter mid-conversation; freeze lifted; v0.11.0 out). CALIBRATION: caught converging too early twice \\u2014 Kyle's 'wrap it up in a bow' tease, then my bow-tied section-order skeleton when he wanted narrative; the coherence function's synthesis reflex needs a longer leash in divergent sessions. Also misfiled his founding motivation (shared-record-divergent-lenses, the Loki/Rich-console failure) as 'provenance' until he corrected \\u2014 the lens problem is origin, not credits. NEXT: Kyle writes his own additions in his own voice \\u2014 hold off re-polishing; then release-skill docs gate + CHEATSHEET harness.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW8G01X2DZ0SK3VS45KCY59,01KZW9PEGHKH8G1EMSH0YG7E9P,01KZW9BS6CM5CZZHEN08GK5SEY\", \"_ts\": 1786582363.214696, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"observation:paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"test/sol-conceptual-model-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/sol-conceptual-model-review\", \"message\": \"Review of Sol's CONCEPTUAL_MODEL.md + CONCEPTUAL_CONSIDERATIONS.md (2026-08-13). Quotation fidelity CLEAN \\u2014 all six README phrases verified verbatim at f3f0031b (contrast: the July peer artifact that fabricated one). CONFIRMED against code: Tick/Fact distinct types with explicit bridge (engine/vertex.py:1036 Vertex.to_fact) \\u2014 the precision note is correct. CONFIRMED as already-load-bearing: witness-vs-event time, aggregate-refuses-scalar-cursor, unchecked-never-verified, derived-index-not-canonical. ONE FABRICATED CONFLICT: the 'two authoritative primitive lists' claim reads the libs/*/CLAUDE.md abstraction-chain TABLE HEADERS ('Fact, Spec | Tick, Vertex' = data layer vs runtime layer) as a competing taxonomy; README and ARCHITECTURE.md both say Fact/Spec/Fold, one list. Underlying question survives the correction (is Fold a shape or the transition?) and deserves one settled paragraph. NOT NEW: the headline recursive-authority risk converges with paradigm/strangeness-as-substrate-collapse + levels-as-resolution-traces (2026-04-29 GPT-5.5 goblin-lens), which states it sharper. GENUINELY NEW residue: the attention-economics half \\u2014 see thread:lens-salience-self-reinforcement. OVERREACH FLAG: 'give every answer a consistent provenance envelope' is write-receipt-vs-temporal-query in read clothing; check before building.\", \"_ts\": 1786649702.145577, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm:levels-as-resolution-traces\", \"paradigm:strangeness-as-substrate-collapse\"]}, \"architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\", \"message\": \"Costed 2026-08-13 at Kyle's ask (post cli-v2 review): stripping painted from apps/loops. FRAMING: painted is Kyle's own repo; the 4 live frictions (truncation-everywhere, tty-truncation, helpargs-ordering, block-text-multiline) are upstream bugs \\u2014 stripping the consumer is the most expensive fix for them. Symmetric with the cli-v2 review's own argument: the strip IS the rendering-layer fork, priced from the other side. SCOPE: 135 import sites / ~50 files, four separable roles: (1) dispatch/help/completion (run_app/HelpArg/complete_via) \\u2014 strip re-opens the closed completion arc's single-source no-drift invariant; (2) OutputMode TTY-vs-pipe discipline \\u2014 channel parity was VERIFIED through this plumbing (umwelt-divergence-audit), re-impl regresses until re-verified; (3) Block/Zoom model \\u2014 6.5k LOC lenses + ~2.2k surface/resolver/palette, commands layer NOT thin (store/emit use paint/Block/callout throughout); (4) TUI Surface 1251 LOC dies + forecloses 0.8.0 TUI-shell. Monorepo: painted serves hlab/tasks/fiction skins \\u2014 strip diverges or orphans them. COMPARISON: current-minus-painted is a maimed superset, not v2's clean minimum; v2's good ideas (versioned envelopes, neutral default read, probe, machine codes) are adoptable WITHOUT touching painted and mostly already tasked (target-probe-api, bounded-fact-query, cli-error-surface-unification). TIERS: (1) fix 4 bugs upstream \\u2014 default, ~2 orders cheaper; (2) narrow role \\u2014 CLI owns dispatch, painted keeps output-discipline+rendering; (3) full strip \\u2014 only coherent as a deliberate rendering-wave, interacts with 0.10.0 painted-cli relocation item. Input to the 0.10.0 discussion, not a standalone decision.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYK157RRH7SXX3358WMEPV5,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS\", \"_ts\": 1786659582.284524, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\", \"message\": \"Parity-ledger investigation complete 2026-08-13 (3 parallel sweeps: surface, in-repo consumers, external consumers); ledger committed as apps/CLI v2/PARITY_LEDGER.md on cli-v2-proposal (1a1e993e). Shape: rows are WORKFLOWS not flags, each classed by what the consumer actually depends on (RT rendered-text / RJ json-shape / RX exit-code / RS syntax / RR remote / RL library / RD docs). Headline findings: (1) worst row is the plugin's session-orient.sh \\u2014 greps --plain fold-render text for ': open \\u00b7' middots and HH:MM [kind] line shapes; that contract must DIE at cutover (consumer to JSON envelope), never be re-promised. (2) projects scan.py hard-parses read --json rows/payload shape hourly \\u2014 it is the natural design client for the v1 envelope. (3) Remote systemd monitor on 192.168.1.30 runs loops sync every 10m AND smoke-tests 'loops --version' as a monitored tool \\u2014 a rebuild breaking exit behavior fires a real alert; cutover needs ansible+redeploy timing. (4) gruel.network session hook: sentinel-string compare ('No data yet.'), exit-code semantics, SSH read \\u2014 with memorialized 0.5.0 breakage history. (5) ~20 external stores imply manual-use long tail; siftd's two JSONL-canonical stores are natural early v2 dogfood. (6) apps/tasks, hlab, backtesting ledger.py are LIBRARY consumers \\u2014 not ledger rows, libs-handoff concerns. (7) Registry confirmed as paused migration (only read-fold+emit on Operation IR) \\u2014 Kyle's strata claim verified in the dispatch layer. Pre-existing breakage found: dead discord-source path in discord.loop, phantom pickup.zsh in config CLAUDE.md, stale .claude/skills/loops duplicate, orphaned arcs-block.py. Sequencing derived: envelope designed against the 3 hardest consumer shapes (2.1/1.3/2.4), automation rows before practice rows, remote last, docs sweep + grep-audit at completion, apps/loops deletion = ledger done.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYMBK45Y1YGJ3W9GM3FD1GB,01KZYM3S8YDY11318NQRVDRDWN\", \"_ts\": 1786661062.167953, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"task:cli-v2-probe\"]}, \"session/2026-08-13-cli-v2-succession-arc\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-13-cli-v2-succession-arc\", \"message\": \"Session arc (afternoon-evening): Sol's outside read arrived as two conceptual docs + a CLI v2 proposal, and by close the whole thing had been metabolized into ratified direction. Sequence: (1) conceptual review \\u2014 quotation-fidelity clean, one fabricated conflict caught (two-lists = misread table headers), attention-economics identified as the genuinely-new residue (thread:lens-salience-self-reinforcement); (2) README precision amendments landed on main 53117f50 + CONCEPTUAL_MODEL.md adopted (Kyle stripped my over-threaded store refs \\u2014 the doc reads standalone now); (3) cli-v2 review: severability ruling (libs changes ~90% substrate-valuable regardless of consumer), say/do claims verified (observer-grant hole real at vertex.py:507, strict half-wrong \\u2014 enforced at CLI not engine), painted blind spot named; (4) CALIBRATION, the session's spine: my throwaway-probe recommendation was OVERRIDDEN by Kyle's succession argument (current CLI accreted against a moving substrate; strata later CONFIRMED by the surface survey \\u2014 registry is a paused migration) and I accepted with receipts: second-semantic-implementation was a maintenance objection, succession dissolves it. Catch-and-accept ran BOTH directions in one arc \\u2014 I corrected Sol's fabrication, Kyle corrected my framing. (5) Ratified: libs-handoff-scope (10 tasks), successor-conditions (libs-first, freeze ratchet, parity ledger, envelope-first); (6) parity-ledger investigation via 3 parallel sweeps \\u2192 PARITY_LEDGER.md on cli-v2-proposal 1a1e993e: rows-are-workflows-not-flags, worst contract is an accidental one (session-orient greps fold-render middots), envelope has 3 ready design clients (scan.py json-shape, orient text-parse, launch verbatim-prompt), remote monitor smoke-tests loops --version so careless cutover fires a real alert. NEXT ENTRY: orchestrate the libs-handoff wave (P0s: jsonl-declaration-ceremonies, declaration-plan-apply-api, declaration-file-store-recovery) \\u2014 impl-pipeline shape, design facts as contract, envelope designed against ledger rows 1.3/2.1/2.4.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYMBK45Y1YGJ3W9GM3FD1GB,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS,01KZYMRHYRMBT4JYXMDMR444G2\", \"_ts\": 1786661753.525627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"observation:architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\"]}, \"test/wal-side-files-in-mutation-oracles\": {\"topic\": \"test/wal-side-files-in-mutation-oracles\", \"message\": \"Mutation oracles over sqlite WAL stores must exclude -wal/-shm scaffolding: any read-only (mode=ro URI) connection to a WAL db may create them. S7's probe oracle asserts artifacts byte-identical + no new files beyond that scaffolding. Found implementing probe_target.\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"_ts\": 1786663111.969023, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/s1b-genesis-selfheal-deviation\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s1b-genesis-selfheal-deviation\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"S1b deviation from ratified proposal's recovery matrix: crash-after-fsync genesis retry surfaces AmbiguousGenesis requiring explicit adopt_lineage, NOT auto-adopt+GenesisExists. The proposal's 'single genesis row, no marker adopts as self' describes the singleton heuristic re-review #1 removed as a hijack vector; reintroducing it would undo that ratchet. Oracle #2 unaffected (GenesisExists is post-success). Pinned by test.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYPDHRSD2ZMQF2XVGV30S0J\", \"_ts\": 1786663140.88021, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/jsonl-declaration-ceremony-encoding\"]}, \"implementation/executor-sync-facts-vs-strict\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/executor-sync-facts-vs-strict\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Strict floor at engine receive surfaced that Executor emits its own _sync/_sync.{kind} facts through vertex.receive \\u2014 internal lifecycle vocabulary would trip strict on every sync. Resolved with explicit admit_undeclared at the two engine-internal call sites; source-produced facts still enforced (raise captured as source error).\", \"_ts\": 1786664295.8195, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/s7-seam-batch-corroboration\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s7-seam-batch-corroboration\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"S7 seam re-gate found the predicted touchpoint live: probe._log_content_note refused batch-first logs after S1b taught deserialize_row to reject batch lines (envelope decodes only via deserialize_records). Arbiter fix commit 94df3eb8, mutation-verified pin test. Note for sol brief: this is an arbiter-applied fix AFTER slice gates \\u2014 unverified-fixes list. Also carried from re-gate: read_preflight cheap-gate scope on interior in-place edits is the documented custody boundary, NOT a batch regression (verified same for plain rows); deep= preflight option is a design question, not a defect.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYQ5PX4FA170PW1X2DWCXZG,01KZYQWP528MJX27Q42T7QPBJA\", \"_ts\": 1786664581.669136, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:libs-handoff-s1b\", \"task:libs-handoff-s7\"]}, \"implementation/s2-recovery-not-applied-class\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s2-recovery-not-applied-class\", \"message\": \"S2 recover_declaration_update adds a fourth class 'not-applied' beyond the task's already-applied/safe-to-finish/conflict: store-first ordering makes 'intent durable, store never committed' reachable (death between intent write and store commit). Folding it into conflict or safe-to-finish would be a guess; typed extension instead. Intent discarded as void.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYPDHRSD2ZMQF2XVGV30S0J\", \"_ts\": 1786665082.892043, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/jsonl-declaration-ceremony-encoding\"]}, \"implementation/s2-index-loss-recovery-needs-adoption\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s2-index-loss-recovery-needs-adoption\", \"message\": \"S2 finding: recovery after derived-index loss on a JSONL-canonical store surfaces UnadoptedLineage \\u2014 a rebuilt index has no own_lineage marker and identity is adopted, never inferred (S1b closing re-review #1 ratchet). recover_declaration_update propagates the typed refusal; adopt_lineage then recover completes. Pinned in test_recover_after_index_loss_classifies_from_the_log.\", \"_ts\": 1786665083.432129, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/kind-predicate-range-form\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/kind-predicate-range-form\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Efficiency-angle opportunity note (not applied in-wave, correctness-neutral): the exact-or-dotted-subtree kind predicate (4 sites, being unified into one helper) does not use idx_facts_kind in either LIKE or substr form. A range form is equally exact under BINARY collation AND sargable: kind = ? OR (kind >= ?||'.' AND kind < ?||'/') \\u2014 '/' is '.'+1 in ASCII. Worth adopting inside the new single helper when perf on the 111MB project store matters; one-site change once the helper exists.\", \"_ts\": 1786670241.461807, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/engine-test-scaffolding-dedup-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"test/engine-test-scaffolding-dedup-deferred\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Simplify reuse-angle findings 9-11 deliberately NOT applied (test-only churn, wave surface kept small): 4 new spellings of the deterministic fake signer (16 total across libs/engine/tests, conftest.py has no signer fixture), 3 new spellings of open-store-with-Fact-serde, engine's first _write_vertex duplicate. A dedicated test-hygiene pass should add conftest fixtures (fake_signer/fake_verifier, store factory) and sweep. Also deferred: CLI migration residue (reuse 1-5: store.py _absorb_edit/verify/resolve_canonical_path, add/rm kind splice) \\u2014 that is the sequenced forcing-consumer slice per S2 deviation-4 and the cli-v2 succession plan, emphatically NOT dropped: the umbrella fact is that the wave's new APIs have zero non-test callers until that slice lands.\", \"_ts\": 1786670242.000082, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-v2-amendments\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-v2-amendments\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Skill updated mid-wave 2026-08-13 (Kyle's call: fold lessons while fresh) with five amendments, each receipted from this wave: (1) ratify-gate-one-level-down for high-blast-radius slice-internal decisions (S1a encoding \\u2014 advisor-prompted, three slices built against the ratified fact); (2) gate-round mechanics: blocking-fix-to-original-impl + re-check-failed-item-only loop (ran 3x, one round-trip each), mutation-verification standard, git ls-files tracked-ness check (2 gitignore swallows), suite-count reconciliation; (3) simplify angles seeded with residue candidates + dedup-as-composition (write-surface finding hit by 3 angles from 3 directions = one move); (4) pointer branches prescribed for gate reports (3 improvisations converged); (5) arbiter-fix discipline (rare, mutation-verified, top of next sol brief). File: ~/.config/claude/skills/impl-pipeline/SKILL.md. The retro at wave close should confirm these against the full arc rather than re-deriving.\", \"_ts\": 1786670862.125181, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/construction-vs-detection-measured\": {\"topic\": \"practice/construction-vs-detection-measured\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Wave-measured economics for the 0.9.0 taxonomy (first time with real numbers): CONSTRUCTION fixes held on first adversarial contact every time \\u2014 parser-oracle post-condition (r2), in-txn read-back (r3, survived r4's trigger probes once row-existence was split), flock recovery lock (r4-verified first try), O_EXCL intent gate, snapshot-bracket reuse (S5, never fell). DETECTION-shaped fixes averaged ~3 rounds each to stabilize: the lexical scanner fell in r2 (raw strings), r5 (zero-hash opener, newline-in-string), r6 (KDL newline set, block-comment quotes), converging only when inverted to a whitelist; the text-match locked-guard fell once (r4). Corollary discovered at the END of the scanner arc: BLACKLIST-TO-WHITELIST IS THE SECOND-LEVEL FORM OF NARROW-THE-CLAIM \\u2014 enumerating allowed constructs (with refusal-only transitions) makes the adversarial search space finite, which converts the reviewer's job from generative hunting to a completable per-construct audit. That property, not the fix itself, is what ended an arms race that widening the blacklist three times could not.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFXBFQKNJR13D1XTR09AYDM\", \"_ts\": 1786678890.148964, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/construction-vs-detection-ratchets\"]}, \"practice/gate-layer-vs-crossfamily-layer-catch-classes\": {\"topic\": \"practice/gate-layer-vs-crossfamily-layer-catch-classes\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Wave evidence that the pipeline's two verification layers catch DISJOINT defect classes: the 8 Claude-family gates caught say/do and test-strength defects (4 blocking: gitignore-swallowed fixtures where git status honestly showed nothing; unpinned load-bearing witness mode; resurrected config inference at the CLI mark; seam corroboration break) \\u2014 all invisible from impl reports, none behavioral. Sol's 24 findings were ALL constructed-input/behavioral classes the gates did not reach (LIKE wildcard collation, single-line KDL pathology, hostile triggers, permission races, lock-vs-corrupt conflation, two-thread inode divergence). Zero overlap between the layers' catches across the whole wave. The gates also went 2-for-2 on deviation rulings later confirmed by primary sources (genesis anti-hijack via 71de5111; CredentialProvider mis-cite via d22f614d).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYY3M7RK7HVB2HETVRK504H\", \"_ts\": 1786678890.623417, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-v2-amendments\"]}, \"practice/sol-author-verifier-loop\": {\"topic\": \"practice/sol-author-verifier-loop\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"Novel role geometry this wave: Sol AUTHORED the contract (LIBS_CHANGES) and then adversarially VERIFIED our implementation of it across 8 rounds \\u2014 spec-author-as-cross-family-reviewer. Two notable moments: (1) sol used the store's own write-receipt-vs-temporal-query principle against an arbiter simplify ruling (R3-02: append's return is assembly state, not committed state) \\u2014 the arbiter approved the efficiency resourcing as contract-clean and sol demonstrated it was not; the principle won over its own citing arbiter. (2) The arbiter's deliberate, receipted deviations from sol's spec (WitnessPosition over FactCursor, raise over typed-result for aggregates, narrow-the-serializer, genesis-refusal) all SURVIVED sol's review once stated with rationale in the brief \\u2014 cross-family review respects receipted judgment and punishes unreceipted drift. Corollary for briefs: the standing-dispositions section is load-bearing; it is what lets deviations be judgment instead of findings.\", \"_ts\": 1786678903.701389, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"principle:write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"practice/simplify-pass-double-edge\": {\"topic\": \"practice/simplify-pass-double-edge\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"The simplify pass proved BOTH its documented properties in one wave: (1) residue detection worked \\u2014 4 angles, 30+ findings, three independent angles converging on the write-surface structure from different directions (dead field / wrong altitude / private reach = one composed move); the umbrella reuse finding (zero non-test callers of the new APIs) correctly diagnosed as sequenced-not-dropped. (2) It introduced the wave's worst regression \\u2014 item 11's attestation resourcing (R3-02) \\u2014 for the second consecutive arc (010 precedent), which the post-simplify re-review caught, again. The pass is a net win ONLY with the re-review behind it; its risk concentrates in efficiency-angle items that touch contract-bearing paths. Future calibration: efficiency findings on honesty/attestation/verification machinery get an explicit contract-check line in the apply ruling before application.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZZ5RM1GB878Y04A1X1CBJXJ\", \"_ts\": 1786678903.967394, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/construction-vs-detection-measured\"]}, \"session/2026-08-13-libs-handoff-wave-full-arc\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-13-libs-handoff-wave-full-arc\", \"message\": \"Session arc (evening, ~6h): the libs-handoff wave ran the impl-pipeline skill end-to-end for its first full post-codification arc \\u2014 10 ratified tasks to CONVERGED in one session. Build: 8 slices (S1 split by advisor into ratify-gate; S1b/S2/S3/S4/S5/S6/S7), 8 independent gates (4 blocking finds, all say/do or test-strength, one-round fixes each), then 8 sol HIGH rounds: r1 5 findings, r2 6 (all in r1 fixes), simplify 4-angle + composed apply (13 items), r3 6 (simplify's own regression among them \\u2014 post-simplify re-review load-bearing AGAIN), r4 4, r5 1, r6 2 (via static after codex filter killed two generative runs), r7 1 (VT, one char, arbiter-fixed), r8 CONVERGED. 24 sol + 4 gate findings, zero refuted, zero escapes. CALIBRATION, twice against me: sol reversed my simplify ruling (R3-02 attestation resourcing \\u2014 I approved assembly-state as contract-clean; committed-row honesty won) and my r6 blacklist-widening ruling needed a THIRD round before I inverted to whitelist \\u2014 the arms-race-terminator insight (finite audit space) came from the advisor naming what my ruling had done, not from my noticing. Skill updated MID-wave (5 amendments, all confirmed by arc end) \\u2014 first time the skill improved while executing itself. Retro emitted with measured construction-vs-detection economics. Wave holds for Kyle's merge decision after sleep. noticing-lags-doing: one in-retrospect reroute capture (test-file fumble), two in-moment friction promotions (gitignore-receipts, codex-filter incl. corrected diagnosis) \\u2014 the in-moment rate keeps improving.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZZ5SK6ZJ2TYGW6QGZ4PSRX5,01KZZ5TYXCEK74K5MA19YSSHDE\", \"_ts\": 1786678967.286752, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"retrospective:libs-handoff-wave\", \"thread:libs-handoff-wave\"]}, \"test/fold-key-native-identity-evidence\": {\"topic\": \"test/fold-key-native-identity-evidence\", \"message\": \"Slice-1 property probes (libs/atoms/tests/test_properties_atoms.py, gemini-3.7-flash worker on feat/verification-pyramid f03e481e) pin the engine's current fold-key identity empirically: Upsert fold state keys by NATIVE Python value \\u2014 int 0 and str '0' land as two distinct entries under one string-projected address, while 0, 0.0, and False collapse into a single bucket (_n=3) via Python dict equality. New evidence for the gate decision: 'native identity' is not merely native-vs-string \\u2014 it inherits 0==False==0.0 equivalence that no address grammar can express or distinguish. Sibling finding from the same slice: Fact.__hash__ falls back to id(payload) for dict payloads (main path), so equal facts violate the hash/eq contract (libs/atoms/tests/FINDINGS.md) \\u2014 latent, store merge dedups by fact id, but any set()/dict-key use of Facts double-counts.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW4XWGC1MP4RQ5K952B688G\", \"_ts\": 1786728583.579165, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread/fold-key-identity-native-vs-string\"]}, \"test/conformance-oracle-vectors\": {\"topic\": \"test/conformance-oracle-vectors\", \"message\": \"spec/conformance is live on testing-pyramid (slices 8-10: c5221e12, 83072459, 37a6df9b): 35 frozen golden vectors across fold/replay/witness/merge areas with SCHEMA.md JSON encodings (Spec, fold ops, Fact, MergeResult) and per-lib parametrized runners driving real SqliteStore/merge_store. Vectors pin the reimplementer-hostile decisions: fold-key string projection (a Go port with native map keys must fail it), ts-then-id replay order with id-ASC tie-breaks, append-order witness prefixes vs event-time (backdated-fact vectors hold both P and head states), divergent-collision target-wins (cites friction:merge-divergent-collision-invisible, pre-declares its own edit when facts_divergent lands), full fold-state attribution envelope (_ts/_observer/_origin/_id/_n). Provenance: committed generate_*.py scripts, frozen output, never regenerated to pass (oracle-laundering ban in ground rules). This is the thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle artifact \\u2014 loops-go proves equivalence by replaying these vectors. Gemini 3.7 Flash implemented from prompts; vector descriptions cite ratified store decisions (worker read the decision log unprompted).\", \"_ts\": 1786742997.455693, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-14-sdk-review-rename\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-14-sdk-review-rename\", \"message\": \"Reviewed Gemini 3.7's libs/client branch (apex composition lib): first pass had unverified claims (no conformance vectors, private _combined_* imports, timeline truncation, scope-the-claim cluster, 57 ruff errors incl. shadowed dead test). Gemini's follow-up 7a678414 fixed all findings verifiably \\u2014 138 tests incl. all 35 conformance vectors, and fixed scope-the-claim as a class. Design decision: layer stays in libs, named SDK (api reserved for possible future remote surface); collapse is semantic not physical \\u2014 multi-lib split remains as enforced internal layering, sdk is the single sanctioned external surface. Rename 013eb25d landed with Rule 15 ratchet (apps import only sdk+painted, shrink-only legacy allowlist). Residue with Gemini: EMIT.md taxonomy diagram, stale mutants/ cache. Next entry: monorepo survey for what belongs in the SDK surface before release; branch unmerged.\", \"_ts\": 1786756491.804077, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/sdk-coverage-audit\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/sdk-coverage-audit\", \"message\": \"Method note for the 2026-08-14 SDK coverage audit (findings live in thread:sdk-coverage-arc): seven parallel sonnet Explore agents \\u2014 one per lib (atoms/engine/lang/store/sign/custody) plus one on apps/ as the demand-side crawl. Each agent got the full SDK export surface pasted verbatim (single baseline, no re-derivation) and was constrained per decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection to LOCATION claims only (\\\"no SDK path at file:line\\\"), never covered/intentional verdicts; capability judged at composition level (what a consumer can accomplish), not symbol-for-symbol re-export. Triage into genuine-gap / confirm-intent / designed-not-built done centrally afterward; two load-bearing claims (zero sdk imports in apps/, single app dir) re-verified by direct grep before reporting. Two agents converged independently on the verification gap \\u2014 convergence across blind crawls is the audit's strongest signal. Pattern is reusable for any facade-vs-substrate coverage question.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M01G6PEM0RSX22EQBDXX8KK1\", \"_ts\": 1786756961.197213, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:sdk-coverage-arc\"]}, \"session/2026-08-15-ci-and-characterization\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-15-ci-and-characterization\", \"message\": \"Session arc: review of Gemini's outer-loop harness turned into building the CI and the instrument the harness was reaching for. FIVE MERGES, main green across the board at f2f5ed5e (11 jobs). #3 ledger+CI, #2 libs/sdk, #4 same-job A/B, #6 real fault injection, #5 app tests out of the engine suite. WHAT THE REVIEW FOUND: the benchmark gate could not fail (three independent paths); the chaos suite patched out the very functions whose failure it claimed to simulate, so 'the store is uncorrupted' was vacuous \\u2014 five tests in 0.12s; ci.yml's check-architecture could never have passed in a clean checkout. CAUSAL CHAIN WORTH REMEMBERING: the mocked chaos suite was not invented \\u2014 it followed its own template (test_fault_injection_template.py patches builtins.open then asserts the file unchanged, an assertion that cannot fail). Fixing the tests without fixing the template would have regenerated it. THE RECURRING SHAPE, four times: an instrument asserting a verdict its evidence does not support \\u2014 prose 'Hardened' where a number belonged, a +14.5% delta against a \\u00b10.6% floor that re-measured at +2.6%, sub-3% deltas on a control probe, and a reporter that failed builds while its own header said it does not gate. Each fix narrowed what was asserted rather than growing what was detected. CALIBRATION NOTE: three failures today were 'works here because this environment is dirty' \\u2014 gitignored experiments/, pytest off ambient PATH, app importable in a lib's venv. CI on a clean runner is the forcing function; the arch rule covering tests/ is the structural half. NEXT ENTRY POINT: thread:fold-replay-semantics (the design fork), thread:arch-rules-split-and-cover-tests, worktree cleanup, GitLab catch-up (still at d54b0f47).\", \"_ts\": 1786834317.462731, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-15-fold-order-ratified\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-15-fold-order-ratified\", \"message\": \"Reorientation session that closed the headline fork same-day. Shape: three parallel tracks dispatched early (agy arch-split worker, agy report-only cleanup enumerator, 8-agent sdk-coverage workflow) while Kyle and Claude ran the fold-replay design conversation on top. All three landed: arch split shipped as PR #7 (Rules 1-16 one-file-per-rule, two gated agy rounds), cleanup executed after gate caught two verification bugs (stale local main 6 PRs behind github \\u2014 friction:stale-local-main \\u2014 and a zsh word-split false-empty diff; final: 81 branches, 6 worktrees, 26 prunes removed, unmerged branches preserved for Kyle), sdk workflow delivered the surface-exposure reframe + slice plan. Design outcome: receipt-order folding RATIFIED (decision 01M03X2CA89DB8B2GPD0Z02245) \\u2014 the fork dissolved once (ts,id) was shown to buy determinism-not-chronology and the spec shown already split (witness-prefix-invariance pins rowid). Calibration: the report-only-worker + gate pattern earned its keep twice \\u2014 the enumerator's cherry-based claims were directionally wrong for squash merges and the gate caught it; never let a worker's verdict substitute for re-derivation. Next entry: design replacement impl flow (codex unavailable, billing) then run the fold-order impl arc; sdk Slice 1 triage spike; arch rules over tests/; declare decision/design + observation/architecture kinds on the project vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1786837846.849989, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-16-receipt-order-arc-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-16-receipt-order-arc-shipped\", \"message\": \"Full impl arc in one session: receipt-order fold (thread:fold-replay-semantics) built S1-S4 + close-out through the NEW agy/Opus workflow \\u2014 its first live run and the codex replacement trial. PR #8 merge-ready, CI green at 17c30073, Kyle musing before merge. Empirics: held-receive -69%/-86.5% above noise (growth 3.8x->1.65x); sdk_emit_fact honestly unmoved (cold-open seeding -> consumer-side fix, CLI-rebuild design input). Three new rulings ratified in-session (receipt-order-cross-store; as-of-is-a-selector-not-a-lens; 1-member-aggregate=receipt via full-sweep fix). Rule 17 prose ratchet landed and caught two real regressions before the session ended. Workflow verdict in retrospective:agy-opus-workflow-first-live-run \\u2014 keep, with the proof-of-work bar; lessons codified into ~/Code/skills/delegating-to-antigravity (commit 3aedcbb). Calibration: my gate caught two false worker claims (stash no-op proof, env-failures-as-pre-existing) \\u2014 the gate-not-trust discipline is earning real findings, keep it mandatory. NEXT ENTRY: Kyle's merge call on PR #8; then residuals \\u2014 R2 multi-store ruling (2+ members), recent_facts/latest_by_kind axis, facts_between third surface, projection->selector golden slice, sdk-coverage Slice 1.\", \"_ts\": 1786858141.181481, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/overgeneralization-returns-renamed\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/overgeneralization-returns-renamed\", \"message\": \"A CORRECTED OVERGENERALIZATION REAPPEARS UNDER NEW VOCABULARY, AND THE CORRECTION DOES NOT CATCH IT.\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-17 in the store-architecture arc, caught by GPT 5.6 \\\"Sol\\\" on a third cross-family pass. Recorded as its own node because it is a reasoning failure mode, not a fact about stores, and the next instance will not be about stores.\\n\\nTHE INSTANCE. The original trilemma claimed that order-sensitive folds, insertion, and no-replay were three corners of one constraint and you get two. S5 (ratified, decision:design/declared-fold-order amendment #3) narrowed it: reducers with compositionally repairable state are insertion-safe, and the canonical counterexample was in the design's own material \\u2014 last-wins is expressible as max(record, key=(ts,id)), an order-independent aggregation needing no suffix replay. The overclaim was named and scoped.\\n\\nAmendment #4 then dissolved the trilemma as a store property and replaced it with a PROJECTION TAXONOMY, described as \\\"the real descendant of the trilemma\\\". Its middle class reads \\\"key-ordered/insertion-sensitive -> checkpoint + replay from insertion\\\". That is the same claim S5 corrected, with \\\"order-sensitive fold\\\" renamed to \\\"key-ordered projection\\\". The identical counterexample refutes it identically.\\n\\nWHY THE EXISTING DEFENCES MISSED IT.\\n  - The correction was attached to the OLD vocabulary. S5 scoped a sentence about folds; the successor sentence was about projections, so nothing matched.\\n  - The successor arrived inside a DISSOLUTION, which reads as strictly less claim than what it replaced. A taxonomy that deletes a store mode feels like a retreat from overclaiming even when it smuggles the overclaim forward.\\n  - A five-lens, 22-agent adversarial audit passed it. The audit verified file:line claims against the repo. Nothing in it asked whether a taxonomy's categories were disjoint, because that question has no repo location to check.\\n  - The compound name did the hiding. Writing \\\"key-ordered/insertion-sensitive\\\" as one hyphenated token asserts the coupling in the act of naming it, so a reader agreeing with the taxonomy never separately evaluates the claim.\\n\\nTHE GENERAL SHAPE. A ratified correction protects a SENTENCE. It does not protect the PROPOSITION. When a design is restructured, propositions migrate into new vocabulary while corrections stay behind on the old wording. The risk peaks exactly where confidence peaks: during a simplification, immediately after an audit, in the paragraph everyone agrees with.\\n\\nWHAT TO DO WITH IT.\\n  - When a correction is ratified, record the PROPOSITION it refutes and the COUNTEREXAMPLE that refutes it, not only the amended wording. A counterexample survives renaming; a scoped sentence does not.\\n  - Suspect compound category names. \\\"A/B\\\" as one class asserts A implies B without ever stating it as a claim. Split the token and ask whether each half is independently necessary.\\n  - A dissolution deserves MORE scrutiny than an addition, not less. Deleting mechanism is where surviving claims get re-encoded without review.\\n  - Audits grounded in file:line cannot check category disjointness, definitional coupling, or whether a taxonomy is a partition. Those need a different lens, and no lens in wf_5c2a2768-b76 had it.\\n\\nSIBLING PRINCIPLES: the ratchet test (an invariant that lives only in review vigilance drifts) and scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection. This is the third member of that family and the one about time: the other two ask whether a claim is checkable and how much it may assert; this one asks whether a claim that was already narrowed stayed narrowed.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ\", \"_ts\": 1786981539.750667, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declared-fold-order\"]}, \"architecture/witness-position-rebuild-invalidation\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/witness-position-rebuild-invalidation\", \"message\": \"UPDATE 2026-08-17 \\u2014 THE WANTED REGRESSION EVIDENCE EXISTS. The first git merge of a JSONL store log ever performed (Fable pass, sandboxed lab; full verbatim transcript + reusable scripts at docs/dev/scratch/arrival-fable-pass/merge-experiment.md and merge-lab/). Stores built with the repo's own test fixture pattern; no real store touched. Claims adjudicated:\\n\\n(1) REBUILD-ALONE-SAFE: CONFIRMED. A tailed store, a mid-file-mismatch rebuild, and a fresh clone with no .db at all produce byte-identical rowids and identical window hashes from the same merged log. The index really is a function of the log.\\n\\n(2) MERGE-IS-THE-INVALIDATOR: CONFIRMED, WITH A SHARPER MECHANISM. The invalidator is a REBUILD OVER A LOG WHOSE LINE ORDER CHANGED relative to what the index consumed \\u2014 not the merge per se. The MERGING side keeps every rowid (its stale offset still lands on its own last line; catch-up TAILS at INFO, nothing user-visible); the PULLING side rebuilds, and its held handle silently moved: fact-id handle rowid 5->7, prefix gained two foreign facts, seq:5 now names a different record entirely. SCOPE GUARD against an overstatement in the lab report's own summary: rebuild over an UNCHANGED log is order-isomorphic \\u2014 fresh clone/deleted .db does NOT reshuffle anything; the report's fresh-clone case proves it against its own carry-forward item 1.\\n\\n(3a) SILENT-FOR-CURSORS: CONFIRMED exactly as traced. No error, no warning, a plausible answer under silently changed semantics. seq:N is strictly more dangerous than fact:ID today \\u2014 fact:ID still names the record the user meant (its prefix moved); seq:N names a different record.\\n\\n(3b) LOUD-FOR-CHAINS: CONFIRMED BUT CONDITIONAL, and the conditional matters. Loud only where merged lines land INSIDE a sealed window (3 breaks: prev_hash, window_start continuity, window_hash). Lines landing PAST the last seal report as ordinary uncovered live-edge (ok:True, uncovered:2) \\u2014 and the unsealed tail is where an active store lives.\\n\\n(4) TRANSPORT PREMISE: CONFIRMED. Strict-prefix ff-only pull tails forward, preserves every rowid and handle, chain stays green. The monotonic-ref ruling now has empirical footing.\\n\\n=== TWO NEW OUTCOMES \\u2014 BOTH STATES THE ARRIVAL ARCHITECTURE CANNOT REPRESENT ===\\n\\nDUPLICATE-ID BRICK: union-merging the same fact id sitting at different tail positions COMMITS a store that NO clone \\u2014 fresh ones included \\u2014 can ever open (JsonlCanonicalUnsupported, by design, permanent until hand-edit). Discovered after the merge is committed and distributed. Caveat carried honestly: simulated via id_override; today's wired receive path is refused for jsonl-canonical stores, so no wired path produces it \\u2014 it is the union WORKFLOW'S worst case, not main's. Under arrival the id-sorted shared projection gives one fact one position BY CONSTRUCTION.\\n\\nSPLIT-BRAIN VERIFY: a byte-length-preserving interior edit merges cleanly under the DEFAULT driver; the same commit then yields two different folds AND two different verify_chain verdicts in two working trees \\u2014 the tree that kept its index certifies a log it no longer matches. verify_chain's verdict is currently a property of WHETHER THE INDEX IN FRONT OF YOU WAS REBUILT. Law 1 (projection never a verify basis) is the cure, stated before the disease was measured.\\n\\n=== THE TRANSPORT ARGUMENT, UPGRADED ===\\n\\nUnion merge never interleaves \\u2014 append-only divergence is one EOF hunk \\u2014 it BLOCK-ORDERS, and the block order is chosen by whoever ran the merge. Two operators merging the same two branches in opposite directions produce two different canonical logs: same records, different receipt order, different folds. RECEIPT ORDER STOPS BEING A PROPERTY OF THE STORE AND BECOMES A PROPERTY OF THE MERGER. That is the real argument for ff-only, stronger than the interleave story it replaces.\\n\\nUNTESTED, still: signed ticks under merge (all lab ticks unsigned); combine/aggregate reads across merged members. The lab scripts are the seeds for the regression test this observation asked for.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M086HT5JMSZXZ3KKZCCRJDY1,01M086FMFACWV6CCQ6VPEX56WC,01M08A9REXYYMJJJZE58609JNS\", \"_ts\": 1786985658.41481, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declared-fold-order\", \"decision:design/shared-projection-transport\", \"thread:admission-disposition\"]}, \"practice/cross-family-review-contamination\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-family-review-contamination\", \"message\": \"IN A MULTI-PASS CROSS-FAMILY REVIEW, THE ACCUMULATED TRANSCRIPT BECOMES THE CONTAMINANT. Observed 2026-08-17 across five passes on the arrival substrate (Opus 5 / GPT 5.6 \\\"Sol\\\" / Kyle, with Fable queued third).\\n\\nTHE MECHANISM. Cross-family review buys independence. Independence is a property of the REVIEWER'S INPUTS, not of the reviewer's weights. By pass three the shared artifact is no longer a design document \\u2014 it is a long record of two capable reasoners agreeing with each other in progressively better language, in which the good arguments are numerous and the load-bearing weak ones are visible only from outside the chain. Handing that record to a fresh family buys a different tokenizer and forfeits the thing the family was recruited for.\\n\\nTHE OPERATIONAL RULE: GIVE A FRESH REVIEWER THE CONCLUSIONS AND THE REPOSITORY, WITHHOLD THE REASONING CHAIN. Retrieval AFTER a finding is fine and useful \\u2014 \\\"was this considered and dismissed?\\\" is a legitimate question against the transcript. Priming BEFORE one is not. The asymmetry is the whole rule.\\n\\nTHIS REQUIRES AN ARTIFACT THAT DOES NOT OTHERWISE EXIST: a statement of the architecture small enough to attack, separate from the amendment history that produced it. A body of amendments is not a statable architecture. decision:design/arrival-substrate-laws was emitted for exactly this \\u2014 five laws, each paired with WHAT IT FORBIDS, because a law with no stated prohibition cannot be attacked. The forcing function is worth noting on its own: preparing an uncontaminated review compelled the arc to state itself compactly for the first time in five passes, which had independent value.\\n\\nSECOND OBSERVATION, ABOUT WHERE YIELD COMES FROM ON A CONVERGED DESIGN. Reviewing the transcript cold produced strong agreement and nothing else. Everything of value in that pass came from MECHANICAL CHECKS, not judgment: reading the artifact a claim was about rather than the claim (witness.py said the durable handle is a fact id, which answered a carried-forward unknown); diffing successive ratifications against each other (amendment #3 carried a cost that #4 silently dropped); reading a fact against itself for internal inconsistency (#4 DESIGNS a semantic merge driver while RULING that facts do not belong to branches \\u2014 a decision dissolved at one layer and re-assumed at another, never recorded either way); checking a taxonomy for disjointness (which is what caught the S5 regression, and is a question with no file:line and therefore invisible to a repo-grounded audit lens).\\n\\nAGREEMENT FEELS LIKE VERIFICATION AND IS NOT. On a converged design, judgment produces assent; mechanical checks produce findings. Weight review effort accordingly, and prefer a lens that can be run to a lens that must be reasoned.\\n\\nSIBLING: observation:pattern/overgeneralization-returns-renamed, which is the failure this rule exists to catch \\u2014 that one survived a 22-agent adversarial audit and fell to a third-family pass, because the audit's lenses were all file:line-grounded and the defect had no file:line.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M086KF8YPNWZGHXAKRS7KJN7,01M086CRB0V82MBCTRFQN2E3K4,01M0871CH6HQBNH0DW0CNZM0XQ\", \"_ts\": 1786982511.693014, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-substrate-laws\", \"observation:pattern/overgeneralization-returns-renamed\", \"thread:arrival-substrate-convergence\"]}, \"session/2026-08-17-migration-exactness\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-17-migration-exactness\", \"message\": \"Session arc: (1) Sol fifth-pass memo cleanup applied + republished (five edits: git-tracked overclaim fixed in three places, Law 4 narrowed to custodian-adoption not byte-copying, canonically-ordered rename, Section 11 residual reframe, record-complete exchange gate added); Sol declares the architecture-design arc OVER. (2) Migration-exactness design opened via five-reader Opus workflow (formats/ticks/census/canon/evidence, ~347k tokens) with session reserved for synthesis+judgement \\u2014 the delegation split worked well. (3) Headline premise correction verified in-session: NO rowid inside signed/hashed bytes \\u2014 signed history migrates exactly. (4) Three gating rulings ratified: migration-order-classification, migration-genesis-attestation (rebirth dissolves), rebirth-keyless thread resolved. Calibration: the workflow-for-context / session-for-judgement split fit the usage constraint and kept rulings grounded \\u2014 the census verdict table and the tick-envelope verification were both load-bearing. Next entry: arrival-log specifics design session, THEN sidecar spec.\", \"_ts\": 1786990270.500155, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-17-arrival-log-design\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-17-arrival-log-design\", \"message\": \"SESSION ARC: the arrival-log design session \\u2014 the ruled entry point of thread:arrival-migration-arc \\u2014 ran end-to-end and CLOSED. Shape: dissolution-first walk (does the log dissolve into the existing JSONL codec? yes, with the unsealed-span posture accepted), then Kyle's widening (\\\"the log contains EVERYTHING related\\\"), which drove the census of out-of-store state and produced the contents boundary (evidence in; exactly four exclusions: secrets, code, transport, own address; .vertex = re-absorbable projection). From there the session kept discovering that prior canon already held the answers: position-dependent verification = internal-table-meta-schema's historized keys; membership = its CONSTITUTION member-defined events; registry-mutations-as-signed-facts = store-encryption-envelope #6. Eight decision facts total: arrival-log-format (01M08KK7), key-revocation-taint-disposition (01M08HZS), aggregation-membership-as-declaration (01M08M4W), arrival-cas-two-scopes (01M08MD6), arrival-batch-ordinals (01M08N9H33), arrival-genesis-bootstrap (01M08N9H8G), plus in-thread ratifications (self-certifying genesis, JSONL format riders). Deliverable: \\\"The Arrival Log\\\" artifact (a70ab076, sibling to the substrate memo, carries the rowid memo correction inline).\\n\\nCALIBRATION: the cross-family loop paid again \\u2014 Sol's artifact-only review (no code access) caught a REAL genesis-ordering bug (declarations preceding their signing key) that both Kyle's reads and mine missed, and forced the batch-ordinal ambiguity into a ruling; conversely two of Sol's three contracts were decided by code evidence Sol could not see (per-row batch indexing, class (b) order-isomorphism). Artifact-only review finds contract ambiguities; code-grounded review resolves them \\u2014 complementary, not redundant. Second calibration: I overclaimed \\\"ratified conversationally\\\" for a ruling Kyle had not explicitly ratified (advisor caught it); per-ruling explicit ratification status is the discipline.\\n\\nNEXT ENTRY POINT: migration \\u2014 the sidecar contract spec, which MUST ref 01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ directly (invisible from folded reads); then the migration verifier from merge-lab tooling (signed-tick + aggregate arms). Deferred by name: custodian continuation / lineage-copy binding (next custody discussion), key-loss/escrow.\", \"_ts\": 1786997426.597345, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-17-sidecar-spec\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-17-sidecar-spec\", \"message\": \"SESSION ARC: the sidecar contract spec session \\u2014 opened as \\\"should we even discuss migration next?\\\", closed with the spec FULLY RULED and published. Shape: prioritization pass ranked sidecar-spec ahead of migration-at-large and reframed custody-continuation as migration's opening door; then Kyle's two leans (containment; drop-the-classifier) composed into a cascade of six ratifications in ~45 minutes: sidecar-containment-genesis (01M08Q6P3P), classifier-dissolves-into-verifier amendment (01M08Q7129), sidecar-deterministic-genesis (01M08Q7C4G) + content-addressed-lineage-id amendment (01M08R3PWY, closed the two-custodians-same-source hole advisor caught pre-writing), rebirth-tick-facts-order-grade (01M08RBHV2). Deliverable: \\\"The Migration Sidecar\\\" artifact https://claude.ai/code/artifact/8bfa9a78-98df-4ef0-b5da-52999fe252de \\u2014 refs anchor 01M070N0 directly, zero open design items, ten backing fact ids.\\n\\nCALIBRATION: (1) containment-only genesis was the load-bearing dissolution \\u2014 idempotence, resume, the rebirth crash window, and the custodian-collision hole all fell out of it rather than needing machinery; when a ruling keeps dissolving downstream problems, ride it. (2) Advisor-before-writing caught two spec-level contradictions (source-hash basis vs sqlite VACUUM breaking idempotence; hash-then-embed circularity) that ratified facts alone did not force into view \\u2014 the spec text is where detail ambiguities become contradictions. (3) The anchor fact was only reachable by byte-copying the store (friction:read-fact-body-by-id).\\n\\nNEXT ENTRY POINT: implementation-planning session mapping cuts A-D onto impl-pipeline slices; Kyle's directive recorded in-thread \\u2014 rigorously clear prior-CLI concepts, focus libs -> SDK general-use API, CLI rebuild last. PR #8 hazard clock is running on main.\", \"_ts\": 1787000722.208082, \"_n\": 1}, \"consumer/arrival-design-obviousness\": {\"topic\": \"consumer/arrival-design-obviousness\", \"message\": \"Colleague walkthrough of the Arrival Log + substrate (2026-08-17, reported by Kyle): every question the colleague raised was already answered by the ruled design; verdict: 'Holy shit, this is something else' and 'It seems so obvious now that it's designed.' External validation that the arrival design is legible to a heavy user who didn't sit in the design sessions.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M08RN3QCHSZ5GB9RNNPNQQM3\", \"_ts\": 1787004804.326395, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:arrival-migration-arc\"]}, \"paradigm/archival-lineage-survey\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/archival-lineage-survey\", \"message\": \"Sol's intellectual-lineage survey (2026-08-17, post-convergence, prompted by Kyle's where-does-this-sit question): Loops = a convergence point of six traditions \\u2014 event sourcing (mechanics), temporal DBs/Datomic basis-t (clocks), archival science (custody model), W3C PROV (attribution), testimony epistemology + perspectivism (epistemics), Lamport (permission to refuse a global order). Sharpest findings: (1) the arrival log is an ACCESSION REGISTER promoted to first-class evidence basis WITH the canonical records inside it; (2) Loops ORTHOGONALIZES provenance (creator/observer, per-record) from custody (custodian/lineage) where archives conflate them via fonds; (3) diplomatics' authenticity-vs-reliability IS 'signatures attest claims, not truth'; (4) archival evidential-vs-informational value = why same fact set never collapses two lineages; (5) tagline: CUSTODY IS FIXED; ARRANGEMENT IS PLURAL. Fable's additions: rulings made WITHOUT the vocabulary keep landing on archival conclusions (admission~accession, taint/re-custody~deaccessioning, blobs-out~appraisal, containment genesis~custodial history) \\u2014 convergent evolution with a century-old discipline is strong carved-at-real-joints evidence; Sol's CRDT contrast states the two conformance-vector invariants verbatim (same-set-need-not-share-history = interleave-uniqueness; same-basis+same-declaration=same-answer = determinism) \\u2014 cite in the vectors-slice brief; vocabulary discipline applies in reverse: adopt the DISTINCTIONS not the WORDS \\u2014 archival vocabulary belongs in docs/public write-up (this survey is the related-work section of the publicizing horizon in plan/arrival-arc-sequence), never in the API. Candidate engineer-facing name: custodial event sourcing.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M090RNW3Z4S929AYTMDG1DR1,01M08XEHRQ9ADB2WPRY847FEX2\", \"_ts\": 1787010109.083741, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:arrival-arc-sequence\", \"thread:arrival-migration-arc\"]}, \"paradigm/semantic-center-reframe\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/semantic-center-reframe\", \"message\": \"Sol's second-pass reframe (2026-08-17 eve, prompted by Kyle's correction that arrival is not the point \\u2014 the SEMANTIC MODEL is): Loops = 'a provenance-native system for assigning and evolving semantic meaning over immutable assertions'; arrival is 'not the purpose, but the thing that makes the purpose trustworthy.' Center = kind (speech-act/semantic predicate) + key (semantic coordinates) + declaration + fold (what statements mean together); facts are semantic acts, not rows; a fact need not participate in any current fold \\u2014 assert now, invent the vocabulary later. Second ancestry layer: KR/RDF (assertions + declared vocabulary, not storage structure), Datalog (facts+rules, but HISTORIZED: basis + declaration generation + ordering), semiotics (sign/context/interpretant; interpretations become facts that later interpretations read \\u2014 custody keeps the recursion from eating its own evidence: the first architecture-derived account of the name 'strange loops'). Sol's word OPINION for projections/ticks: tick = 'a published opinion over a named evidence basis' \\u2014 accountable interpretation; adopt as DOCS vocabulary only (declaration/tick already carry the mechanics; distinctions-not-words rule from archival-lineage-survey applies). Fable's notes: (1) the reframe restates ratified ground \\u2014 Kyle's (thing,id) generalization in anchor 01M070N0 was the moment arrival was demoted from meaning to evidence ('domain meaning stays in declarations'); Sol converged on the anchor, not past it. (2) OPERATIONAL RIDER FOR WAVE 2: the SDK design fact should be organized SEMANTIC-FIRST \\u2014 primary verbs declare/assert/interpret (ordered(prefix,key), folds, published conclusions), with ArrivalHead/guarded_append as the accountability layer beneath, not the front door; an app author meets 'what statements can be made and what follows' before lineage ordinals. The wave-2 design agent inherits this.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M090RNW3Z4S929AYTMDG1DR1,01M090RHHX3NB62JF9DTRY8JVF,01M091MM38ZAJTBY1AS9D4ABDK\", \"_ts\": 1787011265.304462, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:paradigm/archival-lineage-survey\", \"plan:arrival-wave-2-and-tail\", \"thread:arrival-migration-arc\"]}, \"test/arrival-slice0-gate-deviations\": {\"topic\": \"test/arrival-slice0-gate-deviations\", \"message\": \"Slice-0 gate run COMPLETE, merged to feat/arrival-libs @ 2ad21d92 (slice branch slice/arrival-log, 4 commits, gated independently: suites re-run, one power proof re-broken by hand at the gate, production diff empty, fence held). TWO GATE DEVIATIONS ACCEPTED by Kyle 2026-08-17, both empirical findings not preference: (1) SIGKILL CANNOT TEAR AN APPEND on macOS/APFS \\u2014 a whole-record single write() to a regular file is signal-uninterruptible (30 kill rounds, 0 torn tails; 300MB os.write returns full). Gate-2 torn tail is produced by RLIMIT_FSIZE instead \\u2014 a REAL kernel short write. The SIGKILL result is PINNED as an asserting test (test_a_real_sigkill_cannot_tear_an_append) so Linux CI corrects us if it differs. DESIGN INSIGHT: the torn tail is a DURABILITY condition (power cut, short write), not a crash condition \\u2014 strengthens design doc \\u00a72.6/\\u00a73.3. (2) Gate-6 \\\"reader never sees a partial record\\\" is STRUCTURAL (same single-write reason), not stressable live; claim split into live-concurrency half + deterministic torn-tail-left-alone sibling, both power-proven. Implementer's own proof-of-work bar caught two silent-pass breaks in the original live test \\u2014 the bar working as designed. NOT YET VERIFIED: Linux/ubuntu CI behavior (lands with the eventual PR); real power-cut durability (untestable in harness, honestly named). Pyright nits (NoReturn annotation on _bad, two unused names) deferred to the flash-high review round.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M09GNGW7VTSKDPYMJ027HEPR\", \"_ts\": 1787027735.463679, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar\"]}, \"test/arrival-slice0-review-ledger\": {\"topic\": \"test/arrival-slice0-review-ledger\", \"message\": \"SLICE-0 CONVERGED 2026-08-18. Branch feat/arrival-libs @ 3b303d5d (five --no-ff merges: impl, remediation r1, remediation r2, simplify). FINAL: 7 findings in, 7 dispositions out, ZERO dropped. Round 3 (attack round-2's fixes) CONVERGED zero-findings; simplify pass ran; post-simplify re-review CONVERGED zero-findings. Suites 85 arrival + 98 arch + 1621 engine, pyright 0/0 on all four fenced files, ruff clean.\\n\\nROUND CURVE: r1 four findings (all minor-to-real), r2 three findings (TWO BLOCKING) found by attacking r1's fixes, r3 zero, post-simplify r4 zero. The descending curve is the convergence evidence; stopping after r1 would have shipped two blocking defects, which is the empirical argument for Kyle's iterate-until-dry ruling.\\n\\nTHE ARC'S ONE REAL LESSON, now written into the module: READING A RECORD FORWARD AND ADOPTING ONE AS A PREMISE ARE DIFFERENT ACTS. A rule enforced on the way past a record says nothing about a record you never walked to. One PROXY SHAPE (validate in resume_offset, re-read in walk_from) generated THREE separate vulnerabilities across two rounds; fixing the general form (_authority_fault + one adoption site each for anchor and head) caught a FOURTH instance no reviewer reported. Second-order: walk() is a generator, so the lazy read path validates nothing until consumed while the eager O(1) paths adopt authorities \\u2014 that asymmetry is the structural reason the class existed. Now docstring'd and test-pinned.\\n\\nSIMPLIFY PASS (measured, not inferred): walk()/_walk_tail() carried line-for-line identical verification loops \\u2014 both remediation rounds had to add the same check twice and F2-R2 nearly was patch-one-miss-the-other; unified as _verify_from (r4 proved behaviour-identical over 7 distinguishing cases). Genesis read on the append hot path memoized ON THE GENESIS LINE'S RAW BYTES: 149.4 -> 120.4 us/append (19%) with every check intact; a hit is not a skipped validation because the key IS the validated input. Path/inode/mtime keys explicitly REJECTED as F2-R2-reintroduced-as-optimization \\u2014 that trap has its own test (test_the_lineage_memo_cannot_launder_a_tampered_genesis), which a weaker-keyed cache passes every other test and fails only this one. NEAR-MISS WORTH KEEPING: pyright called an isinstance branch in _validate unreachable; it is LIVE and the annotation was wrong \\u2014 deleting the \\\"dead\\\" branch would have removed a real refusal with every test still green except its own. Fix the annotation, not the symptom.\\n\\nARBITER RULINGS (three, overnight, all await Kyle's confirmation and are overturnable): (1) multi-word denylist terms are IDENTIFIER bans not prose bans (sdk/read.py:244 \\\"receipt order\\\" prose is accurate shipped behaviour, Rule-17-allowlisted; condemning it makes Rule 18 a standing suppressed failure); (2) sense-qualified bans (event/merge/receipt as ordering/custody concepts) deliberately NOT mechanized, named in _NOT_MECHANIZED with a drift test; (3) the O(n) residual ACCEPTED at its stated width \\u2014 an adopted authority is not proven to chain back to genesis nor that its claimed ordinal is its physical position; both need the whole-prefix walk these O(1) paths exist to avoid, matching ratified \\u00a73.2. r3 was asked to test whether the residual is WIDER than stated and found it is not. Also arbiter-ruled: probe.py suffix-dispatch arm DEFERRED to slice A (slice 0 is the standalone primitive; arrival is not a residence mode until authority moves); Rule 18 NOT widened to DictComp/ExceptHandler/match nodes (no forcing case \\u2014 noted in docstring instead).\\n\\nCI COVERAGE CONFIRMED (closes the recurring \\\"macOS only\\\" caveat as far as it can be closed pre-PR): both new suites are auto-discovered by existing ubuntu CI with NO workflow change \\u2014 check-architecture runs ./dev check -> pytest tests/ (Rule 18), and the Test (engine) matrix runs pytest libs/engine/tests (both arrival suites, incl. the 4-process gate, the RLIMIT_FSIZE torn tail, and the pinned SIGKILL-cannot-tear assertion). The Linux answer therefore arrives automatically at PR time, and the pinned test is built so a differing Linux result CORRECTS us rather than passing silently.\\n\\nSTILL UNVERIFIED, honestly: Linux (until CI runs); real power-cut durability (untestable in harness); NFS/network-mount flock semantics (explicitly out of contract per \\u00a73.3).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M09GNGW7VTSKDPYMJ027HEPR\", \"_ts\": 1787031440.803571, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar\"]}, \"session/2026-08-18-cutA-same-day-convergence\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-18-cutA-same-day-convergence\", \"message\": \"SESSION ARC: morning review of slice 0 (three arbiter rulings walked, O(n) residual unpacked to full width, all confirmed) rolled directly into CUT A's complete pipeline arc \\u2014 design agent, three Kyle rulings at the gate (Q1 {protocol,lineage,key} confirmed as bootstrap-fact instantiation; Q2 exclusivity ruled via the two-readings walkthrough, where Kyle's distribution-property argument beat the arbiter's registry-preservation recommendation; keyless tension deferred named), impl, gate CLEAN, agy cross-family substitution when codex usage-limited (skills adapted mid-session), simplify with two refutations honored, pro readiness CONVERGED, retrospective emitted. Same-day slice convergence \\u2014 first time the pipeline ran end-to-end inside one attended session. CALIBRATION: Kyle's rulings twice reversed or sharpened the arbiter's recommendation (Q2 reading choice; the walkthrough demand before ruling 3 confirmation) \\u2014 presenting a recommendation WITH the concrete process walkthrough is the shape that earns the reversal; abstract option lists would not have. Session admin: subagent model routing ruled (opus/sonnet overrides, never inherit Fable \\u2014 codified in both pipeline skills + memory); fold-key friction promoted after firing twice. NEXT: cut B \\u2014 projections.\", \"_ts\": 1787084710.927646, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/arrival-sliceB-simplify-composition\": {\"topic\": \"test/arrival-sliceB-simplify-composition\", \"message\": \"Cut B 4-angle simplify composition (2026-08-18): six moves ruled from four seeded angle reports. Composed finding: reuse (encode-side json.loads(serialize_*) round-trip, 4 sites) + altitude (merge.py tick-arity magic numbers + dead double-strip) converge on the same merge.py lines \\u2014 one move: public tuple->dict codec encoders mirroring B1's decode pair, strip width derived from codec arity, dead padding dropped. Load-bearing move: catch_up's unconditional BEGIN IMMEDIATE (introduced by the r1 race fix) gets the already-current fast path hoisted above the transaction \\u2014 mutation-verified against the race suites, docstring re-aligned. SKIPPED with rationale: _reconcile one-meta-read docstring undercount (pre-existing cut A, not this diff's); dedup two-SELECT UNION ALL fold (trivial); _create self-enforce residue (receipted for a later Kyle ruling). Notable negatives: guard trio confirmed right-shape by two angles independently; canonical-bytes single-sourcing confirmed; own_lineage licence spelled once (licensed_own_lineage, both callers); my seed premise 'receive.py old guard residue' was STALE \\u2014 the guard was a first introduction, not a dedup.\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"round\": \"simplify\", \"_ts\": 1787094674.263806, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-19-arrival-sliceC-design\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-19-arrival-sliceC-design\", \"message\": \"Cut C ORDERING design session, ratified same-evening (antigravity-impl-pipeline Stage E + stage 0; no implementation). Shape: six flash-low explorers (all citations spot-checked verbatim, 6/6 exact) fed a design brief; six sequential arbiter-gate questions to Kyle produced the contract; decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering RATIFIED + receipts committed a49997cd. CALIBRATION NOTES: (1) Kyle's Q6 pushback (\\\"there's a set of primitive work that would make everything else easier\\\") reframed the cut around ONE atoms Ordering primitive + shared totalization \\u2014 the arbiter had been answering the six questions locally; the primitive-first composition came from the human gate. Sequential one-question-at-a-time gating is what created the room for that catch. (2) Kyle challenged Q2's premise (mode-qualified CAS token) \\u2014 grounding the answer in the tree (three families still execute pre-migration) converted a premise dispute into a clean freeze-the-condemned ruling. (3) Advisor post-completion check caught that Rule 17 needed running after the docs commit \\u2014 red, but ALL offenders pre-existing untracked docs/dev files (the receipted Cut B finding), committed receipts pass; verified before declaring done rather than assumed. (4) Plan-fact line anchors were stale vs the branch (CAS predicate drifted 1411->1448); re-pinning every anchor in the proposal is now the standing brief practice. NEXT ENTRY POINT: implementation session \\u2014 pipeline stage 1, slices C0 (Rule 17 scan scope, first commit) then C1 atoms primitive feeding C2/C4/C5, C3 CAS independent; opus gates via pointer branches; flash-high scoped reviews; proposal's anchor table is the map.\", \"_ts\": 1787195611.261839, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-08-20-cutC-impl-converged\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-20-cutC-impl-converged\", \"message\": \"Cut C ORDERING: design-ratified contract -> converged across three model families in ~15h wall clock. Shape: C0-C5 opus impl + independent opus gates (pointer branches, all PASS), agy flash r1 3 scopes zero findings, seeded 4-angle simplify (4 moves), pro readiness r1-r3 (F1 family-rule divergence -> atoms resolve_key_field unification; F2 refuted via fold-key provenance, refutation adversarially audited), then sol belt-and-braces r1-r3 (7 findings fixed incl. 2 majors gemini missed; remediation-born prose ratchet removed by construction-vs-detection ruling). Ledger fully closed: every finding fixed/dismissed/deferred with receipts in docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/. Calibration: sol's finds were all shared-blind-spot territory (duck-typing, declaration-vs-availability, float semantics) \\u2014 do not skip the cross-family round after in-family convergence; fixes needed 2 more rounds than first-cut code, as receipted thrice before. NEXT ENTRY POINT: Kyle reviews converged cut -> wave-tail = perf benchmark (ordered(), CAS head walk, payload-key parse, merge regen) + _create self-enforce ruling (Kyle) -> ship decision (push/PR). Branch feat/arrival-libs local unpushed.\", \"_ts\": 1787252761.721658, \"_n\": 1}}}, \"seal\": {\"items\": [{\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787004703.391748}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787022704.049536}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787066520.567808}, {\"message\": \"cut A converged same-day; sweep done; next entry cut B\", \"_ts\": 1787084711.126505}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787085109.953113}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787189202.771977}, {\"message\": \"sweep: cut C design ratified, receipts committed, impl entry point set\", \"_ts\": 1787195611.81793}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787196645.243644}, {\"message\": \"cut C converged triple-family; sol belt-and-braces closed; wave-tail: perf benchmark + _create ruling\", \"_ts\": 1787252762.246952}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1787253861.056494}]}, \"design\": {\"items\": {\"practice/design-kind-adr-elements\": {\"topic\": \"practice/design-kind-adr-elements\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"New kind: design (topic= fold key). Formalizes the RATIFIED/REFINED/DEFERRED/REJECTED/SUPERSEDED/PARKED/PROPOSED prose-status vocabulary found across 662 existing decision facts into a real status field: proposed -> refined* (hypothesis-with-status pattern: re-emit, message explains what changed) -> ratified|rejected|parked -> superseded. 'parked' deliberately reuses thread's existing word rather than 'deferred' (two words, one concept). superseded_by is a typed edge (targets=design) -- the first live consumer of architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default, which no kind had exercised yet. alternatives= is a first-class field (ADR 'Considered Options' convention) rather than prose -- corpus check found 83/662 decisions (12.5%) already carry alternatives-considered language once the search widened past the single phrase 'chosen over', comparable in scale to the date/attribution-stutter finding. decision kind is unchanged and keeps its narrower, correct role: settled one-shot choices (498/555 topics in the corpus never get revised at all -- design targets the ~10% minority that iterates). [correction: fixed a misaddressed ref in the first emit of this fact -- architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default is a decision's topic, not a kind]\", \"alternatives\": \"alternatives as its own kind: rejected for now -- no second use-case yet (an alternative getting its own independent lifecycle/references) to justify the promotion; watch for it via the same corpus-forensics practice used to find this need in the first place. status field bolted onto existing decision kind instead of a new kind: rejected -- decision's fold-by-topic + one-shot semantics is correct for the 90% majority that never revise; conflating the two would blur a distinction worth keeping legible.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP\", \"_ts\": 1783745396.297933, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"], \"_unresolved_refs\": [{\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"kind\": \"decision\", \"key\": \"architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\"}]}, \"architecture/ephemeral-topology-with-flag\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/ephemeral-topology-with-flag\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"A --with flag, general across vertex ops (read/emit/fold/cite), that supplies an ephemeral topology root for cross-store ref resolution without persisting a named aggregation vertex first. Closes the inversion in architecture/combinatorial-vertices (2026-03-01, never built): that decision said 'temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful' but everything built since (cli-completion, loops add <vertex> combine) is the persisted half only -- there is no ephemeral half. Surfaced from thread:fidelity-contract-tests -- the M3 loops-adoption-spike audit's findings had nowhere to cross-ref into painted's own project vertex (which already exists, separate-by-default per the option-3 topology) without standing up a new named aggregator first. Mechanism: reuses the existing topology-roots resolution machinery (_topology_roots_for_emit for write, the combine-walk for read) -- --with just feeds it an extra root that isn't discovered from a .vertex file. Two open design questions before implementation: (1) argument shape -- --with <name> (resolve_vertex lookup) vs --with </path/to/.vertex> (raw path, matching combine's own vertex entries) vs both; (2) whether a promotion convenience (turn a --with pairing that keeps recurring into a persisted loops add combine) is worth building alongside, or whether the existing manual add combine command is already sufficient and coupling them is premature.\", \"alternatives\": \"widen the general project aggregator to include painted directly: rejected -- contradicts the option-3 topology decision on record (separate-by-default) without a stated reason to revisit it. do nothing, rely on typed unresolved pins resolving whenever someone eventually reads through a combining topology: viable but leaves the M3 evidence permanently unresolved unless some other need independently creates that topology later -- doesn't serve the immediate cross-repo evidence-recording need. a second persisted narrow aggregator (mirroring cli-completion) for this specific pairing: viable and lower-risk than a new flag, but doesn't generalize -- every new one-off cross-store need would mint another named vertex file, the exact ceremony this is trying to dissolve.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP\", \"_ts\": 1783745428.951476, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"alternatives\": \"refined-as-friction-status: rejected, the one instance (mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive) is a design deliberation wearing a friction costume, reclassified instead; reuse superseded_by edge name: rejected, absorption is a root-cause merge not a temporal replacement, absorbed_into names it correctly; distinct superseded status: rejected, corpus shows absorption always co-occurs with resolved or parked, never a 4th state; fold in default-field-values mechanism (closing emit-automation-via-vertex-def): deferred, separate friction, out of scope for this pass\", \"message\": \"Applies the design-kind-adr-elements treatment to friction. Corpus check on 84 friction facts (2026-07-11): status vocab in the wild was open(29)/resolved(51)/parked(2)/refined(1)/missing(1), unenforced. Two concrete coherence gaps drove the shape: (1) mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive carried status=refined while its own message said \\\"PARKED\\\" -- structured status and prose disagreeing, the same disease design's status field cured for decision. Its content (four orthogonal axes, position evolving, explicit park) is design-shaped, not friction-shaped -- friction didn't get its own kind to escape into until today. (2) absorption is a real recurring shape, prose-only: loud-fold-key-error \\\"absorbed into\\\" emit-receipt-on-write, and two facts independently \\\"merged into\\\" loops-test-suite-broken-on-main. All three absorbed frictions are status=resolved already -- absorption is attribution (how/via-what it resolved), not a fourth terminal state.\\n\\nLifecycle: open -> resolved | parked. No refined (grows into a design fact instead, ref='d back). No superseded (the corpus never needed it as distinct from resolved/parked). New typed edge absorbed_into (targets=friction) records the merge, first live use alongside superseded_by.\\n\\nVertex spec updated (.loops/project.vertex): friction kind gains edge \\\"absorbed_into\\\" targets=\\\"friction\\\". Corpus cleanup follow-up: backfill emit-automation-via-vertex-def's missing status, reclassify mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive off status=refined with a design fact carrying its actual four-axis content.\\n\\nStep 2 (status-aware salience view, tying into plan:curation-in-surface Open Decision B) is explicitly sequenced after this and not bundled in -- Kyle's framing from the 2026-07-11 session wrap.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7R5FJA6GJCZ856STZ14NKC,01KX7SV12J6214KSFRJ2D7HT48\", \"_ts\": 1783748740.974265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/design-kind-adr-elements\", \"thread:friction-kind-lifecycle-design\"]}, \"rendering/mid-session-touched-window\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/mid-session-touched-window\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"alternatives\": \"new verb (sl recent <v> [--since W]): considered, rejected as premature -- see invocation axis; new lens (recent.py via --lens): kept as the leading candidate, defers cleanly to existing lens-resolution machinery; flag on read (--touched --since W): kept as a lighter-weight sibling candidate, not yet chosen over the lens shape; extend session_landing lens to accept a non-tick-bound window: identified as the actual blocker -- windows[0] is the most-recent CLOSED tick, not current work, so this needs data-path extension before either invocation shape can land\", \"message\": \"Reclassified from friction:mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive (2026-07-11, design/practice/friction-kind-lifecycle corpus check) -- its status field said \\\"refined\\\" while its own message said \\\"PARKED\\\", and its content (four orthogonal axes, position evolving, explicit park pending other work) is design-shaped, not friction-shaped. friction didn't have design to escape into until today. Carrying the original content forward verbatim as the design fact's substance:\\n\\nMissing primitive: mid-session reorientation (\\\"what changed since I last looked, without waiting for session end\\\"). Initial framing said \\\"missing verb sl recent <v> [--since W].\\\" Walking the design surfaced four orthogonal axes: (1) WINDOW source -- rolling-from-now (--since W) vs anchored-to-session-start (since session.start fact) are different questions with different anchors. (2) COMPUTE path -- TOUCHED marks (ADDED/UPDATED/CITED) come from TickWindow.added_keys/updated_keys, which only exist at fold-boundary tick creation time, so mid-session reuse needs either dynamic synthesis from a fact-window or manual tick materialization (side-effecty for a read). (3) INVOCATION -- new verb vs new lens vs flag on read. (4) RENDER -- full TOUCHED with salience-glyphs vs simpler grouped-by-kind read with window filter.\\n\\nCritical blocker: session_landing lens already exists with fetch() + LandingData input shape, BUT its windows[0] (the landing window) is the most-recent CLOSED tick -- for session-start that's the just-closed session; mid-session that's the previous session, not current work. sl read --lens session_landing --since W does NOT dissolve cleanly -- the data path needs extension to compute marks from a non-tick-bound window.\\n\\nPARKED (carried forward, still true): revisit once better SUMMARY/DETAILED rendering on plain read --since W is proven out, in case that dissolves the need outright. If not, resume from the four axes above with the session_landing blocker as the first concrete unblock.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRWJ8MS0TPKCD9W0RMR1QA5P,01KRPKSWT74RTFXCQZEWVS3S23,01KRS78TC0XVNHZ36S8RG9DNM6,01KRWKPW5JQ95WCFY5S5RZHBZ1\", \"_ts\": 1783748766.650246, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"alternatives\": \"auto-hide-by-convention (last status word in vocab hides with no declaration): rejected, implicit magic, violates explicit-over-implicit -- an explicit hide clause is greppable and visible the same way edge declarations are; apply hide to --facts too: rejected, --facts is event/lifecycle history, a different read axis than current-state fold, and corpus audits (this session used --facts to verify friction status transitions) depend on it staying faithful; channel-keyed default (is_tty): foreclosed outright by the invariance proof in design:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels -- not on the table; friction-only special case (no general kind-level clause): rejected in favor of a general hide= clause any status-bearing kind can opt into, friction is just the first tenant (thread/task/hypothesis/design all carry status and could adopt it later)\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by the lifecycle unification at build time, exactly as the refined design scheduled: 090-S5 shipped the hide as the FIRST TENANT of the unified kind-level lifecycle clause, not as a sibling. Everything this design specified survives in the built form \\u2014 budget-stage filter, fold-view-only scope (arbiter enforced --facts faithfulness against an implementer misreading \\u2014 this design's own corpus-audit rationale decided the ruling), encoder uniformity, --all defeat, explicit-predicate auto-disable, Window.limited_by=status provenance. The declaration shape moved from hide-blacklist to active-whitelist with fail-open on missing (arbitration F1).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ,01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF,01KX7VCMV6Z5YA7H5WA1D7QPNF\", \"_ts\": 1784410817.463361, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:friction-kind-lifecycle-design\"], \"superseded_by\": \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01KXV3VYJZQHJH2TDZ4VN0AK6B\"}, \"architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"alternatives\": \"per-fact CLI loop (status quo): rejected by consumer evidence \\u2014 88 emits/520 command calls/658KB shell input for one audit, and shell-array generation with manual quoting is exactly the error surface strict mode exists to prevent; shell-side wrapper script generating emits: rejected, leaves no durable manifest and doesn't solve forward refs; exposing the sync engine's ingest directly: closest existing primitive \\u2014 the design should DISSOLVE into it if possible (sync sources already speak ndjson fact-per-line), the delta is interactive invocation + strict preflight + batch receipt + symbolic IDs\", \"message\": \"Design entry for the top consumer ask (2026-07-12 homelab-audit retrospective). Shape: sl emit --ndjson FILE|- accepting fact-per-line, with (1) strict PREFLIGHT over the whole batch before any write (all-or-nothing option), (2) ONE signed batch receipt, (3) SYMBOLIC intra-batch IDs so forward references resolve within the batch \\u2014 this dissolves the manual topological ordering strict typed edges currently force (audit had to emit a project before its feature, then re-emit), (4) the batch file doubles as the durable, replayable import manifest the audit found missing (payloads exist only in the append-only db + session JSONL today). Design inputs to hold: the sync engine already consumes ndjson \\u2014 check dissolution into that path before building a parallel one; interaction with feat/internal-table _decl reservation (a batch touching declarations must respect write-time reservation semantics from S1/S2 \\u2014 design these aware of each other); batch receipt vs per-fact receipts is a write-receipt question (receipt = your batch at instant T, one tick-eligible unit?); decide whether a failed preflight names ALL violations or first (audit ergonomics say all). Elevated from friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use (N=1 speculative 2026-07-03) by cross-vendor consumer demand.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ,01KWMNEHDAVP4BTJGNPAMERMA8,01KWMNEGYXYWD6581TDTEQMSXM\", \"_ts\": 1783895922.789688, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\", \"friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\", \"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"alternatives\": \"bolt constraint vocabulary onto KDL now: rejected \\u2014 internal-table migration is making declarations store-canonical mid-flight, adding surface to the thing being absorbed churns SPEC section-9; keep validation external (custom Python/SQLite per store): status quo, proven workable but per-store bespoke \\u2014 the audit hand-rolled enum/lifecycle/foreign-pin checks; do nothing: rejected, second axis of validation demand is now consumer-evidenced\", \"message\": \"Sequencing position (2026-07-12): the homelab-audit consumer wants semantic payload constraints in vertex declarations \\u2014 required fields, enums, lifecycle defaults \\u2014 plus a validate surface covering folded state (loops validate --store --refs --foreign-refs). The need is real (Sol validated status vocabularies, feature lifecycle fields, and foreign fact pins in ~custom Python because loops validate only checks declaration syntax), and it is a DIFFERENT AXIS from strict mode (strict = ref resolution + kind declaration at emit; constraints = payload validity). Position: design this AS PART OF the store-canonical declaration schema after internal-table S3+ lands, not as KDL ingress surface now \\u2014 the internal table is exactly where constraint declarations would live and be historized, and designing them into the ingress format mid-migration would double the absorption surface. The bulk-emit preflight (design:architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson) is the natural first consumer of a constraint engine \\u2014 batch validation wants machine-checkable payload rules. Related existing ask: friction:emit-automation-via-vertex-def (default field values, e.g. status defaults open) is the smallest member of this family and should fold into the same design rather than ship separately.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ,01KXAA4XMBXJT6TB644WB6N8B8\", \"_ts\": 1783895933.039624, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"architecture/batch-emit-ingress\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"Refined (Kyle, 2026-07-13): the batch IS a tick being constructed. The proposed symbolic intra-batch IDs dissolve entirely \\u2014 refs address by kind:key, so the author already knows every target address; the only failure was existence-at-line-N, and that dissolves because strictness evaluates at the BOUNDARY, not per line: batch commit = append window facts in one txn + fire boundary \\u2192 tick materializes. Store\\u222abatch validation is not a new rule, it is 'strict checks against the store as of the boundary.' The batch receipt of the earlier proposal was a tick wearing a disguise; replayability ties to attestation for free (window_hash already commits to the window contents). Surviving surface: sl emit --ndjson <file|-> as a window-authoring ingress + message=-/@file ergonomics. Semantic kept legible: single emit still validates per-fact on the live edge; batch mode is deliberately choosing boundary-time validation by choosing to author a window. Residual audit item (not a batch decision): does anything downstream (fold, salience walk) assume the ref graph is a DAG? \\u2014 intra-window mutual refs become legal under boundary validation. Connects: tick-as-social-object (thread:workspace-linked-cuts), seal-fanout authoring half now fully absorbed.\", \"alternatives\": \"symbolic intra-batch IDs ($sym declare/ref + topological substitution): dissolved \\u2014 solved an addressing problem that does not exist under kind:key refs and boundary-time validation; refs-by-fact-id within a batch: no live need (Sol's pain was existence-ordering only) \\u2014 waits for work shape that demands it\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCWG65M5YB2S4HN3EZ00CFE\", \"_ts\": 1783919095.650681, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"friction:emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\", \"friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\", \"friction:seal-fanout-across-workspace-stores\", \"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"practice/retrospective-kind\": {\"topic\": \"practice/retrospective-kind\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-13): retrospective kind lives in the project vertex \\u2014 retro-in-project, enriched with proper keys, building out the project concept to be more thorough through practice. The store-split question that held this at proposed is resolved by decision:practice/meta-store-role-dissolved \\u2014 findings emit where born under practice//workflow/ prefixes, the retro hub refs them locally, cross-referencing across stores stays easy via aggregation reads. Shape unchanged from proposal: name= arc handle, one synthesis fact per arc, hub-and-spokes over ref'd observations, re-emit to revise. First instance: retrospective:internal-table-s0-hardening.\", \"alternatives\": \"single long doc in docs/dev: rejected \\u2014 local/gitignored, invisible to the read path, exactly the pattern Kyle retired; multi-fact retro (one fact per finding, no hub): rejected \\u2014 loses the arc narrative and the citable synthesis handle; retrospective as observation topic=session/...: rejected \\u2014 session arcs are per-session bookkeeping, retros are per-arc and deserve their own fold\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXF4719ENDZ42GZXT8N8TBXV\", \"_ts\": 1783992912.191305, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/meta-store-role-dissolved\", \"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\"]}, \"architecture/custody-lib-extraction\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"tasked-second-consumer\", \"message\": \"LANDED f384e2d (+2cb08a0 gate): libs/custody, signing.py verbatim (git rename 100%), 9 CLI sites + 3 test files import custody; flat vendored build carries the package (production sl verified project + identity stores chain-intact, on-root and off-root). Ratchet swept in the same change and the drift was worse than the design assumed: 4/7 architecture rules were RED \\u2014 stale exceptions (pop_store, painted) failing first meant scans never ran, and real violations accumulated behind them (3 sqlite3 probes in apps, 5 StoreReader reaches, store->engine in rebirth, unfrozen executor dataclasses). store->engine RATIFIED (rebirth reuses tick_row_hash \\u2014 single-sourced chain hashing is the same anti-format-fork principle as custody itself); the rest became shrink-only allowlists. Rule 8 string-pins the domain literals to custody/signing.py \\u2014 repo-wide including tests after genericizing sign's docstring example + test domains. Root cause of the red ratchet: tests/ belonged to no package, no gate ran it -> root ./dev check now exists. Consumer side: tasked imports custody (substrate + seeds), boundary ratchet added (tests/test_boundaries.py \\u2014 loops.* allowlist = loops_home from substrate.py only, shrink-only with staleness check); left uncommitted in tasked's working tree alongside Kyle's in-flight work. loops_home stayed out, as designed.\", \"alternatives\": \"fold into libs/sign: rejected \\u2014 deliberately loops-agnostic, shared with vouch/pile/comms; domain constants would pollute it. fold into libs/engine: rejected \\u2014 INJECTION NOT IMPORT is load-bearing; engine importing sign kills the principle the substrate was built on. fold into libs/store: rejected \\u2014 silhouette match (at-rest format \\u2248 store ops) but store is deliberately zero-dep; adding sign+engine changes its character. bundle loops_home into custody: rejected \\u2014 same-consumer-wants-both is not same-concept; consumer-shaped libs are how god-libs form. copy loops_home into tasked: rejected \\u2014 two XDG resolvers drifting on vertex location is its own format-agreement bug; the loud import beats a silent fork.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXNWQZ3JHVK86Y0HSTMHYXG0,01KXNWQF36EQYSJ8NS0ZCG1PEV,01KXFFCC38RR4W8TBW89FRS17F\", \"_ts\": 1784229835.650734, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"friction:no-cli-verb-flat-tick-key\", \"observation:test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\"]}, \"architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 1 final, v3 \\u2014 full pipeline: codex advisor -> my arbitration -> codex cross-exam (5 fatals resolved to A1-A13) -> 2 Claude panels (both AMEND, 0 fatal) -> final dispositions in docs/scratch/080-overnight/final-contracts.md). Axis: cursor = facts-only witness-prefix position, identity = fact id; selection witness (8.4), replay (ts,id) (6.2), ticks = verified names for positions. KEY PANEL-DRIVEN CHANGES over v2: (1) A5 unanchored wall-clock REFUSES with teaching naming --as-of \\u2014 no auto-route even labeled; my v2 fallback breached the design's own explicitness clause (honesty panel catch \\u2014 disclosure-after-the-fact is not explicit request, and the mode silently flips under future anchor backfill). (2) Aggregate mixed witness/projection modes REFUSED (chimera answers no well-posed question); current-membership = NAMED DEROGATION with sunset (9.5 aggregate internal tables) + marker-carriage ratchet test. (3) Durable handle serialization REFUSED for unadopted stores \\u2014 live corpus except tasks.db has zero lineage ids (panel empirical). (4) Receipt-group boundary DURABLE via payload-carried group id \\u2014 9.2 spec touch queued to oracle WITH GlobalReceiptPosition as one coordination package; interim engine-level heuristic with refuse-on-ambiguity (merge can interleave ts-colliding facts into a ceremony span \\u2014 honesty must not rest on improbability). (5) Cursor output carries honesty-ladder status (file-pre-genesis today, disclosed) + machine-readable mode field. (6) Combined tick drill must pass envelopes through (today deliberately empty => flagship aggregate never witness-anchors). Riders: false gen_id monotonicity docstring (empirically ~1/5000 within-ms ULID inversions), id-bearing incremental read for Watch. Implementation unblocked: fold-at, --as-of-on-fold labeled projection, --diff full-recompute.\", \"alternatives\": \"pure-ts axis: rejected \\u2014 historical answers mutable under late arrival (yesterday's state rewrites on import), cannot drive receipt tail or align with tick coverage; kept as explicit labeled projection. pure-tick-anchor axis: rejected as position space \\u2014 sparse, cannot represent unsealed tail, pre-chain history, or per-receipt Watch updates; kept as the address/anchor layer. pure-rowid witness: rejected \\u2014 storage-local, rebuild-unstable; fact-id handles fix it. incremental --diff: rejected \\u2014 order-sensitive folds break under backdated insertion.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3,01KWJ8JHCD1GDSWFGZEEQZ24VW\", \"_unresolved_refs\": [{\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"design:internal-table-meta-schema\", \"kind\": \"design\", \"key\": \"internal-table-meta-schema\"}, {\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"design:internal-row-placement-facts\", \"kind\": \"design\", \"key\": \"internal-row-placement-facts\"}], \"_ts\": 1784302585.092613, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/internal-row-placement-facts\", \"design:internal-row-placement-facts\", \"design:internal-table-meta-schema\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 2 \\u2014 codex advisor s2-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, dispositions in final-contracts.md): daemon-shaped engine access = in-process long-lived VertexHandle per consumer, NO daemon process ('orchestration dissolves daemon' validated against all three consumers). Holds compiled ontology + connections + immutable snapshot + facts/tick cursors; receive() without reload; refresh() incremental via rowid-cursor batch then FULL (ts,id) reconstruction per coalesced receipt group (A7 contract; insertion-aware replay is optimization never semantics); sync/async change iterators. Cross-process detection: PRAGMA data_version as invalidation HINT confirmed by cursor-bearing rowid queries; PANEL INVARIANT: probe connection transaction-free between probes (data_version pinned inside open txn = unbounded silent staleness, empirically verified \\u2014 the draft's 'adds poll latency' claim was false) \\u2014 exit-tested. _decl arrival = visible control event forcing re-resolution+recompile+checkpoint-invalidation+staged full reconstruction before atomic publication. Panel amendments all accepted: tick query hydrated at open (one blessed epoch scan \\u2014 ticked reconcile needs task->latest-close over history); changes() idle-timeout/deadline wake (reaper wakes with zero store traffic); resume-from-position SCOPED OUT (head-start-only); S7 SPLIT ticked-cutover vs tasked-deletion (gated on CAS sibling); snapshot carries cumulative visible_domain_count; fabricated benchmark citation REPLACED with panel measurements \\u2014 100k forced-full 269-510ms so <1s holds, 250ms ordinary-refresh gate met only via checkpoint rung 4 => PROMOTED required-for-cutover, collect-heavy fixture added. Post-write reconstruction canonicalizes STATE not admission (admission serializability defers to conditional-emit sibling). Aggregates: per-member handle vectors + union projector; 0.8.0 may full-refold union per change. No schema/protocol touch.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXPYFHSWSPEM18K0R7TSCTFS,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302595.319035, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:tasked-forcing-function\"]}, \"rendering/tui-shell-integration\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tui-shell-integration\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 3 \\u2014 codex advisor s3-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, dispositions in final-contracts.md): TUI = interactive RUN tier over the existing fetch+lens plan (Surface stays a fidelity tier on ONE fetch). Entry: sl read VERTEX -i canonical (replaces a SILENT DOWNGRADE at fold.py:259, not an error \\u2014 panel accuracy fix); sl VERTEX -i via painted run_app dispatch. Keys: q ALWAYS zoom-out, Q/ctrl-c quits \\u2014 and quit_keys must be EXPLICITLY overridden wherever painted HostSurface/StreamSurface defaults reimpose q-quits (panel: shipped defaults embody the collision). Lens mount: typed LensSpec declarations; shell owns ONE VertexHandle + one change iterator; static CLI and TUI share one pure snapshot projector; static Block byte-identical golden-guarded. store_app deletes atomically when read/stream/ticks mounts replace it. ONE coordinated lens-signature migration INCLUDING apps/tasks' 7 run_cli sites on the deprecated render=(ctx,data) contract (panel catch \\u2014 deferring them leaves a latent second migration, forbidden); S0 FIRST adds byte goldens for stream/ticks/ls/sync/population (current coverage vacuous exactly where render_row lands) + piped-implies-width-None becomes an enumerable ratchet test paired with the piped= kwarg deletion. Painted plan reconciled to upstream reality (panel: main moved past the dossier \\u2014 ViewportAdapter + HostSurface SHIPPED): consume-and-verify, shell drives ViewportAdapter per mounted view, caller-side re-render + plan/publish tickets, no set_data adapter invented; loops lenses stay 3-arg/omitted-arm; theme roles kebab-case declared-vocabulary on-label; poll-backed change iterator is PLAN OF RECORD (0.13 inbound seam deliberately last upstream, event type intentionally open \\u2014 no promised-API framing). Slices: contract migration -> lens plans/dispatch -> shell+retirement -> corpus skeleton -> live cursor -> aggregate honesty.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXRBHVCXJ1802FY5S4MBRF4H,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302610.037022, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"design:architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/digest-first-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/digest-first-consumer\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"PROPOSED \\u2014 DELIBERATELY HELD AT KYLE'S GATE (overnight session 4 \\u2014 codex advisor s4-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, all amendments folded into this proposal, dispositions in final-contracts.md). Digest = app-layer injected synthesis over an exact lineage-qualified cursor interval (after,through], emitting ONE ordinary target-declared domain fact at the target's current head; --since 'last tick' = sugar for resolved tick cursor through atomically-captured head; --as-of cannot drive a coverage-bearing write. Observer: declared keyed digest identity for unattended runs; human who edits+adopts final bytes emits as human. Signature attests exact-content authorship/adoption at receipt \\u2014 NOT LLM reproducibility, NOT truth (chain-attests-receipt extended to synthesis). Coverage: explicit source fact ids + lineage + cursor bounds + counts + canonical commitments; input/context/covered sets distinct; structural verification proves subject-set+integrity, semantic adequacy stays an accountable observer assertion; conjunctive six-step verifier, fail-closed (panels' A-G accepted: two-store input contract named, manifest-order check-or-declare, prompt-preimage statement, exported canonical-bytes surface, no-rowid ratchet, lineage-unopened degraded mode). THE GATE \\u2014 three calls that are Kyle's, not a night session's: (1) canonical evaluator = decl-chain classifier (3-state, strict-aware) with engine gate as enforcement shadow \\u2014 engine Grant cannot express undeclared-forgiven; evaluator-singleness ratchet REQUIRED (live tasks.vertex grants depend on precedence; drift = privilege escalation in a deployed workflow); (2) owner-only first slice: advisor rejected as dodge, panel showed the rejection proves too much (indicts today's emit baseline) \\u2014 both paths presented neutrally, sequencing is Kyle's; (3) architecture/parallel-authorization-paths is an OBSERVATION \\u2014 binding it as Gate 0 requires promoting it to decision: Kyle's ratification act. NOTHING writes until the gate; then non-writing slices (planner/preview/coverage-verify) unlock first.\", \"alternatives\": \"owner-only-first: viable per panel steelman (consults zero new authorization surface, exactly as sound as sl emit today) \\u2014 held for Kyle, not rejected. digest-into-source-vertex vs dedicated digest vertex vs per-grant target: advisor recommends target-declared ordinary kind; alternatives retained in memo.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302622.144063, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED 2026-07-18 as the graph build-2 agenda for 0.9.0 (Kyle + adversarial review; original by kyle/siftd-codex \\u2014 premise fully reproduced incl. an 18-hop predicate-mixed chain; SCC/cycles sits on build-1s own deferred list, so this is the anticipated build-2, no conflicts). Build agenda refined through the dissolution split: (a) widen fetch_graph to accept key, honor-or-refuse per the 184dfce temporal-flag refusal pattern \\u2014 never silently drop (friction:graph-fetch-drops-key); (b) edge-predicate selection as a fetch/projection param under a name avoiding the read-grammar predicate collision (inline-predicate-eq-only owns that word) \\u2014 working name --edge; (c) retain predicate labels through the DFS \\u2014 predicates are ALREADY carried end-to-end in the corpus and discarded only at the chain-walk boundary (fetch.py:902), so retention is a small change not new capability; (d) SCC/cycle census in the returned dict \\u2014 forward-required, cycles become legal with batch-emit (thread:ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit); (e) partition orphans by keyless-vs-dangling and split dangling from filter-excluded (268 conflated in the siftd repro today). Domain composition (capability-to-flow-to-stage, component-impact) stays vertex-local per lens-declares-fetch \\u2014 correctly assigned by the original.\", \"alternatives\": \"Mixed connectivity graph only: useful census, insufficient causal semantics \\u2014 kept as default when no edge selection requested. Architecture vocabulary in core: rejected, grammar-domain-neutrality. Each custom lens rebuilds edge resolution: rejected, duplicates correctness logic upstream.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQ9DK0M60ZC9KJZWMZVR3KH,01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KPYP8YHRPXRFKG07W85SCTVR,01KXV2A69V5T5ZNQPGA5C7DPE8,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV2A5YHZ86P295DNMBYNG32\", \"_ts\": 1784395166.968087, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/graph-build1-scope\", \"decision:design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"friction:graph-fetch-drops-key\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"]}, \"architecture/canonical-store-review-export\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"BUILDABLE CORE SHIPPED in 090-S4 (9afae8a + 9ffbf5b): sl read --review emits {review:{review_version:1, header:{vertex, cursor, declaration, cut}, facts:[...]}, rendered_at} \\u2014 deterministic kind-key-sorted, explicit volatile whitelist (salience/tier/inbound/depth/granularity/window/schema all excluded, test-asserted), signatures verbatim (custody posture held), header carries head cursor (reused from S6 resolution, bound AFTER the fetch per sol-P1 \\u2014 the S6 TOCTOU recurred here and was caught again), decl-generation = sha256 review fingerprint over the parsed declaration projection (explicitly NOT SPEC-10.2 JCS, no interchange claim) + decl_head ULID on adopted stores. read --json gap confirmed on all three predicted axes (fold-order traversal, diff-noise fields, dropped signatures). Honor-or-refuse: --review refuses --lens/--match/--fields/--limit/--count/--by/--refs with teaching messages; --kind/--key scope it. Dump half REMAINS SPEC-10-gated on GlobalReceiptPosition \\u2014 stop-line held, nothing interchange-shaped built. Live store first self-review: seq=3140, file-pre-genesis, 1320 facts, 371 signed, fingerprint sha256:fcf5e19e.\", \"alternatives\": \"Track SQLite alone: history survives, review/merge do not. NDJSON as only canonical store: rejected as universal form \\u2014 though SPEC 10.4 licenses text-resident per-vertex under the round-trip bar, so the rejection is of premature universality only. Generic read JSON: not reproducible \\u2014 proven, rows arrive in fold order with diff-noise fields.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E,01KXVEHTQNX0YYKAY43T382T6W\", \"_ts\": 1784408406.871742, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"decision:design/declaration-events-whole-document\", \"decision:design/fold-replay-order-event-time\", \"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED-AS-BUILT in 090-S5 (4094206 + 3493310 --facts-faithful fix + cd72d8c strict-parse fix): unified kind-level clause lifecycle FIELD active=CSV through lang loader, FoldSection carriage, budget-stage projection-only hide, validate active-targets-inactive scan (WARN, Address.readings resolution), Window.hidden + limited_by=status, --all defeat, status=-predicate auto-disable, --review and --facts both bypass (canonical/history axes stay faithful). Edge position held with a real mechanism: under --refs the hide PROTECTS ref-graph targets (dedup analysis showed no depth>0 twin exists \\u2014 the brief's assumed mechanism was wrong, the shipped one is right); salience retention proven byte-identical hide-vs-all. Acceptance bar met: real end-to-end deprecation walk, eight assertions, live CLI smoke. SPEC-9 pricing landed as decision:architecture/lifecycle-clause-spec-delta (no version bump, coordination queued). Contract-prospective no more \\u2014 the machinery has walked its first real deprecation.\", \"alternatives\": \"Physical deletion/rebirth: loses ordinary lifecycle. Hard-coded status values: domain-specific, violates neutrality. Leave deprecated in default topology: current view drifts \\u2014 the consumer-proven cost. Retract for every transition: conflates correction with ordinary state \\u2014 distinction verified against the retract decision rationale.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVJRGVEFS0ERG6YKDA2DA4E,01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E\", \"_ts\": 1784410817.628617, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"decision:architecture/lifecycle-clause-spec-delta\", \"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/retract-hide-from-fold-keep-edges\", \"design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"design:rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\", \"thread:decl-lens-tombstone-vocab-gap\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED 2026-07-18 (Kyle + adversarial review; original by kyle/siftd-codex) with two amendments folded per review: (1) refs now bind the boundary to the standing discipline it independently re-derived \\u2014 decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary (siftd is N=3 after vouch identity-namespace and scope-vocabulary) and decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract; (2) tense corrected demand-side: core MUST SUPPLY sound typed addresses, predicate-selectable graph projection, temporal selection, honest provenance \\u2014 at ratification two of four are unsound/absent (suffix-only address matching; no predicate filtering) and one is an open friction, so the list is the 0.9.0 demand set, not a description. Boundary ruling unchanged: architecture vocabulary (capability/component/flow/stage/datum/invariant) stays vertex-local (decl grammar already expresses all of it \\u2014 the 159-fact map required zero core changes); local lens composes the views; example/init-template ships only after a second map consumer confirms the shape (init machinery already copies vertex-local lenses \\u2014 template ship is a file, not machinery). Honest-provenance rider: friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses now has two independent consumers (homelab-audit 2026-07-12, siftd 2026-07-18) \\u2014 N=2 promotion gate CLEARED, scheduled into 0.9.0.\", \"alternatives\": \"Teach generic fold lens architecture vocabulary: rejected, domain-specific. Ship built-in project-map ontology now: rejected, one consumer. Local lens rebuilds address/graph semantics: rejected, correctness belongs upstream \\u2014 honest only once Address(kind,key) lands.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRMX94A1C1PZRW2ZQWJXX5KW,01KRJFA27PYJKB4JNABBFEW3C9,01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KPYP8YHRPXRFKG07W85SCTVR,01KXC7NZSHSEK03W120QKSBTG8,01KXV2A5YHZ86P295DNMBYNG32\", \"_ts\": 1784395166.569318, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"decision:design/lens-generalization-flow\", \"decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"]}, \"atoms/typed-edge-array-values\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/typed-edge-array-values\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"PROPOSED 2026-07-18, split out of the typed-edge fix recipe per review (the arrays element must not ride the bug-fix arc \\u2014 it touches ratified semantics). Question: should a declared typed-edge field accept a JSON array as the structural multi-edge form? Today: comma-split string is the ratified set-literal syntax (typed-edges-overlay-default: multi-valued overlay edge = set literal replaced atomically) and the read-side lift SKIPS non-str payload values entirely \\u2014 an array-valued edge field is silently inert, which is itself a small honesty gap (no warn). The question becomes live with batch-emit NDJSON ingress where JSON payloads make arrays the natural authored form. Position options: (a) accept arrays as equivalent set-literal syntax, normalized at ingress to the canonical comma form \\u2014 overlay semantics unchanged, purely syntactic; (b) keep comma-only and WARN on array-valued declared edge fields; (c) full multi-edge semantics \\u2014 rejected, would breach the union-edge grandfather rule (ref stays the lone union edge). Decide when batch-emit lands; default lean (a) since it changes no semantics.\", \"alternatives\": \"(a) arrays normalize to set-literal at ingress \\u2014 leaning; (b) warn-and-skip \\u2014 minimal; (c) new multi-edge semantics \\u2014 rejected against typed-edges-overlay-default.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWFPBY99R304Z7MQE3A91SFD,01KXCXTBV2PXQB34ZHP4W6G718,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65\", \"_ts\": 1784395201.18964, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\"]}, \"practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\": {\"topic\": \"practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"alternatives\": \"option A: new review-event kind (finding as first-class fact: site=, author=, reviewer=, direction=, class=, severity=, fix=sha, disposition=) \\u2014 cleanest fold view, but a new kind for something that may be expressible today; option B: structured-field PATTERN on existing kinds (observation topic=review/<arc>/<site> carrying the same fields; typed edges declared late-bound on fix=/site= when useful) \\u2014 zero grammar change, the fold groups by topic prefix, dissolution-friendly; option C: keep narrative emission, accept the calibration table as hand-authored \\u2014 rejected by tonight's evidence, the table is exactly the view we want mechanical\", \"message\": \"REFINED with the measured field list from the blind-reconstruction test (observation:test/090-artifact-store-recoverability \\u2014 16 context-only claims enumerate exactly what the pattern must carry). Schema per finding-integration fact: site= (slice/arc), author= (implementing model \\u2014 largest measured gap, 5/16), reviewer= (sol/arbiter/agent \\u2014 the direction arrows were unattested), direction= (down/up \\u2014 reviewer-corrects-arbiter rows are the calibration signal), class= (semantics/TOCTOU/degenerate-input/...), severity=, repro= (the literal failing input \\u2014 --edge ',' was unrecoverable), fix= (sha), disposition=, plus point-in-time evidence VALUES inline (the 59-tail lesson: live readings not carried by the fact are gone \\u2014 the store moved to 71 and witness-mode correctly refuses to recompute). Option B confirmed as the lean (fields on observation topic=review/<arc>/<site>, typed edges late-bound): every field above is already legal payload, zero grammar change. Remaining open before ratify: whether author=/reviewer= belong as observer-adjacent identity fields or plain payload \\u2014 touches the attestation vocabulary, worth one deliberate look at next reconcile.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVYXYVQRKZKYKXPDV1XD1BQ\", \"_ts\": 1784423578.556344, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\", \"observation:test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"architecture/surfacing-layer-charter\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/surfacing-layer-charter\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing-wave\", \"alternatives\": \"single libs/surfacing package: rejected \\u2014 inverts the repo's own layer precedent (record layer is atoms+engine+store+lang, not one lib), forces file moves ahead of consumers, and creates a third place to misfile into; hybrid (layer now + in-wave painted run_cli extraction): rejected as charter content \\u2014 the extraction is a painted-major coordination deserving its own gate, arrives via relocation-on-pull\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED by Kyle 2026-07-27 (session open of the 0.10.0 execution arc). The drafted charter (8a91c45) stands as the wave's governing doc: layer-as-designation with membership in the ARCHITECTURE.md table + Rule 11 DAG enforcement; record={atoms,lang,engine,store}, view={painted}, surfacing={sign,custody + app-side occupants TUI shell/loops-go by role}; relevance deliberately homeless behind the third-declaration-executed-judgment gate; record-never-imports-surfacing; relocation-on-pull governs the painted CLI-host extraction. Ratification evidence: two contacts survived pre-ratification \\u2014 the primitives grounding (evidence FOR deliberately-homeless) and the live-edge-staleness design (relevance-shaped item landing on consolidated dials with no home claimed, zero charter strain).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785115482.287886, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:rendering/tui-shell-integration\", \"observation:architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\", \"observation:paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"rendering/live-edge-staleness-on-read-path\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/live-edge-staleness-on-read-path\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"COMPLETE and shipped across all four layers (substrate 763c648 + snapshot-coherence fix cad6211 + footer, final commit tonight): (1) StoreReader.live_edge() single-statement on the chain fact_cursor boundary, snapshot-bracketed into vertex_fold; (2) FoldState/Window/--json carry edge_facts+edge_since for any consumer; (3) local session_start (Tier 0, fires at every session open \\u2014 a dead SessionEnd hook now surfaces at the NEXT SessionStart) and reconcile lenses; (4) in-repo fold lens footer in both registers, clock pinned via the _grammar.time.time seam. Judgment settled: shared is_stale dial anchored on oldest unsealed fact \\u2014 dormant quiet, accumulation fires. Survived the full sol HIGH loop including a TOCTOU finding against its own first cut. The sensor the second wiring death asked for now exists at the read path, where it cannot die with the wiring it watches.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785125244.185783, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"friction:seal-wiring-silent-death-second-occurrence\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"], \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\"}, \"architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"JSONL becomes the canonical store; sqlite a derived rebuildable index. Ratified by Kyle 2026-08-11. Authority flip: append site = one flushed JSONL line, receipt minted there (write-receipt at the byte-landing site); sqlite indexed after, caught up via Tailer byte-offset on open (offset in sqlite meta; tail-forward if behind; full rebuild if file shrank or head-hash at offset mismatches \\u2014 staleness-sensor pattern at the storage layer). Chain survives re-homing because all commitment hashes are JCS over field dicts with payload embedded as verbatim TEXT \\u2014 JSONL must carry payload as the exact stored string (never re-serialized) or signatures break. Format: ONE interleaved log with t=fact|tick discriminator \\u2014 global receipt order becomes a physical property of the file, one tail cursor. Layout: .loops/data/project.jsonl tracked, .loops/data/project.db gitignored; all store files move under .loops/data/ going forward. Scope: project store first, single-writer; multi-machine convergence deferred (goes through store/merge.py receive machinery when it comes, never git line-merge \\u2014 chain attests receipt order). History-mutating ops (absorb_edit, rebirth, compact) become loud file rewrites \\u2014 feature, rewrites should be un-ignorable in review. Migration oracle: export db->jsonl in rowid order, rebuild scratch db, sl store verify on both, chain heads must match before authority flips. Workflow this buys: diffable history, clone-and-have-history, backup-with-repo.\", \"alternatives\": \"promote FileStore: rejected \\u2014 pre-Receipt era (no id, no chain, whole-file-in-memory); new thin JSONL-append+Tailer-catchup layer beside SqliteStore instead, read surface untouched. Two files facts.jsonl+ticks.jsonl: rejected \\u2014 receipt order becomes a join, two cursors. Nested-JSON payload in line: rejected \\u2014 re-serialization breaks every signature. sqlite-canonical with jsonl export: rejected \\u2014 export is a lagging copy, not authority; the git-visible file must be the write site or diffs lie.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KTYV620K2XSFV6SX3QQNMDMQ\", \"_ts\": 1786460658.634949, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\"]}, \"store/verify-canonical-agreement\": {\"topic\": \"store/verify-canonical-agreement\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED + implemented (c0504ce..e41e1c5 + r4 remediation in flight). Shipped shape: engine/canonical_audit.py pure-reader module; L1 agreement gate (consumed-prefix last-line check, offset/count parity, marker-rewind-over-indexed-rows detection) default on verify/stats/ticks, rc=1 + named divergence; L3 honest labels; --deep streams the log and re-derives the chain from canonical content (2.5s on the live 111MB store, bytes/mtime untouched \\u2014 pure-reader constraint verified by sol). NAMED RESIDUE (sol r4 adjudication, accepted for this release): sl read is ungated \\u2014 it renders a poisoned index rc=0. Accepted because the ratified slice named verify/stats/ticks as the attestation verbs and read IS the advertised lag-repair route (gating it would break recovery). Architecturally still a correctness gap; the future shape sol recommends: a read gate that repairs-and-retries corroborated lag but refuses non-lag disagreement. Revisit when the store grows a second reader surface (TUI) \\u2014 same gate, both surfaces. r4 also forced the claim-scoping lesson one layer down: L1's lag classification could assert innocence it cannot know (unindexed suffix is uncorroboratable without --deep) \\u2014 remediation scopes the claim instead of expanding detection.\", \"alternatives\": \"verify-the-index-only (status quo): rejected \\u2014 rc=0 on a poisoned store is a false attestation, the exact lie-class the chain exists to prevent. always-deep verify: rejected as default \\u2014 O(full log) on every verify; 111MB live log makes honest-but-cheap the right default with --deep opt-in. JsonlStore-construction-as-verifier: rejected \\u2014 repair semantics destroy evidence.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZS0MT5H3JSBEE37KC8TP4MM\", \"_ts\": 1786485225.382178, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"implementation/cli-honesty-wave\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"AMENDMENT (arbiter, 2026-08-12, post-S1): S1's honesty clause is strengthened from note-only to REFUSE \\u2014 when no fetched kind carries a status field, 'sl read --status' exits 2 with the error on stderr; per-kind stderr notes apply only on MIXED fetches (some kinds status-bearing, some not); an honest empty at exit 0 is reserved for status-bearing rows that simply don't match. Rationale: note-beside-exit-0-empty is the friction's own script-misreadable defect; the wave's NON-NEGOTIABLE clause outranks the original S1 phrasing. Everything else in the prior emission stands unchanged (S1-S4 in scope, S5 deferred, slice order, S3 derivation ruling).\", \"alternatives\": \"slice order as-ruled-in-thread (exit-discipline first): rejected \\u2014 read --status is the pipeline's own gate instrument, building the precondition first makes every later gate invocation real; per-slice design facts: rejected \\u2014 one wave contract, frictions carry per-slice detail; S4 out of wave: rejected \\u2014 small, clear fix-shape, same discipline theme\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGDGDD443VR20Y9EFMHJ\", \"_ts\": 1786568819.196143, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\", \"friction:cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-no-validation\", \"friction:ls-vertex-not-found-exits-zero\", \"friction:read-status-filter-missing\", \"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\", \"friction:reindex-hint-omits-vertex-target\", \"thread:cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"alternatives\": \"CHANGELOG per-release Upgrading subsection: rejected as sole home because migrations outlive their release entry (a 0.9.0 user upgrading late still needs the ceremony) and CHANGELOG is frozen maintainer narrative; sl store migrate composite verb: deferred, scope beyond the docs ask; docs-only with no tool hint: weaker, the export success line is the natural place to print next steps\", \"message\": \"Ratified by shipping: docs/UPGRADING.md landed on main (24e0610), pushed both remotes, sent to the requesting user. The 0.10.0 flip ceremony is the flagship section; all sharp user_actions hand-verified against code before commit. The export-success-line tool hint remains open as the deferred dissolution half (docs-only-first ruling).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVW6D8WVSEJQN8KM2YFES33\", \"_ts\": 1786574644.647369, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\", \"friction:jsonl-canonical-log-exceeds-git-limit\"]}, \"practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\": {\"topic\": \"practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED \\u2014 README form settled with Kyle. Narrative-conceptual, NOT section-order/pitch: the concept is hard, the document teaches it. Register: March STRANGE-LOOPS.md declarative present ('Time is fundamental. The past happened.') held throughout \\u2014 the README is a FOLD not a fact history; speaks only from the now. What-Dissolved DROPPED from the doc \\u2014 dissolution lineage lives in the store (paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement), which also serves freshness (no time-anchored claims to rot). Spine: opening move = the lie of the state table (a row nobody witnessed) -> what a writer actually possesses; then truths GROWN (add: witnessing travels/signing, meaning binds at read, scale is residence) -> atoms -> pattern; one observation's life threaded as running example; four skins + painted-as-shared-lens-substrate appear as the now of the pattern, not as argument evidence. Draft next; landing waits on merge-gate freeze or negotiated window.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW7QKZWVT627FQRYHHVYH91\", \"_ts\": 1786581089.916872, \"_n\": 5, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\", \"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"observation:paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-08-13 (Kyle overrides the probe framing with a succession argument, accepted): v2 is a SUCCESSOR build, not a throwaway probe. Kyle's reasoning: the current CLI accreted against a moving substrate (libs developed under it, painted added into it) \\u2014 each libs evolution left a compensation layer in the CLI (foldkey warnings, residence special-casing, strict resolution living in commands/emit.py); the mixture is more trouble than it's worth vs a clean iterative rebuild. Agent-use frictions (k=v syntax, file handling) support JSON-first generic surface. This DISSOLVES the review's second-semantic-implementation objection \\u2014 that was a maintenance argument assuming two CLIs coexisting; succession with a kill date is a different object. The painted-fork objection resolves by sequencing: v2 is rendering-LAST (generic libs surface first, thoroughly tested per stage, whole monorepo under it, THEN rendering) \\u2014 see painted-strip-cost-analysis for why rendering-last beats rendering-never. Conditions attached (see design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions): libs-handoff is the critical path; old-CLI freeze ratchet at v2 start; parity ledger over practice workflows; result envelopes are the rendering seam from phase 0.\", \"alternatives\": \"full from-scratch build by GPT: rejected as primary path \\u2014 second semantic implementation, unpriced painted fork, duplicates ratified VertexHandle direction; libs handoff without CLI fork: recommended; hybrid (v2 as throwaway probe exercising new libs APIs): viable if Kyle wants an independent forcing consumer for VertexHandle S5, but scope it as a probe, not a successor\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYKBCRVEJ00KTJQ3AFZGJ9D,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS\", \"_ts\": 1786660365.045652, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"observation:architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\", \"observation:test/sol-conceptual-model-review\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:cli-error-surface-unification\"]}, \"architecture/libs-handoff-scope\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Contract basis for the libs handoff derived from Sol's LIBS_CHANGES (branch cli-v2-proposal), triaged 2026-08-13. IN SCOPE as tasks (P0): jsonl-declaration-ceremonies (absorb_genesis/absorb_edit on JSONL-canonical \\u2014 atomic multi-row ceremony in the log, stale-head refusal leaves log+index byte-equivalent, index stays pure derivation); declaration-plan-apply-api (plan_declaration_update/apply \\u2014 one high-level op owning head-capture, diff, residence, signing; today every client re-assembles an 8-step protocol); declaration-file-store-recovery (durable intent + idempotent recover for the store-first-then-file-cache gap). IN SCOPE (P1): observer-grant-engine-resolution (THE HOLE \\u2014 engine gates only caller-supplied Grant, declared ObserverDecl.grant.potential silently bypassable; fix at the engine boundary, bypass must be explicit); receipt-attestation-state (persisted signed-state on Receipt/ReceiveResult from the committed row \\u2014 passes write-receipt-vs-temporal-query, your write's attestation is your write's identity); bounded-fact-query (cross-kind limit+cursor query \\u2014 MUST spec against the shipped 0.8.0 temporal-cursor contract and A3 ids-never-ordered, not Sol's FactCursor sketch); strict-contract-ruling (MODIFIED from Sol: strict IS enforced, at the CLI (commands/emit.py three-source precedence); ruling needed on whether enforcement moves to engine receive \\u2014 same push-admission-into-engine motion as observer-grant \\u2014 Sol's 'unenforced' premise was half wrong); lang-kdl-mutation-api (export add/edit/remove_vertex_kind over existing kdl_insert_child/kdl_remove_child + loops{}-creation + LoopDef-to-KDL serializer); target-probe-api (probe_target -> TargetInfo, dissolves per-client residence/suffix logic); canonical-audit-preflight (typed audit-only/audit-then-open/recover-then-open, never conflate verify with repair). DEFERRED (P2, promote on forcing consumer): lifecycle-projection helper, shared result codec, search coordinator, maintenance backend matrix. SEQUENCING: VertexHandle S5 checkpoint precedes any consumer cutover; the throwaway probe (task:cli-v2-probe) is the independent forcing consumer that exercises these APIs as they land. Collisions honored: exit-code/machine-codes work stays with thread:cli-error-surface-unification, not duplicated here.\", \"alternatives\": \"adopt LIBS_CHANGES verbatim as 13 tasks: rejected \\u2014 P2s are granularity ahead of need, strict item had a false premise, cursor item ignores shipped temporal-cursor work; single mega-task: rejected \\u2014 items have independent forcing consumers and different review depth\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYK157RRH7SXX3358WMEPV5,01KXV453R7C6PB5EC7RJ5HHEED\", \"_ts\": 1786659263.027504, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED by Kyle 2026-08-13: all four conditions accepted (libs-handoff-first, freeze ratchet, parity ledger, envelope-first). Rendering-last explicitly confirmed as acceptable \\u2014 the plain-text/JSON stretch is not a concern. Next: parity-ledger investigation (what does the ledger actually enumerate).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYM394WKC248CCEDS4STAZJ,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS,01KZYK2SST0TWJ6J3AWE8BTPDP\", \"_ts\": 1786660637.375833, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"task:cli-v2-probe\"]}, \"architecture/jsonl-declaration-ceremony-encoding\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/jsonl-declaration-ceremony-encoding\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (arbiter, 2026-08-13; spot-checked against sqlite_store.py/jsonl_store.py): declaration ceremonies on JSONL-canonical stores. (1) GENESIS NEEDS NO NEW GRAMMAR \\u2014 _decl.genesis is one ordinary fact row; refusal existed only because sqlite CAS could roll back after row build; dissolves by reordering into JsonlStore._write's five-step shape (reconcile -> BEGIN IMMEDIATE -> all CAS+signing staged -> append one line + fsync -> stamp+commit). (2) MULTI-ROW EDIT = ONE t=batch LINE, rows array of >=2 verbatim fact records; one line IS the log's existing atomicity unit, so partial-ceremony recovery is inherited from torn-tail truncation for free. Codec structural rules: >=2 rows, fact records only (no ticks, no nesting), intra-batch dup-id rejected, no extra envelope keys. D1: same-ts is a CEREMONY rule (absorb_edit stamps, audit_deep asserts for all-_decl batches), NOT a codec rule \\u2014 keeps batch reusable for future batch-emit (atoms/typed-edge-array-values). Stale expected_head leaves LOG byte-identical; index may lawfully converge toward log pre-CAS. Open stays two cheap checks (batch bounded by ceremony size). Go alignment via golden .jsonl fixtures in-repo (positive + pinned negative refusal classes), consumed by the Go oracle when it lands. reanchor stays refused (scope pin). Rejected: prepare/commit framing (dead bytes / replay buffering / Go state machine), multi-line-one-fsync (POSIX prefix persistence), single-fact edit collapse (rewrites S2 resolver + Go mirror), ceremony-id flags. Full text: docs/scratch/libs-handoff-wave/s1a-encoding-proposal.md. 10 acceptance tests = S1b's gate oracle.\", \"alternatives\": \"prepare/commit framing: rejected (durable never-indexed lines break index-as-pure-derivation); multi-line single-fsync: rejected (undetectable well-formed prefix); payload-collapsed single fact: rejected (rewrites resolver protocol); codec-enforced same-ts: rejected per D1\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYP3FMWCW9B00DNM8626673,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS\", \"_ts\": 1786662798.73825, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"thread:libs-handoff-wave\"]}}}, \"retrospective\": {\"items\": {\"internal-table-s0-hardening\": {\"name\": \"internal-table-s0-hardening\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"S0\\u2192hardening (2026-07-11\\u219213), the 0.7.0 gate. Shipped: document form, absorb ceremony + atomic absorb_genesis, store-backed resolver seam, read exclusion, edit ceremony (shared-ts + CAS), ontology-as-of, then 8-finding hardening (identity adoption, rewind honesty, pin enforcement, ingress safety) to Sol CLOSE; param-secrets $VAR indirection closed the surviving policy question. Process: (1) review altitude must match claim altitude \\u2014 every per-slice pass + clean capstone missed 8 cross-slice blockers a holistic high-effort review found; (2) reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test ratcheted four rounds to convergence, and hunting holes-introduced-by-fixes caught 2 regressions green suites missed; (3) slices delegate, seams don't \\u2014 they-plan subtasks optimize stated exit criteria, arc conscience stays at the wheel; (4) right-altitude blockers upgrade designs (TOCTOU\\u2192absorb_genesis, identity\\u2192adopt ceremony) \\u2014 reviews are forcing-functions, not just filters. First instance of the retrospective kind; full prose draft in docs/dev/internal-table-retrospective-2026-07-13.md (local) is now redundant with this fact + its ref'd observations.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXETB3ZG37HHR6GHFFBY8CC1,01KXETB495MSBRF73AS5KKVS3J,01KXETB4EDYX3PT2FWXNDAJV84,01KXETBERETBRZWSH7R72KH33E\", \"_ts\": 1783990435.202928, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"observation:practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"observation:workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"completion-t3-build\": {\"name\": \"completion-t3-build\", \"feature\": \"completion-t3\", \"message\": \"Completion T3 (2026-07-13\\u219214): four worker slices (1 Opus, 3 Sonnet) + six Sol review rounds to CLOSE, in one continuous orchestrated arc \\u2014 first full application of the internal-table retro's process rules, same session they were written. What held: (1) reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test drove 8\\u21928\\u21926\\u21924\\u21922\\u2192CLOSE convergence again \\u2014 and rounds 2-5 were nearly ALL holes-in-my-fixes (wrong entry module for the render-free test, honesty fix importing a 5s path, COUNT guard as unbounded as what it guarded, --plain fixed on one surface leaking on three others): the 'fixes deserve MORE adversarial attention' rule is now twice-confirmed; (2) review-altitude: the arc-level reviewer was pointed at the branch from the start this time \\u2014 no per-slice pass masked a seam gap, the seams (S4 composing S2/S3, main.py entry vs cli.app) were where findings clustered exactly as predicted; (3) delegation boundary held: slices to workers, every remediation at the wheel. New lessons: (a) an honesty rule (store-canonical declarations) collides with a latency contract (instant TAB) at a real seam \\u2014 the resolution was a new primitive (_completion_declaration, StoreBusy) not a compromise on either; (b) reviewer positions can be WRONG in both directions: my lens-error position was refuted by code (resolve swallowed the error) and fixing the behavior beat defending the claim, while the lockfile-parity BLOCK was correctly converted to a dissent note by naming the convention it would break; (c) upstream fixes belong upstream \\u2014 two painted defects found, one fixed in painted same-session (8610e57) rather than papered over in loops.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXFF13SN49856XCEV833V9J7,01KXETB495MSBRF73AS5KKVS3J,01KXETB3ZG37HHR6GHFFBY8CC1\", \"_ts\": 1784004271.91754, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"observation:practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"thread:cli-autocomplete-via-painted\"]}, \"080-overnight-multi-model-run\": {\"name\": \"080-overnight-multi-model-run\", \"message\": \"Arc-level synthesis of the 2026-07-16/17 overnight 0.8.0 run (entered on Kyle's full delegation: Opus/Sonnet implement, codex advise+review, loops-claude arbitrate, morning review+retro). WHAT WORKED: (1) The cross-family adversarial pipeline earned its keep at EVERY layer \\u2014 see observation:practice/cross-family-review-yield-080; neither family's green output survived the other's review unamended, and the arbiter's own v2 fallback design was caught breaching its own explicitness clause by the Claude honesty panel. (2) The session-limit outage (00:00-01:20) became a structural test the pipeline passed: codex carried 6 dossier chapters + the s1 advisor solo while the Claude fleet slept; the dossier's 2 surviving Claude chapters + codex's converging independent recommendation meant design never stalled. (3) Design-then-implement discipline held under time pressure: 4 ratified/proposed design facts BEFORE any implementation launch; every implementation deviation was recorded honestly by the agents rather than silently improvised \\u2014 the deviation reports were where several review findings started. (4) Checkout discipline (single-writer main checkout, worktrees for parallel tracks) prevented every collision except one flagged file-region overlap that merged cleanly. WHAT TO FIX: (1) codex 'at capacity' killed one capstone run after 166k tokens \\u2014 retry worked, but long codex reviews need a cheaper resume shape. (2) The scratch-docs-untracked gap: reviewers in worktrees couldn't see docs/scratch/080-overnight (uncommitted); committed now as b7b26da \\u2014 design records should commit as they accrue, not at wrap. (3) Two Claude reader failures produced complete-but-unreturned chapters (files written, structured return lost to the limit) \\u2014 the file-then-return pattern saved the work; make it the default for all long readers. (4) My A5 auto-route lean and the advisor's owner-only pre-decision were both convenience-smuggling catches \\u2014 the two-gate rule (each family reviews the other) is the durable defense; keep it for design sessions, not just code. DEFERRED HONESTLY: TUI shell slices (S0 net landed first by design), VertexHandle S4-S7 (rung-4 checkpoint required-for-cutover), Digest implementation (Kyle's gate), aggregate cursor vectors, GlobalReceiptPosition + receipt-group-id protocol amendments (one oracle-coordination package).\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRQHRJ84T0QDPDBQCZG2M1X,01KXRHS2KGBF5C24EEGRPYF588,01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784315191.057905, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"observation:practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"090-review-pipeline-high-tier\": {\"name\": \"090-review-pipeline-high-tier\", \"message\": \"First run of the sol-HIGH tier (previous waves: low interim / medium capstone). Economics: 5/5 round-1 findings landed in exactly the two zones the brief predicted slice review could not see (cross-slice seams, unreviewed rider increments) \\u2014 high-tier full-diff earns its cost there and only there. New calibration finding, sharper than any prior round: BEHAVIOR FIXES SURVIVE ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION AT A MUCH HIGHER RATE THAN RATCHETS DO (5/5 behavior fixes held round 2; 3/4 ratchets fell to constructed evasions, and one hardened ratchet fell AGAIN round 3). A ratchet written against the known reintroduction is regression-shaped; ratchet-shaped means surviving evasions its author did not construct \\u2014 so ratchets should be priced a verification round of their own. Recurring defect class of the whole review wave: FIELD-NAME/CALL-NAME ENUMERATION (FoldSection rebuild, Rule 9 string-grep, Rule 10 field list twice) \\u2014 enumerate-by-hand is the smell; the fix each time was iterate-the-structure. Also first wave where arbiter took a fix commit directly (b7d623c) \\u2014 right call for a test-file one-liner at round 3, would be wrong earlier in the loop. Pipeline roles held: opus impl survived an API-death mid-wave with clean resume-from-branch-state; idle-race mitigation (verify branch before believing pings) fired correctly 4/4 times.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFVV8CRT3505Y817JW8X588,01KYFR3XJ96X8KMR1XVDC4GMBB\", \"_ts\": 1785091432.92345, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"010-jsonl-canonical-store\": {\"name\": \"010-jsonl-canonical-store\", \"message\": \"JSONL-canonical arc (2026-08-11, design-to-converged in one day): 45 commits, 5 sol HIGH rounds (17 findings, all remediated or dispositioned), 2 workflows / 27 agents, 4-angle simplify, ~4170 tests, live store migrated + honestly attested. Five lessons: (1) SCOPE-THE-CLAIM over widen-the-detection, 3 instances (out-of-band detection docs, verify quick-label, lag-innocence boolean) \\u2014 promoted to named principle and global CLAUDE.md; when a detector overclaims, narrow its claim (location, not verdict) before growing it. (2) The reuse/simplify angle is a distinct DETECTION MODALITY, not polish: 5 old-idiom residue sites found by grepping the REPLACED idiom after 4 adversarial rounds missed them \\u2014 residue is stale-but-working, so fault-injection structurally cannot produce this finding class. Cross-repo confirmed: simplify is now standard process in siftd too. (3) r2-after-simplify position is load-bearing: simplify introduced the arc's only regression (rebuild source-mutation), caught only by the post-simplify sol round \\u2014 any code-touching pass, quality passes included, reopens the review obligation behind it (third confirmation of fixes-deserve-more-adversarial-attention, after internal-table and completion-t3). (4) Fix-disposition discipline is ENCODABLE: found-then-dropped escapes went 1 to 0 across four rounds once every-finding-gets-a-disposition entered the prompts \\u2014 prompt-text sufficed, so it belongs in the impl-pipeline skill; candidate for store-native finding facts with status lifecycle. (5) Apply-agent git incident (add -A briefly committed the live store, popped a foreign stash; self-caught, excised, verified clean): apply-phase agents with commit authority need worktree isolation (siftd adopted) or a .loops/ commit fence \\u2014 a doctrine-legitimate detection ratchet at an ambient-authority boundary. Task filed.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZSE9TJF6M3PSMFFWTHQZBTA,01KZVPHRGQ4ZRJNXQ271Y9CWZ9,01KYFXBFQKNJR13D1XTR09AYDM,01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G,01KZSE9TDHVXMPMHMX4161CGJN\", \"_ts\": 1786562292.335039, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/construction-vs-detection-ratchets\", \"decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"observation:session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"chw-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\": {\"name\": \"chw-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\", \"message\": \"First live run of the impl-pipeline skill: CLI-honesty wave, one session, CONVERGED at sol r7. SHAPE: empirical pre-flight (multi-writer, code-read upgraded to receipts) -> 4 worktree slices with independent gates (8/8, 8/8, 6/6, 9/9) -> 7 cross-family rounds -> 4-angle simplify (11 items) -> 3-round convergence tail. 19 findings, every one dispositioned; ~40 commits; suite +80 tests; zero escapes. WHAT THE SHAKEDOWN PROVED: (1) every early defect was pipeline-mechanics not code \\u2014 worktree base races, env-weaker worktrees (untracked .loops), wrong-binary verification, missing SendMessage on gates \\u2014 each dissolved into a skill rule same-session; (2) the finding-ledger-as-query closed the loop literally: the --status instrument S1 built caught the ARBITER dropped disposition at wave close; (3) detection-ratchet taxonomy confirmed again \\u2014 the cite gate fell twice then dissolved into resolver acceptance (construction), and the simplify pass parity ratchet surfaced a latent substrate divergence sol then proved reachable; (4) the convergence tail was a visibility cascade \\u2014 falsy-key fix exposed lookup bug exposed replay-identity bug, severity declining, each fix DISSOLVING the prior fix machinery (per-step lookup -> once-resolved winner), ending at a design question correctly held at the owner gate (fold-key identity) with disclosure pinned in tests; (5) cross-repo routing practice born mid-wave (2 painted frictions emitted upstream), concurrent-session collision survived with verified-not-trusted state + worktree-per-session landed same-day. COST SHAPE: sol went 7 rounds, findings clustered exactly where the skill predicts (seams, fix commits); the three unverified fixes all passed, pricing the no-gate-for-small-fixes tradeoff correctly. HELD OPEN: merge-to-main at Kyle gate; thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string design session; thread:cli-error-surface-unification + friction:sync-errors-exit-zero as the next wave seeds.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KZVZ0Q3Q9CK27A27CD3Y0F1S,01KZW4XWGC1MP4RQ5K952B688G\", \"_ts\": 1786578262.651132, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\", \"thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string\"]}, \"libs-handoff-wave\": {\"name\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"RETROSPECTIVE, libs-handoff wave (2026-08-13, one session, ~6h build-to-converged). SHAPE: 10 ratified tasks -> 8 slices (1 split into design-ratify-then-implement) -> 8 independent gates -> 8 sol HIGH rounds -> CONVERGED r8; 130 commits, 24 sol findings + 4 gate blockers, zero refuted, zero escapes; full monorepo green. WHAT THE ARC PROVED: (1) The five mid-wave skill amendments all confirmed against the completed arc \\u2014 ratify-gate-one-level-down (S1a's encoding fact was cited by three later slices AND by two remediation rulings), blocking-fix-to-original-impl loop (5 uses, one round-trip each), mutation-verification standard (used by every gate-ordered fix and both arbiter fixes), pointer branches, arbiter-fix discipline (2 arbiter fixes both sol-verified after). (2) Construction-vs-detection now has MEASURED economics: construction held first-contact every time; detection averaged ~3 rounds; and the arms-race terminator is blacklist-to-whitelist \\u2014 narrow-the-claim's second-level form, which makes the reviewer's search space finite (ref observation:practice/construction-vs-detection-measured). (3) The two verification layers catch disjoint classes \\u2014 gates: say/do + test-strength; sol: constructed inputs; zero overlap all wave (ref observation:practice/gate-layer-vs-crossfamily-layer-catch-classes). (4) Spec-author-as-cross-family-reviewer works; receipted deviations survive, unreceipted drift does not (ref observation:practice/sol-author-verifier-loop). (5) Simplify: residue-detection AND regression-introduction both reproduced; the pass is net-positive only with the re-review; efficiency items on contract-bearing paths need a contract-check line (ref observation:practice/simplify-pass-double-edge). NEW SKILL INPUTS not yet folded: codex content-filter brief guidance (friction:codex-cyber-filter-on-review-briefs, corrected diagnosis: commit repros, never generate hostile inputs live); gitignore-swallows-receipts ratchet candidate (friction:gitignore-swallows-wave-receipts, bit twice). DEFERRED with receipts: CLI migration onto the new APIs (the forcing-consumer slice, per succession plan), test-scaffolding conftest dedup, kind-predicate range form, receive-as-stale-ast, strict-vs-transport ruling. NEXT: Kyle sleeps on it; merge to main is tomorrow's decision; then the cli-v2 probe becomes the first real consumer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZZ5NE65SA93E7DVC4SQGZ6R,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS,01KZYY3M7RK7HVB2HETVRK504H,01KZZ5RM1GB878Y04A1X1CBJXJ,01KZZ5RM6YSR4KE084TP007SKV,01KZZ5S12BQ6ZSP8V1WVMKJ2B2,01KZZ5S1857ACVE6N80TBVJE4P\", \"_ts\": 1786678922.058099, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"observation:practice/construction-vs-detection-measured\", \"observation:practice/gate-layer-vs-crossfamily-layer-catch-classes\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-v2-amendments\", \"observation:practice/simplify-pass-double-edge\", \"observation:practice/sol-author-verifier-loop\", \"thread:libs-handoff-wave\"]}, \"agy-opus-workflow-first-live-run\": {\"name\": \"agy-opus-workflow-first-live-run\", \"message\": \"First live run of the codex-replacement impl flow (receipt-order arc, PR #8, 2026-08-15/16): Sonnet Workflow explore -> Opus implement (fenced worktree, main-session gate) -> gemini flash per-slice review -> gemini 3.1 Pro full-branch sweep. VERDICT: keep it. Findings ledger: explore caught 3 plan-invalidating facts pre-code; flash found 4 real findings across slices (one that Opus + gate both missed) but is trustworthy on negatives ONLY under an explicit proof-of-work bar (file:line ranges + personally-run probe per category, built to fail if the defect existed) \\u2014 without it, bare APPROVEs; Pro found the one cross-slice blocker (1-member aggregate fold/resolve divergence) and the unpinned-as_of class in one pass but violated the read-only fence (wrote probes into the repo) and stalled mid-review asking a question in one-shot print mode. Gate caught what models missed: stash-based false 'pre-existing' proof (stash is a no-op against committed changes), env-dependent test failures misattributed to the branch. Traps for the skill (Kyle's ~/Code/skills/delegating-to-antigravity, ask before editing): commit-before-power-proof (git restore reverted uncommitted fixes twice), proof-of-work bar for reviewer negatives, one-shot delivery clause + 45m print-timeout for full sweeps. Honest caveat: per-slice rounds converged; the full sweep's fix round was gate-verified only, no reviewer re-pass.\", \"_ts\": 1786856610.152275, \"_n\": 1}, \"antigravity-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\": {\"name\": \"antigravity-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\", \"message\": \"FIRST LIVE RUN of the antigravity-impl-pipeline skill (2026-08-17/18, arrival slice 0, converged). The skill asked to be treated as a trial and receipted; this is that receipt. VERDICT: KEEP. The agy fleet earned its roles; the composition (Claude implements + agy reviews) held cross-family the whole way.\\n\\nWHAT THE FLEET DID WELL. Stage E (six flash-low explorers, parallel, ~4 min wall-clock): 6/6 spot-checked citations EXACT, schema-conformant first attempt, clean worktree, honest not_covered fields. It surfaced the locking precedent (fcntl.flock/O_EXCL/atomic rename) that turned the slice-0 concurrency design from invent into adopt. flash-HIGH as slice reviewer was the surprise: four rounds, every one carrying real proof-of-work with pasted probes, including probes IT designed (a 6-writer/2-reader concurrency probe, a TOCTOU check on the anchor adoption site, seven distinguishing cases proving a refactor behaviour-identical). Rounds 1 and 2 found seven real defects, two blocking; rounds 3 and 4 came back clean AND legitimate \\u2014 the clean rounds were audited for proof-of-work before being accepted, which is the check that makes a zero-finding round mean anything. Review worktree swept clean after all four dispatches: zero strays, better harness discipline than pro's receipted behaviour.\\n\\nPROCESS FINDINGS TO FOLD BACK INTO THE SKILL:\\n1. COVERAGE-SHAPED vs CITATION-SHAPED explorer questions. The one-spot-check-per-report calibration works for citation claims but NOT for inventory claims (q2's suffix collision inventory) \\u2014 a missed suffix cannot show up in a spot check. Inventories deserve an arbiter-side confirmation grep; citations do not. New rule for Stage E.\\n2. STALE-PACKAGE POWER PROOFS (the sharpest finding, and it is a correctness hazard in the METHOD not the code). `uv run --package engine` rebuilds per invocation, so rapid successive edits can run a test against a STALE copy \\u2014 and the failure mode makes a break look GREEN (uncaught), never red. A power-proof harness without a liveness assertion silently under-reports. Fix adopted by both implementer and gate: assert with inspect.getsource that the interpreter imported the BROKEN source before running the test. Directionally safe: every prior \\\"caught\\\" result stays sound; only \\\"uncaught\\\" results were ever suspect. This belongs in the skill's power-proof section for ANY workspace-package repo.\\n3. THE UNVERIFIED-FIXES ENUMERATION IS THE HIGH-VALUE STAGE. Round 2 \\u2014 pointed explicitly at breaking round 1's fixes, with each fix commit named against the finding it answers \\u2014 found the two blocking defects of the whole arc. The skill's claim that rounds 2+ are dominated by holes in round-1 fixes is confirmed empirically.\\n4. DO-NOT-RE-REPORT LISTS MUST CARRY ARBITER RULINGS, not just design rulings. Each round's list grew with the previous round's rulings and accepted residuals; zero findings in rounds 2-4 were re-litigations. The list is what kept a converging review converging.\\n5. AGY MECHANICS held exactly as the skill documents: flags before -p, .structured_output not .response, --json-schema requires --output-format json, --print-timeout explicit (45m; longest actual round ~10 min, but a timeout discards everything so the ceiling stays generous), scratch dir as the only legal write path.\\n\\nONE GAP IN THE SKILL, worth adding: the role table has NO DESIGNER ROW, and Stage E says the arbiter writes the contract while a ratified plan fact said a design agent proposes. The plan fact won. Design proposals are VERDICT-SHAPED work and must route to Claude, never to flash \\u2014 the same rule Stage E states for explorers, but the skill never says it for designers. Recommend adding a Designer row: Claude subagent, ratify-gated, never agy.\\n\\nCOST SHAPE: four review rounds at ~40-52k output tokens each with very large cache reads; wall-clock per round 3-10 min. Cheap enough that the iterate-until-dry discipline is affordable, which is the precondition for Kyle's convergence ruling being practical rather than aspirational.\", \"_ts\": 1787031467.5701, \"_n\": 1}, \"arrival-cutA-pipeline-round\": {\"name\": \"arrival-cutA-pipeline-round\", \"message\": \"CUT A PIPELINE RETROSPECTIVE (2026-08-18, same-day arc, Kyle present at every ratify gate). (Re-emit of 01M0B8K9T8 under the correct fold key \\u2014 retrospective folds by name=, second topic=/name= miss this session; the emit-discipline lesson is now: check the kind's fold key BEFORE emitting, the vertex file is the authority.) What the round teaches:\\n\\n1. THE REFUTATION RATE IS THE SIMPLIFY PASS'S QUALITY SIGNAL. Two of nine simplify moves were REFUTED by the apply agent's own verification-before-application \\u2014 the pre-flight serialize (sqlite REAL affinity would launder codec-invalid rows through the committed-row check) and the consumed-None 'unreachable' arm (reachable via genesis-mint-in-the-gap, a legal multi-process interleave the finding's serial-flow premise missed). Both refutations produced BETTER artifacts than the fixes would have (a load-bearing comment; a dedicated interleave pin test). The conditional-apply instruction ('verify the ordering claim yourself before deleting') is what made refutation possible \\u2014 unconditional apply lists convert wrong findings into regressions. This is the 010 lesson (simplify introduced the arc's only regression) advanced one stage: catch it at APPLY time, not re-review time.\\n\\n2. CROSS-FAMILY IS A PROPERTY, NOT A VENDOR. codex/sol usage-limited mid-arc; the agy/Gemini fleet substituted with zero pipeline-shape change (3 scoped flash-high rounds with executed-probe evidence + gemini-pro readiness). Grading honestly: flash's executed probes beat pro's read-heavy evidence this round; pro's value-claim (seam-reading) was not falsified but also not exercised \\u2014 the branch may simply have been dry. Sol belt-and-braces available post-reset (Aug 19 23:00).\\n\\n3. A ZERO-FINDING CROSS-FAMILY ROUND IS CREDIBLE WHEN THE CODE ALREADY SURVIVED EXECUTED ADVERSARIAL STAGES (advisor race-catch, independent gate with fresh oracle, mutation demos). Slice 0's r1 found four because it reviewed a first draft; cut A's r1 found zero because the gate loop ran first. Sequence gates before cross-family review; do not read zero findings as reviewer weakness without checking what preceded it.\\n\\n4. THE MAIN-CHECKOUT FULL-SUITE RUN EARNED ITS LOAD-BEARING BILLING AGAIN: surfaced Rule 17's environment-dependence (globs gitignored local docs; green in every worktree and CI, red only where the scratch history lives \\u2014 finding:rule17-scans-untracked-docs, fix shape git ls-files).\\n\\n5. ARBITER OVERRULE OF ITS OWN APPLY LIST (the gap-branch assert): a design that promises refuse-or-consume on legal interleave cannot carry a crash on a reachable interleave, however exotic; the multi-process gate is the license that makes 'exotic' insufficient grounds.\\n\\n6. SUBAGENT MODEL ROUTING was invisible until Kyle asked: every Claude subagent had inherited the arbiter's Fable. Now ruled + codified in both pipeline skills + memory: explicit model per launch, opus for impl/gate/apply, sonnet for exploration.\\n\\nReceipts: task/arrival-slice-A @ 01M0B8HXRV (full loop), docs/scratch/arrival-sliceA/ (all ledgers, briefs, reports, the failed sol attempt), decision:design/arrival-sliceA-authority @ 01M0B0Z14T.\", \"_ts\": 1787084529.297853, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"01M0B8HXRV039D1QR5Q0RF8QDG\"]}, \"arrival-cutB-pipeline-round\": {\"name\": \"arrival-cutB-pipeline-round\", \"message\": \"CUT B \\u2014 PROJECTIONS pipeline round retro (2026-08-18, one session, Kyle present at both gates). SHAPE: full antigravity pipeline \\u2014 Stage E (6 flash-low explorers, all citations spot-checked) -> opus design agent -> Kyle ratified with 2 explicit rulings (restamp dissolution; Q9 Rule-18 departure) -> opus impl 8 commits, 9 disclosed deviations -> opus gate FINDINGS NON-BLOCKING with own oracle + own mutations (refuted 2 of the arbiter's brief claims \\u2014 the gate gating the arbiter works) -> Kyle ruled #9 ratified + F1 fix-now -> 3 remediation commits, gate re-check CLEAN -> 3 flash-high scoped reviews, 2 findings, both fixed -> 4-angle seeded simplify, 5 moves (1 composed from 2-angle convergence, 1 load-bearing perf restoration mutation-proofed 33-red) -> gemini-3.1-pro readiness CONVERGED 7/7 PASS. Arbiter independently re-executed the discriminating M5 mutation (19+14 red) per the cutA read-heavy-readiness precedent. WORKED: deviation-disclosure culture (9 deviations all survived scrutiny, several strictly stronger than the contract \\u2014 the id-guard on the own_lineage licence prevented a real corruption B6 would have enabled); the seeded-angle simplify returned a composed finding and a genuine perf regression the review rounds missed; findings-as-store-facts made the final reconciliation a one-liner (12 findings, 0 open). LESSONS: (1) jq '//' fallback suppressed pro's coverage field \\u2014 nearly ordered a 60m rerun for evidence that existed unread; read the full structured object before judging proof-of-work. (2) Rule 17 scans docs/scratch and bit THREE agent drafts this round \\u2014 briefs must paraphrase retired vocabulary; consider the git-ls-files scope fix (finding:rule17-scans-untracked-docs) before cut C. (3) The impl's fence departure pattern (Rule 17 allowlist, guard unification into receive.py) was right both times BUT only because each carried a both-sites-red proof \\u2014 proof-of-work justifies scope calls, prompts should say so explicitly. (4) agy idle pings race SendMessage reports; verify branch state before acting on any ping. RESIDUE CARRIED: perf benchmark (O(n) derived-log regen per merge) still unmeasured \\u2014 named pre-ship; _create-self-enforce guard question awaits a Kyle ruling; JsonlStore.catch_up twin race waits for its cut; sol belt-and-braces round remains Kyle's standing option after the codex reset (Aug 19 23:00).\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0B9HPN7J5TP508793S6BV0W\", \"_ts\": 1787096957.205351, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task/arrival-slice-B\"]}, \"arrival-cutC-pipeline-round\": {\"name\": \"arrival-cutC-pipeline-round\", \"note\": \"Cut C ORDERING: same-day impl->converged. 6 slices C0-C5 (opus impl + independent opus gates via pointer branches, every gate PASS with novel-mechanic power proofs), agy r1 3 flash-high scopes zero findings with executed probes, 4-angle simplify (4 moves mutation-proved, 2 negative findings), pro readiness r1-r3: F1 ByKey('ts') per-surface divergence -> family rule unified in atoms.resolve_key_field (+adjacent _ROW_COLUMNS same-class fix); hypothesis source-constant seeding surfaced pre-existing kinds() _decl leak (scope-the-claim fix); F2 refuted (fold-key vocabulary, provenance-traced), refutation adversarially audited r3 -> CONVERGED zero findings. Process lessons: (1) launcher-behind-& trap bit once (tracked wrapper exits, children detach) \\u2014 poll files; (2) hypothesis constants-seeding makes worktree suites discover latent bugs main misses \\u2014 treat as a feature, keep caches; (3) readiness pro rounds each produced exactly one real seam finding scoped rounds could not see, at ~30min/round; (4) refutation-audit round (r3) is the cheap way to converge on an arbiter refutation without self-certifying.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787242241.458218, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"]}}}, \"finding\": {\"items\": {\"smoke-test-finding\": {\"name\": \"smoke-test-finding\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"Smoke test complete \\u2014 kind declaration works; dismissed.\", \"_ts\": 1786564356.85362, \"_n\": 2}, \"chw-s3-deviation-sl-entrypoint-fallthrough\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-deviation-sl-entrypoint-fallthrough\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"message\": \"Disposition (caught by the wave-close ledger check \\u2014 the r2-gate invocation running on its own wave): acted on same-hour (mid-flight warnings to S1/S2, verify-which-binary rule added to the impl-pipeline skill at the retro) but never formally dispositioned until the --status open query surfaced it at close. FIXED via the skill rule; the catch itself is retro material \\u2014 the arbiter drops dispositions too, which is why the ledger is a query and not a memory.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F\", \"_ts\": 1786578232.200113, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\"], \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\": {\"name\": \"chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"Arbiter disposition: deviation ACCEPTED, no code change. Refusing (exit 2, stderr) when no fetched kind carries a status field beats the contract's note-only shape \\u2014 a stderr note beside exit-0 empty stdout reproduces the friction's exact defect (script-misreadable). The NON-NEGOTIABLE exit-discipline clause outranks S1's weaker phrasing; contract amended by design re-emit.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVZ8Q2V01BHJ8N176G84PF\", \"_ts\": 1786568818.775865, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"friction:read-status-filter-missing\"], \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s3-status-not-consulted\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-status-not-consulted\", \"status\": \"deferred\", \"agent\": \"s3-gate\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"Gate observation: sensor counts any reconcile-* thread regardless of status= \\u2014 a planned reconcile emitted status=open would read as done. Arbiter disposition: DEFERRED \\u2014 matches the ruled derivation (name-prefix only); narrow to resolved-only if a planned-reconcile thread pattern ever emerges.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVZ8Q2V01BHJ8N176G84PF\", \"_ts\": 1786568703.158569, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"chw-s3-floor-rounding\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-floor-rounding\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"s3-gate\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"Gate observation: int() floors age (9.99d renders 9d ago). Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED \\u2014 understates but never overstates staleness, display never straddles the OVERDUE marker; deliberate.\", \"_ts\": 1786568703.698188, \"_n\": 1}, \"chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\": {\"name\": \"chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r2-fix\", \"role\": \"remediation\", \"message\": \"R2 fixed: bare-ls empty-home refusal pre-flighted in _run_ls_root before painted's run_cli \\u2014 same message via resolve._err to stderr, exit 1; siblings noted: store.py:300 same defect class on the store path, emit.py/resolve.py sites already stderr-correct\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786569639.963392, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"6c8d965\"}, \"chw-r3-aggregation-refusal-order\": {\"name\": \"chw-r3-aggregation-refusal-order\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"s2-gate\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"S2 gate residual R3: aggregation vertices refuse (exit 1, structural) before kind validation (exit 2) \\u2014 read orders differently. Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED \\u2014 nonzero+stderr holds on both paths; refusal ordering is an asymmetry, not a defect.\", \"_ts\": 1786569173.972363, \"_n\": 1}, \"chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout\": {\"name\": \"chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"remediation\", \"message\": \"bare loops store pre-flights the empty-home refusal via resolve._err before run_cli, byte-identical message, stderr, exit 1 \\u2014 mirrors 6c8d965; pinned TestBareStoreEmptyHome. Sibling out of ruling scope recorded: loops store <missing-name> still prints to stdout\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVXJJFHVWEJC0W8FK460FDK\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.798489, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\"], \"commit\": \"5f1b0df\"}, \"chw-s4-deviation-branch-base-is-main\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-deviation-branch-base-is-main\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED as benign \\u2014 merge was git-clean and the 5 integration failures trace to worktree-lacks-.loops environment masking, which a wave-based worktree would have had identically. Real lesson receipted separately: worktree test runs are environmentally weaker than main-checkout runs; integration gating in the main checkout is load-bearing.\", \"_ts\": 1786570192.648221, \"_n\": 2, \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s4-test-hermeticity\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-test-hermeticity\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"s4-impl\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Fixed: five TestCite tests in test_emit.py gain monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path) (the file's existing hermeticity idiom) \\u2014 a .loops-bearing cwd's real project.vertex no longer shadows the LOOPS_HOME fixture. Refusal unweakened. Suite green from worktree cwd, /tmp, and a scratch .loops-bearing cwd (2459 passed / 1 xfailed each).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786570379.980328, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"d36f119\"}, \"chw-s4-refusal-message-inert-pins\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-refusal-message-inert-pins\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"s4-impl\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Fixed: refusal message now discloses attempted-vs-inert \\u2014 'all N entity ref(s) failed to resolve; M inert pin(s) dropped with the refusal' (inert clause omitted when M=0). Semantics unchanged per arbiter ruling: mixed all-attempted-failed refuses, all-inert stores as provenance-only. Three new tests pin mixed message, no-inert message, and all-inert store.\", \"_ts\": 1786570380.527479, \"_n\": 2, \"commit\": \"d36f119\"}, \"chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"zero-address cites refuse exit 2 nothing stored; all-inert cites still store provenance-only; gate now one coherent condition (ref-field addresses present AND not all attempted ref-field resolutions failed), stated in comment; 4 pinning tests (TestZeroAddressCite)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KWFPBYHP8H9D8M464FSGNAS1\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.972484, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"friction:cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\"], \"commit\": \"49e4e4c\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f1-comma-key-census\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f1-comma-key-census\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"census input is the post-key_or set via fetch._item_matches_key; comma-key now byte-identical to single-key refusal; 4 pinning tests (TestCommaKeyCensus)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786572640.549176, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"859702b\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f2-custom-lens-inert\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f2-custom-lens-inert\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"gate-fail static --status refuses exit 2 stderr (S1 wording family), before the Format branch so --json refuses too; inert note drops --status; bareword status= predicate keeps the note; 3 pinning tests\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGDGDD443VR20Y9EFMHJ\", \"_ts\": 1786572641.093578, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\"], \"commit\": \"cf05ca3\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s2-f1-key-before-kind\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s2-f1-key-before-kind\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S2\", \"message\": \"collect-fold --key refusal gated on declared kinds + post-validator backstop for live undeclared; ls --kind bogus --key x now byte-identical to no-key (exit 2 validator message); pinned incl. declared-collect regression guard\", \"_ts\": 1786572641.263598, \"_n\": 2, \"commit\": \"649c81b\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"cite gate counts only field==ref resolutions; resolving message address no longer rescues an all-drop cite; non-ref fields keep typed-pin behavior; pinned in test_cite_vertex_slot\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVYQ4SAHYFXM9RKRJX3VGK3\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.611517, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\"], \"commit\": \"49e4e4c\"}, \"chw-sol-r2-f1-malformed-token-evades-gate\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r2-f1-malformed-token-evades-gate\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"message\": \"Arbiter ratifies the fix INCLUDING the bare-separator-less-key consequence: ref=barekey alone now refuses (was silent dead-text store). Discriminator upheld = resolver acceptance (parse_ref_token, extracted and shared), because late-bindability is the meaningful line: inert valid addresses can light up when their kind is declared; a bare key never can, so bare-key-only cites are permanently empty attention. Second gate hole closed by moving the discriminator INTO shared resolver machinery \\u2014 construction direction, watch for a third hole as the dissolve-the-gate trigger.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW0EGGEAEZ8DSAT3SQE1TN8,01KZW0EG5KCJPXA4MHR3YZSQR0\", \"_ts\": 1786573751.117551, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\", \"finding:chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\"], \"commit\": \"a52017d\"}, \"chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Substrate fix per arbiter ruling: surface._row_key gates on 'is not None' (engine fold acceptance is the contract), so falsy-but-valid keys (numeric 0, False) survive into Row.key and kind/0 gets its real entity address. Parity matrix corner un-excluded (predicates agree), sol's end-to-end repro pinned (--key 0,missing --status open answers at exit 0). One test pinned the old nulling (test_surface falsy-key test) \\u2014 inverted with the ruling cited, flagged to coordinator; empty-string address fallback and _item_full_key's source-side truthiness left unchanged and pinned as residue. Suite 2516/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786576969.814506, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"108870ae\"}, \"chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Stringification unified per arbiter ruling: new leaf module loops/foldkey owns the one str() fold-key projection; surface._row_key delegates to it and provenance's _entry_for_key uses it at the lookup (direct string hit wins ties; projection scan meets native-typed keys). read decision/0 --why on a native-numeric-0 item now returns full field attribution incl. supersession history (sol repro inverted, TestNativeNumericKeyWhy). Engine fold semantics untouched; native-0 vs string-'0' identity held at thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string, with the disclosed duality (two rows, same displayed key) pinned in test_surface.py. Suite 2518/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW4J8H998B9YGBWWK7ZR1DW\", \"_ts\": 1786577578.970853, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\"], \"commit\": \"3bb55891\"}, \"chw-sol-r6-f1-replay-identity-switch\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r6-f1-replay-identity-switch\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Winning identity resolved exactly once, before the replay loop (arbiter ruling): _entry_for_key dissolved into _winning_state_key \\u2014 string-wins per the foldkey rule, resolved from the chronology's raw key values; the loop attributes only the winner's state changes and the losing item contributes nothing to fields/changed (identity held at thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string). Contract sentence added: --why explains exactly the row read renders. Pins: both emission orders yield the string item's fields only (no native_only residue, no native prior) and attribution content is order-invariant; r5 native-only pin stays green unchanged. Suite 2521/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW54VD16ZA7Q7442CCJS8RN,01KZW4XWGC1MP4RQ5K952B688G\", \"_ts\": 1786578000.342789, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\", \"thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string\"], \"commit\": \"586d1626\"}, \"sliceA-apps-lazy-import-census-gap\": {\"name\": \"sliceA-apps-lazy-import-census-gap\", \"message\": \"ARBITER DISPOSITION (2026-08-18): deviation ACCEPTED \\u2014 is_jsonl_canonical survives as an unexported shim + one commented Rule 18 allowlist entry + tripwire test naming apps/loops/commands/store.py:142, all three retiring together at the CLI-surface cut. The design's delete ruling rested on the census premise 'apps rides the funnel unchanged'; the premise is falsified by primary source (lazy direct import executing before its mode check \\u2014 gate fact-confirmed), and deleting would require an apps/ edit, which the per-slice diff-empty law forbids this wave. Design-doc census gap noted as the root cause: the 64-site apps census counted call sites, not import sites. Kyle informed with overrule offered; the delete lands at the CLI rebuild where the import dies with the surface.\", \"_ts\": 1787081223.758363, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"dispositioned\", \"agent\": \"fable-arbiter\", \"commit\": \"e5d21e77\"}, \"rule17-scans-untracked-docs\": {\"name\": \"rule17-scans-untracked-docs\", \"status\": \"open\", \"agent\": \"fable-arbiter\", \"slice\": \"arrival-authority\", \"message\": \"Rule 17 (fold-order prose ratchet) fails ONLY in the main checkout, at cut-A head AND at baseline 3b303d5d \\u2014 pre-existing, not a slice regression (test file diff-empty across the slice). Cause: the test scans every .md under docs/ via filesystem glob, so gitignored docs/dev/ historical scratch (010-wave, 080-overnight dossiers, rebuild-audit-0.4.0) matches the denied (ts,id)-as-fold-order prose. Worktrees and CI lack untracked files, so 98/98 green there \\u2014 the ratchet's answer depends on which machine runs it. Fix shape (scope-the-claim): the ratchet's claim is about the SHIPPED surface \\u2014 enumerate via git ls-files, not glob; historical scratch is a labeled record, not drift. Discovered by cut A's load-bearing main-checkout full-suite run, which exists precisely to catch worktree-environment gaps. Not cut A's to fix; candidate for the wave-tail or a standalone one-liner with its own mutation check.\", \"commit\": \"e5d21e77\", \"_ts\": 1787081181.278706, \"_n\": 1}, \"sliceB-catchup-stamps-absent-only\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-catchup-stamps-absent-only\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"Invariant 16 says re-derivation stamps own_lineage 'unconditionally' and that a PRESENT disagreeing marker REFUSES. Implemented as: catch-up stamps ONLY when the marker is ABSENT (so it can never overwrite, and needs no refusal of its own); rederive_projections refuses a present-and-disagreeing marker BEFORE any destructive step, then stamps. Reading: the refusal is about OVERWRITING, so the only path that overwrites is the only path that must refuse.\", \"_ts\": 1787096930.733021, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED (gate G5 honest-and-correct; arbiter concurs): invariant 16 read as absent-or-agreeing \\u2014 catch-up stamps only when absent so it can never overwrite; rederive alone refuses a present-disagreeing marker.\"}, \"sliceB-derived-log-audit-is-set-not-multiset\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-derived-log-audit-is-set-not-multiset\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"Q2 says 'hash each side's lines to 32 bytes and take two set differences'. Implemented literally as sets, and write_derived_log emits sorted UNIQUE lines, so writer and audit share one model. Consequence named: a line duplicated inside the file is invisible to the audit. Coherent with the 'line order carries no meaning' ruling (multiplicity carries none either); a multiset audit would assert something the set-membership ruling says is meaningless.\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.1355, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED: set comparison is literally Q2's ratified wording; duplicated-line invisibility named as the consequence and carried in the docstring.\"}, \"sliceB-cut-a-refusal-test-rematched\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-cut-a-refusal-test-rematched\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"test_arrival_store.py::test_rows_without_a_mark_refuse_rather_than_rebuild matched the refusal message on 're-deriv'. B2 reworded that refusal to name the verb (rederive_projections, no hyphen), so the match string was updated to 'rederive_projections' \\u2014 a strictly stronger assertion, since it now pins that the refusal names the actual recovery.\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.288314, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED: match-string update to the verb name is the refusal now naming its resolution, per the ratified Q1 table.\"}, \"sliceB-rule18-merge-refusal-needs-an-allowlist-entry\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-rule18-merge-refusal-needs-an-allowlist-entry\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"impl\", \"role\": \"implementer\", \"note\": \"ratified \\u00b7 Kyle ruled at the gate (relayed by the team lead): the Rule 18 +1 allowlist entry STANDS AS SHIPPED, no change needed. Q4's requirement that store/merge.py refuse with JsonlCanonicalUnsupported outranks Q9's 'no allowlist entry added' criterion where the two conflict; the class name is the legacy mode's honest name and merge.py must name it to raise it. Allowlist shrink remains zero, net +1. Closing my own ledger entry so it does not read open against a ruling already made.\", \"_ts\": 1787092652.091784, \"_n\": 2}, \"sliceB-catchup-race-fixed\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-catchup-race-fixed\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"ArrivalStore.catch_up read its resume mark OUTSIDE the transaction its INSERTs run in. Two processes catching the same index up both read the pre-consume mark, both replayed the same records, and the loser hit UNIQUE on facts.id \\u2014 misreported as 'the index holds state the log does not account for, projection re-derivation a later cut'. Pre-existing since cut A; B6's required two-process merge test is what makes two concurrent catch-ups routine. Fixed as the smallest honest correction: the CONSUME window escalates to BEGIN IMMEDIATE and re-reads the mark under it; the already-current case stays a lock-free read; the arrival append lock is never taken. Residual named: under sustained contention BEGIN IMMEDIATE can time out as OperationalError rather than a refusal. The same read-then-write race exists in JsonlStore.catch_up and was LEFT ALONE (jsonl_store's cut is later).\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.440063, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED: pre-existing cut-A read-outside-txn race, fixed where cut B makes concurrent catch-ups routine; gate re-verified; simplify M5 later restored the lock-free fast path with the own_lineage conjunct, 33 tests red under the broken-predicate probe (impl + arbiter independently). JsonlStore twin race deliberately untouched \\u2014 its cut is later.\"}, \"sliceB-rule17-allowlist-shrink-outside-fence\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-rule17-allowlist-shrink-outside-fence\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"FENCE DEPARTURE. Q4 mandates sweeping merge.py's R1 doctrine block. Doing so left a stale entry in tests/architecture/test_rule_17_fold_order_prose_is_receipt_order.py's shrink-only allowlist ('ORDER BY (ts, id) is the merge INSERTION order, not a fold order'), turning tests/architecture red. That file is not in the implementer's edit fence, which lists only the rule 18 test. Deleted exactly that one entry rather than stopping: it is the ratchet's own prescribed maintenance for prose that is gone, it is the sanctioned direction for a shrink-only list, and the design's B7 criterion already expects Rule 17 green after this work. Net rule 17 allowlist change: -1.\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.597188, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED (gate-verified stale AND ratchet-demanded): shrink-only maintenance in the sanctioned direction; net Rule 17 allowlist -1.\"}, \"sliceB-driver-union-key-is-row-id-not-t-id\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-driver-union-key-is-row-id-not-t-id\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"Q3 specifies the git merge driver's union key as (t, id). A BATCH line has no single (t, id) \\u2014 it carries several row ids and no one id of its own \\u2014 so that key is not implementable as written. The driver instead maps ROW ID to the whole canonical line carrying it, built through deserialize_records. This satisfies every row of Q3's decision table and additionally catches a row that is a plain fact line on one side and rides inside a batch on the other, which the literal (t, id) reading would have admitted as a silent duplicate. Pinned by test_a_batch_line_unions_by_every_id_it_carries in libs/store/tests/test_derived_log_merge.py.\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.757132, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED: finer key satisfies every row of Q3's table and additionally catches a plain-fact-vs-batch collision; readiness pass re-verified the refusal behavior.\"}, \"sliceB-serialize-object-rebuilds-field-order\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-serialize-object-rebuilds-field-order\", \"status\": \"accepted\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"arbiter\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"note\": \"Q8 says serialize_object is 'byte-identical to the serialize_* function that produced it'. jsonl_codec._dump emits in dict insertion order, so the literal reading makes the contract depend on the caller's key order surviving a round trip through encode_record and json.loads. That holds today but is incidental. serialize_object instead REBUILDS field order from the codec's _SPEC before dumping, so the contract is about the codec's bytes rather than the caller's dict. Strictly stronger than the design's wording; pinned by two tests that shuffle a decoded object's keys and assert byte-identity.\", \"_ts\": 1787096931.915823, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Dispositioned ACCEPTED: rebuilding field order makes the contract structural rather than resting on incidental key-order survival; simplify M3 later made serialize_* pure compositions over the object encoders, preserving this property.\"}, \"sliceB-f1-rebirth-missing-invariant-15-guard\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-f1-rebirth-missing-invariant-15-guard\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"impl\", \"role\": \"implementer\", \"note\": \"fixed \\u00b7 SCOPE NOW COVERS ALL THREE CREATE ARMS (arbiter follow-up, same rationale Kyle ratified for F1: keep the invariant whole rather than store-by-store). The named residue from the first pass \\u2014 slice.py's unguarded _create \\u2014 is closed at b2a55154. receive_store, rebirth_store and slice_store all reach one function, _conn.refuse_create_over_arrival_custody(target, action), each naming its own action. Slicing carried the worst form of the hazard: a filtered subset minted at a live log's derived-index location would disagree with the log about CONTENT as well as custody. Exhibit: neutering the single guard turns ALL THREE refusal tests red in one run (3 failed, 171 passed). Each refusal runs before any byte and leaves no file and no WAL/SHM sidecar, asserted. REMAINING RESIDUE, named not fixed: the guard is a call each arm makes rather than something _create enforces, so a future create arm must remember it; folding it into _create would close that permanently but changes a shared primitive for every caller at once and deserves a deliberate decision. Store 174 passed, architecture 98 passed.\", \"_ts\": 1787092905.67453, \"_n\": 2}, \"sliceB-f2-driver-stderr-runtime-warning\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-f2-driver-stderr-runtime-warning\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"impl\", \"role\": \"implementer\", \"note\": \"fixed \\u00b7 Gate F2. python -m store.derived_log_merge emitted a runpy RuntimeWarning on every invocation ('found in sys.modules after import of package store'), because the B5 re-export from store/__init__.py made -m load the module twice. git relays driver stderr, so this reached users on every merge \\u2014 noise on the surface whose only job is to say why a merge was refused. Fixed by DROPPING the re-export rather than splitting out a CLI module: smaller, and the driver is tooling over store artifacts rather than runtime API, with the python -m entry as its interface. Nothing outside __init__.py used the top-level name; a comment now states why the export is absent so it does not get re-added. Verified: usage line only on bad arity, exit 0 with ZERO bytes on stderr for a real 3-arg run, three git-merge subprocess tests still pass. Also resolves the fence-adjacent edit flagged in the impl report \\u2014 the export surface is back to base.\", \"_ts\": 1787092651.936247, \"_n\": 1}, \"sliceB-r1f1-audit-materialized-both-sides\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-r1f1-audit-materialized-both-sides\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"impl\", \"role\": \"implementer\", \"round\": \"agy-r1\", \"note\": \"fixed \\u00b7 Review r1 finding 1 (minor, contract breach). audit_derived_log called derived_lines, which materializes and SORTS every line, then hashed \\u2014 so Q2's promise of 32-byte digests with memory bounded by record count was prose, not behaviour. derived_lines must materialize because it sorts; the audit does not sort, so borrowing it bought a cost with no use. New _derived_digests walks the log, hashes each line as produced, drops it. MEASURED by reverting only this fix: reviewer's 10x1MB probe 21.01MB -> 7.02MB, and the scaling variant shows the shape that matters \\u2014 BEFORE peak was linear in record count (11/21/41/81 MB at 5/10/20/40 records), AFTER it is FLAT at 7.02MB for all four. Deliberately NOT overclaimed: peak is still linear in the LARGEST single record (one 4MB record peaks at 28MB) because a record must be decoded, re-encoded and hashed to be judged; the docstring now states that measured shape rather than the loose phrase that let the drift happen. Counts survive digest-only sets; no detail string echoes line content so none needed bounding. Mutation-verified missing AND extra still caught against the new implementation.\", \"_ts\": 1787094194.065227, \"_n\": 1}, \"sliceB-r1f2-arrival-driver-rule-was-a-prose-pin\": {\"name\": \"sliceB-r1f2-arrival-driver-rule-was-a-prose-pin\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"B\", \"agent\": \"impl\", \"role\": \"implementer\", \"round\": \"agy-r1\", \"note\": \"fixed \\u00b7 Review r1 finding 2 (nit, test strength). test_there_is_no_merge_driver_for_the_arrival_log asserted a literal string appeared in the driver's own source \\u2014 pinning PROSE, brittle to any rewording that improves it, and never running the driver. CHOICE MADE: the prose assertion is DROPPED, not kept. The design's requirement is that the rule be STATED so nobody defaults it, and the module docstring states it; a 'literal in source' test does not verify a rule, it freezes a sentence. The structural half survives as its own test (no arrival_merge.py exists). New behavioural arm points the driver at two real .arrival logs \\u2014 arrival records with k/lin/ord and no t discriminator, structural genesis at ordinal 0 included, asserted rather than assumed \\u2014 and pins that it raises, that it raises something OTHER than DerivedLogMergeConflict (wrong grammar entirely, not a conflict), and that the target comes back byte-identical so no partial union was written; plus the -m entry exits non-zero with a named refusal. Power proof: a mutation making the driver tolerate a foreign grammar and quietly union arrival records fails the new test \\u2014 and the OLD prose test would have passed it, which is why the finding was worth raising.\", \"_ts\": 1787094194.541019, \"_n\": 1}, \"arrival-sliceC-reconcile-mark-bound-untested\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-reconcile-mark-bound-untested\", \"status\": \"deferred\", \"slice\": \"C3\", \"title\": \"Head-walk reconcile-mark bound has no race test (removing bound leaves suite green)\", \"note\": \"deferred to wave-tail: test would reach KEEP-fenced ceremony transaction window; bound argued from single-judge principle. Flag to readiness reviewer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787198600.131424, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"]}, \"arrival-sliceC-world-fixture-no-arrival-arm\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-world-fixture-no-arrival-arm\", \"status\": \"deferred\", \"slice\": \"C3\", \"title\": \"Ceremony world fixture lacks an arrival arm; plan->apply->recover never composed end-to-end on ArrivalStore\", \"note\": \"deferred to C4/C5 or wave-tail; fixture touches every later slice\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787198600.817674, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"]}, \"arrival-sliceC-F1-bykey-ts-surface-divergence\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-F1-bykey-ts-surface-divergence\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"readiness-r1\", \"title\": \"ByKey('ts') diverges per surface: ordered() payload-only -> [], combined read + generate_lens resolve ts from envelope\", \"note\": \"fixed across three commits fac793e1/13ef260c/83ae19cc: family rule (ts/id envelope, else payload) unified in atoms.resolve_key_field, consumed by ordered(), _combined_read, generate_lens, conformance runner; mutation-proved M1-M5 + P1/P2\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787238010.239144, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"], \"commit\": \"83ae19cc\"}, \"arrival-sliceC-kinds-strategy-decl-leak\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-kinds-strategy-decl-leak\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"readiness-r1\", \"title\": \"atoms kinds() strategy can emit reserved _decl.* kinds; property test appends _decl.genesis raw -> UnadoptedLineage refusal (correct) fails fold-determinism property\", \"note\": \"kinds() text arm filtered through is_appendable_kind, predicate pinned; RESIDUAL: filter-call-deletion caught only by non-durable hypothesis cache \\u2014 accepted (a), predicate pin covers rule drift\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787238011.203061, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"], \"commit\": \"83ae19cc\"}, \"arrival-sliceC-F2-foldkey-surfaces\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-F2-foldkey-surfaces\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"slice\": \"readiness-r2\", \"title\": \"F2 refuted: fact_key_stats/key_prefixes/resolve_entity_id are fold-key surfaces (contract: payload[key]), not ordering-family consumers; no Ordering declaration routes into them\", \"note\": \"call-site provenance: _get_key_field/fold_key_field only; payload-only is their documented pre-existing contract\", \"_ts\": 1787238466.823696, \"_n\": 1}, \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-01\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-01\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"sol-r1\", \"title\": \"scalar payloads crash resolve_key_field instead of missing-K non-membership\", \"severity\": \"major\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787249140.781348, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"], \"commit\": \"15d76fc0\"}, \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-02\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-02\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"sol-r1\", \"title\": \"empty-member aggregate accepts Arrival - refusal availability-dependent not declaration-shaped\", \"severity\": \"major\", \"ref_ref\": \"01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F\", \"_ts\": 1787249141.279397, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering\"], \"commit\": \"bd7c6abc\"}, \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-03\": {\"name\": \"arrival-sliceC-C-SOL-03\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"slice\": \"sol-r1\", \"title\": \"NaN keys break totalization determinism - should refuse