./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19065:01KPYN2DS08X6YVGHYQ0PTC23T	design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter			Pattern: a derived view (ref graph, tick window, search, tag selection) yields a bounded key set; that key set filters or marks another view by membership. Known instances: (1) --refs pulls referenced (kind, key) pairs back into FoldState as focus — outbound/inbound refs are a key set, membership filters the target view. (2) TickWindow.added_keys / updated_keys are per-kind tuples of keys touched since prior boundary; they salience-mark items in the accumulated state. General shape: derived_view → key_set → filter(target_view). Captured before the third instance lands. Dissolves ad-hoc 'which items are relevant to X' queries — X produces a key set, membership does the rest. Composition property: key sets union cleanly (refs ∪ window-deltas) and intersect for narrow focus. The principle names what's already there across two features; future features that fit this shape inherit the composition for free.
./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19066:01KPYPA1CHQBRX8DX8V9XH36C8	design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter			Pattern: a derived view (ref graph, tick window, search, tag selection) yields a bounded key set; that key set filters or marks another view by membership. Known instances: (1) --refs pulls referenced (kind, key) pairs back into FoldState as focus — outbound/inbound refs are a key set, membership filters the target view. (2) TickWindow.added_keys / updated_keys are per-kind tuples of keys touched since prior boundary; they salience-mark items in the accumulated state. General shape: derived_view → key_set → filter(target_view). Captured before the third instance lands. Dissolves ad-hoc 'which items are relevant to X' queries. Composition property: key sets union cleanly (refs ∪ window-deltas) and intersect for narrow focus.
./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19069:01KQ3R1QY0BXZXEQDXB5QS6CF7	design/stale-as-focus-filter			IMPLEMENTED. Third instance of derived-keys-as-focus-filter pattern landed via stale-as-focus-filter-impl plan. Stale-open items as a derived (kind, key) set marking the landing view by membership.\n\nPATTERN: structurally derived (clock + status), bounded set, composes with other derived-key sets (window.added_keys, window.updated_keys) by precedence in _compute_marks. _mark_priority is the composition operator: added=3, updated=2, stale=1, unmarked=0.\n\nGLYPH: ⊘ in fp.stale_indicator (orange fg=208) — peer to ✦/◦, not escalation.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: TASK and THREAD sections of session_landing now expose what's been languishing — the four Mar 20 ticks tasks and three 1w-stale threads light up at landing time. This was the original goal: 'make the artifact most relevant to picking up where we left off the one that surfaces.' Combined with the PLAN-section addition this session (rendering/plan-section-tier-0), all four bounded-fact-substrate kinds (plan/task/thread/decision) now contribute to landing salience.
./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19095:01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS	architecture/libs-handoff-scope	proposed		Contract basis for the libs handoff derived from Sol's LIBS_CHANGES (branch cli-v2-proposal), triaged 2026-08-13. IN SCOPE as tasks (P0): jsonl-declaration-ceremonies (absorb_genesis/absorb_edit on JSONL-canonical — atomic multi-row ceremony in the log, stale-head refusal leaves log+index byte-equivalent, index stays pure derivation); declaration-plan-apply-api (plan_declaration_update/apply — one high-level op owning head-capture, diff, residence, signing; today every client re-assembles an 8-step protocol); declaration-file-store-recovery (durable intent + idempotent recover for the store-first-then-file-cache gap). IN SCOPE (P1): observer-grant-engine-resolution (THE HOLE — engine gates only caller-supplied Grant, declared ObserverDecl.grant.potential silently bypassable; fix at the engine boundary, bypass must be explicit); receipt-attestation-state (persisted signed-state on Receipt/ReceiveResult from the committed row — passes write-receipt-vs-temporal-query, your write's attestation is your write's identity); bounded-fact-query (cross-kind limit+cursor query — MUST spec against the shipped 0.8.0 temporal-cursor contract and A3 ids-never-ordered, not Sol's FactCursor sketch); strict-contract-ruling (MODIFIED from Sol: strict IS enforced, at the CLI (commands/emit.py three-source precedence); ruling needed on whether enforcement moves to engine receive — same push-admission-into-engine motion as observer-grant — Sol's 'unenforced' premise was half wrong); lang-kdl-mutation-api (export add/edit/remove_vertex_kind over existing kdl_insert_child/kdl_remove_child + loops{}-creation + LoopDef-to-KDL serializer); target-probe-api (probe_target -> TargetInfo, dissolves per-client residence/suffix logic); canonical-audit-preflight (typed audit-only/audit-then-open/recover-then-open, never conflate verify with repair). DEFERRED (P2, promote on forcing consumer): lifecycle-projection helper, shared result codec, search coordinator, maintenance backend matrix. SEQUENCING: VertexHandle S5 checkpoint precedes any consumer cutover; the throwaway probe (task:cli-v2-probe) is the independent forcing consumer that exercises these APIs as they land. Collisions honored: exit-code/machine-codes work stays with thread:cli-error-surface-unification, not duplicated here.
./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19109:01M08R71G5HNANMTA3JQAKXK9B	arrival-migration-arc	open		SIDECAR CONTRACT SPEC STOOD UP (2026-08-17): "The Migration Sidecar" — https://claude.ai/code/artifact/8bfa9a78-98df-4ef0-b5da-52999fe252de — sibling to The Arrival Substrate memo and The Arrival Log. Refs the anchor fact 01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ directly in its authority line, per the recorded hard requirement. Ten sections: frozen-artifact form + legacy detector residue; containment-only genesis; content-addressed lineage id with the three custodian cases + keyless fork law; exactness contract (four verbatim preservations, per-record ordinals order-isomorphic to legacy rowid); classification as verifier exit codes (table); --allow-unsigned arm; structural idempotence/resume + ceremony order (genesis -> carried records + interleaved classification facts -> sealing tick, unsealed log = named incomplete state); population inventory table; resolved residuals (own_lineage marker dissolves into genesis fact, verified in code); open items with honest status — 216 rebirth tick.* grade PROPOSED not ruled (proposed arm: they migrate as facts under segment grade, tick-hood is historical content), interleave-uniqueness vectors should share fixtures with the sidecar verifier.\n\nColophon carries all nine backing fact ids. REMAINING: Kyle's ruling on the tick.* proposal; then the spec is fully ruled ground and next work is the sidecar implementation itself.
./docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/codex-r3-stderr.log:19117:01M0B0Z14T9ATPRAJTKBBMCQQT	design/arrival-sliceA-authority	ratified		RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-18 session with Fable — the cut-A ratify gate per impl-pipeline stage 0 is now OPEN for implementation). The cut A (AUTHORITY) design fact; proposal doc docs/dev/arrival-sliceA-authority-design-2026-08-18.md (authored by a Claude design agent, all load-bearing citations arbiter-spot-verified against source at HEAD; agent self-corrected one cost claim mid-review — key locality, not an unsigned era — and demoted its own gate overclaim, both kept in the ratified record).\n\nCORE: adoption genesis body = {protocol, lineage, key} — founding public key self-signed at ordinal 0 per bootstrap fact 01M08N9H8G movement 1; slice 0's minimal body was slice-0-scoped, the bootstrap fact ruled the destination. protocol = the founding key-holder's SIGNED claim of the arrival grammar the lineage speaks (forward-versioning of arrival itself, NOT legacy-store support; per-record v is unsigned framing, the genesis copy is the attested one). Document set stays at ordinal >= 1 as movement 2 (declaration absorption) — never in the genesis body. fact_cursor DISSOLVES (ord < N is structural); chain_head OUT (a sqlite tick-row hash frozen into a signed immutable record rests an integrity claim on a projection — Law 1's first prohibition). Cut A builds arrival.py's FIRST VERIFIER implementing the ruled rule: key valid at N iff introduced at < N, or N is genesis and self-certifying.\n\nKYLE'S TWO RULINGS THIS SESSION: (1) Q1 as above. (2) Q2 = the gate's libs/sign + observer-key registry file-position trace is an EXCLUSIVITY claim (reading 2): the arrival verifier resolves every verifying key from (lineage, ordinal) coordinates ONLY, no libs code consults the .vertex for arrival keys; G2 gate artifact = (key, lineage, ordinal) rows produced with every projection deleted after a second key is introduced at a stated ordinal. BOUNDARY: the apps-composed tick-chain verifier and the .vertex observers{} block are untouched this slice (apps/ diff-empty is law) — the block is DEMOTED to legacy projection-era artifact, retirement scheduled at the surface cut/CLI rebuild. Total-rewrite detection RESTATED as a distribution property: a fresh mint diverges in every rh from ordinal 0 against any copy (peer, backup, git history, aggregator lineage-id pin); a local owner-level rewrite is undefendable by ANY local artifact including the .vertex (an attacker who can rewrite the store can rewrite the .vertex — the registry tripwire's true width was store-write-but-not-vertex-write plus tool mistakes, never the admin adversary). Self-containment is the point; horizon/potential out of scope. Q3 discharged (all three slice-0 rulings Kyle-confirmed same morning).\n\nDEFERRED EXPLICITLY, NAMED: the keyless-genesis tension. 01M08N9H8G rules a keyless genesis variant (no key field, unsigned, era UNSIGNED — the sidecar's keyless-migration customer, load-bearing for keyless-custodians-same-lineage determinism since a key field sits inside the content-address); 01M09GNGW7 rules sig REQUIRED and slice 0 refuses unconditionally. Cut A takes NO position — its live ceremonies always have a signer. The SIDECAR SLICE must resolve it: deliberate grammar amendment (carve-out/version bump) or deliberate retirement of keyless migration, trade visible, Kyle's ruling then. The doc must not claim supersession.\n\nINSTANTIATIONS (ruled ground, doc specifies the how): is_jsonl_canonical DELETED (head of Rule 18's denylist) for three-arm canonical_mode() -> arrival|jsonl|sqlite; canonical_store_path/resolve_store_path/sqlite_sidecars unchanged (reads execute through projections, Law 1 permits — why apps/ stays diff-empty); log_path_for's pure inverse breaks under three modes -> explicit-mode signature, existence-based disambiguation moves to probe where existence checks are legal; probe wired FIRST (discharges the slice-0 deferral), .arrival corroboration via open('rb')+decode_record, half-migrated store (.db with BOTH .arrival and .jsonl siblings) named: arrival wins per Law 1, .jsonl classifies as projection — the one place cut A could silently mint two custody holders; own_lineage becomes a PROJECTION of the arrival genesis (written from ArrivalLog.lineage(), read from sqlite, rebuildable by cut B) — six sqlite readers incl. a raw SELECT at apps/loops store.py:942 ride unchanged; adopt_lineage in arrival mode REFUSES (restamp is projection repair = cut B's verb; delete breaks legacy stores per seam rule S3); late_arrivals KEEPS its name (user-visible JSON key, witness-time sense already labeled at witness.py:584-594, rename needs a CLI-surface cut + CHANGELOG); Rule 18 _SCAN_TARGETS gains residence.py + probe.py ONLY (custody has not left jsonl_store et al. until cut B); the shrink-only mechanism that moves is Rule 17's _ALLOWLIST via test_allowlist_has_no_stale_entries (Rule 18's _ALLOWED is empty — brief's shrink premise corrected by the agent).\n\nSEAM (three rules): S1 a live-store genesis NEVER carries a containment claim — containment belongs to the sidecar's frozen content-addressed genesis (01M08Q6P3P); S2 migration pins resolve to the sidecar's containment evidence — cut A's answer is dissolution, not relocation; S3 cut A converts NOTHING — every ceremony change is conditional on the declared locator being .arrival, .jsonl and sqlite ceremonies stay byte-identical.\n\nGATE: G1 authority test literally (build, exercise incl. declaration absorb + seal, delete .db/-wal/-shm and any .jsonl, everything answers from .arrival alone incl. own_lineage with store_meta gone, via walk()); G2 the exclusivity trace as ruled above; G3 apps/ diff-empty. Carried: every new reader that ADOPTS an on-disk record validates at the adoption site (_authority_fault); the O(n) residual stays at confirmed width, any narrowing is Kyle's flagged call.
